      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 20\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nClick here for an overview of cultural armor introduced with Dragons of Norrath.\nFind Srekta Froreki in the Rathe Mountains at -2200, +190.\nYou say, 'Hail, Srekta Froreki'\nSrekta Froreki says 'Welcome back to the swamps, ______. Cripes! You've been away for awhile; that's the worst case of dry-foot I've ever seen. You should stick around and rehabilitate; there's plenty of interesting [things] to be found right around here.'\nYou say, 'What things?'\nSrekta Froreki says 'A group of us just returned from an expedition into deepest Guk. Turns out that some of our ancestors had learned to create some rather remarkable armor, well, you know, before they were cursed to undeath and all. The designs must have been lost during our years of enslavement but we've recovered a few pieces, enough to make a [pattern book] so we can reproduce their designs. You should see these; the craftsmanship is remarkable! We also found some [cultural symbol patterns] if you were interested in them.'\nYou, 'I want to make a pattern book.'\nSrekta Froreki says 'Well, I only have one pattern book but I can make you a copy. To do this I will need a torn sash for the cover, a low quality cat pelt for the pages, a dune tarantula abdomen for the clasp, and a snake venom sac to grind down and make a salve which will protect and preserve the finished product. I have heard most of these items can be found in the Oasis of Marr. Bring them to me and the pattern book shall be yours.'\nThe items drop from various mobs in the Northern and Southern Desert of Ro, as well as the Oasis of Marr.  Hand in the items.\nSrekta Froreki says 'Well done, ______. As promised, here are the armor patterns of our ancestors. May they serve you well.'\nYour faction standing with Citizens of Gukta got better.\nYour faction standing with Protectors of Gukta got better.\nYour faction standing with High Council of Gukta got better.\nYour faction standing with Lorekeepers of Gukta got better.\nYour faction standing with Guktan Elders got better.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive Ancestral Froglok's Armor.\nYou say, 'What cultural symbol patterns?'\nSrekta Froreki says, 'You're interested in cultural symbol patterns, I see. I can give you the cultural symbol patterns but I will need you to run a few tasks for me before I can give them to you. What do you say, would you like to run a few short [tasks] for me?'\nYou say, 'I will run your tasks.'\nSrekta Froreki says, 'I have four tasks that need to be completed. The first is an adventure into the desert of [South Ro] where you will gather some charms to replace some broken charms on my necklace. The next you will be tasked with venturing into the heart of [Kithicor] where you will hunt for a few items that I can use to create a new cloak. The third task leads you into [Velketor's Labyrinth] where you will collect a few items to make my old hat appear like a new one. The final task I have for you is an adventure into the [Stillmoon temple] where you will learn about the creatures that inhabit the area.'\nJourneyman's Book of Froglok Culture\nYou say, 'South Ro?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Srekta's Charms'.\nSrekta's Charms\n1) Southern Desert of Ro:  Kill 20 dervish cutthroats\n2) Southern Desert of Ro:  Loot 4 Cutthroat Golden Teeth\n3) Mountains of Rathe:  Deliver 4 Cutthroat Golden Teeth to Srekta Froreki\n4) Southern Desert of Ro:  Explore the merchant camp in the desert\n5) Southern Desert of Ro:  Kill 10 crypt mummies\n6) Southern Desert of Ro:  Loot 1 Rotting Zombie Skull\n7) Mountains of Rathe:  Deliver 1 Rotting Zombie Skull to Srekta Froreki\nUpon handing in the Rotting Zombie Skull:\nYour task 'Srekta's Charms' has been updated.\nI'm glad to see you have made it back. Let me look at that skull. Yes that is indeed rare and will go perfect on my necklace. Thank you. You have earned these cultural symbol patterns.\nReceive Journeyman's Book of Froglok Culture.\nExpert's Book of Froglok Culture\nYou say, 'Kithicor?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Srekta's Cloak Collection'.\nSrekta's Cloak Collection\nKithicor Forest: Kill 50 zombies\nKithicor Forest: Loot 20 Shriveled Flesh\nMountains of Rathe: Deliver 4 Shriveled Flesh to Skekta Froreki\nKithicor Forest: Explore the lake in the south east\nKithicor Forest: Kill 5 dread wolves\nKithicor Forest: Loot 1 Essence of Moonlight\nMountains of Rathe: Deliver 1 Essence of Moonlight to Skekta Froreki\nOnly zombies with \"zombie\" in the name count toward your task, but you can loot the Shriveled Flesh from anything and have it count.  Any wolf with \"dread\" in the name, including \"dreaded,\" will count as a dread wolf.\nUpon handing in the Essence of Moonlight:\nOh dear what a glorious cloak this will be. Thank you. You have earned these cultural symbol patterns.\nYou receive your Expert's Book of Froglok Culture.\nMaster's Book of Froglok Culture\nYou say, 'Velketor's Labyrinth?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Srekta's Hat of Shame'.\nSrekta's Hat of Shame\nVelketor's Labyrinth: Kill 80 icepaw kobolds\nVelketor's Labyrinth: Loot 20 Icepaw Kobold's Paw\nMountains of Rathe: Deliver 4 Icepaw Kobold's Paw to Srekta Froreki\nVelketor's Labyrinth: Explore the entrance to the labyrinth\nVelketor's Labyrinth: Kill 5 gargoyles\nVelketor's Labyrinth: Loot 1 Block of Velium\nMountains of Rathe: Deliver 1 Block of Velium to Srekta Froreki\nUpon handing in the Block of Velium:\nYour task 'Srekta's Hat of Shame' has been updated.\nWhat a beautiful piece of velium you have there. It will look wonderful on my hat as I parade around the streets of Gukta. You have earned these cultural symbol patterns.\nHas this dialogue changed since the frogloks were kicked out of Gukta?\nYou receive your Master's Book of Froglok Culture.\nGrandmaster's Book of Froglok Culture.\nYou say, 'Stillmoon Temple?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Scouting the Temple'\nScouting the Temple\nStillmoon Temple: Kill 120 Stillmoon creatures\nStillmoon Temple: Recover 80 patches of rough goblin skin from Stillmoon goblins\nMountains of Rathe: Take 4 samples of the rough goblin skin to Srekta\nStillmoon Temple: Kill 10 stillmoon dirt tenders\nStillmoon Temple: Recover a stone necklace from the stillmoon dirt tenders\nMountains of Rathe: Deliver the stone necklace to Srekta\nUpon handing in the stone necklace:\nNeed completion dialogues.\nYou receive your Grandmaster's Book of Froglok Culture.\nTypes of Armor\nFarsight - Rogue, Shaman\nLorekeeper - Necromancer, Wizard\nProtectorate - Cleric, Paladin, Shadowknight, Warrior\nNeed updated dialogues, task names and stages and descriptions, additional quest items, additional rewards.Rewards:\n- Elaborate Lorekeeper Armband [item=54421]\n- Elaborate Lorekeeper Boots [item=54422]\n- Elaborate Lorekeeper Breeches [item=54423]\n- Elaborate Lorekeeper Cap [item=54424]\n- Elaborate Lorekeeper Gloves [item=54425]\n- Elaborate Lorekeeper Robes [item=54426]\n- Elaborate Lorekeeper Sleeves [item=54427]\n- Elaborate Protectorate Armband [item=56496]\n- Elaborate Protectorate Boots [item=56497]\n- Elaborate Protectorate Cuirass [item=36851]\n- Elaborate Protectorate Gloves [item=37046]\n- Elaborate Protectorate Greaves [item=36852]\n- Elaborate Protectorate Helm [item=36853]\n- Elaborate Protectorate Sleeves [item=36854]\n- Elegant Farsight Armband [item=74437]\n- Elegant Farsight Cuirass [item=72628]\n- Elegant Farsight Gloves [item=73842]\n- Elegant Farsight Greaves [item=73133]\n- Elegant Lorekeeper Armband [item=74088]\n- Elegant Lorekeeper Breeches [item=73492]\n- Elegant Lorekeeper Robes [item=73491]\n- Elegant Lorekeeper Sleeves [item=73493]\n- Intricate Lorekeeper Armband [item=54428]\n- Intricate Lorekeeper Boots [item=54429]\n- Intricate Lorekeeper Breeches [item=54430]\n- Intricate Lorekeeper Cap [item=54431]\n- Intricate Lorekeeper Gloves [item=54432]\n- Intricate Lorekeeper Robes [item=54433]\n- Intricate Lorekeeper Sleeves [item=54434]\n- Intricate Protectorate Armband [item=39211]\n- Ornate Farsight Armband [item=38138]\n- Ornate Farsight Boots [item=38591]\n- Ornate Farsight Cuirass [item=38542]\n- Ornate Farsight Gloves [item=38566]\n- Ornate Farsight Greaves [item=38543]\n- Ornate Farsight Helm [item=38565]\n- Ornate Farsight Sleeves [item=38567]\n- Ornate Lorekeeper Armband [item=38278]\n- Ornate Lorekeeper Boots [item=38279]\n- Ornate Lorekeeper Breeches [item=38810]\n- Ornate Lorekeeper Cap [item=38280]\n- Ornate Lorekeeper Gloves [item=38281]\n- Ornate Lorekeeper Robes [item=38340]\n- Ornate Lorekeeper Sleeves [item=38282]\n- Ornate Protectorate Armband [item=39209]\n- Ornate Protectorate Cuirass [item=56528]\n- Ornate Protectorate Gloves [item=56529]\n- Ornate Protectorate Greaves [item=56530]\n- Ornate Protectorate Helm [item=56531]\n- Ornate Protectorate Sleeves [item=39208]\n- Seals of Darkhollow [item=44967]\n- Simple Farsight Armband [item=58807]\n- Simple Farsight Boots [item=57052]\n- Simple Farsight Cuirass [item=58806]\n- Simple Farsight Gloves [item=38384]\n- Simple Farsight Greaves [item=59643]\n- Simple Farsight Helm [item=57000]\n- Simple Farsight Sleeves [item=57004]\n- Simple Lorekeeper Armband [item=38271]\n- Simple Lorekeeper Boots [item=38272]\n- Simple Lorekeeper Breeches [item=38273]\n- Simple Lorekeeper Cap [item=38274]\n- Simple Lorekeeper Gloves [item=38275]\n- Simple Lorekeeper Robes [item=38276]\n- Simple Lorekeeper Sleeves [item=38277]\n- Simple Protectorate Gloves [item=38385]\n- Simple Protectorate Helm [item=57001]\n- Simple Protectorate Sleeves [item=57006]\n[",
