      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 70\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nThis is the first of five tasks in a series. (At one point in this series you receive the Ashengate Seal, an item which allows you to bypass the golems guarding the gate to Ashengate.)\nThis task begins in the Direwind Cliffs with Scout Zryan, located just east of Sunderock Springs zoneline by a rock with another NPC, at -1620, -1010.  He is the one crouching.\nYou say, 'Hail, Scout Zryan'\nScout Zryan says 'Greetings, ______!  It's nice to find a friendly face in these forsaken lands.  I've been scouting the Ashengate temple, looking for a way in.  Dyn`leth's armies keep the [approach] heavily guarded, but we may just have a chance.'\nYou say, 'What approach?'\nScout Zryan says 'When outnumbered, the superior warrior stalks with patience and strikes only when the time is right.  Here is what must be done. . . '\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Gray Legion'.\nKill 10 Gray Legion Soldiers - Direwind Cliffs\nKill 2 Gray Legion Clerics - Direwind Cliffs\nKill 2 Gray Legion Mages - Direwind Cliffs\nKill 5 Gray Legion Sergeants - Direwind Cliffs\nThis last step becomes available after completion of the previous steps.\nDeliver Orzhok's Shattered Shield to Scout Zryan - Direwind Cliffs\nYour task 'The Gray Legion' has been updated.\nZryan says, 'Well done.  You are now ready for the main attack on the [approach].'\nThis is the lead-in to the next task, \"The Approach\".\nYour faction standing with Crusade of the Scale got better.\nYour faction standing with Forces of Dyn'leth got worse.\nYour faction standing with Circle of the Crystalwing got better.\nYou gain experience!!\nThese mobs that you need to kill can be found just south-east of the Scout's location. They are in groups of usually 2 soldiers, 2-3 orcs (level 65) and either a cleric or mage. The sergeants roam from group to group and can see-invis. It is suggested to pull to a spot near the task giver. These mobs have a fairly large assist range, so FD pulling and/or crowd control is a must.\nOrzhok's Shattered can be looted at anytime (looting is not part of the task just turning it in is).\nOrzhok Shattered Shield is dropped by Captain Orzhok (drops 6), who is 75+ and rampages.Submitted by: Restorer, Quellious ServerRewards:\n[",
