        { id = 67744, name = "Battlelancer Sleeves", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 75\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is the outline for armor tasks offered by Terraxs. You will not be able to complete these tasks without an upper-end raiding guild. These tasks result in armor with stats in the neighborhood of 450-475hp/mana/end. After completing one of these tasks, you can request a task in which you add stat bonuses to your armor piece. That outline can be found here.\nFind Terraxs on the second floor of Crescent Reach at location -1395, -1920. He is located next to the alchemy vendors.\nYou say, 'Hail, Terraxs'\nTerraxs says 'Vasha, _____. Have you come to me because you hunger for a [challenge]?'\nYou say, 'I hunger for a challenge'\nTerraxs says 'Indeed! I have learned the secret of forming together armors of amazing power but only the strongest and most valiant should attempt to walk the [road] I can lead you down!'\nYou say, 'A road...'\nTerraxs says 'Well not an actual road, no, of course not! I meant it more figuratively! I have discovered the forms of a [recipe] that I think may wish to explore with me, _____!'\nYou say, 'What recipe is that?'\nTerraxs says 'I have compared notes with my friend Tenish about the magical relics we have been coming across. We both have a theory about how to leverage the power lying dormant in these items but Tenish thinks too small for my taste. I have heard that the really powerful relics are closer to the [source] of the magic that has enchanted the relics we have found.'\nYou say, 'What magic source?'\nTerraxs says 'I suppose I should say sources, not source. The peak our cousin Dyn`leth sits atop and the mighty giant enclave both appear to be focal points for incredible energy. If you would like to experiment with me, and if you and your companions are strong enough, then I can share with you my [thoughts] on the subject'\nYou say, 'Please, share your thoughts'\nTerraxs says 'Excellent _____! Return to me when you have gathered these items and we will attempt to craft something fantastic together!'\nThe following tasks are available, depending on your class (the name of the task is the piece of armor you will receive):\nYou have been assigned the task '_____'.\nBerserkers:\nBattlelancer Coat\nBattlelancer Leggings\nBattlelancer Sleeves\nBattlelancer Gauntlets\nBattlelancer Boots\nBattlelancer Wristguard\nBattlelancer Coif\nRangers:\nEvergreen Coat\nEvergreen Leggings\nEvergreen Sleeves\nEvergreen Gauntlets\nEvergreen Boots\nEvergreen Wristguard\nEvergreen Coif\nRogues:\nDeadkeeper Coat\nDeadkeeper Leggings\nDeadkeeper Sleeves\nDeadkeeper Gauntlets\nDeadkeeper Boots\nDeadkeeper Wristguard\nDeadkeeper Coif\nShamans:\nSilverfanged Coat\nSilverfanged Leggings\nSilverfanged Sleeves\nSilverfanged Gauntlets\nSilverfanged Boots\nSilverfanged Wristguard\nSilverfanged Coif\nTerraxs believes that he can help you craft new and powerful armors. All you need to do is collect several components and return them to Terraxs so he can construct the final item. Terraxs believes that you should focus your search far to the North.\nFrom what Terraxs can gather there are two types of ancient artifacts that he thinks he can use to construct new armor items.\nAncient artifacts have become infused with a magical coating that looks strangely like Frost. Search along the path to the Giant city we have heard rumors of for such artifacts.\nThe ash from a distant volcano has fused itself with ancient artifacts, lending strange properties to them. Search along the path to this volcano for these artifacts.\nThe molds you will need can be found in the same areas as the artifacts although they may be much harder to locate. The local denziens of these areas have become aware of the unique properties of these molds and the most powerful among them are hoarding them for their own purposes. From what Terraxs can gather you may need to face the master of each area to find the molds you seek!\nFor the Chest Piece:\n4x Power Infused Chain Link\n1x A Timeworn Chestguard Mold\nFor the Legs Piece:\n4x Power Infused Chain Link\n1x A Timeworn Leggings Mold\nFor the Arms Piece:\n3x Power Infused Chain Link\n1x A Timeworn Armguard Mold\nFor the Hands Piece:\n2x Power Infused Chain Link\n1x A Timeworn Glove Mold\nFor the Head Piece:\n3x Power Infused Chain Link\n1x A Timeworn Skullcap Mold\nFor the Boots Piece:\n2x Power Infused Chain Link\n1x A Timeworn Boot Mold\nFor the Wrist Piece:\n1x Power Infused Chain Link\n1x A Timeworn Bracer Mold\nPower Infused Chain Links drop from random trash mobs in Ashengate and Froscrypt raid instances while Timeworn Molds drop from various high-end raid encounters in the same instances.\nGive the required items to Terraxs in exchange for your armor piece and completion of the task.\nYour task '______' has been updated.\nYour task '______' has been updated.\nIn yellow text:\nWell done! I'm impressed at what you accomplished in gathering together the supplies for this item!\nYou have been given: ______\nThis is the lead-in to another series of tasks, in which you can enhance you armor with stat bonuses.Rewards:\n- Battlelancer Boots [item=53958]\n- Battlelancer Coat [item=67758]\n- Battlelancer Coif [item=54331]\n- Battlelancer Gauntlets [item=53539]\n- Battlelancer Leggings [item=55962]\n- Battlelancer Sleeves [item=67744]\n- Battlelancer Wristguard [item=54839]\n- Deadkeeper Boots [item=54095]\n- Deadkeeper Coat [item=67761]\n- Deadkeeper Coif [item=54636]\n- Deadkeeper Gauntlets [item=53636]\n- Deadkeeper Leggings [item=54592]\n- Deadkeeper Sleeves [item=54096]\n- Deadkeeper Wristguard [item=54097]\n- Evergreen Boots [item=54841]\n- Evergreen Coat [item=54950]\n- Evergreen Coif [item=54842]\n- Evergreen Gauntlets [item=54835]\n- Evergreen Leggings [item=54938]\n- Evergreen Sleeves [item=54843]\n- Evergreen Wristguard [item=54844]\n- Silverfang