      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 65\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Expedition\n**Group Size:** Raid\n**Min. # of Players:** 10\n**Max. # of Players:** 54\n\nThis expedition is given by Kroggl at the Wayfarers Brotherhood camp near the passage to Greater Faydark.\nYou say, 'Hail, Kroggl'\nKroggl says 'Me gots big jobs to do for de Wayfarers. Vampires really bad tings but dey gots lots of stuffs we want to see. Me gets to go with adventurers to see. You go too if you gots a strong head. Spooky dere. Really spooky.  If you can rally de call of your friend perhaps you can help wit a serious [problem].'\nYou say, 'Problem?'\nKroggl says 'De power struggles in Mistmoore's Catacombs just keep goin' and goin'. Mayong's young kiddies called de Scions want to rule over de older kiddies, de Trueborn. Me know they hate each other lots! De smart Scions learned how to make really bad monsters dat they are aiming at de Trueborn and us too. We need a powerful force to go and kill dose beasts before they come to de surface. Are yous [interested]?'\nYou say, 'I am interested.'\nKroggl says 'No mercy.  Smash dem vampires, ______.'\nHead to Lesser Faydark and zone in from the mine entrance at -90, +3870.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Mistmoore's Catacombs: Struggles within the Progeny.\nDespite the name, it uses \"The Asylum of Invoked Stone\" map.\nMost trash mobs are weak to at least cold and poison, and strong against at least fire.\nUndead mobs (rawbones and Trueborn night agents) are weak to at least fire and poison, and strong against at least cold.\nAs you progress, you'll find a few \"Kel`Novar Warder\", who are tougher than the zone trash.\nThe real Valdoon Kel`Novar seems weak against at least fire, and resisted all magic spells even after being debuffed. He is extremely resistant to both magic and disease-based slows.\nClear your way through the zone. As you do, you'll come across 3x \"Guardian of Kel`Novar\". Each Guardian you kill lowers Valdoon's hps by 5%.\nOn the death of the each Guardian, you'll see:\nThe massive stone beast shudders violently as it transforms into a lifeless statue. The power of its master wanes slightly by the loss of its soul-bound guardian.\nOn the death of the third Guardian, you'll see:\nYour victory has weakened a shroud of magic cloaking the dungeon's treasure.\nIn the northwest corner of the zone, there is a north passage and a west passage. The final room in each one will have a Valdoon in it.\nOne of the Valdoons is at 100% health while the other is at 85%. The one at 100% is \"fake\" and can be ignored if you want (although killing it will result in three chests instead of two).\nOn the death of the fake Valdoon Kel`Novar' (starts with 100% health):\nYour faction standing with Progeny got worse.\nA mighty laugh echoes out into the night from the gargoyle aviary. The sound of Valdoon Kel'Novar's voice is clear, 'Did you fools really believe I would be so careless? You'll not live to regret the mistake of crossing the Trueborn!'\nGuardian of Kel`Novar rises off its haunches with its claws outstretched.\nAt this time a fourth (spawned) Guardian of Kel`Novar will pop at the site of the fake Valdoon Kel'Novar's corpse and attack.\nOn the death of the forth (spawned) Guardian of Kel`Novar:\nThe massive stone beast shudders violently as it transforms into a lifeless statue. The power of its master wanes slightly by the loss of its soul-bound guardian.\nYour victory has weakened a shroud of magic cloaking the dungeon's treasure.\nOn the death of the real Valdoon Kel`Novar (starts with as low as 80% health):\nYour faction standing with Progeny got worse.\nYour victory has shattered the shroud of magic surrounding the dungeon's treasure\nUp to three chests spawn in the room after Valdoon's defeat\nNote that by skipping to the real Valdoon Kel`Novar without, \"Your victory has weakened a shroud of magic cloaking the dungeon's treasure,\" will result in the chests not spawning and a reduction in the total number of loot.\nKnown raid loot from this event (Two items from each chest, can have duplicates from the same chest):\nGuardian`s Granite Chest\nBloodbond Stone\nFaded Gloves of the Shadows\nReflection Shard of Kel`Novar\nValdoon's Bloodstone of Power\nValdoon's Stone Beast Shard\nValdoon`s gilded coffin\nBracer of Forbidden Paths\nEnchanted Orb of Defense\nGuardian's Stone of Enhanced Protection\nSharp-Edged Pearl Shard [Blessed Healing]\nStone Guardian's Conjuration Shard\nValdoon's Immortal Blood Gem\nGuardian`s Stone Chest\nBloodied Shard of Kel`Novar\nBloodstone of Blinding Strikes\nNightstone of the Vampire Slayer\nScion Stone of Disruption\nSilvery Slippers of the Evoker\nSubmitted by: KyrosKraneRewards:\n- Bloodbond Stone [item=25084]\n- Bloodied Shard of Kel`Novar [item=25077]\n- Bloodstone of Blinding Strikes [item=25085]\n- Bracer of Forbidden Paths [item=25946]\n- Enchanted Orb of Defense [item=25079]\n- Faded Gloves of the Shadows [item=25257]\n- Guardian's Stone of Enhanced Protection [item=25075]\n- Journal of Valdoon -- Page I [item=46963]\n- Journal of Valdoon -- Page II [item=46964]\n- Journal of Valdoon -- Page III [item=46965]\n- Journal of Valdoon -- Page IV [item=46966]\n- Journal of Valdoon -- Page V [item=46967]\n- Journal of Valdoon -- Page VI [item=46968]\n- Nightstone of the Vampire Slayer [item=25086]\n- Reflection Shard of Kel`Novar [item=25087]\n- Scion Stone of Disruption [item=25088]\n- Silvery Slippers of the Evoker [item=25600]\n- Stone Guardian's Conjuration Shard [item=25090]\n- Valdoon's Bloodstone of Power [item=25091]\n- Valdoon's Immortal Blood Gem [item=25092]\n- Valdoon's Stone Beast Shard [item=25093]\n[",
