      walkthrough = "**Level:** 65\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is a grand task which begins with Phara Dar in the Field of Scale.\nYou say, 'Hail, Phara Dar'\nPhara Dar says 'I do not have time to indulge in idle chat, small one. My father and I must find a way to crush these Iksar. We all grow [weary] of such prolonged battle.'\nYou say, 'Weary?'\nPhara Dar says 'It is slow going, destroying such a large number of foes. We gnaw on the tail, but the body and head remain inside the [walls]. I would prefer a quick, decisive final battle. I would prefer to end this foolishness now. But the Ring of Scale is nothing if not wise, and so we fight this war as we must. Only Talendor appears to be enjoying the delay. I suspect he appreciates the anticipation of victory nearly as much as the victory itself. Though the appearance of the [Sokokar] give me pause for concern.'\nYou say, 'Its walls...'\nPhara Dar says 'The buildings to the east and the tower to the north. Emperor Ganak himself has taken up residence in the village. Kaesora I believe they call it. With the increased guard and now the presence of Ganak himself, it's plain to see something big is happening in there. If only we could [get inside] and find out what! The tower to the north is reported to house one of the Iksar's greatest generals, though I have not yet met him on the battlefield myself.'\nYou say, 'How could we get inside?'\nPhara Dar says 'Quite a challenge to be sure. The lizards won't allow outsiders into their most holy chambers, but if I were to craft a special [illusion] I believe you could slip by the guards unnoticed.'\nYou say, 'An illusion?'\nPhara Dar says 'That of an Iksar Skeleton! Such an illusion would be quite difficult however. No simple spell will convince Ganak's elite guards. No no, this must be a [special] incantation for certain!'\nYou say, 'A special incantation?'\nPhara Dar says 'In order to create a convincing illusion, I require some rather unique items in order to help visualize the final form. I warn you, this will NOT be easy. Do not waste my time if you cannot finish the job. I have little time or patience to deal with distractions as Ganak's forces bear down upon us! Can you [see this through]?'\nYou say, 'We will see this through'\nPhara Dar says 'We shall see ______. We shall see. In order to make a convincing illusion, I will need a [ribcage], a [foot], a [hand], and finally a [skull]. Once I have all 4 pieces of this skeletal puzzle, not even Ganak himself will be able to see through your disguise.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Grand Illusion'.\nNote: Also go through trigger text for the four sub-tasks. You cannot pre-loot anything throughout these tasks, so be sure to request them before looting anything.\nCollect an Iksar Ribcage 0/1 (ALL)\nThis step updates upon completing \"Purify the Body\" [quest=4714].\nCollect an Iksar Skeletal Hand 0/1 (ALL)\nThis step updates upon completing \"Idle Hands\" [quest=4716].\nCollect an Iksar Skeletal Foot 0/1 (ALL)\nThis step updates upon completing \"Evil Afoot\" [quest=4715].\nCollect a Petrified Iksar Skull 0/1 (ALL)\nThis step updates upon completing \"The Skull of the Ancient\" [quest=4717].\nSpeak with Phara Dar 0/1 (Field of Scale)\nAs the last piece of the puzzle is delivered to Phara Dar, a broad smile forms on her toothy maw. \"When I sent you out searching for these items, I must admit I did not believe you'd actually find them. You have proven yourself worthy of great respect amongst my brethren, and I hope this illusion will serve you well. Return to me whenever you have need of my assistance.\"\nFinal Reward:\nBone Mask of the Ancient Iksar\nMAGIC ITEM NO TRADE\nSlot: FACE\nCharges: Unlimited\nEffect: Illusion Ancient Iksar (Any Slot/Can Equip, Casting Time: 2.0)\nWT: 0.3 Size: MEDIUM\nClass: ALL\nRace: ALL\nThe illusion effect makes you non-KOS to all iksars in the \"Field of Scale\" theme (Field of Scale, Kaesora, and Kurn's Stronghold).\nAlso:\nA number of Chronobines (varies)\nIksar Left Ribcage Bones\nExperience\nFaction with Tynoc, Herald of Scale\nNote: This task is no longer repeatable.Submitted by: OlivanRewards:\n- Bone Mask of the Ancient Iksar [item=77408]\n- Chronobine [item=76893]\n- Iksar Left Ribcage Bones [item=77407]\n[",
    },
