      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Time Limit:** 01:00:00\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nThis shared task (1-6 players) is the second in a series of three. It begins with Berrina Saltidnarik at location -650, 200, 37 in Brell's Rest.\nThis task has a one hour timer.\nYou say, 'Hail, Berrina Saltidnarik'\nBerrina Saltidnarik says 'Hello there, _____.  You look like you're a [visitor] to this realm.'\nYou say, 'Yep, I'm a visitor'\nBerrina Saltidnarik says 'Not all of us are here by choice.  Some who dwell in this realm are bound to it due to our devotion to Brell.  That is the position that I find myself in, for example.  Still, one does what one [can], no?'\nYou say, 'They do what they can'\nBerrina Saltidnarik says 'Even in the realm of a god, there is always work that can be done.  I pride myself on being a problem solver, personally.  I try to find and fix [problems] whenever someone comes to me with one.'\nYou say, 'Problems?'\nBerrina Saltidnarik says 'Well, the kobolds have been a bit restless recently.  I suppose we all have, but when they get restless, they tend to start fights.  While battle is one of our great pleasures here, their aggression is starting to be a real problem in our day-to-day life.  Would you be [willing] to contact their leader and try to find out what's going on?'\nYou say, 'I'd be willing'\nBerrina Saltidnarik says 'Their leader is named Graztuk, and he's normally found near their camp to the east.  Hopefully you can talk some sense into him.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Clash of the Kobolds'.\nThe direction to someone related to your current Task has been marked on your compass.\nBerrina is concerned about the unrest amongst the kobold clans to the west. Even the excitement of Brell's Arena is no longer enough to contain their thirst for conflict. They are leaving their camps and goading others into joining their fights, and that does not appear to be part of Brell's plan for his realm.\nFind out what is troubling the kobolds. Seek their leader, Graztuk, and parley with him.\n1. Speak with Graztuk 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nGraztuk [npc=34064] is located just outside Brell's Arena (eastern part of Brell's Rest). Location: -215, -580, 17.\nYou say, 'Hail, Graztuk'\nGraztuk says 'Rrrrrrrr... _____, you aren't here to [fight], are you?'\nYour task 'Clash of the Kobolds' has been updated.\nYou say, 'I'm here to fight!'\nGraztuk says 'Fighting is great.  It lets us work out anger and energy.  We love to fight, and especially with the gnolls!  They're not around [much] any more.'\nYou say, 'Much more?'\nGraztuk says 'Some of them will fight, but not as many as there were before.  We don't know why.  We try to [start] fights with others, but they never want to fight.'\nYou say, 'Start fights...?'\nGraztuk says 'The Burynai don't like to fight us!  They never counterattack.  Some of the gnomes and dwarfs will fight, but I don't know how to tell if they will fight or not.  If only there were a way to find some [volunteers] for my best fighters to spar with, we could stop bothering others.''\nYou say, 'I have some volunteers'\nGraztuk says 'You volunteer?  This is great!  I'll have Recloso meet you on the battlefield to the north of us, near the lava.'\nSpeak with Recloso 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nTask Window Says: The kobolds have agreed to reign in their patrols, but only if you are willing to provide them with their entertainment! Meet Recloso near the lava lake.\nHead a little ways northwest, by the edge of the lava. Approximate location -70, -275, -8. You'll see four totems and a kobold named Recloso [npc=34065].\nYou say, 'Hail, Recloso'\nRecloso says 'Were you [sent] by Graztuk?'\nYour task 'Clash of the Kobolds' has been updated.\n2. Kill 5 raging kobolds 0/5 (Brell's Rest)\nYou say, 'Graztuk sent me'\nRecloso says 'Good.  I have some kobolds here who are aching for a good fight.  Let me know when you are ready to join the [battle], or if you want me to explain the [rules].'\nYou say, 'Tell me the rules'\nRecloso says 'The rules are simple.  Stay in the ring and fight.  If you leave the ring, you lose.  If you all die, you lose.  If you wait too long to fight, you lose.  Stay in the ring and defeat all of your opponents to win.'\nYou say, 'Ready for battle'\nRecloso says 'Round 1 begins.  Fight well!'\nFive raging kobolds spawn. They each hit for a max ~5,000, so you'll have your hands full. Some are mezzable.\na raging kobold champion says 'A fight!  A fight!'\na raging kobold champion says 'A fight!  A fight!'\nStay within the totems while fighting, otherwise you'll see this:\nYou have left the bounds of the ring.  Return quickly or be disqualified.\nRecloso says '_____ has left the bounds of the ring and must return quickly.'\n...And the task will fail.\nUpon killing the last of the five kobolds:\nRecloso says 'Round 1 complete!  Let me know when you are [ready] to continue, or if you want the [rules] explained again.'\n3. Kill 5 raging kobolds 0/5 (Brell's Rest)\nSaying \"Ready\" spawns the second wave.\nRecloso says 'Round 2 begins.  Fight well!'\nUpon completion:\nRecloso says 'Impressive.  Round 2 is complete.  Inform me when you are [ready] to continue.'\n4. Kill 5 raging kobolds 0/5 (Brell's Rest)\nSaying \"Ready\" spawns the third wave.\nRecloso says 'Round 3 begins.  Fight well!'\nUpon completion:\nRecloso says 'Round 3 is complete. Let me know when you are [ready] for the final battle.'\nYou say, 'Ready'\nRecloso says 'Round 4 begins.  Fight well!'\nRecloso says 'You're a match for my kin, but how about me?'\n5. Kill 2 raging kobolds 0/2 (Brell's Rest)\n5. Kill Recloso 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nTwo raging kobolds as well as Recloso attack. Recloso isn't much more difficult than the rest of the waves, but he AE rampages.\nRecloso has been slain by _____!\nRecloso's corpse says 'Finally, a worthy opponent...'\nYour task 'Clash of the Kobolds' has been updated.\nSpeak with Graztuk 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Graztuk'\nGraztuk says 'It seems you have more fight than even we could handle.  I'm sure my brethren will desire a rematch at some point in the future.'\nYour task 'Clash of the Kobolds' has been updated.\nThe kobolds appear to be more bloodthirsty because their normal sparring partners, the gnolls, are not as interested in fighting.  Perhaps the ultimate answer lies with them.\n157 platinum, 5 gold\nYou gain experience!Rewards:\n[",
