      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Time Limit:** 06:00:00\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nThis group task begins with Algera Chindlebolt at location -675, 265, 52 in Brell's Rest (by the zone-in from The Hole). In order to request this task you must first have completed Berrina's three tasks.\nYou say, 'Hail, Algera Chindlebolt'\nAlgera Chindlebolt says 'You there! By what unnatural means have you come to Brell's Rest? Oh, I suppose it matters not. The [threat] that is coming, after everything else that has happened lately around here, it cannot be the fault of adventurers like you.'\nYou say, 'What threat?'\nAlgera Chindlebolt says 'You may have heard talk of something called The Destroyer since you came to Brell's Rest. I assure you, it is real, though the dwarves and gnomes have been confounded in our attempts to learn more about it. The gnolls know of this menace, and though some of them are concerned, others seem to be supporting it with magical means. This must [stop] at once. While Brell does not appear to be present to exert his will in this place of eternal rest, its residents appear to be free to act as they will, possibly with deadly effects on what we thought were our everlasting spirits.'\nYou say, 'Yes, it must stop'\nAlgera Chindlebolt says '[Dealing] with gnolls has always been a slippery proposition, even when I was a mortal. Getting them to cease and desist from unwise or unsavory behavior is one of the more futile things one can hope to do. With so many things in Brell's Rest spinning out of their proper order, the last thing we need is a gigantic monster on the loose, much less one that is aided and boosted by a band of death-worshipping gnolls, beloved of Brell though they may be.'\nYou say, 'Dealing with the gnolls?'\nAlgera Chindlebolt says 'Loathe I am to say these words in this sacred place, but it may require violence to thwart the plans of these gnolls. Even then, this Destroyer monster may not be stopped, but his further growth prevented. This cannot happen unless we know which gnolls are actually up to no good. If we harm innocents here and cause Brell to have to retrieve them from oblivion, we will be cast out. If you will, please form a party of inquiry into this matter, and [investigate].'\nYou say, 'I'll investigate'\nAlgera Chindlebolt says 'The gnoll most open to talking about what the gnolls are up to is Shorf the Shaman. He is the one most willing to part with information regarding the Destroyer. Go to Shady Nook and let him be the beginning of your quest. Tell me when you are [ready] to be attuned to his presence, and I shall aid you in locating him.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Don't Fear the Destroyer'.\nAlgera Chindlebolt is now aware of the existence of the Destroyer, whoever that is, and now believe that the gnolls are taking advantage of the arrival of this 'Destroyer' for the advancement of their own agenda. Seek them out and decide whether or not they are a threat to the general order of things, and learn anything you can about this 'Destroyer'.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nAlgera Chindlebolt says 'May Brell watch over you and keep you safe.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Brell's Rest - Don't Fear the Destroyer.\nLocate Shorf the Shaman at the Shady Nook in the southwestern edge of Brell's Rest 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nShorf is located in the western part of Brell's Rest (midway through the valley that leads to Pellucid Grotto).\nSpeak with Short the Shaman about the Destroyer 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Shorf the Shaman'\nShorf the Shaman says 'Yes, the Destroyer. You seek the Destroyer? Why? Destroyer rearrange Brell's Rest soon, they say. Make it more to some gnolls' liking, they say. Maybe you learn more from Zakarf.'\nYour task 'Don't Fear the Destroyer' has been updated.\nSpeak with Zakarf the Assassin regarding the Destroyer's whereabouts 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nZakarf stands next to Shorf. Be ready for a fight.\nYou say, 'Hail, Zakarf the Assassin'\nZakarf the Assassin says 'So you think to ply me for talk about the Destroyer? Forget it! You die now! I kill you, and when you dead, you not remember anything, like me telling you where Groth'roth has secret meetings in Watery Nook! After I kill you, maybe I kill that Garrhuff Gabblepaws too!'\nZakarf the Assassin pounces!\nZakarf hits for a max ~6,500.\nKill Zakarf the Assassin 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nZakarf the Assassin has been slain by _____!\nZakarf the Assassin's corpse falls in defeat.\nYour faction standing with Underfoot Autarchs got worse.\nYour faction standing with Underfoot Citizens got better.\nYour task 'Don't Fear the Destroyer' has been updated.\nLook for Grothroth's hideout in Watery Nook, in the southeastern side of Brell's Rest 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nGrothroth and company are found at the waterfall in the eastern valley of Brell's Rest (leads to the Underquarry). Be advised the gnolls around him are KOS.\nSpeak with Grothroth, leader of the Destroyer-worshipper group 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Grothroth'\nGrothroth says 'Grothroth smash you up but good! You no ask about Destroyer. Destroyer soon will get even with you and your ilk! You push him around, slay him too often! You dare not know Destroyer? You sound like Garrhuff. He not know meaning of Destroyer either! I hammer you both in your stupid faces with angry fists!!'\nYour task 'Don't Fear the Destroyer' has been updated.\na gnoll henchman pounces!\nGrothroth pounces!\nThis opens up the next steps:\nKill the gnoll henchmen 0/4 (Brell's Rest)\nKill the gnoll reavers 0/4 (Brell's Rest)\nGrothroth's cult appears to be centered around the Priests of Undeath. Kill them! 0/3 (Brell's Rest)\nTake the Badges of the Destroyer from the dead Priests of Undeath 0/3 (Brell's Rest)\nGrothroth will not allow himself to be taken prisoner! 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nKilling all the gnolls around this area updates these steps. They hit for a max ~5,800 and can be split from one another (unknown if mez works). Be sure to loot the badges from the undead priests.\nGrothroth has been slain by _____!\nGrothroth's corpse falls in defeat.\nYour faction standing with Underfoot Autarchs got worse.\nYour faction standing with Underfoot Citizens got better.\nYour task 'Don't Fear the Destroyer' has been updated.\nGrothroth mentioned Garrhuff Gabblepaws. Bring him the Badges of the Destroyer 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nGarrhuff Gabblepaws is located a little ways west of the area where you zoned in. Hand him the three badges.\nSpeak with Garrhuff Gabblepaws about the Badges of the Destroyer 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Garrhuff Gabblepaws'\nGarrhuff Gabblepaws says 'Destroyer is a gnoll. A crazy, crazy gnoll. I not know why he so crazy, but he crazy-mad and big, too. He wreck Brell's Rest, given chance. You maybe not strong enough to scratch him. He destroy every dimbulb sword-swinger that went to find him. He destroy you, too. That why he called Destroyer. He destroy things. Uh oh, more bad gnolls come to rough me up, make me worship Destroyer!'\nYour task 'Don't Fear the Destroyer' has been updated.\nThis triggers an ambush and opens up the next four steps:\nKill the gnoll reaver ambushers! 0/4 (Brell's Rest)\nKill the gnoll gutpiercer ambushers! 0/4 (Brell's Rest)\nKill Reufhof the Conspirator! 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nKill Vark the Conspirator! 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nYou'll have 10 gnolls in total, each hitting for a max ~6,000 (the two named hit for ~7,500). Once their initial aggro is dropped, they'll go back to their spawnpoints and can be split from one another.\nSpeak with Urkbark. Try and learn what he knows of The Destroyer 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nYou say, 'Hail, Urkbark Pinchpaw'\nUrkbark Pinchpaw says 'Grr! You scum not belong here! Only true gnolls who know of Destroyer belong here! You see! You learn of Destroyer soon enough; he happy to pick his fangs with your bones!'\nUrkbark Pinchpaw pounces!\nUrkbark hits for a max ~9,400.\nKill Urkbark before he can warn The Destroyer 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nHail Algera Chindlebolt, so that she can return you to the 'normal' plane of Brell's Rest 0/1 (Brell's Rest)\nNOTE: The task locks at the time you hail Algera.)\nYou say, 'Hail, Algera Chindlebolt'\nAlgera Chindlebolt says 'There is not much I can do to repay you in a way that you would be accustomed to, except perhaps to give you this. I really wish I could do more; the information you have gained in battle will at least help us prepare for whatever the Destroyer really is. I suppose it could be an oversized gnoll, but that would be too unimaginative; every race projects their collective ego in such a fantastical way at least once in their history.'\nA simple chest spawns with loot (1 item per task). Known drops:\nCharger Backup Sword\nChoxar Bauble\nFlamepaw's Soothing Basher\nGolden Mask of Champion Oricx\nGreken Goldstone\nNeppigrim's Longcutter\nRomix Ringlet\nSignet of Earthen Devotion\nSoothsayer's Eye\nSteam Sublimated Death Stone\nRewards (everyone in task):\n175 platinum\nExperience (1.1 AAs)\nSome (not all) classes also receive a spell for completion of this mission:\nBard - You'll get nothing and like it!\nBeastlord - Spell: Friendly Pet\nBerserker - You'll get nothing and like it!\nCleric - You'll get nothing and like it!\nDruid - Spell: Blast of Hypergrowth\nEnchanter - Spell: Chaotic Befuddling\nMagician - You'll get nothing and like it!\nMonk - You'll get nothing and like it!\nNecromancer - You'll get nothing and like it!\nPaladin - Tome of Honorific Mantle\nRanger - You'll get nothing and like it!\nRogue - You'll get nothing and like it!\nShadowknight - You'll get nothing and like it!\nShaman - Spell: Healing Counterbias\nWarrior - You'll get nothing and like it!\nWizard - Spell: Crystallizing Circle\nYou say, 'Hail, Algera Chindlebolt'\nAlgera Chindlebolt says 'If you would like to [leave], just let me know.'\nYou say, 'Let me leave...'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Brell's Rest.Rewards:\n- Spell: Blast of Hypergrowth [item=88102]\n- Spell: Chaotic Befuddling [item=85847]\n- Spell: Crystallizing Circle [item=85879]\n- Spell: Friendly Pet [item=85884]\n- Spell: Healing Counterbias [item=85890]\n- Tome of Honorific Mantle [item=88111]\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "4936",
      title = "Unrest in the Metal Mines",
      exp = "16",
      exp_name = "Underfoot",
      min_lvl = 85,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = -15.0, x = 150.0, z = -193.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Clontik Beardburner",
        "Moved?!",
        "Why do you fear this?",
        "How could I help?",
        "The metal mines?",
        "I could see about having them restored",
        "moved",
        "fear",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 88944, name = "Brellium Token", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis solo task begins with Clontik Beardburner who is located in the zone-in area of the Underquarry (location -15, 150, -193).\nYou say, 'Hail, Clontik Beardburner'\nClontik Beardburner says 'Eh? Who are you? You don't belong here! Well, seeing as how there are so few of us left still devoted to carrying out the will of Brell Serilis, it would only harm our cause to waste effort having you [moved] from this place.'\nYou say, 'Moved?!'\nClontik Beardburner says 'This is the Underquarry; we mine and quarry material here, endlessly. Stone, precious metals, marble, you name it. At the moment, however, things are in a disastrous state. My stone-mining crews are being insubordinate, the Burynai are claiming the copper mine for themselves, there are Cliknar invading the silver mine, and everyone I've sent to the gold mines has yet to return. I [fear] the entire Underquarry may spin completely out of control soon, and if our production isn't corrected, there will be terrible ramifications for the entire Underfoot and all the worlds that connect to it.'\nYou say, 'Why do you fear this?'\nClontik Beardburner says 'So much depends on me, but ever since the influence of this Church of Self began to be a problem, more and more of my Underquarry crew have failed to follow my orders! Being assigned to the Underquarry is the highest of honors a Dwarf or even a Gnome could ever hope to achieve!  Why would one risk losing the favor of Brell by abandoning one's sacred duties? Yet that is precisely what has happened. I, and these few who remain here, are all that are left who remain dedicated in service to Brell. Yet it is strange, Brell no longer appears, or has not been seen or heard from in a very long time. I may need your [help] if we are to restore the Underquarry to its proper functioning.'\nYou say, 'How could I help?'\nClontik Beardburner says 'Much to do, much to do. Your help would genuinely be appreciated. I will need help with restoring order in the [Stonequarry] as well as in the [Metal Mines]. When you have completed these tasks I have [other work] I need completed.'\nYou say, 'The metal mines?'\nClontik Beardburner says 'I have lost so many guildsmen of late in the Metal Mines alone it is enough to make me thirst for a soothing ale again. I can send no more of my own dwarves and gnomes down there; so few are left, we need them to endure if the Underquarry is to be [restored].'\nYou say, 'I could see about having them restored'\nClontik Beardburner says 'You will go in their stead? What a noble creature you are. When Brell returns, I will be sure to mention your name to him in a most favorable light. Go into each of the metal mines in the Underquarry. You will need to seek out the leader of each of the groups occupying each of the mines, and eliminate them.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Unrest in the Metal Mines'.\nBrell's absence has turned the Underquarry upside down. The golems and burynai are in revolt, and the cliknar have been persuaded to tear the silver mines from Brell's grasp. Go to each of the three metal mines of the Underquarry and put an end to any insubordination taking place there.\nThe copper mines have become a nest of Burynai rebels. Go there and stop their leader from turning the Burynai even further against the Way of Brell. Cliknar have burrowed into the silver mine and are definitely up to no good. Go there and eliminate their Protauris so that their activities will be slowed. Most of the remaining golems have found their way into the Underquarry's gold mines, and they too are refusing to follow the tasks which gave them purpose. Destroy the leader of the golems and stop them from abandoning their purpose.\n- 1. Investigate the rebel presence in the Underquarry Copper Mine 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n- 2. Kill the rebellious Burynai leader, Lord Ragarrh 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n- 3. Go to the Silver Mine and locate the rebel leader there 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n- 4. Destroy the cliknar leader, known as the 'Protauris' 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n- 5. Explore the Underquarry Gold Mine and learn which golem is leading the insurrection there 0/1 (The Underquarry)\n- 6. Eliminate the rebellious golem known as Keolyx 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nLocations for map file:\nP 765.0728, -187.5706, -199.1053,  0, 0, 0,  1,  copper_mine\nP 605.1702, 445.2426, -431.2084,  0, 0, 0,  1,  silver_mine\nP 176.7785, 711.2474, -368.3794,  0, 0, 0,  1,  gold_mine\nP 1373.1821, 248.6674, -313.4822,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Lord_Ragarrh\nP 672.2256, 658.0920, -541.6625,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Protauris\nP 779.4237, 590.4119, -634.2004,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Keolyx\nCopper mines are due east from the zone-in area (the burynai caves). Lord Ragarrh is in the southeasternmost cave.\nTo get to the silver mines, go to the large room with the giant stone genari and head into the tunnels from the eastern wall of this room. These are the cliknar caves. Towards the bottom/back of these tunnels are three identical looking open caves. Protauris is in the northwestern one.\nTo get to the gold mines, go to the large room with the giant stone genari and head into the tunnels from the southern wall of this room. These are the golem caves. All the way at the very bottom is Keolyx.\n- 7. Report back to Clontik and tell him the rebel leaders have been dealt with 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nYou say, 'Hail, Clontik Beardburner'\nClontik Beardburner stares at his boots. \"There are better things I'd like to be doing than sending people to kill the creatures of Brell in the metal mines, but I must do what I can to preserve this sacred place, this eternal Underquarry.\"\n175 platinum\nExperience (about 1.5 AAs at Level 85)\n~17 Brellium TokensRewards:\n- Brellium Token [item=88944]\n[",
