      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis solo task begins with Clontik Beardburner who is located in the zone-in area of the Underquarry (location -15, 150, -193).\nIn order to request this task, you must first have completed two of Clontik's other solo tasks: \"Chaos in the Stonequarry\" and \"Unrest in the Metal Mines\".\nYou say, 'Hail, Clontik Beardburner'\nClontik Beardburner says 'Much to do. Much to do. Your help would genuinely be appreciated. I will need help with restoring order in the [Stonequarry] as well as in the [Metal Mines]. When you have completed these tasks I have [other work] I need completed.'\nYou say, 'Other work?'\nClontik Beardburner says 'There are some follow-up tasks to be performed now that I have been getting feedback from the rest of the Underquarry. My plan for restoring order has [failed]. The Underquarry is producing quantities of stone and metal that just aren't needed, and we will have to find a [solution] somehow.'\nYou say, 'Failed?'\nClontik Beardburner says 'Yes, the elimination of the corrupted managers and workers in the Underquarry has done nothing to restore harmony with Brell's vision among the workforce. We must dig [deeper] if I am to know what to do.'\nYou say, 'Deeper?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'An Alternative Explanation'.\nLook for Reggund Tilecracker in the northern stonequarry room, deep in the Underquarry 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nThis step updates at -31, -66, -363 (In the large quarry room -- entered through a tunnel leading out of the genari/Goralf room with the pit. He is in the northern part of this room.)\nReggund Tilecracker supposedly has a different approach to the situation in the Underquarry 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nThere are many see invis genati around here. Hail Reggund for the update (+417, +40, -334).\nYou say, 'Hail, Reggund Tilecracker'\nReggund Tilecracker says 'Ahh. Clontik finally seeks out my assistance, when all else fails. Killing won't suffice to put the Underquarry back on track, my friend. Not now. Perhaps you'd like the key to resolving this breakdown of order?'\nHear more of Reggund's ideas 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nYou say, 'Hail, Reggund Tilecracker'\nReggund Tilecracker says 'The creatures here in the Underquarry aren't concerned with their work any longer. They still do their work, but at their own pace and on their own schedule, which no doubt infuriates Clontik to no end. For thousands of years he has been set by Brell to manage the Underquarry and never had a problem until now. Further, this problem cannot be solved the way he is now going about it. For him to understand how to get what he wants, he will need to understand what now motivates his workers. To do that, you will have to help him acquire copies of their recent communications.'\nMemorize the details of Reggund's plan for the Clontik's benefit 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nYou say, 'Hail, Reggund Tilecracker'\nReggund Tilecracker says 'Unfortunately, though we all abhor killing in the Underfoot, the creatures here guard their possessions most jealously. You will no doubt have to slay the creatures to get their secret communications. Every group of creatures I've mentioned has a unique method of relaying information. The burynai plotters use a drumlike cylinder called an Archtone Wheelstick; the cliknar sergeants receive Command-Flavor Hivejelly which tells them what is expected of them; and the Iron Golems have been seen accepting some sort of golden crystals from the golden golems of late. Bring one of each of these items to Clontik, those may give him a better idea of how to solve his dilemma.'\nThis opens up the next three steps:\nA Golemite Sagecrystal of Emergent Awareness may be of use to Clontik 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nGo and find a vial of Cliknar command jelly... The Cliknar commander might be an obvious source 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nCollect several Archtone wheelstick message devices from the Burynai 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nA Golemite Sagecrystal of Emergent Awareness is dropped by an iron golem (usually only found deep in the southern tunnels, located around /way -482, -410, -607 and /way -526, -387, -589).\nThe Vial of Protaurian Command-Flavor Hivejelly is dropped by a cliknar sergeant (found among the cliknar in the east tunnels).\nThe Archtone Wheelstick is dropped by burynai plotters and mineblades.\nThese three items have been reported to be pre-lootable (hand to any NPC and hit cancel).\nDeliver the Golemite Sagecrystal of Emergent Awareness to Clontik 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nDeliver the vial of Cliknar command jelly to Clontik 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nDeliver the Archtone wheelstick message device to Clontik 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nSpeak with Clontik Beardburner 0/1 (The Underquarry)\nYou say, 'Hail, Clontik Beardburner'\nClontik Beardburner shakes his head. \"So it's more than just obstinacy and unwillingness to follow my orders in Brell's absence. Examining the information these items contain, it's clear that these creatures have all been convinced that their lives have special meaning, that their purpose requires their own input and acquiescence. Individuality has been given to them. Once given, it cannot be taken away. I fear the Underquarry may have been changed forever; Brell may never get it back the way it once was.\"\n210 platinum\nExperience (2.2 AAs at Level 85)\n20 Brellium Tokens\nThe task \"Overheated Production\" opens up after completing this task.Rewards:\n- Brellium Token [item=88944]\n[",
