      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Time Limit:** 06:00:00\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nThis group mission (3-6 players) begins with Darott in the Foundation. He is located far north of the zone-in, outside the burynai caves.\nIn order to request this mission, you must have completed Trullica's three solo tasks.\nYou say, 'Hail, Darott'\nDarott says 'Hey, you. You help Adherent burynai like me, yes? We grateful. You do us another favor, we do something [nice] for you.'\nYou say, 'Something nice?'\nDarott says 'You know Saunk? Young shaman, very powerful. He even more powerful now. We are [worried] about him, what he will do now.'\nYou say, 'Worried?'\nDarott says 'Saunk a good friend, Saunk fight bad ones who follow bad ways. Saunk also fight cliknar. But Saunk [learn] bad things from cliknar.'\nYou say, 'What did he learn?'\nDarott says 'Saunk find out what cliknar ants are up to, he eat their jelly-words and know their thoughts. Secret things only cliknar know, Saunk learned. They after the sacred Clay. They take Clay of Cosgrove, they do things to it to make their Queen smarter and stronger, then feed it to her. Saunk learn how to do this too. He [change] himself.'\nYou say, 'How did he change?'\nDarott says 'Saunk make cliknar formula for himself, give himself many magic powers. Too many, if you ask me, if you ask Greph. He use powers to kill enemies attacking us. Then he use powers to kill enemies not attacking us. Then he use powers on rival burynai, then on his friends. Saunk lose mind, Saunk [betray] himself and other burynai.'\nYou say, 'How did he betray you?'\nDarott says 'Saunk decide we all no more than bugs to him, he go somewhere else and make another Foundation where he most important person. Here where Darott need favor. Darott have enough power to find Saunk in place where he went. But Saunk not trust Darott anymore, and Darott not strong enough to defeat Saunk or stop Saunk from sending me back here to real Foundation. Darott stay in not-real Foundation long enough to see another Darott there, a shade of real Darott which is me, but is also not-me. He like me enough to help you know what to do when I [send] you there, which I hope is really soon, before Saunk's power grow to large and mighty and he finally decide to become a god and destroy us all.'\nYou say, 'Send me there'\nDarott says 'I will use magic, I will send you to Saunk's not-real-Foundation place. Hold still, tell Darott when [ready]!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Search for Saunk'.\nDarott the Adherent is sending you to the pocket-dimension his former friend Saunk has created for himself. You must find him and destroy him if necessary to keep him from becoming even more powerful!\nSpeak with the Shade of Darott, once you have been ported into Saunk's demi-plane. The Shade will tell you how to get Saunk to appear.\nSay \"ready\" to zone into an instanced version of the Foundation. No mobs are in aggro range of the zone-in point.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nDarott says 'Okay, your skin start tingling, and soon you go 'whoosh' into not-real-Foundation. Say hello to Saunk, if you can get him to talk and be nice again.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Foundation.\nSpeak with the Shade of Darott; find out how to find the real Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nYou say, 'Hail, Shade of Darott'\nShade of Darott says 'I am glad you came here. I am the Shade of Darott. I suspect I truly exist not. Here in this place, this mirror-image of Foundation, Saunk reigns supreme. See around you the other Shades -- copies of creatures Saunk knew or remembered from his days in the real Foundation. They act like the real thing, but they, like everything else here, are but figments of Saunk's imagination. You not find Saunk as he meditating, gather power for the next step towards godhood! He impatient with visitors even if he know you're here, send avatars to kill you or drive you away. If you destroy enough of his shades, maybe he take notice. Destroy shades of adherents, autarchians, cliknar, and bellikos, that enough to make him mad.'\nKill the Shades of Burynai; they aren't real 0/24 (The Foundation)\nBurynai Adherents are found throughout the zone-in area and at the clay production area of the regular Foundation zone, while Autarchians are found in the eastern half of the zone in camps of 3-4. There is a total of 24 spawns in the zone.\nKill the Shades of Bellikos Emissaries; they aren't real 0/3 (The Foundation)\nTwo bellikos are found in the autarchian camps. A third bellikos is found in the easternmost part of the zone.\nKill the Shades of Cliknar Warriors; they aren't real 0/24 (The Foundation)\nThe cliknar are located in the western caves.\nTell the Shade of Darott the false citizens of the unreal Foundation are now gone 0/1 (The Foundation)\nYou say, 'Hail, Shade of Darott'\nInsignificant beings. How dare you disturb my menagerie! This place was to be my refuge, my playground, where I would repose until I learned what to do with my former brethren. As for you, you do not even belong in Underfoot at all, I shall test your mortal resilience with destructive force!\nShade of Darott says 'Yes, you done it now. Darott sense rumbling in not-real-Foundation, Saunk now awake and alert, wonder what happening. You face first avatar of Saunk now. Be careful. They powerful.'\nYour task 'The Search for Saunk' has been updated.\nFrom here on, you'll have to defeat seven versions of Saunk, each one more difficult than the previous. You'll have time to med between fights as each spawns in a different location in the zone.\nNamed locations:\n- First Avatar: +502 -9 (northern boundary of the eastern half of the zone)\n- Second Avatar: -53, 97 (central area of the eastern half of the zone)\n- Third Avatar: -555, 255 (southern boundary of the eastern half of the zone)\n- Fourth Avatar: -130, 1015 (central area north of the Underquarry zone)\n- Fifth Avatar: 100, 1190 (northern half of the western half of the zone)\n- Saunk the Shaman: -200, 1800 (near zone-in)\n- Genati of Saunk: Very close to -200, 1800 (zone-in area)\nLocations for map file:\nP 10.2464, -495.8269, -150.4684,  0, 0, 0,  1,  First\nP -93.8467, 46.4823, -133.0777,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Second\nP -253.4342, 555.2084, -142.7878,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Third\nP -1013.9325, 121.0205, -145.4890,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Fourth\nP -1196.7479, -106.1445, -201.9860,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Fifth\nP -1854.3297, 242.6473, -210.0227,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Saunk_the_Shaman\nP -2101.0005, 322.1855, -210.1438,  0, 0, 0,  1,  Genati_of_Saunk\nThe first named hits for ~5,500. They escalate in strength up to the final named which hits for a max ~8,500, casts a self-buff and silence:\nGenati of Saunk has a self-buff and a silence:\nResolve of the Genata: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Absorb Damage by 250000\n2: Increase Hitpoints by 2500\nBrazen Hammerblow: Single Target, Magic (-600)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 3600\n2: Unknown #380 (100/2/0)\n3: Add Effect: Brazen Hammerblow Stunned Silence\nSpeak to the First Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nFirst Avatar of Saunk says 'You think to test my fighting spirit, my stamina? I assure you, this is a mistake.'\nDestroy the First Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nFirst Avatar of Saunk has been slain by _____!\nSo you are indeed powerful, and not to be trifled with. So be it. I have many avatars. These are made from the former bodies of my friends, whose minds I destroyed and replaced with copies of my own will. I am so much more now than I was. You can't even grasp the experience of amassing so much power and growth in so short a time. I have increased my intellect a thousand-fold from only a few days ago, when I was barely smarter than the average burynai! Now I and my avatars stand on the brink of godhood!\nSpeak to the Second Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nSecond Avatar of Saunk says 'Destruction is your only reward, you have chosen a poor opponent if you were expecting anything else!'\nDestroy the Second Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nSecond Avatar of Saunk has been slain by _____!\nYou destroy my avatars so casually, not realizing that they grow stronger! There is only one outcome to this contest, and it shall be your end. I, Saunk, shall prevail and rise to godhood, the first everlasting burynai god!\nSpeak to the Third Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nThird Avatar of Saunk says 'I am no longer burynai, but a god. I am multiple beings, and yet one. My power grows with each passing second!'\nDestroy the Third Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nThird Avatar of Saunk has been slain by _____!\nPerhaps you persist in killing my avatars to learn more about how I achieved this incredible power, and escaped the fetters of my mortal burynai existence. Perhaps you are merely foolish, and have extended your reach far beyond your grasp. The secrets of power are locked within the Clay of Cosgrove, which the cliknar have succeeded in discovering, within days of the disappearance of Brell Serilis. Their thinker, Qeyn, was considering the recipe for the extract. I simply intercepted it. It was astonishingly easy to make. Alas, you will die before you learn the secret yourself. A god tolerates little in the way of competition!\nSpeak to the Fourth Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nFourth Avatar of Saunk says 'The secret of the cliknar has given me strength, soon I will re-order your world! I shall rule the planes! Soon enough, there will be nothing I cannot do!'\nDestroy the Fourth Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nFourth Avatar of Saunk has been slain by _____!\nPitiful. You cannot destroy me! Avatars may fall, but my essence is imbued into the very reality here, all around you. I am godlike, and you are not. Dare you tear down my works, my greatest avatars? After I have defeated you, I shall alter you, and make you my pets!\nSpeak to the Fifth Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nFifth Avatar of Saunk says 'You are too troublesome to tolerate any longer. The destruction of my avatars is an inconvenience, yes, and now an irritation as well.'\nDestroy the Fifth Avatar of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nFifth Avatar of Saunk has been slain by _____!\nYour task 'The Search for Saunk' has been updated.\nFine. Destroy my avatars. Break my concentration. I will have no choice but to meditate on the next stage of my escalating godhood later.\nSpeak to Saunk the Shaman 0/1 (The Foundation)\nSaunk the Shaman says 'You are the stem, and I am the razor. Fall on your knees and worship me, or meet your peril!'\nKill Saunk the Shaman 0/1 (The Foundation)\nSaunk the Shaman has been slain by _____!\nYour faction standing with Underfoot Autarchs got worse.\nYour faction standing with Underfoot Citizens got better.\nWHAT HAVE YOU DONE! You've destroyed my original body! I shall have vengeance! You've trapped my consciousness inside my last avatar, the body of a genari! I will destroy you utterly for this outrage!\nGenati of Saunk spawns nearby. Although you've made him quite angry, he doesn't attack. You can still med here if needed prior to engaging.\nKill Genati of Saunk 0/1 (The Foundation)\nGenati of Saunk has been slain by _____!\nYour task 'The Search for Saunk' has been updated.\nYour shared task is now locked.  You may no longer add or remove players.\nSpeak to the Shade of Darott to return to the real Foundation 0/1 (The Foundation)\nYou say, 'Hail, Shade of Darott'\nShade of Darott says 'You defeat Saunk? You truly powerful! Saunk gone, this place crumble soon, it not stay solid without Saunk's power. You tell real-Darott I say 'goodbye'. Here, I send back to real-Foundation now.'\nYour task 'The Search for Saunk' has been updated.\nYou have succeeded in killing Saunk the Shaman before he could become truly godlike. In doing so, you have saved Underfoot and probably Norrath as well.\nYou can hail him again to zone out (note: there is a roaming genati who sometimes wanders into aggro range of the zone-out point).\nA chest spawns with loot (1 item per task). Known drops:\nDoll Smasher\nGenari Tibia\nGolden Ore\nGrekenplate Shield\nIsopexine Swiftbow\nLuminous Seeding Gem\nMany-Pocketed Pouch\nMorose Puncher\nRazorjaw Fang\nSpong's Digging Tool\nVine-Crested Shoulderpads\nRewards (everyone in task):\n20-30 Brellium Tokens\n105 platinum\nExperience (1.1 AAs at Level 85)\nSome (not all) classes also receive a spell for completion of this mission:\nBard - You'll get nothing and like it!\nBeastlord - You'll get nothing and like it!\nBerserker - Tome of Axe of Rallos\nCleric - You'll get nothing and like it!\nDruid - Spell: Sundew Blessing\nEnchanter - You'll get nothing and like it!\nMagician - You'll get nothing and like it!\nMonk - Tome of Flinch\nNecromancer - Spell: Necrotic Pustules\nPaladin - Spell: Glorious Vindication\nRanger - You'll get nothing and like it!\nRogue - Tome of Desperate Escape\nShadow Knight - You'll get nothing and like it!\nShaman - You'll get nothing and like it!\nWarrior - You'll get nothing and like it!\nWizard - Spell: Self-ImmolationRewards:\n- Brellium Token [item=88944]\n- Spell: Glorious Vindication [item=86770]\n- Spell: Necrotic Pustules [item=86921]\n- Spell: Self-Immolation [item=86601]\n- Spell: Sundew Blessing [item=86600]\n- Tome of Axe of Rallos [item=86816]\n- Tome of Desperate Escape [item=86705]\n- Tome of Flinch [item=86660]\n[",
