      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 90\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nThis shared task (1-6 players) begins with Inventor Biddlebokk in Lichen Creep. He is located at -395, 915, -16.\nTo request this task, you must first have completed his two prior tasks: \"The Grand Experiment\" and \"The Experiment Begins\".\nYou say, 'Hail, Inventor Biddlebokk'\nInventor Biddlebokk says 'Did you think I wouldn't be [busy]? With [Bub] drinking on the job, I have my hands full. Do you think you could bring me some [lichen] samples so I can finish my experiment?'\nYou say, 'Lichen samples?'\nInventor Biddlebokk says 'I will need a few samples of the lichen that the cliknar eat. They must be using some special enzymes to break it down. Could you [harvest] some of it for me?'\nYou say, 'I'll harvest some'\nInventor Biddlebokk says 'Thank you, _____!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'What Could Go Wrong?'.\nDeliver 10 Lichen Sample to Inventor Biddlebokk 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nThese drop from cliknar scouts and gatherers in Lichen Creep.\nInventor Biddlebokk says 'These samples are perfect! Now, to analyze all the components you have brought to me. Thereâ€™s one problem, though: My tools are missing. I was doing some research when a lava mephit cornered me and stole them. If you can, please find my tools so I can finish the experiment!'\nDeliver 1 Biddlebokk's Tools To Inventor Biddlebokk 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nThe tools drop from lava mephit workers and guards.\nInventor Biddlebokk says 'Ok, now that I have my tools, I should be able to create a mixture for the base of our new humanoid. Oh, this is so exciting! I hope nothing goes wrong. . . So far so good. . . Ok, the mixture has been created. Whew! Now you need to take the mixture to Falrorn Borlakio in the Shining City. I think heâ€™s in the same workshop as Halgin. He can create a mold of the new humanoidâ€™s form from the mixture.'\nDeliver 1 Undulating Mixture to Falrorn Borlakio 0/1 (Kernagir)\nThe locations of Falrorn and the other turn-in NPCs will be marked on your compass.\nFalrorn is at 115, 700, 54.\nFalrorn Borlakio says 'Oh, great. Another one of Biddlebokk's experiments? This should be good. You might want to stand back in case something happens. Let me just put this in the mold here. Here you go. I don't know what it is, but it's probably not what Biddlebokk envisioned. In fact, it appears to be highly toxic. I would give this to the Cleaner Bot over there to dispose of.'\nDeliver 1 Failed Experiment to Cleaner Bot 0/1 (Kernagir)\nThe Cleaner Bot is next to Falrorn (135, 715, 54).\nCleaner Bot says 'Highly toxic substance identified. Please stand back. Destroy mode initiated. Item has been destroyed. Here is your empty mold. Report to Bookkeeper Blanch for experiment failure protocol 8A processing. Thank you for using Cleaner Bot. Your efforts help keep the Shining City shiny and clean.'\nDeliver 1 Empty Mold to Bookkeeper Blanch 0/1 (Kernagir)\nBookkeeper Blanch says 'So Biddlebokk's creation experiment failed? Wow, what a surprise. That substance you had in the mold could have made the entire city sick. I guess I shouldn't have expected anything less from that daft inventor. Take this reprimand to Biddlebokk. I will let you off the hook, but don't go helping him with anymore of his so-called experiments.'\nDeliver 1 A Reprimand to Inventor Biddlebokk 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nI knew I couldn't do it! And now I have a reprimand! Oh, well, it's not the first I have received, and I am sure it won't be the last. It's too bad things didn't turn out as I had hoped. I was going to name the creation after you! Ah, well, maybe another time, eh? Thanks for all of your help. I should get ready to see Brell and receive my punishment. Maybe I will see you again, when I get out of prison. Take care, my friend!\n315 platinum\nExperience (3.3 AAs at Level 85)\n~60 Brellium Tokens\nCompletion of this task arc allows you to request the Lichen Creep group mission, \"Bonfire of the Adherents\".Rewards:\n- Brellium Token [item=88944]\n[",
