      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 90\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Time Limit:** 06:00:00\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nThis group mission begins with Gweddon Tinkertasker in Lichen Creep. He is located at -320, 145, -65 (northeastern part of the zone).\nIn order to request this task, you must first have completed Inventor Biddlebokk's three tasks.\nYou say, 'Hail, Gweddon Tinkertasker'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'Greetings, friend. Are you a friend? Or are you in league with those who are behind the recent unsavory [events] taking place in Underfoot?'\nYou say, 'Events?'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'The autarchians, they call themselves. Traitors to Brell Serilis they are! I and several of the others have held out against their strange teachings, but I fear we are no match for their sheer numbers here. Nearly all of the gnomes now subscribe to the Faith of Self and will wait no longer for Brell's voice to return to their ears. The autarchians have grown a great [cult], and strong it is among the mephits and lava creatures who watch over the sources of lodestone.'\nYou say, 'A great cult?'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'There is no telling where they will stop. They spread their insidious teachings to even the lava golems, the most trusting of creatures, and persecute those of us adherents who desire only to wait for Brell awhile longer. Then, some of our number were called by the mephit Zwurek deep within Lichen Creep, where mutiny has been simmering for many days. I have not heard from Fiddy, Duerg, or Neerda since! Will you please [help] me?'\nYou say, 'I can help'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'You must go deeper into Lichen Creep, and release each of the three missing Adherents by teleporting them to safety with a magic wand, when all of their captors have been eliminated. Only then will they be free of any magic wards that may restrain them. I do hope you can help; your presence here must be a [sign].'\nYou say, 'A sign of what?'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'A sign of Brell's return, of course. I despair we shall ever find my fellow Adherents alive, but if we do it will be thanks to the blessing of Brell Serilis, who shall return to us and reward us for our unshakable faith. Here, take the Metacrystalline Teleportation Wand, and head first to the Searing Prominence, where Fiddy is held. It is located just beyond where this stream meets the lava. Let me know when you are ready to [go].'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Bonfire of the Adherents'.\nAnyone in the zone with the task requester receives a Wand of Metacrystalline Teleportation. (Another Wand can be requested by saying \"sign\" again.)\nTo zone in:\nYou say, 'Ready to go!'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'Are you ready to depart?'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Lichen Creep - Bonfire of the Adherents.\nYou hear Gweddon shout in the distance, \"Don't forget, the wand's only tuned for rescuing my friends!\"\nExplore the disturbance at the Searing Prominence 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nKill Norket the Disgruntled and his minions 0/11 (Lichen Creep)\nNorket hits for a max ~8,000 while his minions are slightly less difficult.\nNorket the Disgruntled says 'Invaders have been spotted! Attack! For the Underfoot!!!'\nNorket the Disgruntled has been slain by _____!\nNorket the Disgruntled's corpse falls to the ground. \"Forgive me Brell, I have failed you!\"\nTask Window Says: Gweddon Tinkertasker, a loyal servant of Brell, is troubled that the mephits of Lichen Creep have been summoning the adherents of Brell to other parts of the Creep for reasons unknown. You must locate the adherents and ensure their safety.\nLook for Fiddy near the Searing Prominence, which is north of the Boiling Waterfall. You will need to kill the gnomish autarchian minions and their leader, Norket the Disgruntled. Their magic is preventing Fiddy from being rescued.\nUse the wand to rescue Fiddy 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nTask Window Says: Fiddy looks a little out of it. You'll have to rescue her with the teleporter wand.\nSpeak to Gweddon 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gweddon Tinkertasker'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'Yes! Fiddy magically appeared right next to me, no problem! Now, if you wouldn't mind locating Duerg Rockpiker. I think he might be held by the lava golems by the Peninfernal Lava Pool. Don't worry about its exact location; it should be west of the Boiling Waterfall, below the cliknar camp. Look for the overly-zealous lava golems.'\nExplore the Peninfernal Lava Pool 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nKill the lava golem zealots 0/10 (Lichen Creep)\nTask Window Says: Press on westward into the Lichen Creep and try to locate another adherent, Duerg, who is being held hostage by the magic of the zealous lava golems. The golems will need to be eliminated before you can free Duerg.\nUse the wand to rescue Duerg 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nSpeak to Gweddon 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nNote: The task locks upon hail.\nYou say, 'Hail, Gweddon Tinkertasker'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'Duerg also arrived unharmed! He and I both thank you very much! The last bit of rescuing you must do is to find Neerda Stoneguard. Duerg says that the lava mephits, led by Zwurek, plan to push him off a cliff into a lava pool if he doesn't join the autarchians! Zwurek and his troublemakers must be defeated; we can't allow them to cause any more trouble here in Lichen Creep. Save Neerda and bring me proof that you have killed his captors. They are camped at the Serrated Cliff, the edge of a basin where lava cascades into the lower pools of the Creep. Hurry!'\nExplore Zwurek's mephit camp along the Serrated Cliff 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nKill the lava mephit executioners 0/6 (Lichen Creep)\nKill Zwurek 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nThe lava mephit executioners hit for a max ~7,500 while Zwuerk hits for a max ~8,500 (he has ~1.4m hp). He also casts the spell \"Zwurek's Sputum\" with fair frequency:\nZwurek's Sputum: Targeted AE 35', Fire (-650)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 6500\nLoot six ceremonial blades from the executioners 0/6 (Lichen Creep)\nAutarchian Execution Blades are dropped by the mephit executioners surrounding Zwurek.\nUse the wand to rescue Neerda 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nTask Window Says: Poor Neerda is ready to pass out from the heat, it will never be a better time to use the wand!\nSpeak to Gweddon 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gweddon Tinkertasker'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'Goodness! You have saved all three of them from...well, whatever it is that happens after a person becomes an autarchian and falls from the grace of Brell Serilis!'\nGive the ceremonial blades to Gweddon 0/6 (Lichen Creep)\nReturn the metacrystalline teleportation wand to Gweddon 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'Thank you for returning the wand; I know you've put it to good use!'\nSpeak to Gweddon for further instructions 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gweddon Tinkertasker'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'I must now ask you to leave Lichen Creep for a while, my friend, and take this message to [Tronten] the Subnexus, our adherent ally in Pellucid Grotto. I need to inform him of what we have seen. And while you're doing that, I'll arrange for the safe passage of my friends to the Underquarry, where we have a few remaining allies! Please, go quickly!'\nYou receive \"Gweddon's Warning\".\nSay \"Tronten\" for a teleport straight to Tronten's location in Pellucid Grotto.\nDeliver Gweddon's warning message to Tronten the Subnexus 0/1 (Pellucid Grotto)\nTronten the Subnexus looks at you with his simmering crystal eyes. 'I thought these autarchians were mostly confined to the Pellucid Grotto and portions of the Underfoot under cliknar control. Now they have virtually conquered Lichen Creep! I can do little to repair the damage they have already done, but I can certainly aid [Gweddon] with this powerful orb. Take it to him; he can protect himself with it while the adherents regain their strength. Tell him he can count on our assistance soon!'\nYour task 'Bonfire of the Adherents' has been updated.\nYou say, 'Send me to Gweddon'\nTronten the Subnexus says 'Give my regards to Gweddon.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Lichen Creep.\nYou receive \"Tronten's Protocrystalline Orb\".\nDeliver Tronten's orb to Gweddon 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'Oh, very good! I knew Tronten would be a good enough ally to send me something of assistance! This orb looks as though I could use it to hide indefinitely from my persecutors!'\nSpeak to Gweddon 0/1 (Lichen Creep)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gweddon Tinkertasker'\nGweddon Tinkertasker says 'Thank you for all you have done. You have prevented our enemies from wiping us all out! Thanks to you, we will be able to wait until Brell returns and tell him what we have seen!'\nYour task 'Bonfire of the Adherents' has been updated.\nYou have prevented the Autarchians from completely wiping out the Adherents in Lichen Creep. Brell Serilis would be most pleased!\nA singed chest spawns with loot (1 item per task). Known drops:\nAncill's Hatchet\nAnvil Forged Axe\nDeathspike Spear\nHunter's Claw\nIncarnadine Gemstone\nMephit's Hoop of the Trickster\nPolished Rockomancy Diamond\nPurifying Pyrite Stone\nRuned Longsword\nSpiked War Maul\nStriped Agate of Devotion\nWorkmaster's Horn Fragment\nNote: The chest spawns outside the instance. You must be IN the task in order to loot anything from it.\nRewards (everyone in task):\n440 platinum\nExperience (about 4.4 AAs at Level 85)\n~160-180 Brellium Tokens\nSome (not all) classes also receive spell for completion of this mission:\nBard - none\nBeastlord - none\nBerserker - none\nCleric - none\nDruid - none\nEnchanter - none\nMagician - none\nMonk - none\nNecromancer - none\nPaladin - Spell: Protective Confession\nRanger - Spell: Focused Storm of Arrows\nRogue - none\nShadow Knight - none\nShaman - Spell:  Wind of Malis\nWarrior - Tome of Bracing Defense\nWizard - noneRewards:\n- Brellium Token [item=88944]\n- Spell: Focused Storm of Arrows [item=87105]\n- Spell: Protective Confession [item=86784]\n- Spell: Wind of Malis [item=87025]\n- Tome of Bracing Defense [item=87318]\n[",
