      rewards = {
        { id = 88944, name = "Brellium Token", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis solo task is the fifth in a series of five that begins with Gihbra Artinguard [npc=35069] in Volska's Husk. He is located at approximately -140, -165, -47. Be careful in this zone as there are no especially safe points, including the locations of task givers.\nIn order to request this task, you must first have completed Into the Fire [quest=5023], Uncover the Truth [quest=5024], Autochthonous Support [quest=5036], and The Arms of Brell [quest=5037].\nYou say, 'Hail, Gihbra Artinguard'\nGihbra Artinguard says 'Our plan to destabilize the husk is now fully in motion. Let us go [further].'\nYou say, 'Further?'\nGihbra Artinguard says 'Let's finish what we've started. Order in here is starting to break down, but we must still contend with one more leader. Interix Tanglefuze, by my estimation, is the chief Gnome in this husk. I'm sure if you [speak] with him you'll find a way to discredit him in the eyes of his followers.'\nYou say, 'I'll speak to him'\nGihbra Artinguard says 'Go with Brell's blessing, _____. Soon the Autarchians and the Bellikos will be crushed under Brell's fist, and his will shall reign once again in the Underfoot.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Brell's Will Be Done'.\n1. Interrogate Interix Tanglefuze 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nTask Window Says: Perhaps Interix Tanglefuze, leader of the Gnomes, has a weakness that can be exploited.\nInterix Tanglefuze [npc=35087] is found in the main Autarchian den at approximately -1115, 250, -95. Keyword for update is \"supplies\".\nYou say, 'Hail, Interix Tanglefuze'\nInterix Tanglefuze  looks you up and down and laughs. 'You're some kind of enchanter, aren't you? No, by the looks of you I'd say it's not your own enchantment. We normally wouldn't be talking; my clockworks would have beaten in your silly _____ face by now. But it's as if I feel the presence of Brell himself -- some sort of powerful persuasion spell. You think you're clever? You think you would even begin to comprehend the things I could reveal? Go ahead and ask me [questions]. Trying to understand my answers will be like Sessiloids studying the charts and motions of stars.'\nYou say, 'I have questions for you...'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'Yes, of course I am in charge. I'm the smartest. I know how the chain of supplies works in the husk; I know the fastest way to build the strongest clockworks; I know what everyone is doing and why they're doing it. I can see how everything fits together, from the bolts and gears in my clockworks, to the living cogs and widgets grinding away in these caverns. They think they're free, but someone else is always [turning] their crank.'\nYou say, 'Turning their crank?'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'The Bellikos aren't vacationing in the husk, admiring the sights of golems and Mephits and lava. There's only one reason why they're here: This is their labor camp. Don't you get it? The Sporali feed on the minerals in the hot springs; the Kobolds and the Gnolls bring us Sporali meat and serve as sentient -- or at least semi-sentient -- guards; the Dwarves mine the metals and minerals in the caverns; and the Gnomes craft war devices with those supplies. We're a Greken and clockwork factory here, building and growing the [weapons] with which to oppose Brell himself.'\nYou say, 'What weapons?'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'That's why I came here in the first place. Do you think a Gnome as smart as I would leave Kernagir for any other reason than crazy, wild, dangerous ambition? I want to build the most deadly clockworks I can, large or small -- it doesn't matter. Do you think Brell would allow me to build a clockwork that could raze the foundation of Kernagir in mere hours? Of course not! And you can only keep plans for such things secret for so long, so I [came] here.'\nYou say, 'Came here?'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'I didn't need to listen to any Bellikos silliness about choosing your own path or following your inner self. That sort of nonsense is for the cretins in these caverns or those dumb beasts that bumble about near the lava pits. Small minds never have large egos. And if you need to be told to [think] for yourself, you shouldn't.'\nYou say, 'Think for yourself?'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'Even before the explosion that sent me to the Underfoot, I lived according to my own will, and I never stopped doing so. I don't care what tricks Brell's First Creation uses to get people to follow him. I follow myself, and I can't be tricked. I get what I want: a place to experiment that is far from Brell's eyes. He gets what he wants: clockwork warriors. But I'm chafing under the current arrangement. I have [grander] plans!'\nYou say, 'What are these grander plans?'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'You think I want the Bellikos telling me what to do? I outsmart them every time, but I can't stand their arrogance. A suggestion here and there: modify this, fix that, and on and on -- I've had enough! I have plans for new clockworks that will put fear into Brell and his First Creation! When I'm done with construction, I'll drive the Bellikos from this husk. This will be my lab, my factory. From here I will create the ultimate clockworks of destruction and strike out at both Brell and his First! All I need now are the proper [supplies] to build them...'\nYou say, 'Supplies?'\nInterix Tanglefuze  laughs at you again. 'I know you work for Brell. You're his good little puppet, dancing about whenever he pulls the strings. You're just the sort of _____ the Bellikos' words were meant for. Ha! You want to kill the Bellikos, and so do I, but you don't trust me. Well, I don't care. You need me; I need you. And I don't think you're smart enough to double-cross me. I know by your persuasion spell that you have contacts in Kernagir. I need some parts from there to build my clockworks. Here is a list: Mithril Ore, Golden Cogs, Silver Wires, and Voltage Regulators. Go talk to your handler and see what you can arrange. If you get me the parts, I'll help you get rid of the Bellikos.'\nYour task 'Brell's Will Be Done' has been updated.\n2. Speak with Gihbra Artinguard 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nTask Window Says: It appears that Interix wants the Bellikos out of the husk too, if only for his own nefarious purposes. Perhaps Gihbra will have an idea of how to use this to your advantage.\nYou say, 'Hail, Gihbra Artinguard'\nGihbra Artinguard says 'I was wrong about Tanglefuze, but I don't trust him in the least. We can't just hand him all the supplies he requires and expect him not to pose a threat to us. You can find everything you need in the Shining City, but your first stop when you get there should be Percy Scrapfisher. He's in a building in the southwest of the city, near the gates. He deals with all the junk parts that the Gnomes throw out when they're done building their contraptions. If there's one thing he knows, it's where to find components for clockworks -- especially [faulty] ones.'\nYou say, 'Faulty ones?'\nGihbra Artinguard says 'Let's give Tanglefuze what he wants. His plans, along with the chaos we've already caused, should be enough to require Bellikos reinforcements. If we give him a few sub-par components, though, his clockworks shouldn't last long enough to cause any real problems for us. Besides, we can deal with Tanglefuze after the Bellikos have been taken care of.'\n3. Speak with Percy Scrapfisher 0/1 (Kernagir, the Shining City)\nPercy Scrapfisher [npc=34731] is found at approximately (5, 475, -50) in Kernagir.\nTask Window Says: To find scrap for Tanglefuze's clockworks, Gihbra said you should look for Percy Scrapfisher, who is near the southeast gates of Kernagir.\nYou say, 'Hail, Percy Scrapfisher'\nPercy Scrapfisher says 'Greetings, _____. It's a perfect day for sifting through junk piles, isn't it? That's why you're talking to me, right? Well, if you're looking for scrap or [junk], you've found the right Gnome!'\nYou say, 'I'm looking for some junk'\nPercy Scrapfisher says 'Hmm...that sounds like some high-end scrap you're after. I think I saw a pile of Mithril Ore in the building west of here. You should check the building with lava tubes for a bag of Golden Cogs. Silver Wires? I think they're in a building to the northeast. And you want what? Faulty Voltage Regulators? Actually, I was carrying some of those when I stopped off at the bar last night. When I woke up today, I didn't have them anymore. I also didn't have my pants. What do you want all this for, if you don't [mind] my asking?'\nYou say, 'I do mind'\nPercy Scrapfisher says 'Okay, sorry! Just curious!'\nTask Window Says: Percy says that while in Kernagir you should find all the scrap you need - a Pile of Mithril Ore in a building west of Percy, a Bag of Golden Cogs in a building with lava tubes, a Bag of Silver Wires in a building to the northeast, and Faulty Voltage Regulators near a bar.\n4. Deliver 1 Pile of Mithril Ore to Interix Tanglefuze 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nPile of Mithril Ore [item=87056] is a ground spawn at 123, 740, 53 in Kernagir.\n5. Deliver 1 Bag of Golden Cogs to Interix Tanglefuze 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nBag of Golden Cogs [item=87057] is a ground spawn at 1036, 592, 135 in Kernagir (bottom floor).\n6. Deliver 1 Bag of Silver Wires to Interix Tanglefuze 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nBag of Silver Wires [item=87050] is a ground spawn at 855, 123, 167 in Kernagir.\n7. Deliver 1 Bag of Faulty Voltage Regulators to Interix 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nBag of Faulty Voltage Regulators [item=86982] is a ground spawn at 119, 979, 219 in Kernagir.\n8. Speak with Gihbra Artinguard 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nYou say, 'Hail, Gihbra Artinguard'\nGihbra Artinguard says 'Brell's will is about to be done. You've already disrupted the Bellikos' plans for the Sporali, Mephits, Gnolls, and Dwarves. Now Tanglefuze will spring the trap we have laid. I'm sure at any moment more Bellikos will arrive to quell the unrest and put a stop to Tanglefuze's plan. Hurry: before they do, use Tanglefuze's clockworks to kill the remaining Bellikos overseers in the husk. Go see if Tanglefuze has finished his work. The time is at hand...'\n9. Speak with Interix Tanglefuze 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nTask Window Says: Interix should be done with the clockworks by now.\nYou say, 'Hail, Interix Tanglefuze'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'Yes, I know what's happening. Reinforcements will be here soon. Take these clockworks and kill the overseers.'\nYou'll get two mobs to assist you, each called \"Mithril Clockwork\" which you can take with you to complete the next kill steps. You don't have to use them, but they'll make quick work of the bellikos mobs. If you do use them, you don't even have to aggro the bellikos. The clockworks will do all the work.\nThe clockworks despawn if you die, zone, or take longer 20 minutes. If this happens, you can hail Interix again for another pair of clockwork helpers by hailing Interix again:\nYou say, 'Hail, Interix Tanglefuze'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'You need reinforcements? Take these!'\n10. Kill 5 Bellikos overseers 0/5 (Volska's Husk)\nTask Window Says: Now is the time to strike at the Bellikos. Interix has given you powerful clockworks to deal with the overseers.\nAny five bellikos count towards this step, including wardens and lecturers.\n11. Hail Interix Tanglefuze 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nTask Window Says: The Bellikos have been eliminated, for now. See what Interix wants to do with his clockworks.\nYou say, 'Hail, Interix Tanglefuze'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'You thought you were going to double-cross me? I told you you couldn't! I knew you gave me faulty voltage regulators, and I repaired them. Do you think I am that easily fooled? This is my cavern now. Go and deal with any Bellikos reinforcements if you must. I'll keep my clockworks with me. If the Bellikos enter here, I'll deal with them. If they manage to destroy the clockworks, I'll only create more. I cannot be stopped. Now hurry back to your master, like the good [lapdog] you are.'\nYou say, 'Lapdog?!'\nInterix Tanglefuze  laughs. 'Knowing the truth only makes life harder to bear, doesn't it, _____?'\nThis step triggers the spawns of three Bellikos at the cave entrance, one of which is a named. They are not linked, but will assist each other. The Autarchian mobs in the area will also assist them.\n12. Speak with the Bellikos arbiter, Bryxyx Kyzox 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nTask Window Says: The plan has worked. A Bellikos arbiter, Bryxyx Kyzox has arrived to put down the unrest in the husk and eliminate any unwanted intruders.\nYou say, 'Hail, Bryyxyx Kyzox'\nBryxyx Kyzox says, 'Are you happy? Has Brell told you to do this, or are you acting of your own accord? If you have chosen this path without any [prodding], I praise you. It takes great courage to defy someone as powerful as the First and kill his beloved creations. Please continue as you wish; for I will welcome you to carry out your will as far as you are able.'\nYou say, 'Prodding?'\nBryxyx Kyzox says, 'But if Brell's will has overpowered your own, desist from this course. Is it really your desire to see your life spilled into lava pools over the arbitrary commands of a distant god? Whose [interest] does Brell hold in mind, yours or his?'\nYou say, 'Interest?'\nBryxyx Kyzox says 'If you desire, live here in the husk. Do whatever pleases you: work or do not work. And if we anger you, attempt to strike us down. You are only as [free] as you allow yourself to be.'\nYou say, 'Free?'\nBryxyx Kyzox says 'Anything as complex as a grouping of free creatures will fall into balance. It is the way of things. From what Brell would call chaos arises order. Dwarves mine, Gnolls hunt, and Gnomes create. It is only natural. Order without [imposition].'\nYou say, 'Imposition?'\nBryxyx Kyzox says 'You would return all these creatures to subjugation? You are confused, as you are under subjugation yourself. Consider my words. Put Brell's will aside; he will carry it out on his own. As I said before, if you, of your own accord, still wish to overpower me, I welcome you to try. Struggle and contention will decide whose will is greater, as it should be.'\nYou say, 'Hail, Bryyxyx Kyzox'\nBryxyx Kyzox says, 'It is a shame our wills could not coexist.'\nYou say, 'Hail, Bryyxyx Kyzox'\nBryxyx Kyzox says, 'I welcome your expression of will _____, Now I shall show you mine.'\nNOTE: If you take too long and Bryxyx despawns, you can hail Interix again to respawn her:\nYou say, 'Hail, Interix Tanglefuze'\nInterix Tanglefuze says 'I think those arbiters are still out there. Take care of them!'\nYou will have to go through Bryxyx's dialogue again to make her aggro.\n13. Defeat Bryxyx Kyzox 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nTask Window Says: Bryxyx is unwilling to allow you to continue your plan of sabotage.\nThe two adds with her are mezzable and stunnable, but Bryxyx is not. The fight is pretty straight forward.\n14. Return to Gihbra Artinguard 0/1 (Volska's Husk)\nTask Window Says: You have driven back the Bellikos and depleted their numbers. Gihbra will want to hear of this.\nYou say, 'Hail, Gihbra Artinguard'\nYour task 'Brell's Will Be Done' has been updated.\nYou have disturbed the balance in the husk and killed a powerful Bellikos Arbiter. Brell's First will be on the defensive.\nGihbra Artinguard says 'We've done it, _____! This is surely a blow to the Bellikos! It will take them a while to clean up the mess we've caused here. Brell's [will] has surely been done. Without him it would not have been possible.'\nYou say, 'Brell's will has been done?'\nGihbra Artinguard says 'Do not listen to the lies of the Bellikos, _____. You've seen the chaos they have caused. Without the word of Brell, the creatures of the Underfoot do not know what to do with themselves. Everything devolves into chaos. Once the Autarchians and Bellikos have been dealt with, the rule of Brell will be exerted once again over everything in the Underfoot, as it should be.'\n512 platinum\nExperience\n~200 Brellium Tokens\nCompletion of this task allows you to request the group task for Volska's Husk, Kill the Hatchlings [quest=5043].Rewards:\n- Brellium Token [item=88944]\n[",
