      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 86\n**Maximum Level:** 90\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis task is the first in a series of three that begins with Scholar Kintorom at the zone-in of The Library.\nYou say, 'Hail, Scholar Kintorom'\nScholar Kintorom says 'Oh, hello there. Are you here to do some research? It's been my lifelong dream to find the answers to the origins of Norrath and the Gods we worship. I had researched everywhere in the world, but to no avail. Not too long ago though, I stumbled across this house and its wondrous [library].'\nYou say, 'What's up with this library?'\nScholar Kintorom says 'There any more books here than I have seen in all the libraries in my lifetime combined! Never in my wildest dreams did I ever expect to find a library such as this. The answers I seek must be within them, so I began to conduct my [research].'\nYou say, 'Your research?'\nScholar Kintorom says 'Not long after I started, the mysterious wardens here kicked me out. Why would they deny me access to these tomes? I must continue my research! While I cannot get back in to do my research, you may be able to go in my place. Would you be willing to go inside the library and [interview] the other scholars here regarding my research?'\nYou say, 'Of course I'd be willing to interview some other scholars'\nScholar Kintorom says 'Great! Please come back as soon as you have the results.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Interview with a Scholar'.\nScholar Kintorom recently arrived in the library and began researching the origins of the godsand the creation of norrath. Shortly after though, he was kicked outfor unknown reasons. Because he cannot get back inside, he has asked you to enter the library and interview various scholars regarding his research.\nInterview a preoccupied scholar 0/1 (The Library)\nInterview an absorbed scholar 0/1 (The Library)\nInterview an oblivious scholar 0/1 (The Library)\nInterview an obsessed scholar 0/1 (The Library)\nInterview a fascinated scholar 0/1 (The Library)\nThese mobs are found a few rooms deep into the zone. You can hail them with invisibility up. The first four scholars you hail will give you responses like this:\nan oblivious scholar says 'I'm busy with a project of my own so I can't help you right now.'\nan obsessed scholar says 'This is most fascinating.....hmm? Research? I don't have time for that. Go ask someone else.'\nThe fifth one you hail (doesn't matter which is last) will become aggravated enough with you to attack (and will also aggro nearby mobs).\na fascinated scholar says 'I'm trying to read. Why are you bothering me!'\nDefeat the crazed scholar who attacked you 0/1 (The Library)\nIt hits for a max ~6,000.\nSearch the scholar for anything of interest 0/1 (The Library)\nLoot a \"Volume 791\" from its corpse.\nBring 'Volume 791' to Scholar Kintorom 0/1 (The Library)\nYou were helping Scholar Kintorom with his research and delivered an interesting book to him.\nScholar Kintorom says 'This is a most interesting book you have brought me. I'll need some time study it further, but do come back soon. I suspect this may lead to something.'\n159 platinum\nExperience\nFaction with Dream Delvers\nDream Motes (# varies)Rewards:\n- Dream Mote [item=90255]\n[",
