      rewards = {
        { id = 90255, name = "Dream Mote", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 90\n**Maximum Level:** 95\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is one of five pre-requisite tasks leading up to the Miragul's Nightmare mission, \"Miragul's Vendetta\". There are no pre-requisites for requesting this task.\nThis is a solo task that begins with a glittering portal in Miragul's Nightmare. It's located in the castle of Miragul's Nightmare (center room of the bottom floor). Beware there is one roaming mob that paths through the room and a mob on either side of the portal (though slightly out of aggro range).\nA faint voice from beyond the glittering portal calls out to you for help.\nYou say, 'Hail, a glittering portal'\nA faint voice calls to you from beyond the portal, 'Has someone heard my pleas at last? Do not be frightened. I am neither golem nor mephit, but a helpless [prisoner] of this portal!'\nYou say, 'Prisoner?'\nThe voice continues, 'When the nightmare began my father, Dridus, thought he would spare my life by sending me through the portal, but his actions have only forced me to be an [unwilling] witness to the extinction of everything I loved. The brilliance that once filled these halls has been reduced to a dull and colorless haze.'\nYou say, 'An unwilling witness?'\nThe voice responds, 'Devoid of vibrancy or not, I still yearn for a [life] beyond this portal. To feel the cool air rush over my skin or delight in the fragrance of wild flowers, are unimaginable pleasures.'\nYou say, 'What life?'\nThe voice explains, 'My father, in all his well-meaning ignorance, would never have condemned me to this fate without being certain there was a way to reverse it. Lacking a physical form certainly hinders me from discovering how, though. You, on the other hand, you could [help] me; you have the kiss of life shimmering on your skin, and a sense of altruism in your heart, I can sense it.'\nYou say, 'How can I help?'\nThe girl from beyond the portal says, 'My father's quarters are not far from here. He always kept his work closely guarded. Whatever knowledge he gathered about the portal would be within an arm's reach of where he slept.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Prisoner of the Portal'.\nA faint voice from beyond the glittering portal has asked for your help in breaking free.\n- 1. Locate Dridus' quarters 0/1 (Miragul's Nightmare)\n- 2. Recover Dridus' journal 0/1 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nThe journal is a groundspawn in a northwestern room upstairs in the castle at location 1135, 710, 138. You can pick it up safely with invisibility (provided no named is up).\n- 3. Deliver Dridus' journal to the girl beyond the portal 0/1 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nYou hear the faint rustle of pages turning, as the girl beyond the portal hums with quiet understanding.\nThe girl beyond the portal is the portal itself. You trade the book to the portal and hail it for this step.\n- 4. Speak to the girl beyond the portal 0/1 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nYou say, 'Hail, a glittering portal'\na glittering portal shimmers as the girl on the other side speaks, 'It's here, the information I need to set myself free. Take careful note, _____. The delicate balance of force within the portal must remain constant, or it will become unstable. There will need to be equal amounts of energy on both sides before I can pass through safely. Vibrant life is in limited supply, but I'm sure some of the creatures you encounter will have a hint of vigor left within them.'\n- 5. Loot chromatic essences from ravens 0/2 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nThis is a common drop from any raven.\n- 6. Pass the chromatic essences through the portal 0/2 (Miragul's Nightmare)\n- 7. Speak to the girl beyond the portal 0/1 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nYou say, 'Hail, a glittering portal'\na glittering portal shimmers as the girl on the other side speaks, 'According to my father's notes, the portal draws its power from the blackened runes found outside of these halls. Destroying the runes should weaken the portal enough for me to pass through safely.'\n- 8. Destroy the blackened runes 0/2 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nThere are two blackened runes you must destroy: One is located at the very southern part of the zone. The other is located in the first large clearing south of the castle (near the quest NPC Xilixizan).\nThe runes are surrounded by mobs you'll most likely want to clear away. The runes fight back (though don't hit very hard) and summon once damaged. In addition, shortly after attacking a rune, \"a runic sentinel\" spawns and attacks you (hits for a max ~7,500).\na blackened rune has been slain by _____!\na blackened rune's corpse is nothing but a pile of rubble.\n- 9. Return to the portal 0/1 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nWarning: Don't go into the room with the portal until you're ready for a fight. Stepping into the room will trigger the following:\n- 10. Release the girl 0/1 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nEvelynn appears from beyond the portal, peering around at her new surroundings. 'I can't believe it. I'm finally free!' As the newly freed girl exits the portal, her color begins to fade.\nEvelynn doubles over with pain, as a confused and colorless expression spreads across her face. 'What.. what is happening to me?!'\nEvelynn stares down at her distorted body in horror as the vibrance that brightened her existance is consumed by the colorlessness within Miragul's Nightmare. 'No, nooo! This can't be real. Please, make it stop!'\nEvelynn attacks, hitting for a max ~7,800.\n- 11. Put Evelynn out of her misery 0/1 (Miragul's Nightmare)\nEvelynn has been slain by _____!\nEvelynn's corpse falls silently to the ground.\nYou helped Evelynn travel through the portal, only to watch her succumb to the darkness that infects all within Miragul's Nightmare.\n315 platinum\nExperience (1.5 to 2 AAs worth at Level 90)\nFaction with Dream Delvers\n30 Dream MotesRewards:\n- Dream Mote [item=90255]\n[",
    },
