      items_required = {
        { name = "the Nightmare Blood to Alezra 0/1 (Fear Itself)", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 90255, name = "Dream Mote", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 90\n**Maximum Level:** 95\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis solo task is the second in a series of three. It begins with Alezra D`Vour in Fear Itself. She's found in a small tower a little ways east of the zone-in.\nYou must have completed the \"Bite of the Beast\" task before you can request this one.\nYou say, 'Hail, Alezra D`Vour'\nAlezra D`Vour says 'There are many who come here, eager to join the ranks of Cazic's chosen, though not all are destined to become disciples of Fear. One must prove themselves loyal, resourceful, and remorseless if they wish to stand before our leader and be judged. You will have my recommendation, if you can withstand the [trials] I set before you.'\nYou say, 'Trials?'\nAlezra D`Vour says 'A handful of those who pledged themselves as servants of Thule, have now dissented and are cowering away somewhere in this realm. Your first test is one of loyalty. Pledging yourself to Cazic Thule is a commitment that extends well beyond death, and those who have dissented shall be disposed of by your hand.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Follower of Fear'.\nTo prove yourself worthy, Alezra has asked you to complete a series of trials before joining the ranks of Cazic devotees.\nDispose of the dissenters who are cowering in fear around the realm.\nXoraik was last spotted near the gorge to the northwest. Lorenai has taken refuge in a fallen bell. Vendula was seen hiding beneath the western stone bridge.\nDispose of Xoraik 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nDispose of Lorenai 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nDispose of Vendula 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nXoraik is found in a ruined building in the very northwest part of the zone.\nLorenai is found under a fallen bell in the northeast part of the zone (head due east of the southernmost point of the ring of fire).\nVendula is just south of the ring of fire (on the ground, beside the north ramp leading up to the top of the frightfinger structure).\nThey are all straight-forward fights, difficulty on par with trash in the zone. They're immune to stun and mez.\nSpeak to Alezra 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nYou say, 'Hail, Alezra D`Vour'\nAlezra D`Vour says 'The dissenters have been disposed of? I wish I could have seen the overwhelming fear in their eyes as they met their end. You have passed the trial of loyalty. Are you ready for your next [test]?'\nYou say, 'I'm ready for the next test'\nAlezra D`Vour says 'Resourcefulness should never be underestimated. A devotee of Thule needs to be more than just a loyal strong-arm. We need well-rounded followers, who excel in tasks of a more... agreeable nature. To test your resourcefulness, I ask you to gather rare ingredients used in crafting a slow-killing poison.'\nThis opens up the next three steps:\nGive the Clump of Diseased Flesh to Alezra 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nGive the Ruptured Tear Duct to Alezra 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nGive the Nightmare Blood to Alezra 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nTask Window Says: Alezra has asked you to find rare ingredients for a slow killing poison as a test of your resourcefulness; a clump of diseased flesh from a boogeyman, a ruptured tear duct from a glarelord, and nightmare blood.\nThese are an uncommon drop from boogeymen, glarelords, and nightmares (respectively). They are confirmed to drop from any mobs with \"boogeyman\", \"glarelord\" and \"nightmare\" in their names.\nThey are pre-lootable.\nSpeak to Alezra 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nYou say, 'Hail, Alezra D`Vour'\nAlezra D`Vour says 'To kill those who defy us simply isn't enough; we must inflict pain and suffering along with death. Your apt resourcefulness will allow us to craft many deadly poisons, which will do just that. Speak to me when you are ready to [prove] you are remorseless.'\nYou say, 'I'll prove it...'\nAlezra D`Vour says 'There are a few who have entered this realm with the intent of doing harm to Cazic Thule. These people thrive on honesty and morals. They are weak, and their trusting nature will be their undoing. Speak to them and convince them to drink the poison you have helped create.'\nPoison trapped dreamers 0/2 (Fear Itself)\nTask Window Says: To show you have no remorse, Alezra has asked you to convince trusting trapped dreamers to ingest deadly poison. They should be wandering within the first level of the large temple.\nThe trapped dreamers are found in the temple within the ring of fire. There are a few spawnpoints on the second floor down from the top. They're typically found in dead-ends.\nThe regular amygdalans don't see invisibility, so unless you run into a named, you'll be fine to run around it with invis.\nNOTE: These trapped dreamers have a 20-minute respawn time.\nYou say, 'Hail, a trapped dreamer'\na trapped dreamer says 'You've come the [help] me, yes? I've been so terrified wandering this place alone. My only wish is to return to my wife and small children.'\nYou say, 'Yes, I've come to help you...'\na trapped dreamer says 'So this is all a dream? This potion will rouse me from my sleep? More of a nightmare I say, but I trust you stranger. I'll drink it as I am told.'\nThe trapped dreamer keels over and dies.\nYou say, 'Hail, a trapped dreamer'\na trapped dreamer says 'At last, a friendly face! I was beginning to think I'd die down here... Can you [help] me escape?'\nYou say, 'Yes... I can help you escape...'\na trapped dreamer says 'A gate potion you say? Are you sure it's safe? Oh, you seem trustworthy, and taking a risk is better than the alternative I suppose.'\nYou've gone and killed this one too.\nReturn to Alezra 0/1 (Fear Itself)\nYou say, 'Hail, Alezra D`Vour'\nAlezra D`Vour says 'Well done, _____. I don't see a trace of guilt lingering on your face. Earning my recommendation to stand before our leader, Tiseth, is no easy feat. If you wish to join our ranks, I will aid you in completing the process.'\nYou have passed the trials put before you, and earned Alezra's recommendation to join the ranks of Cazic's devotees.\n158 platinum\nExperience\nFaction with Dream Delvers\n15 Dream Motes\nThe task \"At the Altar of Fear\" follows this one.Rewards:\n- Dream Mote [item=90255]\n[",
