      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 90\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nVeil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview | Group Progression & Task List | Raid Progression | Visible Armor\nThis task is the second in a series of six; a solo task that begins with Troopwielder Baris in Argath at about -235, -235, 12.\nPre-requisites for requesting the task:\n- Completion of \"This is Argath\"\n- (no minimum skill level in Alaran Language)\nYou say, 'Hail, Troopwielder Baris'\nTroopwielder Baris says '_____, you live! I had hoped Altara might send you. Erillion has intensified its barrage on the Neck, and the defensive barriers we placed there are weakening. Someone needs to shore up the walls. The last mechanic I sent to do the job took an arrow in alir eye. Will you [finish] the task?'\nYou say, 'I'll finish the task'\nTroopwielder Baris says 'I hope you will have better luck. Take these bricks and mortar. Do what you can. If you survive, speak with Troopwielder Balath. Al has been looking for an outsider.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Shoring Up Defenses'.\nErillion's magic wielders and catapults pound the Neck of Argath, wearing down the defensive barriers that protect the citizens and refugees. Troopwielder Baris has asked you to repair any broken barriers. Once you have done this, Troopwielder Balath has need for you.\nUse the Brick and Mortar Baris gave you to repair any walls in the Neck that have been damaged, but be mindful of Erillion's projectiles.\nYou receive a \"Brick and Mortar\".\nRepair 5 broken defensive barriers on the Neck 0/5 (Argath)\nMidway down the neck, you'll find several destructible objects called \"a wall\". You'll have to attack these until they're below 80%, and then right-click your Brick and Mortar to repair them.\nWhile you're doing this, dervishes called \"a malevolent exhalation\" will float by and nuke you for 7,500 dmg at a time. These mobs are attackable and killable.\nSpeak with Troopwielder Balath 0/1 (Argath)\nYou say, 'Hail, Troopwielder Balath'\nTroopwielder Balath says '_____, I need all the outsiders I can get! The Erillions have intensified their barrage, and they are pummeling the Neck. Take a bow and strike down the siege troopers below us! But take heed: Their aim is improving. You must strike swiftly!'\nYou receive Balath's Bow.\nShoot 6 siege runners with Balath's Bow 0/6 (Argath)\nAt the bottom of the ramp that leads into the \"belly\" (lowest level; forge area), you'll see several spawns of non-combative siege runners. You need to equip Balath's Bow and right-click it, then try to target the siege runners as they move towards the ramp.\nSpeak with Troopwielder Balath 0/1 (Argath)\nYou say, 'Hail, Troopwielder Balath'\nTroopwielder Balath says 'That should quiet the enemy for a while. I have heard reports that Troopwielder Latakan needs assistance, though.'\n213 platinum\nLeather-bound BookletRewards:\n- Leather-Bound Booklet [item=99362]\n[",
