      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 95\n**Maximum Level:** 95\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Time Limit:** 06:00:00\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nVeil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview | Group Progression & Task List | Raid Progression | Visible Armor\nThis group mission begins with Captain Portencia in Argath (just outside the air ship drop-off point at 238, 492, 2).\nPr-requisites for requesting the task:\n- Completion of \"Beasts for the Stew\"\n- Completion of \"A Question of Integrity\"\n- Completion of \"Message of Faith\"\n- Completion of \"Trial of the Beast\"\n- Completion of \"One to Lead Them\"\n- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Portencia'\nCaptain Portencia says 'You are _____, correct? Mea has told me about you. I have been meeting with Mea for some time now and we have reached a [deal] that could benefit Argath immensely.'\nYou say, 'What deal?'\nCaptain Portencia says 'Mea has informed me that some members of the Domain clan have recently acquired a brood of naeya pups. These pups would make great [companions] on the battlefield if trained correctly. I want those pups and I want you to [get] them for me.'\nYou say, 'Companions?'\nCaptain Portencia says 'The naeya pups would be very useful as scouts to help defend our lands. They also have an incredible sense of smell and are deadly in a fight.'\nYou say, 'I'll get them'\nCaptain Portencia says 'Getting to the naeya pups won't be easy unfortunately. A strong sect of the Domain clan are guarding them. You look like you might be able to handle them though. I will compensate you for your time if you are able to get the pups for me. Can you [do this] for me?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Pups of War'.\nMea has told Captain Portencia that a new brood of naeya pups has been born to one of the clans. These creatures would be very useful to help the folk of Argath scout and defend their own lands, as the creatures have an amazing sense of smell, good enough to find invisible and hidden enemies of all sorts. Of course they are deadly in a fight too. Captain Portencia has asked you obtain the naeya pups.\nYou say, 'I will do this'\nCaptain Portencia says 'I knew I could count on you. When you are [ready], I can send you to the Beasts' Domain. When you arrive, speak with Mea. One of Mea's offspring, named Trag, has agreed to show you the way to the Domain camp where the naeya pups are being kept.'\nYou say, 'Ready!'\nCaptain Portencia says 'I await your return.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Beasts' Domain.\nNOTE: All mobs in this zone see invisibility. They hit for a max ~12,500 and are stunnable. Mobs are fairly spread out, but sometimes difficult to see due to the terrain.\nSpeak with Mea Treg 0/1 (Beasts' Domain)\nYou say, 'Hail, Mea Treg'\nMea Treg says, in Alaran, 'The heroes return. I take it that you have agreed to get the naeya pups for Portencia? So be it. Trag here will show you the way do the Domain camp. Also, if you need to [leave] here for some reason, just let me know.'\nSpeak with Trag 0/1 (Beasts' Domain)\nYou say, 'Hail, Trag'\nTrag says, in Alaran, 'Are you ready to [depart]?'\nYou say, 'Ready to depart'\nTrag says, in Alaran, 'Follow me.'\nFollow Trag to where the domain hunters are keeping the naeya pups 0/1 (Beasts' Domain)\nTrag will make his way southeast, along the east river, and towards the narrow valleys located in the northeastern part of the zone's middle section.\nHe doesn't aggro mobs unless the mobs aggro you first. Likewise, mobs don't aggro him unless he attacks them first. He can't tank a mob very long without dying, so try not to let him tank much.\nOnce he gets to the domain hunter camp entrance, you'll see this:\nTrag says, in Alaran, 'The clan is near. I cannot help you fight them. Good luck.'\nDefeat the domain hunters in your way 0/18 (Beasts' Domain)\nKill any 18 domain hunters. There is nothing special about them; just regular trash mobs.\nFree the naeya mother from her crate and kill her 0/1 (Beasts' Domain)\nDestroy the large crate to free the naeya mother, and kill her (again, nothing special about this mob).\nCollect the naeya pups from the small crates 0/6 (Beasts' Domain)\nDestroy the small crates and loot the pups.\nGive the pups to Mea Treg 0/6 (Beasts' Domain)\nSpeak with Mea Treg 0/1 (Beasts' Domain)\nYou say, 'Hail, Mea Treg'\nMea Treg says, in Alaran, 'I'm sorry little ones, but you'll be happier where you now go. You have done as asked. Portencia will come my collect the pups. Take something from the chest beside me and when you are ready to [leave], let me know.'\nLoot the chest for your reward 0/1 (Beasts' Domain)\nAnyone within 300 range of the chest gets experience (1-2 AAs depending on your AA count).\nEltarki's Diary - Beasts Know More\n273 platinum\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip Per Task)\nAfton's August Amethyst\nAquamarine Ring of the Serpent\nCarved Bone Sabre\nCijerst's Decayed Targ Shield\nDecorative Earhook of the Tides\nDeteriorating Hammer of the Zombified\nGrimy Stone of the Slothlord\nHegul's Splendorous Shoulderguards\nSeaweed Lined Mask of the Serpent\nShrieking Staff\nMedian Alaran Cantrip\nGreater Alaran CantripRewards:\n- Eltarki's Diary - Beasts Know More [item=99366]\n[",
