      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 95\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Alaran Language:** 81\n**Time Limit:** 06:00:00\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nVeil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview | Group Progression & Task List | Raid Progression | Visible Armor\nThis group mission begins with \"a shade\" on the center island in the Pillars of Alra (20, 40, 667).\nNote: This NPC may only visible if you've done all of the task's pre-requisites.\nPre-requisites for requesting the task:\n- Completion of \"The First Pilgrimage\"\n- Completion of \"The Word of Melretia\"\n- Completion of \"The Word of Anriella\"\n- Completion of \"The Word of Fal`Kaa\"\n- Completion of \"The Word of Erion\"\n- Completion of \"Crisis of Faith\"\n- 81 Skill Level in Alaran\nYou say, 'Hail, a shade'\na shade continues staring at the stone shrine as it speaks, 'You have walked alir path and now your eyes are open to the [truth]?'\nYou say, 'The truth?'\na shade says, in Alaran, 'The truth surrounds us and yet evades the eyes of so many. Few are ever privileged enough to understand the reality around them. Even in death many will never see beyond the [grand deception].'\nYou say, 'What grand deception?'\na shade says, in Alaran, 'It should be no surprise by now that someone has been lying to you. You are not the first and will not be the last. It is in the nature of mortals to deceive, it is a selfishness that many will never outgrow. I do not condemn you for being the same. Though, if you are [willing] to reveal the truth, then I have an assignment for you. If you are not, I will not spite you for it, traveler...'\nYou say, 'I'm willing'\na shade says, in Alaran, 'Let me know when you are [ready] and I shall open your eyes to the truth that evades you...'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Truth'.\nThe mysterious shade stands alone at the shrine of Alra. There seems to be more to this place than you may have originally imagined. Let the shade know that you are 'ready' to see the hidden truth of the shrine.\nLet the shade know you are 'ready' 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\nNOTE: The task locks here.\nYou say, 'Ready!'\na shade says, in Alaran, 'Very well.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Pillars of Alra.\nSpeak with the shade 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\nYou say, 'Hail, a shade'\na shade says, in Alaran, 'You stand witness to the true shrine of Alra, seeker.' The shade motions toward the statue, its previously pristine construction now lies as twisted remains. The figure nods mournfully, 'The facade, the grand deception, the lies that one stood upon these grounds have been wiped away. So too will you find with the [teachings] these factionalized sects have attempted to indoctrinate you with...''\nYou say, 'What teachings?'\na shade smiles, expressing a warm peacefulness as it speaks, 'What I ask of you is obedience, not compliance. I simply ask that you seek the truth for yourself... The upper castes of the Pillars are gathered together tonight to pay homage to their respective leaders. The teachings of Lrah, the great one, are far from the forefront of anyone's mind. The purveyors of deception, the readers of worthless [stones], the practitioners of torture, they are gathered while the lesser guard stands watch to keep outsiders away. Make your way to the source of each Pillar's power. I assure you that the answers you seek will be found within those halls...'\nYou say, 'What about the stones?'\na shade looks into your eyes, an expression of pained embarrassment passes the figure's visage, 'I am sorry, seeker... I stood upon these grounds as you made your first pledge. I watched as you walked the ancient paths in the crests of division. I saw the glimmer of hope in your eye as you carried the stones of these grounds to the purveyors of separation... I offer you this moment to atone, to see past the deception and lies. Even if you return from this unchanged, unwilling to part ways from your teachings, I shall not spite you...'\nFrom here, the four \"Lower the barrier...\" steps open up. The next four sections listed below can be done in any order.\nLower the barrier in the Pillar of Light 0/9 (Pillars of Alra)\nTask Window Says: Gain access to the lower hall of the Pillar of Light by eliminating the barrier sustainers.\nKill the nine sustainers in the entrance area of the Pillar of Light. These mobs appear to be aggro-linked in groups of three. \"Stoic\" mobs are mezzable, \"timid\" mobs are stunnable, and \"lumbering\" mobs are rootable/snareable. They each hit for a max ~13,000.\nUpon killing the last of the nine:\nThe Pillar of Light shakes as its glowing barrier fades from sight!\nDefeat the Pillar of Light's Mana Ward 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\nTask Window Says: Find what hides in the depths of Erion's mana pool.\nSolinvitare P`Trenvell can be found in the basement of the Pillar of Light.\nSolinvitare P`Trenvell begins radiating beautiful shades of pearl as it focuses its energy to purge the chamber of its newest unwelcomed guests.\nSolinvitare hits for a max ~18,000. It casts \"Grasp of Light\", \"Unwavering Gaze\", and the emote-based \"Blinding Luminosity\":\nGrasp of Life: NPC Hatelist 1000', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Disease Counter by 30\n5: Set Healing Effectiveness to -65%\n11: Decrease All Resists by 400\nUnwavering Gaze: Single Target, Chromatic (-800)\n1: Stun (6.00 sec/200)\n2: SpinStun\nBlinding Luminosity: Single Target, Chromatic (-800)\n1: Mesmerize (2/200)\n2: Blindness (2)\nYou have a 10-second warning before \"Blinding Luminosity\" hits:\nSolinvitare compels you to look at toward its light!\n5 seconds later: Solinvitare begins glowing brilliantly, you should look away!\n10 seconds later (with the spell cast): Solinvitare's skin flares with light then begins to dim.\nSolinvitare P`Trenvell has been slain by _____!\nAs Solinvitare falls an otherworldly cry tears through the Pillar of Light...\na forlorn spirit looks confused and disoriented as it rises from the coalesced mana.\nEscort the freed spirit to the Shrine of Alra 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n\"a forlorn spirit\" appears and wanders up to the entrance of the tower. Tell it you'll \"help\" to get it moving (and be prepared for a fight a short time later).\nYou say, 'Hail, a forlorn spirit'\na forlorn spirit says, in Alaran, 'I... I cannot go alone... They will stop me... Please stranger, will you... [help] me escape?'\nYou say, 'We'll help!'\na forlorn spirit bows its head in thanks.\nIt wanders outside the pillar towards the walkway to the center. Shortly before reaching it, you'll be ambushed by 2x \"an undying fragment of light\" (hit for a max ~20,000).\na forlorn spirit looks hesitant as it draws away from the pillar.\na forlorn spirit freezes as the guardians of the pillar descend upon it!\nan undying fragment of light roars furiously as it moves to intercept the escaping shade, 'Not even in death shall you escape!'\nAfter the fragments are dead, the spirit walks to the Shrine.\na forlorn spirit calls out in an ethereal whisper, 'I thank you for releasing me, seekers... My story shall be yours when we reach the shrine of the great one...'\na forlorn spirit nods, 'We are close, stranger, very close...'\na forlorn spirit raises its arms to the sky and gives thanks, 'Blessings be upon the seekers who free us from the bonds of torment!'\nYou say, 'Hail, a forlorn spirit'\na forlorn spirit looks down to the small apparition before speaking, 'Al does not [remember] me... It is for the best... It is the 'purifiers' whom shall face the worst torment in their afterlife. The torture I have suffered pales in comparison to the wrath the great one will hold for slayers of innocents... Though perhaps this is not my end...'\nYou say, 'Remember you?'\na forlorn spirit turns away, 'The light blinds all to the foul truth of the sect... They... I...' The figure struggles for breath, '...To sacrifice my own child for the purity of our worship...' The figure shakes its head and returns looking toward the apparition...\nLower the barrier in the Pillar of the Arcane 0/9 (Pillars of Alra)\nTask Window Says: Gain access to the lower hall of the Pillar of the Arcane by eliminating the barrier sustainers.\nKill the nine sustainers in the entrance area of the Pillar of the Arcane. These mobs appear to be aggro-linked in groups of three. \"Stoic\" mobs are mezzable, \"timid\" mobs are stunnable, and \"lumbering\" mobs are rootable/snareable.\nUpon killing the last of the nine:\nThe Arcane Pillar shakes violently as its barrier is depleted.\nDefeat the Pillar of the Arcane's Mana Ward 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\nKrillionovar Lodindral motions its hands in complex patterns as it conducts tendrils of raw mana around the room.\nKrillionovar hits for a max ~18,000 and casts \"Grasp of the Arcane\" as well as an emote-based \"Arcane Torrent\":\nGrasp of the Arcane: NPC Hatelist 1000', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Disease Counter by 30\n7: Decrease All Resists by 400\n9: Negate Chance to Avoid Melee Effect\n10: Negate AC Limit Modifier Effect\nArcane Torrent: Single Target, Chromatic (-800)\n1: Decrease Mana by 75000\n2: Decrease Endurance by 75000\n3: Decrease Hitpoints by 92400\nYou have a 5-second warning to move away from it to avoid \"Arcane Torrent\":\nKrillionovar glares at you angrily. You should move further away!\nIf you see this emote, you need to run a distance away until you see this, five seconds later:\nKrillionovar prepares a devastating attack. You appear to be at a safe distance.\nSimilarly, there is an emote that beckons you closer:\nKrillionovar glares at you furiously. You should move closer to it!\nFive seconds later:\nKrillionovar prepares a devastating attack. You should move closer to avoid it.\nKill Krillionovar to update this step.\nKrillionovar Lodindral has been slain by _____!\nKrillionovar curses your name as it falls to the ground dead. The buzzing of the arcane pool is overshadowed by a mournful cry...\na forgotten soul looks around the room, now realizing it has been freed from its prison. It struggles for a moment before moving to escape the Pillar.\nEscort the freed spirit to the Shrine of Alra 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n\"a forgotten spirit\" appears and wanders up to the entrance of the tower. Tell it you'll \"help\" to get it moving (and be prepared for a fight a short time later).\na forgotten soul looks panicked as it surveys the room, 'No... They will not allow this... You must [help] me escape the clutches of this accursed place!'\nYou say, 'We'll help you'\na forgotten soul looks around the room in terror before moving out the archway.\nIt wanders outside the pillar towards the walkway to the center. Shortly before reaching it, you'll be ambushed by 2x \"an undying fragment of arcana\". These mobs hit for a max ~20,000.\na forgotten soul looks hesitant as it draws away from the pillar.\nan undying fragment of arcana roars furiously as it moves to intercept the escaping shade, 'Not even in death shall you escape!'\nAfter the fragments are dead, the spirit walks to the Shrine:\na forgotten soul calls out in an ethereal whisper, 'I thank you for releasing me, seekers... My story shall be yours when we reach the shrine of the great one...'\na forgotten soul raises its arms to the sky and gives thanks, 'Blessings be upon the seekers who free us from the bonds of torment!'\nYou say, 'Hail, a forgotten soul'\na forgotten soul looks to the small apparition before speaking, 'Few outside of the high-courts ever learn of anything more than the bitter contention between sects. From the learned to the lowest caste of outsiders, none are told of the [pact]...'\nYou say, 'What pact?'\na forgotten soul says, in Alaran, 'The 'harmony' that exists between the Pillars is not a product of complacence or chance...' The figure looks around before continuing, '...Despite this fact, fraternization outside of your sect for any outside the high-court is grounds for execution. Those who would commit the most heinous crime of bringing impurity to our bloodlines are left to the lightwards for torture... Even that fact is more respectable than what the monsters of the 'arcane' are responsible for...' The spirit lowers its head and sighs.'\nLower the barrier in the Pillar of the Black 0/9 (Pillars of Alra)\nTask Window Says: Gain access to the lower hall of the Pillar of the Black by eliminating the barrier sustainers.\nKill the nine sustainers in the entrance area of the Pillar of the Black. These mobs appear to be aggro-linked in groups of three. \"Stoic\" mobs are mezzable, \"timid\" mobs are stunnable, and \"lumbering\" mobs are rootable/snareable.\nUpon killing the last of the nine:\nThe Pillar of the Black shudders as its shadowy barrier vanishes.\nDefeat the Pillar of the Black's Mana Ward 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\nKrathavik Mis throws its arms back and begins drawing dark power from the pillar walls.\nKrathavik Mis hits for a max ~18,000. It casts \"Grasp of the Black\" and \"Reaching Shadows\" (hits everyone on around him):\nGrasp of the Black: NPC Hatelist 1000', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Disease Counter by 30\n6: Decrease All Resists by 400\n10: Cap Endurance (75%)\n11: Cap Mana (75%)\n12: Cap Hitpoints (75%)\nReaching Shadows: Lifetap 0', Chromatic (-800)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 10000\nKrathavik Mis has been slain by _____!\nKrathavik accepts its death gracefully, falling to the ground and vanishing into the shadows. The moment of peace is broken by the soft cry emanating from the shadowy pool.\na frightened spectre looks confused and disoriented as it rises from the coalesced mana.\nEscort the freed spirit to the Shrine of Alra 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n\"a frightened spectre\" appears and wanders up to the entrance of the tower. Tell it you'll \"help\" to get it moving (and be prepared for a fight a short time later).\na frightened spectre calls out in a hoarse whisper, 'Seekers? ... The final pilgrimage, it cannot be walked alone...'\nYou say, 'We'll help you'\na frightened spectre nods quickly and begins moving.\nIt wanders outside the pillar towards the walkway to the center. Shortly before reaching it, you'll be ambushed by 2x \"an undying fragment of shadow\". These mobs hit for a max ~20,000.\na frightened spectre looks hesitant as it draws away from the pillar.\na frightened spectre freezes as the guardians of the pillar descend upon it!\nan undying fragment of shadow roars furiously as it moves to intercept the escaping shade, 'Not even in death shall you escape!'\nAfter the fragments are dead, the spirit walks to the Shrine:\na frightened spectre raises its arms to the sky and gives thanks, 'Blessings be upon the seekers who free us from the bonds of torment!'\nYou say, 'Hail, a frightened spectre'\na frightened spectre looks to the twisted shrine of Alra before speaking, 'I thank you, adventurer, you have done more than I could ever hope to repay you for... To be free from the clutches of those [deceivers], to be free in death to stand in the presence of the great one...' The figure motions its arms in a curious manner, an expression of gratitude perhaps...\nYou say, 'What deceivers?'\na frightened spectre looks to the ground, 'As you may know, the agents of the black claim they only wish to spread the truth. Their non-violent methods lead most to believe they are the most reasonable of the sects. The reality is that their corruption runs deepest of all. They have taken it upon themselves to lead all lower castes to believe whatever the high court decrees to be the 'truth'... May Alra forgive me for all that I have done in my life...'\nLower the barrier in the Pillar of Nature 0/9 (Pillars of Alra)\nTask Window Says: Gain access to the lower hall of the Pillar of Nature by eliminating the barrier sustainers.\nKill the nine sustainers in the entrance area of the Pillar of Nature. These mobs appear to be aggro-linked in groups of three. \"Stoic\" mobs are mezzable, \"timid\" mobs are stunnable, and \"lumbering\" mobs are rootable/snareable.\nUpon killing the last of the nine:\nThe sound of snapping twigs echoes out in all directions as the Pillar of Nature's verdant barrier fades from view.\nDefeat the Pillar of Nature's Mana Ward 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\nKysinval En`Revos looks to its newest guests and shouts, 'We offer you life and yet you try to kill us?! Your people are hopeless...'\nKysinval En`Revos hits for a max ~18,000; buffs himself with \"Verdant Field\" and AEs \"Grasp of Life:\nGrasp of Life: NPC Hatelist 1000', Unresistable (0)\n1: Increase Disease Counter by 30\n5: Set Healing Effectiveness to -65%\n11: Decrease All Resists by 400\nVerdant Field: Self 0', Unresistable (0)\n5: Increase Damage Shield by 800\n10: Spell-Damage Shield (-3000)\n12: Increase Hitpoints by 3500 per tick\nKysinval En`Revos has been slain by _____!\nKysinval falls backwards, its body immediately being consumed by the pillar. The room is quiet, save for the lone whimper echoing from the verdant pool.\nEscort the freed spirit to the Shrine of Alra 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n\"a fearful shadow\" appears and wanders up to the entrance of the tower. Tell it you'll \"help\" to get it moving (and be prepared for a fight a short time later).\nIt wanders outside the pillar towards the walkway to the center. Shortly before reaching it, you'll be ambushed by 2x \"an undying fragment of life\". These mobs hit for a max ~20,000.\nAfter the fragments are dead, the spirit walks to the Shrine:\na fearful shadow calls out in an ethereal whisper, 'I thank you for releasing me, seekers... My story shall be yours when we reach the shrine of the great one...'\na fearful shadow lets out a small smile, 'Thank you... Seeker...'\na fearful shadow raises its arms to the sky and gives thanks, 'Blessings be upon the seekers who free us from the bonds of torment!'\nYou say, 'Hail, a fearful shadow'\na fearful shadow gazes at the twisted shrine before speaking, 'I hope in time that the great one will [forgive] me...'\nYou say, 'Forgive you?'\na fearful shadow hangs its head in shame, 'For all the harm I have caused, the lives I have ruined. The high court must be dismantled... There can be no other redemption for my soul...'\nSpeak with the shade 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\nTask Window Says: With the captured souls now freed, speak with the shade at the Shrine of Alra.\nYou say, 'Hail, a shade'\na shade nods as it speaks, 'I thank you for opening your eyes to the reality of this place, seeker.' The shade pauses, 'Even if your goal was simply to pillage what remains of our fallen empire, you have done a great service in freeing these souls today... When you are ready to [leave] this place and return to the facade of peace, I shall close your eyes to this vision.'\nThe shade smiles as its allies find peace in their final pilgrimage. The cold iron chest sits solitary at the foot of the shrine as the requited spirits begin fading from view.\nClaim your reward from the cold iron chest 0/1 (Pillars of Alra)\n600 platinum\nElatarki's Diary - Four Cornered\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip Per Task)\nAzure Stud of the Breeze\nBurning Belt of Endless Shadow\nHardened Band of Beaten Earth\nIl`Valrikar's Verdant Orb of Life\nIllum's Cross\nJlane's Visage of Defense\nMace of Forgiveness\nSoapstone Crystal\nStunning Sapphire of the Sepulcher\nGreater Alaran Cantrip\nGlowing Alaran CantripRewards:\n- Azure Stud of the Breeze [item=101245]\n- Burning Belt of Endless Shadow [item=101367]\n- Eltarki's Diary - Four Cornered [item=100418]\n- Glowing Alaran Cantrip [item=99752]\n- Greater Alaran Cantrip [item=99412]\n- Hardened Band of Beaten Earth [item=101819]\n- Il`Valrikar's Verdant Orb of Life [item=101370]\n- Illum's Cross [item=101341]\n- Jlane's Visage of Defense [item=102907]\n- Mace of Forgiveness [item=100768]\n- Soapstone Crystal [item=101159]\n- Stunning Sapphire of the Sepulcher [item=101238]\n[",
