        { id = 145200, name = "Locket of the Disciples", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 115\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Expedition\n**Time Limit:** 06:00:00\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nPrerequisite Quest(s): Death Finds a Way [quest=10725]\nThis group mission is part of the 23rd anniversary.\nThere is a minimum level to request the mission. (maybe 115? Let us know)\nYou can get this shared task from Krastoraab Puremane in Shar Vahl. He is in the city at the entrance leading from Shadeweaver's Thicket at /waypoint -496, 79, -190 or you can find him via the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Krastoraab Puremane'\nKrastoraab Puremane says, 'If you would like a reminder of why the [cycle] is important, I would be more than glad to talk to you about it again. However, if you wish to continue your [education], I can offer some assistance in that request as well.'\nYou say, 'education'\nKrastoraab Puremane says, 'I'm glad to hear that you decided to take up a higher education about the cycle. You may have noticed that each of the disciples you spoke with are, ironically, not continuing onto the next stage of the cycle. Concepts such as what is \"living\" and \"dead\" usually can cause confusion when it comes to living and dying, especially when it comes to the undead. Ghosts and spirits have the capacity to take a moment to pause and observe the cycle. These entities are not outside of the influence of the cycle. It is quite the contrary actually. They are still a part of the cycle of life and death, though their [journey]to Ehayae is postponed for the time being.'\nYou say, 'journey'\nKrastoraab Puremane says, 'The disciples you spoke with want to test your mettle and make sure you fully understand their lessons. If you are willing to take up arms, I have already spoken with the four spirits and they will meet you at the Deep. Be warned as once they start fighting, their emotions will take over and there is no stopping them. You must give them your all in order to defeat them. They will not hold back. Are you sure you are [ready]?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Beyond Espoir'.\nYou say, 'ready'\nKrastoraab Puremane says, 'Excellent, I will wait here for your return. To prove to me that you have a full understanding, you will be given a bauble after you have finished your lesson. None of the spirits know what is inside the box so you won't be able to cheat. Bring that item to me.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Trial of the Cycle.\n1. Defeat the first disciple, Jonus 0/1 The Deep\nJonus is nearby, where you zone in.\nHe is not aggro until you hail him. You can kill trash around the area first, if you want to. The various horror fiends (trash MOB's, all appear to be around the level of the highest level in the group) seem to see through both Invisible and Invisible to Undead.\nWhen you hail Jonus he morphs into a Hooded Shade and attacks.\nThe Bonus step here (for the Challenge Achievement) is to kill him while your health is below 50%. This will require careful healing, after Jonus is below 5% to 10% health.\n2. Defeat the second disciple, Lorelei 0/1 The Deep\nNOTE: All of the targets (Boss's) are on Find.\nWhen you hail Lorelei, she morphs into a Banshee.\nLorelei Carversbane scowls at you, ready to attack -- looks like quite a gamble. (Lvl: 120)\nYou say, 'Hail, Lorelei Carversbane'\nLorelei Carversbane says, 'HA HA! Come adventurer, show me what you are made of!'\nAt about 50%-ish Lorelei Carversbane calls for assistance and two adds spawn and attack you, as well as heal Lorelei Carversbane.\nA devout trumpeter (Level 120) will heal Lorelei.\nA stalwart herald (Level 120)\nThey do not de-spawn if Lorelei dies first.\nChampions from the past, lend me your aid!\nLorelei Carversbane's corpse disperses and an image of the original Lorelei appears for a moment. 'I had such fun today adventurer! I enjoyed our battle for glory! You understand this more than most! Continue your lesson eastward. Till we meet again!'\nYou have slain Lorelei Carversbane!\nYour task 'Beyond Espoir' has been updated.\nThe Bonus step here (for the Challenge Achievement) is to kill her while her 'healer' add (a devout trumpeter) is still alive.\n3. Defeat the third disciple, Salk 0/1 The Deep\nWhen you hail Salk, she morphs into a Tiger.\nYou say, 'Hail, Salk Hopfit'\nSalk Hopfit says, 'Your path requires balance between life and death. Stray but a hair's width away from the edge and you will not succeed!'\nThe cycle of life and death demands balance. Are you capable of the same?\nSalk Hopfit's corpse dissipates, but an image of Salk appears to say, 'Well fought, you understand why there needs to be a balance between life and death now more than ever. Sineb is waiting for you near the bridge to the northeast.'\nYou have slain Salk Hopfit!\nYour task 'Beyond Espoir' has been updated.\n4. Defeat the fourth disciple, Sineb 0/1 The Deep\nWhen you hail Sineb, she morphs into an Owlbear.\nYou say, 'Hail, Sineb'\nSineb says, 'I will show you what primal energies are at play!'\nAt 60%-70%, he calls for assistance and two adds spawn, attack and also heal him.\nA brawny auger (Level 120)\nA primal soothesayer (Level 120)\nThey do not despawn if Sineb dies first.\nPrimal forces protect bring me vitality! Ehayae sows...\nYou gain party experience!\nYou have slain a primal soothesayer!\nYou gain party experience!\nYou have slain a brawny auger!\nBalance is required to fully understand where you stand in the cycle. Sahteb Mahlni drives...\nYou gain party experience!\nSineb's corpse falls, and reappears again as the Sineb you know before saying, 'Well struck! You have completed your path on understanding the cycle! Let me know when you are ready to [leave] and I will bring you back to Shar Vahl.'\nYou have slain Sineb!\nYour task 'Beyond Espoir' has been updated.\nSineb respawns in his original form, once killed.\n5. Open the lockbox 0/1 The Deep\nOpen the lockbox.\nYour task 'Beyond Espoir' has been updated.\nYou have been given: Primal Owlbear Beak\n--You have looted a Shroud of Unending Cycles from a lockbox .--\nYou say, 'Hail, Sineb'\nSineb says, 'Well done mortal. You fully grasp how important the balance of life and death is. You understand that without that fire in your belly to drive you forward, there can be no progress. Moving on from loss is something that we all have to deal with from time to time. That does not mean we forget who we lost. We just get better at fighting without them by our side. Remember this, and you will do well in your future struggles. Now, if you wish to [leave], I can show you the exit. Grow in your adventures as you would, but remember that everyone is fighting their own fights. May the cycle watch over you and bless you in your journeys.'\nYou say, 'leave'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Shar Vahl.\n6. Return the beak to Krastoraab 0/1 Shar Vahl\nGive the Primal Owlbear Beak to Krastoraab Puremane.\nKrastoraab Puremane says, 'Excellent. Thank you for returning this to me. This proves that you were able to overcome the challenges that the disciples have given you. Your understanding is complete. Without Ehayae's work, there can be no death. Without Drinal's work, there can be no life. Without Sahteb Mahlni, there can be no strength or drive for progress. Thank you for taking these lessons to heart Bonzz. I do hope we cross paths again in the future. Until then, go in peace and know that you play an important role in cycle of life and death.'\nYour task 'Beyond Espoir' has been updated.\nYou have received a replay timer for 'Beyond Espoir': 0d:0h:2m remaining.\nYour education about the work of Ehayae, Drinal, and Sahteb Mahlni is complete.\nYou receive alternate currency.\nYou have completed achievement: 23rd Anniversary Mission\nOPTIONAL STEP\nYou can turn in the Primal Owlbear Beak to Sineb in Shar Vahl to receive \"Fungal Shrieker Spore,\" which is a pet clicker that summons a pet with stats or can change the look of your pet.\nUpon turn in,\nSineb says, 'I have to admin, when Krastoraab gave us the lockbox as part of the test, we didn't know what was inside. Bringing this to me confirms my fears. Wherever this beak was found, it was a place of immense power. I do not know where he got this, but he would be wise to return it to whatever corner of Luclin it was taken from. Take this. It should protect you in your journeys. Give the beak back to Krastoraab. I will speak with him later about what he has found, once I learn what it means myself.'\nReward(s):\nYou gain experience!\n20 Commemorative Coins [item=116720]\nLoot from the chest\nChest Loot:\nCollar of Infinite Struggle [item=145201]\nDeteriorating Silk Wrap [item=145202]\nFurry Feathered Cloak [item=145744]\nLocket of the Disciples [item=145200]\nPendant of Repetitiousness [item=144610]\nShroud of Unending Cycles [item=145203]\nBonus reward: Fungal Shrieker Spore [item=144649]Submitted by: GOMNRewards:\n- Collar of Infinite Struggle [item=145201]\n- Commemorative Coin [item=116720]\n- Deteriorating Silk Wrap [item=145202]\n- Fungal Shrieker Spore [item=144649]\n- Furry Feathered Cloak [item=145744]\n- Locket of the Disciples [item=145200]\n- Pendant of Repetitiousness [item=144610]\n- Shroud of Unending Cycles [item=145203]\n[",
