      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 120\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Expedition\n**Group Size:** Raid\n**Min. # of Players:** 6\n**Max. # of Players:** 54\n\nThis raid is part of the 23rd Anniversary.\nYou can get it from a frightened guardian out to the left of the entrance to Karnor's Castle in Dreadlands. a frightened guardian is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, a frightened guardian'\nA frightened guardian startles at your voice, 'Oh, I done! Not fight. Not going back to [castle]!'\nA frightened guardian says, 'You go, not me.' A low growl comes from its tightly closed teeth. 'Crazy sarnak. Screaming! Can't stay there.\nYou say, 'want'\nA frightened guardian says, 'I can show you how to get in, if you [ready]!'\nKarnor's Castle: Mad Emperor is now available to you.\nYou say, 'ready'\nA frightened guardian says, 'Grrrrr...'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Karnor's Castle: Mad Emperor.\nWhen you zone in, a frightened guardian is there with you.\nA frightened guardian regards you indifferently -- You could probably win this fight. (Lvl: 40)\nYou say, 'Hail, a frightened guardian'\nA frightened guardian says, 'I will not blame you if you would like to [leave].'\nIn the next room are red con MOB's of seemingly 2 types. They are all inactive until the you activate the event.\nA sebilite golem scowls at you, ready to attack -- what would you like your tombstone to say? (Lvl: 125)\nThis creature would take an army to defeat!\nYou suspect that this being can see you.\nAn Imperial construct scowls at you, ready to attack -- what would you like your tombstone to say? (Lvl: 125)\nThis creature would take an army to defeat!\nYou suspect that this being can see you.\nIf you cross the room to the far side and go into a room back there, you will find A Kar`Zok maniac.\nA Kar`Zok maniac scowls at you, ready to attack -- what would you like your tombstone to say? (Lvl: 125)\nThis creature would take an army to defeat!\nYou suspect that this being can see you.\nYou say, 'Hail, a Kar`Zok maniac'\nA Kar`Zok maniac says, 'You are just in time to hear them scream! Their pain is glorious! Have you come to bathe in my [revenge]?'\nYou say, 'revenge'\nA Kar`Zok maniac says, 'Come and I will show you what true revenge is!'\nA Kar`Zok maniac says, 'I have been betrayed more times than I can count, but this, this will be the last. Never again will such a thing happen. Love and family are for fools and my brief time as a fool has passed! As I was reborn, so shall I return to what I was meant to be!'\n(He walks off back towards the first room. You can follow to see the scripted sequence. As a note, A Kar`Zok maniac is holding a flask, which is mentioned in the emotes.)\nA Kar`Zok maniac says, 'I can never die. Mine is a destiny of empire! We shall rise again! Norrath will once again chant my name! But first, I must satisfy my revenge.'\nA Kar`Zok maniac says, 'Scream, you pathetic creature. You betrayed me! I must admit that I was a fool to let you, to fall for your plea to save our son at my own expense. In the end power holds the truth and my power is the strength of empires!'\nInarticulate screams come from the glowing flask. Even without understanding the words, you can understand the pain that scream represents. Hearing those sounds is horrific. It is hard to imagine how feeling their cause must feel.\nA Kar`Zok maniac says, 'Good! Suffer!' The Kar'Zok focuses closely on the bottle, 'You betrayed me and would have cast me away. And I must admit that you would have succeeded if it were not for our son's first-hatched. It was Atrebe that gave me this body even as you stole mine for our worthless hatchling.'\nThe horrific screaming from the flask continues.\nA Kar`Zok maniac says, 'I have been born, reborn, and recreated, and every time I have been Emperor, Emperor Venril Sathir! I have tolerated your interruption long enough. Begone!' There is a frighteningly unhinged look on the creature's face. 'Stay and I will submit your spirit to the same pain as my treacherous wife and useless son! But you are not the only one that needs to be punished. These soft-skinned creatures have been at the heart of all that has gone wrong with my empire and it is time to make them suffer as well!'\nVenril Sathir roars with laughter, shaking the walls and calling forth wailing spirits to destroy his foes.\nPowerful magic engulfs the massive sarnak. It morphs in an obviously painful manner, taking on a familiar shape.\nVenril Sathir scowls at you, ready to attack -- what would you like your tombstone to say? (Lvl: 125)\nThis creature would take an army to defeat!\nVenril Sathir then aggros. He can hit for at least 100K.\nReward(s):\nChest Loot:\nArch Convoker's Pantaloons\nBlood Cinder Greaves\nCobalt-Reinforced Greaves\nCollar of Drolvarg Loyalty\nDeepwater Encrusted Greaves\nDemi Lich Pantaloons\nDonal's Leggings of Grieving\nDrusella's Wedding Ring\nEldest Spiritist's Greaves\nIksar Hide Pantaloons\nJaundiced Ossified Greaves\nKly Skinned Pantaloons\nLeggings of Wrathfulness\nLeggings of the Whistling Fists\nMrylokar's Insidious Greaves\nNecklace of the United Tribes\nPulsating Green Stone Amulet\nSathir Dagger of Sacrifice\nSathir Staff of Conflict\nSathir Staff of Forbidden Magic\nSathir Staff of Leadership\nSathir Staff of Ritual Magic\nSathir's Ring of Eternal Life\nSpellsung Steel Greaves\nTolan's Brightwood Greaves\nVenril's Wedding Ring\nWilderness Lord's TrousersSubmitted by: GOMNRewards:\n[",
