      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = -1529.0, x = 40.0, z = -293.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Spiritist Nathra",
        "Why are you troubled?",
        "What is a whisperling?",
        "What poachers do you mean?",
        "What of the Shak Dratha?",
        "I would like to help.",
        "lead",
        "troubled",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "the Spirit-filled Medicine Bag or Khrix", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 116720, name = "Commemorative Coin", type = "item" },
        { id = 144650, name = "Spirit of the Lost", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 115\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Expedition\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nYou can get this group mission by talking to Spiritist Nathra about mid zone around the pool at /waypoint -89, -193, -188. They are on the find tool CTRL F.\nWe need all dialogue, details to each step and task window text for each step.\nYou say, 'Hail, Spiritist Nathra'\nSpiritist Nathra says, 'Hail and well met. It's good that you've reached out to me, for I'm quite [troubled].'\nYou say, 'Why are you troubled?'\nSpiritist Nathra says, 'The spirits are crying out to me. One of their [whisperling] kin has been stolen, and they fear for the safety of the little spirit, especially when he is reported to be in the hands on the [poachers]. Would you be able to [help]?'\nYou say, 'What is a whisperling?'\nSpiritist Nathra says, 'Whisperlings are the spirits who bring our night visions, our dreams. You could say that they \"whisper\" to us in our sleep. They do not persist in our world by default, but only if they are attached by a spirit anchor, which keeps them in our physical realm. It doesn't hurt the whisperling, but it needs a strong anchor to maintain its hold.'\nYou say, 'What poachers do you mean?'\nSpiritist Nathra says, 'The Loda Kai poachers in and of themselves are not directly concerning, as objects such as the whisperling's spirit anchor may be considered more for-profit than something more dangerous for the little spirit. However, it's also known that the Loda Kai are loosely allied with the [Shak Dratha]. At the very least, they have openly bartered. It's the Shak Dratha that I'm worried about. If the Loda Kai traded it over to them... I don't want to think about it.'\nYou say, 'What of the Shak Dratha?'\nSpiritist Nathra says, 'The Shak Dratha delve into the dark arts of the spirit. Their hearts are full of shadow, whether they weave silk directly from it, or pull from it to consume a traveler's soul. If he changes hands before we can get to him, our whisperling friend may not be long for this or any world.'\nYou say, 'I would like to help.'\nSpiritist Nathra says, 'You have no idea how much we appreciate this. I can [lead] you to the cavern shared with me, but from there, it's up to you and any adventuring companions you wish to have accompany you. I'm ready when you are.'\nYou have received a request timer for 'Whispers in the Dark': 0d:1h:0m remaining.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Whispers in the Dark'\nYou say, 'lead'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Shadeweaver's Thicket: Whispers in the Dark.\n- 1. Check in with Spiritist Nathra 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nHail Spiritist Nathra\n- 2. Explore the Loda Kai poachers' cavern 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nUpdate around location -1529, 40, -293\n- 3. Defeat several Loda Kai 0/8 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nKill any a Loda Kai\nThey are all Level 116 to 118.\nIt is recommended to dispel their damage shields and buffs.\n- 4. Check the chest on the far end of the Loda Kai cavern 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nThe chest is in the east side where the Loda Kai are at around location -1543, -180, -431\nAfter opening the chest, 'The chest has alerted the Shak Dratha. Defend yourself!\n2x 'a Shak Dratha guardsman' appear around the nearby rock\n- 5. Defeat the Shak Dratha that have spotted you! 0/2 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nKill 2 'a Shak Dratha guardsman'\nThey spawn next to two Loda Kai around the rock and they can be pulled single with cc.\n- 6. Move north to explore the northern pathway 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nUpdate around location -303, -171, -429   this is right before you enter the next cavern from the Loda Kai area.\n- 7. Continue deeper into the caverns, moving further north 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\n'This room is heavily guarded which is a good indication that the whisperling is hidden here.'\nUpdate around location 13, -148, -291\n- 8. Defeat several Shak Dratha 0/8 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nKill any a Shak Dratha IN the room. The script is bugged and killing roamers and certain mobs over and over again may jam the mission.\nThey are all level 116 to 118.\nIt is recommended to dispel their damage shields and buffs.\n- 9. Check the chest on the far end of the Shak Dratha training cavern 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nUpdate around location 891, -766, -480\nNote: before you continue and open the chest to loot the Khrix, it is recommended to clear out the area around the Shak Dratha Overseer spawn location.\n- 10. Pick up the whispering Khrix 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nLoot 'Khrix' from 'a secured chest'\n- 11. Return south to the circular room and head back to Spiritist Nathra 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nUpdate around location -258, 248, -430\n'The Shak Dratha Overseer is blocking the exit south!'\n- 12. Kill the Shak Dratha Overseer 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nThis step can be completed at any time and still get credit\nShak Dratha Overseer is a rare creature, level 123\nAt ~80% and ~45% 'Shak Dratha Overseer yells, 'Guards! Xauis xua!'\n'A guard comes at the Overseer's call.'\na Shak Dratha guardsman will appear\nAn easy way to kill the Overseer without CC is to camp the corridor south of the boss spawn point, wait for roamers and kill them one by one, then pull boss\nand kill adds as they spawn.\nLoot an Owl Totem\nBonus Item:\nLoot \"Khrix\" and \"Owl Totem\" on the same character\nTarget Spiritist Nathra and say, 'spirit anchor'\nSpiritist Nathra says, 'It's possible that with the Shak Dratha's work with spirits and shadows that they have a strong spirit anchor that could bring strength to the whisperling. We don't know the current state of our friend, so please take this bag and if you find a sufficient anchor in the caverns, please use this bag to strengthen the whisperling with the spirit anchor before bringing him back to me.'\nYou receive Empty Medicine Bag\nCombine both \"Khrix\" & \"Owl Totem\" in the Empty Medicine Bag\nYou have fashioned the items together to create something new: Spirit-filled Medicine Bag.\nGive the Spirit-filled Medicine Bag to Spiritist Nathra\nYou receive Spirit of the Lost\nOnly one character can receive this item per run.\nSpiritist Nathra says, 'Thank you for bringing back the whisperling and finding a suitable anchor for him. The Dar Khura will do everything we can to bring him back to strength. Thanks so much. We can [leave] whenever you're ready.'\n- 13. Hand Khrix over to Spiritist Nathra 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\nThis step will update if you hand in the Spirit-filled Medicine Bag or Khrix.\nMission locks here\n- 14. Open the chest and receive your reward 0/1 Shadeweaver's Thicket\n'a reward chest' spawns around location -1850, -304, -247\nYou have received a replay timer for 'Whispers in the Dark': 0d:5h:0m remaining.\n'With the rescue of Khrix, the whisperling has the chance at an extended life.'\nReward(s):\nExperience\n15 Commemorative Coins\nChest loot:\n1 range or shoulder item\nDrape of Dreams\nMantle of the Dar Khura\nShawl of the Shak Dratha\nTotem of the Loda Kai\nKhrix's Brilliant Idol of the Dawn\nStone Idol of Spirituality\nSpirit of the LostSubmitted by: Less3D and GOMN, VeludeusRewards:\n- Commemorative Coin [item=116720]\n- Spirit of the Lost [item=144650]\n[",
    },
