      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAfter completing the \"Series C Black Boxes\" [quest=19] quest, you received a Daily Log [item=57358] (\"Log Sheet of Clockwork 27c2\"). Take this to Drekon Vebnebber [npc=19] (General Supplies) in Ak'Anon at location +875, -475 (he's on Find).\nYou say, 'Hail, Drekon Vebnebber'\nDrekon Vebnebber says 'Hello, _____. It is grand to make your acquaintance. I am the in-house merchant-slash-file clerk. I have goods to offer and I handle all the Gemchopper paperwork. Thrilling, don't you think?'\nHand in the Daily Log:\nDrekon Vebnebber says 'Oh my! It seems two of the obsolete duster models were not fully shut down. You must find them. They could be anywhere in Ak'Anon! After you destroy them, take their scraps to Sanfyrd Montop. He is the operator of the scrapyard.'\nYour faction standing with Gem Choppers has been adjusted by 5.\nYour faction standing with Merchants of AkAnon has been adjusted by 1.\nYour faction standing with King AkAnon has been adjusted by 1.\nYour faction standing with Dark Reflection has been adjusted by -1.\nYour faction standing with Clan Grikbar has been adjusted by -1.\nYou gain party experience!!\nKill \"Duster X\" and \"Duster V\" and loot their scrap metals.\nDuster V [npc=8] spawns near the clockwork receptionist [npc=81] and travels to the pod area and back before despawning. It can sometimes be seen walking down the path through \"the wall\" just inside the city entrance and around the Priest of Discord [npc=28580] area. At a certain point in his usual path he goes from walk speed to run  speed. He shares a spawn cycle with Scrubber IV [npc=12] and Cleaner X [npc=56504], each one of them despawns after a few minutes before another one from the cycle respawns.\nDuster X [npc=5094] is reportedly triggered after you gave the report to Drekon. It spawns by the mechanic by the tinkerer and travels up to the bridge then back near the paddlewheel. It's loot-locked, which means it shows as *Duster X and shows at the first rank on alphabetic track.\nYou have slain Duster V!\n--You have looted a Scrap Metal. [item=49611]--\nItem Lore: Duster V Scrap Metal.\nYou have slain Duster X!\n--You have looted a Scrap Metal [item=49609].--\nItem Lore: Duster X Scrap Metal.\nFind Sanfyrd Featherhead [npc=23] at location 2020, -240 in Ak'Anon (on the other side of the river across from the Mines of Malfunction).\nYou say, 'Hail, Sanfyrd Featherhead'\nSanfyrd Featherhead says 'Greetings! I am the operator of this scrapyard. If you have any scrap metal, I would be glad to purchase it from you in loads of four. The Gemchoppers no longer allow me to accept blackbox fragments and micro servos.'\nHand in the two Scrap Metals:\nSanfyrd Featherhead says 'I hear there is one more on the loose. Find him and then I shall pay you.'\nSanfyrd Featherhead says 'Good. The citizens of Ak'Anon are safe from those little critters. They may have injured someone; that is why they were deactivated. Here is something I found in the scrapyard. I hope you can find a purpose for it.'\nYour faction standing with Gem Choppers has been adjusted by 10.\nYour faction standing with Merchants of AkAnon has been adjusted by 2.\nYour faction standing with King AkAnon has been adjusted by 2.\nYour faction standing with Dark Reflection has been adjusted by -2.\nYour faction standing with Clan Grikbar has been adjusted by -1.\nYou gain party experience!!\nYou receive 4 silver from Sanfyrd Featherhead.\nYou receive 1 gold from Sanfyrd Featherhead.\nReward:\nBootstrutter's Framed Pack [item=2368] (common)\nForging Hammer [item=6] (rare)Submitted by: SluglugRewards:\n- Bootstrutter's Framed Pack [item=2368]\n- Forging Hammer [item=6]\n[",
