    {
      id = "1224",
      title = "Captain Nalot's Triple Strength Rum",
      exp = "02",
      exp_name = "The Scars of Velious",
      min_lvl = 40,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Nelet Durzit",
        "what cold",
        "Hail, Nilham the Chef",
        "what crate",
        "What cat",
        "Hail, gnomish deserter",
        "what is that box",
        "how did you get your hand stuck",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "Qarrgy TWO Barracuda Livers", count = 1 },
        { name = "the Dissolving Liquid to the gnomish deserter", count = 1 },
        { name = "Fresh Chunk of Wooly Rhino to the Mist Panther", count = 4 },
        { name = "Errgriz a High Quality Dire Wolf Fur", count = 1 },
        { name = "the Wolf Fur Earcovers to Sojan", count = 1 },
        { name = "Nelet the Capt", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 5377, name = "Rough Silver Chain", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 40\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nNOTE: In order to complete this quest you will need the ability to Forage OR possibly have someone multiquest a foraged item for you (Multiquest not confirmed to work).\nOn the docks arriving into Iceclad are two gnomes, Nelet Durzit and Rendap.\nYou say, 'Hail, Nelet Durzit'\nNelet Durzit sneezes and wipes his hand across his nose.  'H-h-h-i.'\nRendap says, 'Nelet don't talk much anymore.  All this cold really gets to 'im.'\nYou say, 'what cold'\nNelet Durzit talks through clenched, chattering teeth.  'Y-y-yeah.  C-cursed cold.  Sh-sh-shot of gnomish pirate triple strength rum's all I need ta fix me up, Rendap tells me.  N-n-nilham lost it all, though.'\nInside one of the igloos in the gnome camp in Iceclad you can find Nilham the Chef.\nYou say, 'Hail, Nilham the Chef'\nNilham the Chef says, 'Ahoy, Bobbybick.  Welcome ta the brig.  I didn't get ta the 'B' section of my piratisms manual so I'm not sure what a brig is but I'm guessin' it means 'really small place without enough food or water.'  So, ya here ta stay or just visitin'?'\nUnknown how to coax the information out of Nilham from here as to the rum.\nYou say, 'what crate'\nNilham the Chef says, 'I'll be an aft port if I think anyone will ever see the crate and key again.  If by some act o' Prexus you do, then take them ta the Cap'n.  I'm sure he'd be thrilled to see it.  Just don't remind him I'm here cause he might let me go and make me work again.'\nYou say, 'What cat'\nNilham the Chef says, 'That was a nasty cat.  I dun think it was after us, though. I think it just smelled the fresh chunk of wooly rhino jerky I had.  It didn't do anythin' but knock us over.  I guess that's what it likes, walrus.  After it knocked us over it slipped away towards the bridge island like a ghostly mist.  I'm thinkin' I saw a glimmer in its maw while it was runnin' off.'\nThe Crate\nGnomish deserter can be found in the middle of Great Divide, on top of a mountain that sits above the wurm caves. He is sitting down at the peak and can be easy to miss.\nYou say, 'Hail, gnomish deserter'\nGnomish deserter smiles at you and nods congenially.  'Hullo there.  Nice ta meet ya.' He moves to shake your hand and then seems to remember that his hand is currently frozen to a very heavy, very solid hunk of metal shaped somewhat like a box.\nYou say, 'what is that box'\nGnomish deserter says, 'Huh?  Box?  Where's a box?  Heh.  I don't see a box.'\nYou say, 'how did you get your hand stuck'\nGnomish deserter says, 'Erm.  Well ya see.  One day I was on guard duty and a huge white cat knocked me over.  It looked like it was running away towards the bridge island.  Anyways, I fell into the water.  I guess I passed out because next thing I knew I was over near the gnolls laying on top of this huge box.  It's then that I made the decision.'\nYou say, 'what decision'\nGnomish deserter says, 'To leave.  I'm really tired of this pirate stuff.  Captain Nalot said it was gonna be great fun and an adventure but all I've seen is a lot of biscuits, slush water, and guard duty.  So I'm here.'\nYou say, 'how did you get here'\nGnomish deserter says, 'Yup.  This isn't such a bad spot.  It's nice and peaceful.  I can see for miles and every once in a while someone like you drops by to talk.  There's no guard duty and I don't have to say 'Arrrr' anymore.  That really starts to hurt your throat, you know.  The only problem I have anymore is my hand frozen to this box.  If ya find a way to fix it let me know.'\nFind Pythic Urson in Thurgadin.  He can be located inside the large bar in the northeast of the zone. You will need high Amiably faction for him to respond to hails but turnins can be done as low as dubious.\nYou say, 'Hail, Pythic Urson'\nPythic Urson turns and looks at you.  'What?' He goes back to drinking his ale and resting.\nYou say, 'what ale'\nPythic Urson says, 'Its a fine Coldain ale.  Good for quenchin yer thirst after a hard day of minin.  The ales name doesnt matter cause ya wouldnt be able to hold it down anyways.  Har har.'\nYou say, 'what mining'\nPythic Urson says, 'Aye.  Mining.  Im a miner.  Thats a hard one to put together eh?  Yer about as sharp as me hammer and as quick as the mining crud on me boots.'\nYou say, 'what crud'\nPythic Urson says, 'Mining crud, thats what I said.  Mixture o' velium dust, mud, and whatever other junk is left on the floor after I be minin.  Hard as a giant to fight off me boots.'\nYou say, 'boots'\nPythic Urson says, 'There used ta be a mixture we used ta clean off our boots but that was when we had more warriors ta get ta different places.  Now it aint possible so the crud just keeps buildin up on me boots.'\nYou say, 'what warriors to get to different places'\nPythic Urson says, 'If you think ya can get what's needed then go ahead.  The mixture used ta be made out of saps and acidic oozes.  You find some and bring it to me maybe I can slap it together.'\nThe items Pythic needs are Bladder of Acidic Ooze which is a small side quest out of Cobalt Scar and Fresh Tree Sap which can be foraged in either Wakening Lands or Plane of Growth.\nFind Qarrgy Scallopgobbler, an othmir located on the beach of Cobalt Scar.\nQarrgy Scallopgobbler sets down several large crustacean shells covered in foreign runes, then extends his large, coarse hands in a gesture of friendship. 'I am pleased to see friendly visitors to our villages. I am the head craftsman of the village. The crustacean shell armor worn by the warriors of our village was crafted by me and by my apprentices. I will craft other materials as well when they are available.'\nYou say, 'what crustacean shell armor'\nQarrgy Scallopgobbler says 'It takes awhile to make each piece. It has to go through a long burning process to clean away all old meat and dirt. Then it needs shaping and etching with runes.\nYou say, 'what burning process'\nQarrgy Scallopgobbler says 'Usually I use a mixture made from the livers of barraccudas. Their liquids are very strong and make good burning liquid. If you want some you need to bring me two barraccuda livers.\nBarracuda Livers are uncommon/rare drops off the \"a coldwater barracuda\" located just off the shores of Cobalt Scar. You will need two of them.\nGive Qarrgy TWO Barracuda Livers.\nQarrgy Scallopgobbler slams a knife into the various livers and squeezes out all of their various goos and juices. Eventually he seperates a bit of it and pours it into a protective bladder. 'Excellent work.  This is a good catch. Here, you have sack of ooze. Its good for burning things off or etching metals. Thank you for your help.'\nReceive: Bladder of Acidic Ooze.\nReturn to Pythic Urson in Thurgadin once you have both the Ooze and Tree Sap.\nGive the Bladder of Acidic Ooze Ooze and Fresh Tree Sap to Pythic.\nPythic Urson laughs at you and then takes the sap and bladder. He mixes the two together and then adds something from a small pourch he carries. With a quick sizzle he pours some on his boots and the crud melts away. 'See that? Didn't do anything but get rid of the crud. This stuff is great. It doesn't burn yer skin or valuables. Here ya go, you can have the rest.'\nReceive: Dissolving Liquid\nReturn to the gnomish deserter in Great Divide\nGive the Dissolving Liquid to the gnomish deserter.\ngnomish deserter grins and pours the ooze on his hand and the box. You hear a burning sizzle and then the box thumps onto the ground. 'Ow! Ow! Take it! Hah. I never thought I would get rid of that piece of...'\nReceive: Locked Rum Box\nThe Key\nFor this part you will need FOUR (4) Fresh Chunk of Wooly Rhino, these are rare drops from wooly rhinos in Eastern Wastes.\nMist Panther can be found in Wakening Lands, a bit south of the lake in the center. NOTE: This is not one of the many \"haze panthers\" that are found throughout the zone.\nGive 4 Fresh Chunk of Wooly Rhino to the Mist Panther.\nmist panther jumps at you and snatches the meat from your hand. It runs away from you and feasts on the other side of the water. As it runs away you notice a small shiny object fall from its mouth.\nReceive: Golden Broken Key\nSojan the Sleepless can be found in one of the igloos in the gnomish camp in Iceclad.\nYou say, 'Hail, Sojan the Sleepless'\nSojan the Sleepless stares at you through bleary eyes.  'I get enough conversation from my wife.  If ya want water or biscuits, buy em!  Otherwise, leave me alone!'\nYou say, 'what conversation from your wife'\nSojan the Sleepless says, 'Since ya like talkin', then fine.  You wanna do me a favor?  Go get me some wolf fur earmuffs so I don't gotta listen to ya, or her,  any more.'\nErrgriz is a gnoll that can be found in one of the huts southwest of Tower of Frozen Shadow in Iceclad Ocean.\nYou say, 'Hail, Errgriz'\nErrgriz says 'Errrr. You come for master, learning like me?'\nYou say, 'What are you learning?'\nErrgriz says 'I am learning ways of skinning and tailoring. None left but the master so I must learn to help. For now I only clean the furs.'\nYou say, 'You clean furs?'\nErrgriz says 'Yes. I clean the furs and then the master makes things from them.'\nYou say, 'What things do you make?'\nErrgriz says 'I wish I could make things. Headcoverings, to keep cold from head is what I want to make. I think I ready but not able to make until I get furs. Master says to find skin of high quality, thick and strong, but I have no training in hunting.'\nHigh Quality Dire Wolf Fur are uncommon drops from Dire Wolves throughout Velious.\nGive Errgriz a High Quality Dire Wolf Fur.\nErrgriz starts to cut and scrape the furs. He growls softly as he works and his master watches his progress. 'Grrr. Much too small. I fail. I not ready to work on my own. Sorry to waste your time. Here, take what I made. Maybe you can find use for it.'\nReceive: Wolf Fur Earcovers\nReturn to Sojan the Sleepless back at the gnome camp.\nGive the Wolf Fur Earcovers to Sojan.\nSojan the Sleepless stares at you and then laughs before putting on the earmuffs. As he moves around, blissfully protected from the noise, a fine chain slips from his coat. 'Hey! Look at that! What a fine chain! It looks familiar but I can't tell how. Oh, well, you can have it. It looks like it could be used to fill gaps or if needed to repair another similar metal object. I can do that if you ever find need.\nReceive: Fine Gold Chain\nGive Sojan the Fine Gold Chain and the Golden Broken Key.\nSojan the Sleepless puts a tiny eyeglass up to his eye and studies the key and chain. \"Aye, this looks like the perfect metal to fix this key. Gimmie just a moment.\" He uses fine and minute tools to pick and push the chain and key over a fire. \"Ha!\" Don't say I ain't never done anythin for ya. There ya go, Bobbybick.\"\nReceive: Rum Box Key\nWith both the Rum Box Key and the Locked Rum Box you are almost done.  Head to Captain Nalot in one of the igloos opposite of Sojan in Iceclad.\nGive Captain Nalot the Rum Box Key and the Locked Rum Box\nCaptain Nalot says, \"Land ho! That be me rum! Where did ya get that? Ah nevermind. Gimme those things. Just a bit of a turn here... and a pick there... and a twist... and she's unlocked, har! Here, take a jug. It'll be the least I can do fer ye. We'll be havin a party tonight lads!'\nReceive: Capt. Nalot's Triple Strength Rum\nReturn to Nelet Durzit down by the docks in Iceclad.\nGive Nelet the Capt. Nalot's Triple Strength Rum\nNelet Durzit greedily swigs rum from the jug. After a few drinks, he starts to gag and make faces. 'Oh geez! Rendap told me this stuff was strong, but this tastes like clockwork grease! It burns but now I feel - ugh.\nNelet doubles over and passes out on the ground. As he falls over, a small silver trinket slips out of his pocket.\nRenday points and laughs as Nelet falls over. \"That'll put hair on yer ears, boy. Suck it up. Least ya ain't shiverin' o' cold anymore, eh?\"\nReceive: Rough Silver Chain\nSubmitted by: Bobbybick, Kiritin, Nawak, Bulla, IventheassasinRewards:\n- Rough Silver Chain [item=5377]\n[",
