    {
      id = "1275",
      title = "Tunic of Riddosan",
      exp = "02",
      exp_name = "The Scars of Velious",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = 1300.0, x = 680.0, z = 0.0 },
      triggers = {
        "What more important task?",
        "I will be the knight.",
        "What assignment?",
        "What goblin source?",
        "What green river sludge?",
        "What portion of an experimental nature?",
        "Hail, Driana Poxsbourne",
        "deliver",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "you the fourth portion", count = 1 },
        { name = "her 3 x Reagent Pouch from Najena mages)", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 6451, name = "Tunic of Ridossan", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
        { name = "Bloodsabers", change = 2 },
        { name = "Guards of Qeynos", change = -1 },
        { name = "Opal Dark Briar", change = 1 },
        { name = "Priests of Life", change = -1 },
        { name = "Corrupt Qeynos Guards", change = 1 },
        { name = "Heretics", change = 40 },
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is a followup to the Cold Iron quest.\nFind Royal Guard Sheltuin at location 1300, 680 in Paineel.\nYou say, 'What more important task?'\nRoyal Guard Sheltuin says 'According to the evidence we've uncovered, it appears the kobolds are nothing but pawns to harass us. Or perhaps even all of Odus. If they wish to play these games, then we'll humor them. We'll take their pawn with one of our knights. Will you be the knight, ______?'\nYou say, 'I will be the knight.'\nRoyal Guard Sheltuin says 'Then you will deliver this chest for us. Don't worry about what's inside it. Although we enjoy our solitude, we do make allies. We also make use of those allies. We will do so now. Take the chest to Lyris Moonbane below the human city of Qeynos. You will then follow her instructions and complete any tasks she assigns you. In return, she will send you back with what we wish. Fear is our armor.'\nYou receive a Heavy Locked Chest.  Take it to Lyris Moonbane in the Qeynos Aqueducts at location 305, -445.\nLyris Moonbane examines the lock on the chest and pulls a black key from a pouch at her hip. The lock clicks open. Her eyes widen as she carefully opens the chest, revealing a pile of platinum coins and a small note. After admiring the coins she takes the note and reads it. The necromancer glances up, then at her spectral pet who then hands you a glass jar. She says, 'Are you ready for your first [assignment], Erudite?'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Thick Glass Jar, a 4-slot container.\nYou say, 'What assignment?'\nLyris Moonbane says 'We have just the thing for your friends back home. It will take some doing, but the pay off will be lovely indeed. In that jar you must combine 4 substances. You'll need two portions of a [goblin..source], one portion of [green river sludge], and one [portion of an experimental nature] that an agent of ours is working on. Bring the mixture back to me and we'll speak again.'\nYou say, 'What goblin source?'\nLyris Moonbane says 'The goblins of Antonica are known for their filthy habits and unclean practices. They often carry a menagerie of diseases and conditions. A more concentrated form of this aspect of goblin life cannot be found anywhere else but in the sewers of their citadel in the Sepent Spine. They must have workers who maintain the sewers. Find them and find the substance.'\nYou say, 'What green river sludge?'\nLyris Moonbane says 'The ogres of Oggok don't spend much time on sanitation, so naturally their kind harbors many diseases. This is easily apparent in the river that runs near their city, Greenblood. Down at the very bottom of the river is where the ancient plagues have come to rest and hibernate. Once the sludge is mixed in with the other substances, those glorious blessings of Bertoxxulous will most assuredly awaken.'\nYou say, 'What portion of an experimental nature?'\nLyris Moonbane says 'We have an agent studying in Freeport. Well, she actually isn't in Freeport proper but rather under it, in the sewers. Her name is Driana Poxsbourne. When you find her, tell her I have sent you for the substance. She will most likely have a task for you to complete before she can give you the fourth portion. Obey her.'\nYou can find Driana Poxsbourne at location 920, -1100 in East Freeport.\nYou say, 'Hail, Driana Poxsbourne'\nDriana Poxsbourne says 'Leave before I call the guard. Don't come back, Erudite.'\n[ Theoretically you need to say: [Lyris Moonbane sent me for the substance of an experimental nature]] I tried this at ally but same response.  She did take the 3 reagent pouches however at ally.  She will also take the pouches at apprehensive.\nHand Driana Poxsbourne 3 Reagent pouch.\nDriana Poxsbourne says 'Ahh, wonderful work, Rumrumm. Here is the substance...don't spill it! HAHAHAaahhahehehe...yes...you don't want to spill that, heheh.'\nYour faction standing with Bloodsabers has been adjusted by 2.\nYour faction standing with Guards of Qeynos has been adjusted by -1.\nour faction standing with Opal Dark Briar has been adjusted by 1.\nYour faction standing with Priests of Life has been adjusted by -1.\nYour faction standing with Corrupt Qeynos Guards has been adjusted by 1.\nYou gain experience!!\nReceive: Putrid substance.\nItem Lore: Upon examination you notice tiny bugs within.\nThe items you need are:\n- 2 x \"A vile substance\" (dropped by \"goblin janitor\" in Clan RunnyEye)\n- 1 x \"Green river sludge\" (ground spawn in the river in The Feerrott, near Oggok at +135, +705)\n- 1 x \"portion of an experimental nature\" (putrid substance) (given by Driana Poxbourne after you give her 3 x Reagent Pouch from Najena mages)\nAfter you get all four items, combine them in the Thick Glass jar and return the result (Sealed Jar) to Lyris Moonbane.\nLyris Moonbane's eyes light up with childish glee as she takes the jar containing the disgusting and deadly substance. From her pouch she removes a gob of putty and a gem carved into the likeness of a flying insect. After sticking the putty to the lid of the jar, she mashes the carved gem into the putty and hands the jar back you. She then says, 'This is the Harbinger of Bertoxxulous. When the gem is brought near the kobold lair it will enchant the substance. You must then [deliver] the substance.'\nReceive: Harbinger of Bertoxxulous\nItem Lore: Harbinger of Bertoxxulous\nYou say, 'deliver'\nLyris Moonbane says 'You'll need to find the source of the kobold water supply and pour the substance into it. Once you do that, the disease will infest whatever living organisms it comes in contact with so do yourself a favor and leave the area quickly. You can then take the empty jar to your master for your reward.'\nriver source is at location 355, -535 in the Warrens.\nHand river source the Harbinger of Bertoxxulous.\nYou gain experience!!\nReceive: Empty Jar\nItem Lore: Once held the Harbinger of Bertoxxulous.\nHand Royal Guard Sheltuin the Empty Jar.\nRoyal Guard Sheltuin says 'Well done, Rumrumm! Now we need only wait for the kobolds to start dying off and our plan will be complete. Should only take 8 years or so. One such as yourself will wear this ancient armor well. The Tunic of the crusader Ridossan is now yours. He shall watch over and praise you in your triumphs... your defeats on the other hand... well, never mind that.'\nYour faction standing with Heretics has been adjusted by 40.\nYour faction standing with Deepwater Knights has been adjusted by -40.\nYour faction standing with Gate Callers has been adjusted by -40.\nYour faction standing with Craftkeepers has been adjusted by -40.\nYour faction standing with Crimson Hands has been adjusted by -40.\nYou gain experience!!\nReward(s)\nTunic of RidossanRewards:\n- Tunic of Ridossan [item=6451]\n[",
    },
