      title = "Fusibility Research",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 55,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = 900.0, x = -1500.0, z = 0.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail Makil Rargon",
        "Who is Al",
        "Research?",
        "Fusible ores?",
        "Experiments?",
        "Fusibility test?",
        "Al'kabor",
        "research",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "you the Strength of the Elements", count = 1 },
        { name = "Makil Rargon the Full Crate of Fusible Ore", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 6989, name = "Strength of the Elements", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Time:** days\n**Level:** 55\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis quest starts in Western Wastes and is given out by Makil Rargon. When Makil is hailed he will talk about the fusibility of elements and ask you to bring him 4 items to combine in a box he gives you. After you combine the 4 items and hand the combined box back to him he will give you the Strength of the Elements. The 4 items that are needed are:\n-- Fusible Coral Ore - Off Phinigel Autropos in Kedge Keep\n-- Fusible Earthen Ore  - From An Animated Construct in the Hole\n-- Fusible Igneous Ore - Ground spawn by the large volcano in Sky Fire mountains around 900, -1500\n-- Fusible Velium Ore - Off a large air elemental named Guardian Kozzalym in Western Wastes.\nYou say, 'Hail Makil Rargon'\nMakil Rargon says, 'Greetings, _____. I am Makil Rargon, an esteemed Assistant to the great wizard [Al'kabor].  What can I help you with?'\nYou say, 'Who is Al'kabor?'\nMakil Rargon says \"Al'Kabor is the most powerful wizard on all of Norrath.  He is currently back to his Combine Empire research.  Being his most trusted assistant, he assigned me to follow up on his fusibility [research] findings.  Do you have any information to offer?'\nYou say, 'Research?'\nMakil Rargon says, 'Ah. Yes, his fusibility research.  Al'Kabor has been studying the melting point of minerals. Here. Take this journal. It explains what fusibility is.  Over the last few years, he has conducted several tests on [fusible ores].'\nReceive Fusibility Study: Part 1\nYou say, 'Fusible ores?'\nMakil Rargon says, 'An ore is considered fusible if it can be melted.  Now, this book explains the most unique forms of fusible ore that the master has conducted [experiments] on.'\nReceive Fusibility Study: Part 2\nYou say, 'Experiments?'\nMakil Rargon says, 'So far his research has been quite successful.  This journal explains what he has been able to accomplish.  He has managed to create several magical items including an artifactual scepter of great power.  While only he can grant permission to a worthy wizard to possess the artifact, if you are willing to help me complete a [fusibility test], I can offer you another item of great strength against the elements.'\nReceive Fusibility Study: Part 3\nYou say, 'Fusibility test?'\nMakil Rargon says, 'Very well then ... Fill this Empty Fusible Ore Crate up with four different fusible ores then seal it.  Bring me back the Full Crate of Fusible Ore and I will use the compound to create a magical item that was developed by Master Al'Kabor.'\nReceive Empty Fusible Ore Crate\nCombine Fusible Carol Ore + Fusible Earthen Ore + Fusible Igneous Ore + Fusible Velium Ore in the Empty Fusible Ore Crate to receive a Full Crate of Fusible Ore.\nGive Makil Rargon the Full Crate of Fusible Ore.\nMakil Rargon begins to examine the contents of the crate and proceeds to conduct an experiment.  He then turns toward you and says, 'Excellent job! As promised, here is one of Master Al'Kabor's fusiblity research creations.'\nYour faction standing with Temple of Sol Ro got better.\nYour faction standing with Shadowed Men got worse\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive 26 copper from Makil Rargon.\nYou receive 26 silver from Makil Rargon.\nYou receive 41 gold from Makil Rargon.\nYou receive 28 platinum from Makil Rargon.\nYou receive Strength of the Elements.Rewards:\n- Strength of the Elements [item=6989]\n[",
