      },
      factions = {
        { name = "Scaled Mystics", change = 5 },
        { name = "Legion of Cabilis", change = 1 },
        { name = "Scaled Mystics", change = 5 },
        { name = "Legion of Cabilis", change = 1 },
        { name = "Scaled Mystics", change = 8 },
        { name = "Legion of Cabilis", change = 2 },
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 3\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is a series of armor quests for newbie Iksar Beastlords. They are given out by Prime Patriarch Vuzx [npc=8441] in the upper level of the shaman guild of East Cabilis.\nFirst test of the Patriarch - Level 3\nYou say, 'Hail, Prime Patriarch Vuzx'\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'Greetings. I only train those who follow the path of the Patriarchs of Cabilis and have yet to develop their [powers] over the beasts of the wild, or maybe you are trained and are here to [help aid in our cause]?'\nYou say, 'What powers?'\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'A Patriarch of Cabilis must learn to survive the hard way, by heading into the wild lands and mastering the creatures that reside in them. First you must learn to defeat even the most insignificant of nuisances. Go from this temple and return to me with four Leech Husks that have been skinned from the creatures by your own claws.'\nBring him four (4) Leech Husk [item=2971] from Cabilis East or the Swamp of No Hope. They drop from swamp leechs and giant swamp leechs.\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'Well done young patriarch! I believe you are ready to face larger nuisances that prowl outside our city walls. Head out to the Field of Bone and return to me bearing three Spiderling Silks and a Scarab Carapace.'\nYour faction standing with Scaled Mystics has been adjusted by 5.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis has been adjusted by 1.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive Patriarch's Bracer [item=7382].\nSecond test of the Patriarch - Level 4\nWhen you bring the leech husks back from the first quest, Prime Patriarch Vuzx asks you to bring him back three (3) Spiderling Silk [item=3138] and one (1) Scarab Carapace [item=3100]. These drop in the Field of Bone from many beetles and spiders: Bonebinder Hatchling, Burynai-bane spider, bonecrawler hatchling, a carrion beetle hatchling, emerald scarab.\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'You have overcome sturdy yet unintelligent creatures that plague our kind. You are now ready to face our foes that are more intelligent than the insects you have defeated. We have many foes possessing a degree of intelligence, the least of these foes being the tribes of goblins that inhabit our Empires lands. Even now there are goblin watchers prowling just outside our gates. Locate four of these watchers, slay them and return to me with their Goblin Watcher Signal Torches.'\nYour faction standing with Scaled Mystics has been adjusted by 5.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis has been adjusted by 1.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive Patriarch's Cap [item=7380].\nThird test of the Patriarch - Level 5\nUpon completing the second Beastlord Quest, Prime Patriarch Vuzx asks you to bring him four (4) Watcher Signal Torch [item=3183]. They are found in the Lake of Ill Omen and Warsliks Woods on goblin watchers.\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'You have triumphed over the watchers, young patriarch, but they are among the weakest of our sentient foes. Mere fodder sent to warn to the more powerful goblins of an opportunity to strike. It is time for you to face the Goblin Hunters, and learn of our enemies the Sarnak, a species of dragonmen that once served the Iksar Empires of old. Journey to the wilderness and return with two Goblin Hunter Javelins and two Sarnak Broodling Fangs.'\nYour faction standing with Scaled Mystics has been adjusted by 8.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis has been adjusted by 2.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive Patriarch's Legging [item=7379].\nFourth test of the Patriarch - Level 10\nUpon completing the third Beastlord Quest, Prime Patriarch Vuzx asks you to bring him two (2) Goblin Hunter Javelin [item=609] and two (2) Sarnak Broodling Fang [item=21818]. The javelins are a fairly common drop while the fangs take a few more kills. Try around /waypoint +4715, -4236 and /waypoint +5248, -4696 in Lake of Ill Omen. These items are found on goblin hunters and Sarnak broodlings.\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says, 'Now you will learn of another enemy of the Legion of Cabilis, the frogloks. The frogloks from the froglok settlement of Krup often sent their tuk warriors to prey on unsuspecting Iksar citizens that venture outside the gates of Cabilis. Find these Froglok Tuk Warriors and return with four of their buckler shields.'\nYour faction standing with Scaled Mystics has been adjusted by 20.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis has been adjusted by 4.\nYou gain experience!\nYou receive Patriarch's Claw [item=7381].\nFifth test of the Patriarch - Level 13\nAt the successful completion of the fourth quest, the Prime Patriarch charges you with retrieving four (4) Froglok Tuk Buckler [item=21819] from froglok tuk warriors in the Swamp of No Hope.\nMissing dialogue and faction hits\nYou receive Patriarch's Leather [item=7556].\nSubmitted by: Dreadfist; Revamped by IventheassassinRewards:\n- Patriarch's Bracer [item=7382]\n- Patriarch's Cap [item=7380]\n- Patriarch's Claw [item=7381]\n- Patriarch's Leather [item=7556]\n- Patriarch's Leggings [item=7379]\n[",
