      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 8\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nIn order to do this quest you must have received a Wooden Practice Flail from the quest \"Cook Yalkiin's Worm Meat Broth\" or have bought one from a vendor in Shar Vahl.\nYou say, 'Hail, Captain Alim'\nCaptain Alim says 'Have you come for training young one?  The way of the Beastlord teaches many things about the forces of nature.  The [forces] in the thicket are very interesting.\nYou say, 'what forces'\nCaptain Alim says 'Yes, the force that compels a creature to adjust to their surroundings in particular.  The Saruek have seem to adapted to their environment very well.  I am studying the effects of their claws.   It seems the different [variety] of Saruek have special enhancements.\nYou say, 'what variety'\nCaptain Alim says 'Well, for example the Firefall Saruek can attack with claws that burn the flesh, the Deathmaw attack with poisonous claws, the shredder Saruek are especially skilled in fending off the Tegi that threaten them, and lastly there is a more uncommon Claw Beast that is very strong but does not appear that often.  I believe I could take their claws and affix them to a weapon to [enhance] it.\nYou say, 'how do I enhance'\nCaptain Alim says 'If you would like to test this theory, speak with my trainees, located behind me. I have taught them everything I know about making these clubs. Each trainee specializes in creating a different club, based upon the components they require. Return to them with the correct components, and they will attempt to fashion the claws to the flail.'\nAt this point you are directed to speak to the Captain's four Trainees; Jolneg, Ferdrin, Kylfa, and Shekar.\nNote:You will only be able to do ONE of these trainee quests per Wooden Practice Flail you have quested previously so choose wisely.\nYou say, 'Hail, Jolneg'\nJolneg says 'Hello there, young one, has the Captain sent you to speak with me about the [Deathmaw Club]?'\nYou say, 'Deathmaw Club'\nJolneg says 'Ahh, well, since you do not know of the Deathmaw club, then I will tell you about it. Captain Alim has taught me how to make this club. In order to make one, I will require three deathmaw claws, and a wooden practice flail. Return to me these components, and I will craft a Deathmaw Club for you.'\nBring Jolneg three Deathmaw Claws along with a Wooden Practice Flail in exchange for a Deathmaw Claw Club\nJolneg takes the flail and starts placing the claws into it forming a formidable looking weapon. 'This seems a good weapon indeed. Here, you can take it for helping to test my theory of weapon crafting. Safe travels to you friend.'\nYou receive a Deathmaw Claw Club [item=8024].\nYou say, 'Hail, Ferdrin'\nFerdrin says 'Welcome Hazan! Have you been sent to speak with me by [Captain Alim]?'\nYou say, 'I have been sent by Captain Alim'\nFerdrin says 'Excellent, I presume you wish to speak with me about the [Firefall Club]?'\nYou say, 'Firefall Club'\nFerdrin says 'If you provide me with three firefall claws, and a wooden practice flail, I am able to fashion them together into a Firefall Claw Club, for you to use.'\nBring Ferdrin three Firefall Saurek Claws along with a Wooden Practice Flail in exchange for a Firefall Claw Club\nYou say, 'Hail, Kylfa'\nKylfa says 'Greetings, young one, what is it that you [seek]?'\nYou say, 'I seek club'\nKylfa says 'Ahh, so you seek the Shredder Claw Club, aye? Indeed, I am the apprentice to Captain Alim who was trained to make that item. I will craft one for you if you wish to gather the [components].'\nYou say, 'components'\nKylfa says 'Return to me with three Shredder Claws, and a wooden practice flail, and I will attach the claws to the flail and create a Shredder Claw Club for you to use out here in the Thicket.'\nBring Kylfa three Saurek Shredder Claws along with a Wooden Practice Flail in exchange for a Shredder Claw Club\nKylfa takes the flail and starts placing the claws into it forming a formidable looking weapon. 'This seems a good weapon indeed. Here, you can take it for helping to test my theory of weapon crafting. Safe travels to you friend.'\nYou receive a Shredder Claw Club [item=8025].\nYou say, 'Hail, Shekar'\nShekar says 'I suppose you are here to ask me how to create a Claw Beast Talon Club? Yes, yes, I thought you might be. So many young ones looking for these, my poor claws are sore from all the assembly. Of course, I will make one for you, so long as you return to me with the correct [items].'\nYou say, 'items'\nBring Shekar one Claw Beast Talon along with a Wooden Practice Flail in exchange for a Claw Beast Talon Club .\nShekar takes the flail and starts placing the claws into it forming a formidable looking weapon. 'This seems a good weapon indeed. Here, you can take it for helping to test my theory of weapon crafting. Safe travels to you friend.'\nYou receive a Claw Beast Talon Club [item=8177].\nGathering claws is not an easy task.  They drop quite rarely off the appropriately named hoppers in Shadeweaver's Thicket.\nNeed completion dialogues, faction adjustments, and droprate information.Rewards:\n- Claw Beast Talon Club [item=8177]\n- Deathmaw Claw Club [item=8024]\n- Firefall Claw Club [item=11521]\n- Shredder Claw Club [item=8025]\n[",
