      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 55\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nNOTE: A patch on March 25, 2015, added a work-around to obtain items from Cazic Thule, Dread, Fright, and Terror:\nIn the Plane of Fear, a harbinger of Fear can help adventurers get their epic 1.0 pieces that would normally drop from Cazic-Thule or the golems. These pieces cannot be multi-quested or traded. In addition, a harbinger of Fear can advance the Whistling Fists quest in the same way as Cazic-Thule.\nYou must first do the monk shackle quests.  Once you finish with the steel shackle you need to do 3 tests.\n1. Newbie note hand in ( Else wise known as Shackle of Dust quest)\n2. Shackle of Clay\n3. Shackle of Stone\n4. Shackle of Rock\n5. Shackle of Copper\n6. Shackle of Bronze\n7. Shackle of Steel\n8. Shackle of Tynnonium\nThe first is in town with Grandmaster Glox.  Say \"I am Ready for the Trial of Agility\".  You then will have to fight him (he is light blue to a 59).  He drops the Mark of Agility.\nNext there is an Iksar Monk in Timorous Deep named Grandmaster Rinmark.  You tell him \"I am ready for the Trial of Patience\" and he will say that you will know when it's the time to attack.  Wait for a few minutes and he will change from GrandMaster to Master. Wait again and he will change from Master to just plain Rinmark. Kill him at that point.  He is a little thougher than Glox.  He drops a Mark of Patience.\nThe last test is in Kaesora.  You must have the shackle of Steel for this. Take this Shackle to the library and look for a mob on the second floor called Tome Keeper.  Hand him the shackle and he gives you a book (called what?).  There are different books, so this step varies depending upon which book you get.  The book tells you what item you need, where to get it and who to hand it to.  Get that item and hand it into the person it tells you to in the book and you will receive the Mark of Mind.\nOnce you have all 3 marks head to the Dreadlands and look for a monk named Veltar.  He is near the FV zoneline on top of the ruins in the desert area.  Hand him the 3 marks to get your shackle of Tynnonium.  Once you have that shackle head over to Cabilis.  Right next to the arena is an underground entrance and look for a monk named Marthor hidden in there at -352.00, -119, -52.\nYou say, 'Hail, Marthor'\nMarthor hiccups and breathes drunken breath in your face saying, 'Leave me be, can't you see that I am meditating or something?'\nYou say, 'I have the shackle of Tynnonium.'\nMarthor says 'Supreme Master Tynn was the only one that has even seen the weapon. I do not know its origin. I tell you though, you would need to be as powerful as he was to be able to wield the weapon. Only an Iksar of the last rung would be able to use it, come back and show me you have earned your Tynnonium Shackle and I will discuss with you what I know.'\nHand him the shackle.\nMarthor says 'You earned the Tynnonium Shackle? I am sure you wish to seek the fists of lore. Gandan has come as close as anyone, you would have to talk to him. Last I heard his expedition has taken him to the Howling Stones.'\nYou get the shackle back.\nHead to Howling Stones (Charasis).  Fall to the bottom near the entrance (+1 Safe Fall).  Find Gandan Tailfist feigning death at 278, -15, -175.\nYou say, 'Hail, Gandan Tailfist'\nGandan Tailfist places a foul smelling book in your hands and speaks to you slowly. 'Take this rotting book given to me by lord Cazic-Thule himself, I was given another but it has been lost. The search for the fists will be the end of me. If you are a monk of the final rung show me your Shackle of Tynnonium and I will share with you what I have found.'\nYou receive a Flayed Skin Tome..\nGive him your shackle, which you receive back.\nGandan Tailfist says ' The search for the fists has killed many so I hope that your strength is more than mine and those in the past. I was given this satchel by the lord Cazic-Thule. I have searched for the fists in this place but they are not here. I suggest you seek audience with our lord. Tell him that I have failed in my task. I am sure that he ugnnnnnhnnn.' One last look to you is given before falling completely lifeless to the cold stone.\nYou receive a Satchel of Flayed Skin.\nNow head to PoF and go up to Cazic (or the Shade of Cazic Thule) and tell him that Gandan has failed in his task. You will receive a book (called what?) that tells you what you have to place in the bag.\nYou then need to head to Feerott and talk to a new gnome necro named Annaelia Wylassi:\nYou say, 'Hail, Annaelia Wylassi'\nAnnaelia Wylassi says 'If you have nothing other than a hail to offer me you best move along, I need concentration to study these odd bones that I unearthed. Funny thing about them though, they seem to resonate a hum. Quite unusual, you probably aren't interested in that though.'\nYou say, 'I am interested in that.'\nAnnaelia Wylassi says 'Are you? I didn't take you for a necromancer. I tried to reanimate these remains but due to the vibration it was too unstable and collapsed. I have given up trying to animate them. I would need more supplies if I were to try again. I am too busy with other research to care though. If you are so interested you could go fetch the supplies for me. I suspect the bone structure is of a human, so I would need a vial of human blood. A jade inlaid coffin would be needed to perform the ritual in. Also a vial of clear mana to bind the bones with strong magic, and an essence emerald to complete the ritual.'\nGive her the four items and she gives you Resonant Bone Chips, which identify as \"Remains of Zan-Fi.\"\nThere is a small quest from the Cabilis monk guild that requires 2 torn halves for a note that you hand in to the master behind Glox and he gives you a Thin flute.  Take this flute and hand it in to Brother Balathin in the Dreadlands and he spaws up as a pissed off version of himself -- lvl 61 and hits for a max of 240 and can be slowed.  Once killed he drops another flute.  That is your second piece.\nNow head to Sebilis in the crypt area and look for a skeleton named a fallen monk [npc=10044].\nYou say, 'Hail, a fallen monk'\nA fallen monk says, 'Failed to find the rest I have. If you wish what is mine then give proof of the shackle unto me.\"\nHand him in your Shackle of Tynnonium [item=8957].\nfallen monk says, \"Earn what is mine. Show me when you have the power worthy to wield what i posses.'\nIt will keep it and respawn as a fallen iksar master [npc=18254]. Kill it and and loot Faintly Glowing Fist [item=25941]. That is the 3rd item.\nThe last piece is hard to get since you have to do the stupendous tome quest (see the write-up for the Crusader's Test of the Lord [quest=1202] quest).  Once you have that done, head to Trakanon's Teeth with the book and a Crusaders Coffin(Sold in Cabilis).  Hand them in to Crusader Vragor (spawns at around n2800 p2785).\nYou say, 'Hail, Crusader Vragor'\nCrusader Vragor says 'Perhaps you would care to hear a tale, and perhaps you could help me with the ending. it is the tale of the end of Grandmaster Tynn. We all know that Tynn came into Sebilis with no rebirth. I suppose you know he created the caste of Iksar monks, but I doubt you know where he now rests do you?'\nYou say, 'No, I do not.'\nCrusader Vragor says 'Then I shall tell you. Master Tynn chose a place of rest in his old age. While deep in meditation he slipped away and breathed no more. His corpse remained in teh stance of meditation for many years unyielding to the elements. This brings us to recent times. A Trakanasaur that has been named Zhaoku came along the remains and devoured them. The bones too hard to be chewed, he swallowed them whole. To this day he wanders with them lodged in his stomach. Are you interested in knowing where Zhaoku is?'\nYou say, 'Yes, tell me!'\nCrusader Vragor says 'I will tell you but you must help me first. I have been tied to this plane because of deeds unfinished. I was questing for the stupendous tome for ages to no avail. Without this tome I can not pass on in peace. finish my quest, bring me the stupendous tome and a crusader coffin. I will tell you where the beast rests before I pass on. I doubt you can finish this, but i can always hope.'\nHand him the items he seeks.\nCrusader Vragor says 'The tome! I can finally pass on in peace. Before i go I will tell you that Zhaoku rests to the east of here near Old Sebilis. He is gigantic and not easily missed.' Crusader Vragor vanishes into a mist, his sigh of relief the only thing left behind.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou gain experience!!\nHe will then spawn a lvl 59 Giant Dino named Zhaoku.  Kill him and he will drop Thule Touched Bones and some rare spells.  Those bones ID as the Remains of Tynn.\nCombine all the bones in the bag and you will get the satchel of Cazic Thule.  Then take the bag and the 2 tomes back to Cazic Thule and you receive the Whistling fists.\n\"Cazic-Thule seems pleased at the amount of pain that you have been able to inflict. Cazic-Thule then grabs your hands and begins to infuse them with his power. Your hands burn like they were placed in lava for a moment, then feel cool as ice. You can feel the sheer power flowing through your new weapons of pain.\"\nNeed all dialogues, faction hits if any, minimum required faction to get quest, missing quest mobs/steps, /loc of quest mobs, drop information, missing names of quest items, etc.Rewards:\n- Whistling Fists [item=10340]\n[",
    },
