      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 55\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nHand Loremaster Solstrin your Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl (Mark 1).\nLoremaster Solstrin says 'Incredible! Never before has an outlander been skilled and determined enough to craft our sacred rune. You are now worthy of the Dain's most perilous task. You should seek an audience with the Dain immediately. Show him your Runed Prayer Shawl; he will give you the task that has been prepared for you. If the Dain is away show your Shawl to Chamberlain Krystorf and he will call for him.'\n- Receive Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl (Mark 1) and an Empty Coldain Issue Kit.\nDain's Chamber - Icewell Keep\n(note: This step is not required, if you spawn Dain, you may not respawn him later)\n- Give Chamberlain Krystorf the Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl (Mark 1) if the Dain is not spawned. This can only be done ONCE.\n- Receive Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl (Mark 2) - (To prevent respawning of Dain)\nChamberlain Krystorf says 'One moment the Dain has been waiting for you. I will call for him.. oh here he is now, show your shawl to him.'\n- Hand the Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl Shawl to Dain Frostreaver IV.\nDain Frostreaver IV says 'Ah Trewayn. I was hoping to see you. We require your skilled hand. The Armory is overtaxed preparing armor for the war that we are preparing to wage on the Kromzek. We need you to help them by creating some Field Plate for a mission that is near to execution. Go see Loremaster Solstrin in the Hall of Ancestors, give him these orders. He holds the lore recorded on how to make the field plate. Return to me when you have completed a Standard Issue Kit.'\n- Receive Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl (Mark 2)\nReceive set of orders for Solstrin.\nHall of Ancestors - Icewell Keep\n- Give the orders to Loremaster Solstrin.\nLoremaster Solstrin says 'So, the Dain needs your assistance with the Field Plate. The Dain must trust you a great deal to impart the wisdom of our armor creation to you. Here are the tomes. The first details how to make the basic armor, the other details how to begin [working with gemstones]. If the Dain is asking you for them you should place them in an [Issue Kit].\nMay Brell guide your hand friend, good luck to you.'\n- Receive Forge of Icewell Arms and Precious Gem Study.\nYou say, 'Working with gemstones?'\nLoremaster Solstrin says 'Aye, gems are placed within the armor. Brell is pleased with this fusion of ore and gem. The combination produces a sturdy piece of armor. You will need some Etching Tools to work with the gems. If you ask Meg Tucter for a set, she should have some lying about.'\nYou say, 'An Issue Kit?'\nLoremaster Solstrin says 'The Standard Issue Kit is what we issue to soldiers at the beginning of their mission. I have this empty one here. Place a complete set of Imbued Royal Velium Armor into it before you give it to the Dain.'\n- Receive Issue Kit, an 8-slot container with a combine button. Holds large items and is LORE MAGIC and NO DROP\nJewelry Shop - Thurgadin\nYou say, 'I need a set of Etching Tools'\nMeg Tucter says 'Oh, really? There are not many around that work in faceting gems. I am surprised to see your interest. You can have this old set of mine. There is no need to return them, Talem recently made me a new sturdy set. Brell bless him.'\n- Receive \"Tools\". Make the armor, put in issue kit, hit combine.\nRecipes:\n- Combine in Tailoring Kit: (Recipe)\nVelium Hound Fur + Silver Thread\nThis makes Soft Fur Padding (Tailoring 176)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\n3 Small Piece of Velium + Coldain Velium Temper\nThis makes Small Brick of Velium (Smithing 30)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\n3 Small Brick of Velium + Coldain Velium Temper\nThis makes Large Brick of Velium (Smithing 27)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe [item=49834])\n3 Large Brick of Velium + Coldain Velium Temper\nThis makes Block of Velium (Smithing 30)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\nLarge Brick of Velium + File + Coldain Velium Temper\nThis makes 2 Velium Rings (Smithing 49)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\nBlock of Velium + Coldain Velium Temper + Velium Smithy Hammer\nThis makes Forge-Folded Sheet of Velium (Smithing 42)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe [item=11996])\nVelium Rings + 1 Forge-Folded Sheet of Velium + Soft Fur Padding + Velium Smithy Hammer + Plate Bracer Mold\nThis makes Royal Velium Bracer (Smithing 178)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\nVelium Rings + 1 Forge-Folded Sheet of Velium + Soft Fur Padding + Velium Smithy Hammer + Plate Boot Mold\nThis makes Royal Velium Boots (Smithing 176)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\nVelium Rings + 2 Forge-Folded Sheet of Velium + Soft Fur Padding + Velium Smithy Hammer + Plate Vambrace Mold\nThis makes Royal Velium Vambraces (Smithing 178)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\nVelium Rings + 2 Forge-Folded Sheet of Velium + Soft Fur Padding + Velium Smithy Hammer + Plate Gauntlet Mold\nThis makes Royal Velium Gauntlets (Smithing 178)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\nVelium Rings + 2 Forge-Folded Sheet of Velium + Soft Fur Padding + Velium Smithy Hammer + Plate Helm Mold\nThis makes Royal Velium Helmet (Smithing 178)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\nVelium Rings + 3 Forge-Folded Sheet of Velium + Soft Fur Padding + Velium Smithy Hammer + Breastplate Mold\nThis makes Royal Velium Field Plate (Smithing 187)\n- Combine in Forge: (Recipe)\nVelium Rings + 3 Forge-Folded Sheet of Velium + Soft Fur Padding + Velium Smithy Hammer + Plate Greaves Mold\nThis makes Royal Velium Greaves (Smithing 187)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nUnrefined Diamond + Etching Tools\nThis makes Faceted Diamond (Jewelcraft 182-184)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nUnrefined Emerald + Etching Tools\nThis makes Faceted Emerald (Jewelcraft 173-177)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nUnrefined Sapphire + Etching Tools\nThis makes Faceted Sapphire (Jewelcraft 173-177)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nRoyal Velium Bracer + Faceted Sapphire + Etching Tools\nThis makes Imbued Royal Velium Bracer (Jewelcraft 177-182, need 2)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nRoyal Velium Boots + Faceted Emerald + Etching Tools\nThis makes Imbued Royal Velium Boots (Jewelcraft 177-182)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nRoyal Velium Vambraces + Faceted Sapphire + Etching Tools\nThis makes Imbued Royal Velium Vambraces (Jewelcraft 177-182)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nRoyal Velium Gauntlets + Faceted Emerald + Etching Tools\nThis makes Imbued Royal Velium Gauntlets (Jewelcraft 177-182)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nRoyal Velium Helm + Faceted Emerald + Etching Tools\nThis makes Imbued Royal Velium Helm (Jewelcraft 177-182)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit: (Recipe)\nRoyal Velium Field Plate + Faceted Diamond + Etching Tools\nThis makes Imbued Royal Velium Field Plate (Jewelcraft 177-182)\n- Combine in Jewelry Kit:  (Recipe)\nRoyal Velium Greaves + Faceted Diamond + Etching Tools\nThis makes Imbued Royal Velium Greaves (Jewelcraft 177-182)\nDain's Chamber - Icewell Keep\n- Give Chamberlain Krystorf the Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl (Mark 1) if the Dain is not spawned.\n- Receive Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl (Mark 2) - (To prevent respawning of Dain)\nChamberlain Krystorf says 'One moment the Dain has been waiting for you. I will call for him.. oh here he is now, show your shawl to him.'\n- Hand the Coldain Standard Issue Kit which you created to Dain Frostreaver IV.\nDain Frostreaver IV says 'Excellent work Adorean. If I didn't know I would assume this was made by our most skilled artisans. You must hurry, General Bragmur has formed camp in Iceclad. Take the kit to the General, he had to drudge forward without any armor. His [mission] must be a success if we hope to successfully defend Thurgadin against the Giants.'\n- Receive two items: Approved Issue Kit and Expedition Orders.\nYou say, 'What mission?'\nDain Frostreaver IV says 'After General Bragmur has equipped the armor you have created for him, give him these orders. He is a skilled diplomat and will need to reach the pirate Gnomes. We must enter into a pact with them. We will supply them with the velium that they need to build their silly gadgets, and they will take their ship back to Antonica and call for reinforcements from our ancestors. We hope they will accept this pact, after all Brell has been known to align himself with Bristlebane whom the Gnomes of Iceclad follow. You may be an important [factor] in their success'\nYou say, 'What factor?'\nDain Frostreaver IV says 'I fear that spies lurk in every corner. You may need to help the General reach the gnomish camp if the Kromrif has gotten word of our efforts. You should call on any allies that you have to assist in case they ambush you. Brell bless you Adorean, good luck.'\nIceclad Ocean\n- Find General Bragmur at location -3400, +9000.\nYou say, 'Hail, General Bragmur'\nGeneral Bragmur says 'Please keep yer voice down I am busy here. If you do not mind I would ask that ya kindly leave.'\n- Hand General Bragmur the Approved Issue Kit.\nGeneral Bragmur begins to put the  armor, 'Finally the Dain has gotten word of my arrival here. I await his final orders before proceeding.'\n- Hand General Bragmur the Expedition Orders.\nGeneral Bragmur says 'The final orders, follow me closely! I pray that the Kromrif have not learned of our plans to allign with the gnomes.'\nYou will face 5 Encounters.\nFirst Encounter: -3550 +7550\nCommander Vjorik shouts 'The tracking wolves have found the Coldain! To the South West, Charge him!'\nFour Kromrif Tracking Wolves spawn and attack. These cannot be snared or rooted. Unsure about stuns or mezzes. The wolves are not difficult.\nThe Tracking Wolf Coller drops here.\nAfter the fight the General heads to the north again.\nSecond Encounter: -2200 +7250 (right next to the stone building)\nFour Frost Giant Skirmishers spawn and attack. They hit for a max ~178 and are again easily dispatched.\nThe Spiked Velium Mallet drops here.\nAfter the fight, the General heads northeast.\nThird Encounter: -1100 +5950 (by one of the square dragon pillars)\nCommander Kvarid and three Frost Giant Skirmishers spawn and attack. (They spawn on the General.) They cannot be stunned, mezzed, rooted or snared. The Frost Giant Skirmishers are level 55 and Commander Kvarid is 57.\nCommander Kvarid's corpse shouts 'Arghhhh! Though you have felled me your plans shall not succeed! Rallos will destroy you all for invading our lands!'\nThe Ice Forged helmet drops here.\nAfter the fight, the General heads northeast.\nFourth Encounter: +1500, +2250 (near Tower of Frozen Shadow)\nFive Kromrif Tracking Wolves spawn and attack.\nThe Drakkel Wolf Claws drop here.\nFifth Encounter: +3700, +2650 (the lone tree on the hill)\nCommander Vjorik and five Frost Giant Skirmishers spawn and attack. (They spawn on the General.)\nThe Snowchipper drops here.\nAfter the fight, the General heads to the pirate island.\nIceclad Dock\nGeneral Bragmur says 'Lo there gnomes! Tell me is your camp located nearby?'\nRatop says 'Yar ye scruvy bearded dwarf, just over tha hill there.'\nRitap says 'Arrrrrrrrrrr!'\nIceclad Pirate Encampment\nCaptain Nalot says 'Hrm? Who is scuffin' around out here?'\nGeneral Bragmur says 'Greetings Captian Nalot, I have come to you with a proposition to make.'\nCaptain Nalot says 'Arrrrrr what is it ye want?'\nGeneral Bragmur says 'Well ya see sir, we have a surplus of Velium that we would not mind sharing with you for yer tinkerin' but would ask a favor in return for it.'\nCaptain Nalot says 'Velium eh? Well there matey lets hear what you have got to say!'\nGeneral Bragmur says 'I represent the Dain in this matter, we would like for you to use yer Icebreaker there to head to Antonica and bring reinforcements for the war that is preparing to ensue. We are needin' all the help we can get against the Kromrif.'\nAdisson Stubblechin says 'Don't be thinkin' I was forgettin' ya, Nilham, ya spotty-faced salt licker. Remember, ya tell us where ya put our rum, an' we let ya out. Otherwise, ya have ta stay here!'\nAvatar of Below 's voice echoes through the area. 'The efforts to help the Coldain and bring them together with the gnomes of Iceclad is quite impressive. There will be no doubt that they will continue to increase in power until they can overtake the Giants of Zek. Hey there, what is that on your shoulder?'\nYou say, 'Its a runed coldain prayer shawl'\nAvatar of Below says 'So it is the sacred rune of the Coldain. Let me have a closer look at it.'\n- Hand the Avatar of Below the Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl.\nAvatar of Below holds the shawl up close to one eye to look at the rune sewn into it. He smiles to himself and then drops it to the ground and places one hand on it. A bright blue glow starts to emanate in the snow, then there is a sudden flash! The Avatar has dissipated. All that is left behind is the Shawl lying in the snow, shimmering with a new power. Pirotess slowly bends down to pick it up, and is infused with a blessing from Brell.\n- Receive Blessed Coldain Prayer Shawl.\nGeneral Bragmur says 'I must go tell the Dain of these events immediately!'\nCaptain Nalot scratches his head, 'Yar ya do that ya crazy Coldain.'Rewards:\n- Blessed Coldain Prayer Shawl [item=11999]\n- Drakkel Wolf Claws [item=12002]\n- Ice Forged Helmet [item=12003]\n- Runed Coldain Prayer Shawl [Approved by the Dain]\n- Snowchipper [item=12001]\n- Spiked Velium Mallet [item=12000]\n- Tracking Wolf Collar [item=12307]\n[",
