      },
      walkthrough = "**Time:** 5 hours\n**Level:** 45\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAsk the guy who sells books in the monk guild, 'What lost book of the scale?' He will say some stuff about the lost records of talon and his life, and give you the book\nof scale.  Here is the part about the shackle sash and shuriken: \"...ripping the shackle from his wrist, Talon gave it to Kiraikuei, telling him he must return it to the courtyard at any costs, including his life...Talon removed a small knife, and began to cut away the sash from his waist, letting his robe become loose, turning to Kiraikuei, Talon placed the chords of soild power around Kiraikuei...Talon fell to the ground, feeling his life draining slowly.  He scrounged through his tattered belt pounches, and removed a Shuriken of imense power. Using his last bit of strength, he thrusted the Shuriken deep into a diamond, and told Kiraikuei to bring it to the ones who guarded the gates of the peaks...\nGrand Master Glox holds the shackle, returned to him by kira.  He needs the gem of yet to come and the broken piece of the key to open the box holding the shackles.  Both camoe from lake of ill omen.  The gem drops off the Sarnak Gem Oracle in Lake of Ill Omen, and the key drops from the head bloodgill.  When you give them to him, Grand Master Glox attempts to open the box, but time has rusted the lock. He needs a skeleton key which is being guarded by Venril in Karnor's Castle. Rewards:\n[",
    },
