      },
      walkthrough = "**Time:** 360\n**Level:** 15\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nNoxhil needs someone to be a courier. He wants you to seek out three individuals and ask them if they have [any messages for Neriak].  The first person is Kizdean Giz located in the Western Commonlands. The second person Cytodl Krish, is on the second floor of the Inn that is NE of the entrance to the High Hold Keep. I'm not sure where the third one is.\nNeed all dialogues, faction hits, quest items, /loc of quest mobs, list of quest rewards.\nKizdean Gix roams in Commonlands.\nYou say, 'Hail, Kizdean Gix'\nKizdean Gix says, 'If you have business then out with it! If not, then please be gone. I have little time to waste on chitchat!'\nYou say, 'any messages for neriak'\nIf you do not have the correct version of Kizdean:\nKizdean Gix says, 'Inform the Dead that I have no further information at this time. I shall continue with my work as directed. Please return regularly, for I am expecting to break new ground.'\nIf you have the correct version of Kizdean:\nKizdean Gix says, 'It's about time a courier reached these wastelands of humanity. I have urgent news for the Dead. Take this message at once. Let no one stop you. Be on the lookout for the Feir'Dal [Silent Watch]! They have learned of our quest.'\nReceive: Sealed Letter [Letter To Loveal Of The Dead]\nYou say, 'What Silent Watch?'\nKizdean Gix says, 'The Koada'Dal have created an elite band of paladins, greater even than our own Teir'Dal Dragoons. They exist on the edge of righteousness. They will perform despicable acts in the name of their deity, barely skimming the edge of evil.'\nLoveal S`Nez is a shadowknight guildmaster in Neriak Third Gate. Hand Loveal the Sealed Letter [Letter To Loveal Of The Dead]\nLoveal S`Nez says, 'I see my expeditionary unit has encountered problems. I must send a dragoon unit to [Befallen] at once. I must not allow the Thex Mallet] to fall into the hands of some simple adventurer. Here is payment for your quick service.'\nYour faction standing with The Dead has been adjusted by 10.\nYour faction standing with Queen Cristanos Thex has been adjusted by 1.\nYour faction standing with King Naythox Thex has been adjusted by -1.\nYour faction standing with Keepers of the Art has been adjusted by -1.\nYour faction standing with Eldritch Collective has been adjusted by -1.\nYour faction standing with Primordial Malice has been adjusted by -20.\nYou gain experience!\nYou receive 4 copper from Loveal S`Nez.\nReceive: 2 Bandages, 2 Iron Rations, Torch\nYou say, 'Befallen'\nLoveal S`Nez says, 'Long ago, Befallen was a military outpost of the Koada'Dal. When they fled this continent for Faydwer, they hastily abandoned the place. All save Commander Windstream. He and a few stayed on to seek the lost [Thex Mallet]. All that is known is that he never found it. In the centuries since, Befallen has become a haven for the undead.'\nYou say, 'Thex Mallet'\nLoveal S`Nez says, 'All you can know is that the Thex Mallet is desired by our Queen. If we are not successful in its retrieval, it will be our heads which adorn her trophy room. We have learned its location and believe it to be broken into three separate pieces.'\nYou say, 'Who is our Queen?'\nLoveal S`Nez says 'The Queen of the Teir'Dal is the most powerful of all. It is she who should sit on the throne and not King Naythox. The Dead are her humble servants. We await the day when she shall finally take her rightful position as ruler of Neriak.'\nYou say, 'Who is King Naythox?'\nLoveal S`Nez says 'A competent and powerful warrior, but a warrior nonetheless. He has suppressed the true glory of the Teir'Dal. Perhaps it is time for a new ruler of Neriak.'\nCytodl K`rish is upstairs in the Golden Roosters in Highpass Hold.\nYou say, 'Hail, Cytodl K`rish'\nCytodl K`rish says, 'What do you want? I have no reason to waste my time with the likes of you!'\nYou say, 'any messages for neriak'\nCytodl K`rish says, 'Yes! Yes, of course. I have been waiting for you. The last four couriers made the mistake of asking the High Keep Guards for directions. Now they are breathing dirt, six feet under. Take this to Neriak at once.'\nReceive: Sealed Letter [Letter To Loveal Of The Dead].\nIt is the same letter that is given by Kizdean Gix and Loveal responds the same way.\nSubmitted by: Lord VormulakRewards:\n- Bandages [item=7944]\n- Iron Ration [item=7939]\n- Torch [item=10159]\n[",
