      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 18\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAfter completing quest No 3, Crusader Quarg says... \"The temple shall be pleased. As instructed by the Hierophants, here is your Iron Cudgel of the Mystic. You have done well that I must ask you to [collect the Crusaders of Rok Nolok].  Take this chest (6 slot).  Inside you shall combine the skull of their\nleader and at least five of the caste members (sound familliar). You then will go to the Swamp Garrison and deliver the full chest and your Iron Cudgel of the Mystic to Mystic Dovan. Go to him now and inquire of the Crusaders of Rok Nolok.\"  Mystic Dovan spawns after 9pm on top of the building with the warlord in Swamp of no hope and says when you inquire \"Mystic Dovan lowers his head in sorrow let us have a moment of peace. I cannot find the words to speak of the unspeakable act of the gods which took the lives of the legendary Crusaders of Rok Nolok. You must find the answers for yourself. All I can do is wait for their return.\"  The legend of Nolok says that he and his followers were shrunk down by a magical rain and that Nolok's head burns red.  You need to go to the first goblin ruins in Warsilik's Woods (when entering from Field of Bone) and hunt the Goblin Bloodtracers.  These drop the 5 glowing skulls you need. You also need to get one Lore glowing skull (also dropped by these goblin bloodtracers, but much more rare).  Combine the 5 skulls and lore skull in the box given by Dovan and return them to Donovan, along with your previous cudgel I think, and you will receive the Iron Cudgel of the Prophet. Rewards:\n- Iron Cudgel of the Prophet [item=45]\n[",
