      id = "2161",
      title = "The Crude Bone Altar",
      exp = "05",
      exp_name = "The Legacy of Ykesha",
      min_lvl = 55,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = -1460.0, x = 1046.0, z = 0.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Aqaar Aluram",
        "i",
        "What temple?",
        "What expedition?",
        "What first night?",
        "What visions?",
        "What black ooze?",
        "What happened to the others?",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "the phobonomicon to Aqaal Aluram", count = 1 },
        { name = "the phobonomicon to the living void", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 10438, name = "Amygdalan's Chain Mask", type = "item" },
        { id = 16239, name = "Book of Unspeakable Fear", type = "item" },
        { id = 49229, name = "Earring of Silent Screams", type = "item" },
        { id = 16240, name = "Horror Shard Blade", type = "item" },
        { id = 25964, name = "Loathsome Bludgeon of Depravity", type = "item" },
        { id = 14990, name = "Medallion of the Arcane Scientists", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 55\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis quest begins with Aqaar Aluram, located at -1460, +1046 in a camp with Eleann Morkul and Spanner Scrapsnatcher on the edge of a hillside...\nYou say, 'Hail, Aqaar Aluram'\nAqaar Aluram says 'Hail, traveler. May I assist you with something, or are you just passing through?'\nYou say, 'i'm just passing through'\nAqaar Aluram says 'Very well, friend. Please take care when passing beyond the river to the east. Several researchers and their mercenary escort passed through our camp en route to the temple. That was last week and they have yet to return. We are holding off on our expedition until we can learn more about what happened to them.'\nYou say, 'What temple?'\nAqaar Aluram says 'The temple of the lizardmen. The lost temple of Cazic-thule. It's just to the east of here... across the river.'\nYou say, 'What expedition?'\nAqaar Aluram says 'Several weeks ago, I received the news from M'lady Morkul that the Academy was researching this temple. It had been years since I last visited this site, so naturally I was interested. Of course, that was before we set camp in this accursed place. I must be honest; I was quite ready to leave after our first night here.'\nYou say, 'What first night?'\nAqaar Aluram says 'After securing the site, we set sentinels to alert us to any patrols or prying jungle eyes. Unfortunately, our magic did little to provide us with a night's rest that eve. The incessant sound of drums and the screams from within the temple had little regard for our lack of rest and already nervous disposition. Several times during the course of my slumber that night, I was taunted by foul visions of an unnatural sort.'\nYou say, 'What visions?'\nAqaar Aluram says 'My mind was filled with images of grotesque rituals. The lizards that inhabit that place were gathered around magical portals, chanting in a tongue too wretched to recall. As they spoke and danced, the denizens of some horrid void were pouring from the shimmering rifts! I awoke to find the others in the same state of horror! When I gathered my senses, I noticed that all of our equipment has been covered in some sort of black ooze, though our sentinels displayed no signs of having been triggered.'\nYou say, 'What black ooze?'\nAqaar Aluram says 'I really cannot recall much about the ooze. We have noticed that our memories seem to be affected by this place as well. I know that the ooze was present when we awoke, but it seemed to have been absorbed into the ground. It moved on its own volition. That is all that I can recall'\nYou say, 'What happened to the others?'\nAqaar Aluram says 'There was a story that floated about when I was a student. In summary, there was a tome of similar nature to the Phobonomicon. An ambitious mage recovered the tome from the possession of several faceless creatures in the Abysmal Sea. This mage reportedly went quite insane. The story claims that his last act of madness was to cast the tome into a living rift of matter. The rift then opened and released a creature of an unspeakable nature. This cured the mage of his problems... for good. That is why you should return all items of that sort to me.'\nYou say, 'What phobonomicon?'\nAqaar Aluram says 'A Phobonomicon, book of fear, is rumored to be creatable through the use of rituals and tools too disturbing to describe. Once the ritual or process is complete, the book will begin to take on its own... life, for lack of a better word. The book of fear is capable of unthinkable magic. Watch yourself, should you stumble into such a tome.'\nTo create the Phobonomicon, you need to collect the following items in Cazic Thule:\n- Crude Bone Altar (container from \"a Thulian High Ritualist\" at the top of the northeastern pyramid)\n- Black Powdered Incense (dropped by \"a Thul Tae Ew judicator\" in the Avatar pyramid)\n- Flesh Bound Tome (dropped by \"a Thul Tae Ew lifestealer\" in the temple area)\n- Tear Encrusted Obsidian Quill (rare drop from Thul Tae Ew bloodcallers, defenders, justicars, and zealots in the pyramid area)\n- Black Ooze Phylactery (dropped by \"a pool of black ooze\", common spawn upon death of Thul Tae Ew lizardmen mobs)\nThe Flesh Bound Tome is written in Lizardman, and reads:\nLike the mist that rolls through the jungles, the screams of the soft and terrified will fill the fields and hills of this land.\n-=The voids shall open=-\nPrimordial memories of things that rest in the darkness of ancient voids will force the screaming souls to look towards the Faceless for an end.\nHis will shall fill their minds like the mist the rolls through the jungle.\n-=This is the instrument of gathering=-\nThe black ichor of the Faceless brings life to its pages.\nDark smoke pours from the alter, like fear from the weak.\nA quill desecrated in terror will inscribe the summoning words.\nThe bones of the alter cast shadows of things to come in this ceremony of ancient rites.\nWhen combined, the summoning shall ensue.\nWhen cast into the living void, the Phobonomicon shall pull from the coldest void of Fear, an ancient horror of an age forced from the memory by terror.\n=============\nThul Tae Ew, the reign of blood will begin.\n=============\nWhen you combine the ooze, quill, incense, and tome together in the crude bone altar, it produces a \"Phobonomicon of Thul Tae Ew\". The Phobonomicon can either be handed in to Aqaal Aluram or turned in to the living void on the top of the northeastern pyramid.\nIf you hand in the phobonomicon to Aqaal Aluram, you receive the Medallion of the Arcane Scientists:\nAqaar Aluram says 'Thank you for returning this to us. I'll secure it until it can be returned for analysis. Please take this as a sign of my appreciation.'\nYou gain party experience!!\nYou receive 1 platinum from Aqaar Aluram.\nIf, instead, you give the phobonomicon to the living void, it summons a horror construct:\nA loud explosion sends ripples of energy through the air! Matter seems to lose its substance, but quickly solidifies. A shriek fills your ears, followed by the pounding sound of drums!\nThe horror construct spawns on top of the pyramid. It's rooted in place; hits for a max ~600; and casts \"Vortex of Horror\" (AE knockback) and \"Horrific Force\" (another strong knockback). Levitation effects are recommended for this encounter.\nThe construct's loot table (drops 4 items per kill):\nAmygdalan's Chain Mask\nBook of Unspeakable Fear\nEarring of Silent Screams\nHorror Shard Blade\nLoathsome Bludgeon of Depravity\nThulian Visage of Horror\nUntouchable Tome of Lunacy\nWailing Bone Mace\nWailing Bone Shield\n- Amygdalan's Chain Mask [item=10438]\n- Book of Unspeakable Fear [item=16239]\n- Earring of Silent Screams [item=49229]\n- Horror Shard Blade [item=16240]\n- Loathsome Bludgeon of Depravity [item=25964]\n- Medallion of the Arcane Scientists [item=14990]\n- Thulian Visage of Horror [item=25066]\n- Untouchable Tome of Lunacy [item=16243]\n- Wailing Bone Mace [item=16244]\n- Wailing Bone Shield [item=16230]\n[",
