      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 55\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is a ring event which starts in the \"bubble room\" of Cazic Thule.\nUpon getting in aggro range (about 50') of a Thul Tae Ew High Priest:\na Thul Tae Ew High Priest says 'Fools! It isss dangerouss to interrupt the sssacrifice! Guards, assssissst me!'\nGuard Khataruss attacks with eerie speed!\nGuard Scithiss attacks with eerie speed!\nGuard Thrasciss attacks with eerie speed!\nThree guards spawn. If you pull them out of his room and kill them, they will pop again when you go back into aggro range of the High Priest.\nUpon his death:\nYou have slain a Thul Tae Ew High Priest!\na Thul Tae Ew High Priest's corpse says 'Oh facelesss one, I have fallen! Pleasse avenge the death of your faithful ssservant!'\nThe High Elf laying on the ground wakes up after the priest's death:\nTahia Felwah says 'Brave adventurers, I am Tahia Felwah, and I owe you my life. I was to be a sacrifice to the faceless. Listen to my words carefully, there isn't much time now.'\nThe walls of the temple begin to crack as the ground beneath your feet shakes violently\nTahia Felwah says 'You have interrupted a complicated ritual and soon the rift to the Faceless will become unstable. I must collect three runes of the Faceless for my research. I have been appointed to uncover the source of these lizards' newfound power. If I fail, their kind will surely spread across the land and threaten the balance of Norrath.'\nThe lizards blow up:\na Tae Ew Justicar looks paniced as planar forces shoot through it's body\na Tae Ew Justicar looks paniced as planar forces shoot through it's body\na Tae Ew Justicar looks paniced as planar forces shoot through it's body\na Tae Ew Justicar begins to cast a spell.\na Tae Ew Justicar begins to cast a spell.\na Tae Ew Justicar begins to cast a spell.\na Tae Ew Justicar begins to cast a spell.\nTahia Felwah says 'This failed ritual presents a unique opportunity to gather the runes I desperately need. Recover the runes from the fallen minions of the faceless. When your need is greatest, hand me a rune and I will replenish you and your companions.'\nThe explosion stuns you as bits of lizard fly everywhere. You have taken 750 points of damage.\nThe explosion stuns you as bits of lizard fly everywhere. You have taken 750 points of damage.\nThe explosion stuns you as bits of lizard fly everywhere. You have taken 750 points of damage.\nEveryone turns into skeletons.\nAn unstable rift glows, and then dissipates\nA piercing, disembodied scream echos from deep within the temple. Your body begins to tremble uncontrollably with fear.\nAn unstable rift begins to cast a spell.\nThis is the Avatar of Fear spawn (2.5 minutes after the priest's death). He's untargettable.\nYou struggle with the desire to flee in terror!\nTahia Felwah says 'Prepare youselves! You must repel the denizens of Fear itself! Good luck brave souls, I will remain here until my task is fulfilled.'\nAvatar of Fear shouts 'Minions of fear hear me now! The temple of the great Cazic Thule has been defiled. I summon you to assist me in its cleansing!'\nFour minutes after the priest's death and 30 sec after he spawns, the Avatar of Fear starts to do a circle around the room. This seems to be the circuit that he'll do throughout the event.\nAvatar of Fear shouts, 'In the name of the faceless, I command you, the minions of fear, ARISE!\nExactly 6 minutes after the Avatar spawns, the first wave appears: ~5 spinechiller spiders.\nFurther waves consist of level 60 Gorgons, Shiverbacks, Spinechill Spiders, etc...\nThree Avatar mobs spawn, each after a certain wave. They correspond with the Golems in Fear (Dread, Fright, Terror).\nRunes drop during the event. Turning them in to Tahia Felwah gives everyone full health and mana.\nThe Avatar of Fear casts a dispell when you engage him.\nEach of the Avatars can drop loot.\n- Bladed Thulian Eviscerator [item=14792]\n- Boots of Hidden Terror [item=18977]\n- Dread Coronet [item=11411]\n- Fearsome Girdle [item=24832]\n- Feartouched Greatsword [item=13645]\n- Fright Imbued Battlestaff [item=11410]\n- Frightful Shroud [item=17794]\n- Mantle of Paralyzing Fright [item=13646]\n- Pearl of Dread [item=18960]\n- Ring of Dreadful Dreams [item=13647]\n- Scalecracker [item=21390]\n- Slime Crusted Shoes [item=24833]\n- Talisman of Fright [item=24512]\n- Terror Forged Short Sword [item=17439]\n- Terror Woven Wraps [item=24511]\n- Trinket of Ancient Fears [item=24831]\n[",
