      walkthrough = "**Level:** 30\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis quest begins in the Plane of Knowledge on the ï¿½goodï¿½ side. At one of the pools you will find Tratlan Jowyr and Wicas Adaolath.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tratlan Jowyr'\nTratlan Jowyr looks deeply into the pool in front of him, 'Well darn it! I still can't see anything in this blasted [pool], can you Wicas?'\nWicas Adaolath says 'Nothing at all.  Do you think that he led us astray?'\nYou say, 'What pool?'\nTratlan Jowyr glances up at you like he just noticed your presence, 'This pool.  There is supposed to be strong [magic] in it.'\nYou say, 'What magic?'\nTratlan Jowyr says 'Scrying magic.  These pools can supposedly glance into all of the knowledge past, present, and future.'\nWicas Adaolath says 'I think we should just do what [Tarerd] wants us to do.'\nYou say, 'Who is Tarerd?'\nWicas Adaolath says 'Tarerd is the one who told us about these pools. He wanted us to kill some sort of lizards for him, but we have neither the time nor energy for such adventures.  Perhaps you can get some information about the pools from him.'\nTarerd Gahar is at another nearby pool.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tarerd Gahar'\nTarerd Gahar says 'I'm sorry, I have neither the time nor the patience to chat right now.'\nYou say, 'Tell me about the pool'\nTarerd Gahar says 'Oh Tatlan and Wicas sent you did they?  I'll tell you what I told them, nothing is free.  If you want to know about the pools then I need something [from you] first.'\nYou say, 'What do you want from me?'\nTarerd Gahar says 'I'm sure it'll be easy for an adventurer as you. I am working on a potion, and I cannot currently travel to gather my last component.  If you could bring me the blood of a Sarnak I'd be willing to share what I know.'\nSarnak Blood is of course a random drop from nearly any Sarnak. You can probably find one at a merchant for sale.\nWhen you have it give it to Tarerd Gahar.\nTarerd Gahar says 'Ahh this is exactly what I was looking for. All the information I've gathered from these pools has come from Myrist. Thiran will give you the book I used as a reference. Give him this note so he knows I sent you'\nThiran is a Vicar he's on the first basement floor of the basement (go down one lvl when you enter.)\nYou say, 'Hail, Vicar Thiran'\nVicar Thiran says 'A dark day to you. New Tanaan has opened its arms to all of Norrath's travelers and scholars alike -- though still I doubt most are worthy of our infinite and unsurpassed knowledge. In any case, we all must uphold the laws of our city, else we become as debased and pathetic as the secular, warring cultures of the material universe. You will find that, despite the medium of our birth or the shadow of faith in our hearts, we are all equally tolerant of each being to approach us. Though I myself am no stranger to the duties of a mentor, I do not think that at this juncture, I would provide any useful assistance to any not of the many clergies associated with the pantheon. If you do indeed serve one of the gods of Nature and Influence, then my services may not prove a waste of our collective time. Search my inventory at your will, and purchase what you wish should you find anything of use to you at this point in your life of service.'\nGive him the note:\nVicar Thiran quickly reads the note, and says 'Tarerd wants me to give you that book?  I thought he wanted me to keep it secret.  Well no matter.' Thiran rummages through the books in front of him. 'Well this is unfortunate.  It looks like I loaned my friend the incorrect book.  I'm not sure where he's gone off to, here is the book he was looking for.  If you happen to run into Jeren Manri anywhere, he'll probably exchange this book for the book on the scrying pools.'\nThiran gives you a book ï¿½Goblins and their religionï¿½. This is the only clue as to where Jeren Manri is: In the Temple of Droga. His loc is +473.95, +1747.91, -252.16. Itï¿½s a very tiny room really a tunnel with fake walls on each end.\nHail, Jeren Manri'\nJeren Manri says 'Shhh, be quiet!  The goblins may hear you.'\nGive him the book that Thiran gave you:\nJeren Manri says 'Oh! Thank you, I assume this means that Thiran sent you.  I ran off with the incorrect book without thinking to check.  Would you be kind enough to return this to him?'\nYou actually do not return it to Thiran, the book has 5 charges of bind sight, but donï¿½t panic, thatï¿½s not the end. Go back to the very first guy you talked to, Tratlan Jowyr back in Plane of Knowledge, Good Side. Give him the book:\nTratlan Jowyr leafs quickly through the book.  'Thank you, it will take quite some time to go through all the information here.  Here is a little something for your troubles.'\nYou gain party experience!!\nAnd your reward is the:\nFine Cut, Diamond Inlaid Mask.Rewards:\n- Fine Cut, Diamond Inlaid Mask [item=16394]\n[",
    },
