      items_required = {
        { name = "him the antidote to get your charm reward", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 19563, name = "Charm of the Emerald Warrior", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Time:** Several Hours\n**Level:** 45\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Faerik Windrunner' (NPC by the PoD lift in Kelethin).\nFaerik Windrunner says 'Hello. I am afraid I do not have time for small talk I have a very important job to do here and unless you are [interested in helping] me please leave me alone.'\nYou say, 'I am interested in helping you'\nFaerik Windrunner says 'I didn't think I could get anyone to assist me with this, and you don't look like much but any help is good help. Allow me to introduce myself, I am Faerik Windrunner of the Emerald Warriors. I have been tasked with finding a party that is [willing to assist] us in investigating the disappearance of one of our own at sea.'\nYou say, 'I am willing to assist'\nFaerik Windrunner says 'I am very happy to hear this Fynder. I shall tell you what I know about this delicate situation. Gandak Whisperwind is one of the finest Emerald Warriors this town has ever seen. His weapon mastery skills are unmatched by anyone. Recently, his wife fell ill and there was a need for an antidote component that is grown by a well respected [farmer in the karanas]. Only if we receive these herbs from our friend in the karanas will Gandaks wife live.'\nYou say, 'Who is the farmer in the karanas'\nFaerik Windrunner says 'The farmer that I speak of is Tarnic McWillows, he runs a farm in the karanas that grows the herbs that we need for Lady Jernca`s medicine. So with that known we sent out 3 of our finest rangers and druids to obtain this herb and bring back the medicine but for the sake of if anything happened Gandak insisted to go along for the [ill-faded trip] because he loves his wife so very much.'\nYou say, 'What ill-faded trip?'\nFaerik Windrunner says 'Well it would seem that something went terribly wrong not long after they set out on their journey to the karanas. We know this for sure because sadly we found their boat that washed up on shore with all of the bodies of the original party on board, except for Gandak's. So with this knowledge it is that we hope and believe somehow Gandak is still alive and is either making his way to the Karanas or is just somewhere that we cannot find him yet. We have heard of a group of Pirates originating from a [fortress in the sea] that might be responsible.'\nYou say, 'What fortress in the sea?'\nFaerik Windrunner says 'There are many talks of a fierce and deadly troll pirate clan that calls themselves Broken Skull. They are claiming responsibility for many of these sea hijackings and I believe that if Gandak is alive he might be there. If you wish to travel to attempt to gain knowledge about his disappearance seek out the mystical boat that docks in the Stonebrunt Mountains. If you should find Gandak please give him this medallion that he will know has come from us.'\nFind Gandak Whisperwind in Torgiran Mines (random spawn in mines) and hand him the medallion.\nHe'll tell you to retrieve four insignias, all found in Dulak's Harbor:\nInsignia of Hatred: Drops from Emissary of Hate\nInsignia of Slaying: Drops from Emissary of Suffering\nInsignia of Suffering: Drops from a Windscorn Buccaneer\nInsignia of the Blackblood: Drops from a Broken Skull Guardian (possibly other trolls)\nReturn to Gandak and hand him the four insignias to receive an elven medicine bag.\nFind Tarnic McWillows in West Karana (-2270, -5540)\nand give him the elven medicine bag to receive an Antidote of the Wind.\nReturn to Faerik in Greater Faydark and give him the antidote to get your charm reward.Rewards:\n- Charm of the Emerald Warrior [item=19563]\n[",
    },
