    {
      id = "2414",
      title = "Aid Grimel No. 3 - Jewelcraft",
      exp = "02",
      exp_name = "The Scars of Velious",
      min_lvl = 60,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "I would like to put my jewel craft skills to the test.",
        "What bar of pure enchanted velium?",
        "I need a set of Etching Tools.",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "you the tools if you ask her", count = 1 },
        { name = "it to someone else", count = 1 },
        { name = "Aid Grimel the resulting ring", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 20198, name = "Wooden Signet", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 60\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAid Grimel is located at the top of the elevator in the Library in the Plane of Knowledge. Before you hail him, you must be flagged from killing Saryrn.  You must also have an unmodified skill >= 220 in jewelcraft.\nAt the end of the previous quest [quest=2413], Aid Grimel asked whether were willing to put your jewel craft skills to the test.\nYou say, 'I would like to put my jewel craft skills to the test.'\nAid Grimel gives you Etching Dust.\nAid Grimel says 'My hand was crushed when I used it to deflect a blow from a War Boar that was headed towards Taldarius's back. For some time afterwards my hand was crippled but Brell saw to it I regained full use of it. The ring I used to wear was damaged beyond repair and my hand was never steady enough to etch a new one. If you would make me a new one by combining a mounted blue diamond, the etching dust and etching tools in a jewelry kit. Then take the faceted gem and combine it with a bar of pure enchanted velium and my signet. I have no idea how the pure bars are made. You may want to seek the help of the ice dwarves.'\nYou must go to Thurgadin and hail Meg Tucter with the appropriate text.  Note that you will need at least apprehensive faction with the Coldain. Meg might be reluctant to talk to you if you have apprehensive faction but will still give you the tools if you ask her.\nYou say, 'What bar of pure enchanted velium?'\nMeg Tucter says 'Wow that is an odd request ______. Very rarely do we make an item that requires a pure bar of metal. Pure enchanted velium bars are made by combining three enchanted velium bars in a forge along with a coldain velium temper, pure water and a Coldain smithy hammer. Tis quite expensive but it enables the crafter to obtain pure working materials.'\nYou say, 'I need a set of Etching Tools.'\nMeg Tucter says 'Oh, really? There are not many that work in faceting gems. I am surprised to see your interest. You can have this old set of mine. If you are working with Royal Velium and want to give it to someone else, you can use these etching tools and your jewelers kit to engrave the piece for them. Be careful though, because once the armor is engraved you cannot remove it and it will be useless to the Dain. There is no need to return the tools, Talem recently made me a new sturdy set. Brell bless him.'\nMeg gives you Etching Tools.\nTo make Purified Water, combine one Celestial Essence with two Flask of Water in a brew barrel (trivial 66).\nTo make a Mounted Blue Diamond, combine two Velium Bar with one Blue Diamond in a jewelry kit (trivial 16).\nTo make a Faceted Blue Diamond, combine one Mounted Blue Diamond, the Etching Tools, and the Etching Dust in a Planar Jeweler's Kit or Jewelry Making Table (trivial 280-300).\nTo make a Pure Enchanted Velium Bar, combine three Bar of Enchanted Velium, one Purified Water, one Coldain Velium Temper, and one Coldain Smithing Hammer in a forge (trivial 255-300).\nTo make the special Velium Blue Diamond Ring, combine one Faceted Blue Diamond, one Pure Enchanted Velium Bar, and your Clay Signet in a jewelry kit (trivial 268-300).\nGive Aid Grimel the resulting ring.\nAid Grimel grins. 'Quite a nice ring you have made for me ______. May it serve me as well as my old ring. Here take this signet. We seem to be finishing the tasks on my list at a nice pace. Tell me when you are ready to use some clay.'Submitted by: FlevenRewards:\n- Wooden Signet [item=20198]\n[",
