    {
      id = "2420",
      title = "Protection of the Cabbage (Earring)",
      exp = "03",
      exp_name = "The Shadows of Luclin",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 130,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Rebecca Cabbageleaf",
        "What earring?",
        "scroll",
        "earring",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "it to me and I'll happily swap you", count = 1 },
        { name = "it back", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 15315, name = "Demi-Sec Champagne", type = "item" },
        { id = 12504, name = "Mistletoe Cutting Sickle", type = "item" },
        { id = 12096, name = "Golden Idol of Tunare", type = "item" },
        { id = 12729, name = "Blessed Fishing Rod", type = "item" },
        { id = 12327, name = "Star Ruby Encrusted Stein", type = "item" },
        { id = 20281, name = "Ceremonial Solstice Robe", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThere are ten Liber Brassica books in the game written in various languages.  Together, they give details on how to craft Xanthe's Earring of Nature (named after the first person to discover the recipe, Xanthe Ravenwolf).  The recipe also yields the level 59 Druid spell Protection of the Cabbage [item=20280] ; named after an insider running gag within the EQ community.\nCombine the following nine ingredients in a forge or New Tanaan Forge (no-fail combine, only use one of each):\n- Demi-Sec Champagne [item=15315]\n- Mistletoe Cutting Sickle [item=12504]\n- Golden Idol of Tunare [item=12096]\n- Blessed Fishing Rod [item=12729]\n-  Star Ruby Encrusted Stein [item=12327]\n- Ceremonial Solstice Robe [item=20281]\n- Lotus Pie [item=15488]\n- Misty Thicket Picnic [item=12802]\n- Lucky Cabbage [item=15111]\nThe ingredients require high tradeskill abilities to craft, but they're tradeable, so they can be purchased from other players if necessary.\nThe results are:\n1. Xanthe's Earring of Nature [item=12455]\n2. Spell: Protection of the Cabbage [item=20280] (Level 59)\nIf you are not a druid, or if you're after the Earring of the Solstice, go see Rebecca Cabbageleaf [npc=9395] in Fungus Grove at /waypoint  -1449, -803, -276 .\nYou say, 'Hail, Rebecca Cabbageleaf'\nRebecca Cabbageleaf  seems lost in thought and looks up only briefly from her work.  'Oh, hello ______, welcome to the New Thicket Inn!  If you'll excuse me, I'm a bit busy copying this [scroll].  I'll be with you in a moment to chat, or to trade if you've come about the [earring]'\nYou say, 'What earring?'\nRebecca Cabbageleaf  looks up again, 'Oh, have you come about the earring then? That's wonderful!  As you probably know, the druids have recently completed an ancient ceremony, and some delightful people who weren't druids were able to participate.  Sadly though, only druid's were able to use the Earrings of Nature that were created with the ceremony.  I've been collecting spare earrings of Nature from those who can't use them, and giving an Earring of the Solstice in return.  It's a good deal all around, as we both can benefit from the trade.  If you have an earring of Nature to trade, just give it to me and I'll happily swap you, and if you don't like it, you can give it back.'\nGive her your Xanthe's Earring of Nature to receive the Earring of the Solstice [item=12456].\nSubmitted by: Fleven ; Revamped by iventheassassinRewards:\n- Earring of the Solstice [item=12456]\n- Spell: Protection of the Cabbage [item=20280]\n- Xanthe's Earring of Nature [item=12455]\n[",
