    {
      id = "2596",
      title = "Free the Nurgan Slaves",
      exp = "05",
      exp_name = "The Legacy of Ykesha",
      min_lvl = 55,
      max_lvl = 130,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Rinnala Sweetsong",
        "home",
        "escape",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 55\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Time Limit:** 02:00:00\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nIn the Mines of Nurga, there are slaves of various races who wish to be set free. Each slave asks for three (3) items: Strong Restorative, Pouch of Supplies, and the Small Iron Shackle Key, which drop off Slave Driver Nimol, Taskmaster Yajo, and Overseer Pruckib. They appear to be on eight-hour timers.\nMake sure that you have pre-collected all required advanced quest items that the freed slaves offer, before starting this event. See quest entries: \"Vengeance of ... \". The freed slaves possibly despawn after an unknown amount of time. Depending on which slave you free, the rewards are different. Freeing a slave is only spawning an NPC (in a different zone) that offers a sub-quest with an item reward. The event itself has no other function or reward to offer.\nHanding all three items to any of the slaves, starts the slave release event. This may be a somewhat tough fight for a single group, but is certainly single groupable. It involves killing off 6 waves of 5 goblins that are somewhat tougher than any of the ones otherwise found in Nurga (they hit a little bit harder, mitigate slows, and have about three times as much HP). At the end, Mine Overseer Narrik spawns. When he is killed, the slave escapes and flees to his home where it offers another quest. A different slave will spawn to take the freed slave's place.\nNote that the ring event seems to be bugged at the moment, so that the prisoner may be freed even if you don't defeat this named NPC.\nKnown slaves:\n- Pungub Brawlum (Ogre male)\n- Xiokai Rissthrum (Iksar female)\n- Rinnala Sweetsong (Wood Elf female)\n- Rock Shaper Dritam (Burynai)\n- Crix Tzo`mok (Sarnak)\n- Wekland Greenfoot (Wood Elf male)\n- Osvima K`Matim (Dark Elf female)\n- Doovix Mruzzik (Iksar male)\n- Cenobite Pakclaw (Burynai)\n- Yimic Pxo`hab (Sarnak)\nAfter a server reset, Pungub Brawlum is the slave that spawns. Once Pungub Brawlum has been freed, Xiokai Rissthrum spawns in his place. The sequence is Pungub Brawlum > Xiokai Rissthrum > Rinnala Sweetsong > Rock Shaper Dritam > Crix Tzo`mok > Wekland Greenfoot > Osvima K`Matim > Doovix Mruzzik > Cenobite Pakclaw > Yimic Pxo`hab\nThis spawn order might not be correct. More info is needed.\nYou say, 'Hail, Rinnala Sweetsong'\nRinnala Sweetsong says, 'Hello. Do keep it down. If the goblins see you talking to me I will be punished for sure. It has been such a long time since I've been home. I've nearly forgotten the constant chirping of the birds there.'\nYou say, 'home'\nRinnala Sweetsong says, 'I used to call my home Firiona Vie but it has been a long time since I have even seen the sun. Perhaps you could help me escape?'\nYou say, 'escape'\nRinnala Sweetsong says, 'That is wonderful to hear! For me to escape I will need a small iron shackle key, a pouch of supplies, and a strong restorative. The key can be found on a nasty goblin named Pruckib. The supplies can be found on the Taskmaster Yajo. Slave Driver Nimol has the supply of the restorative that keeps us miners going. Be warned, though. I am sure the goblins will try to prevent my escape.'\nUpon handing the three items to the slave:\nRinnala Sweetsong says, 'You have done well thus far, now is the time to make my escape. Defend me!'\nYou gain party experience!\nYou gain party experience!\nAn alarm sounds summoning goblins to prevent the enslaved miner from escaping.\nA wave of 5 static goblins spawns around the pit where the slave is. When you kill the last of the goblins in the current wave, the next wave spawns immediately. The final wave (#6) includes Mine Overseer Narrik.\nYou have slain Mine Overseer Narrik!\nThe mine overseer and his minions have been defeated. An enslaved miner has been successfully freed.\nThe slave returns to their homeland, and a different slave spawns immediately in their place.\nNeed all dialogues, faction hits if any, fight information, slave spawn order, etc.\nSubmitted by: Nogili Razorclaw ; Revamped by iventheassassinRewards:\n- Freed slaves offer quests\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "260",
      title = "Bone Chips",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 130,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Trooper Mozo",
        "kill the decaying skeletons",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "Bone Chips", count = 1 },
        { name = "them to Trooper Mozo", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
        { name = "Legion of Cabilis", change = 1 },
        { name = "Cabilis Residents", change = 1 },
        { name = "Scaled Mystics", change = 1 },
        { name = "Crusaders of Greenmist", change = 1 },
        { name = "Swift Tails", change = 1 },
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nTrooper Mozo is guarding the entrance to Cabilis East in The Field of Bone.\n/waypoint -2559, +3566, +8\nYou say, 'Hail, Trooper Mozo'´\nTrooper Mozo looks upon you smugly.  'And what are you?  Some sort of adventurer.  Bah!  You will be shaken by the first undead you come across.  Wetting your pants you shall be.  Ha ha!  I doubt you could even [kill the decaying skeletons].'\nYou say, 'kill the decaying skeletons'\nTrooper Mozo says, 'You kill skeletons?!  I think not!  They will bounce you with no trouble at all.  Ten silver says you cannot collect four bone chips!  When Velious melts! Hah!'\nHunt decaying skeletons (in the Field of Bone) until you have collected four (4) Bone Chips and hand them to Trooper Mozo.\nYou offered 4 Bone Chips to Trooper Mozo.\nTrooper Mozo gasps in astonishment.  Wha...?  This!  But...  I...  Why you...  I oughta... All right!  A bet is a bet.  Here you go.  A few silver pieces for your achievement.  What?!  You thought I would give ten?  Fat chance!  Now get lost or I will haul you in for impersonating a froglok.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis has been adjusted by 1.\nYour faction standing with Cabilis Residents has been adjusted by 1.\nYour faction standing with Scaled Mystics has been adjusted by 1.\nYour faction standing with Crusaders of Greenmist has been adjusted by 1.\nYour faction standing with Swift Tails has been adjusted by 1.\nYou gain experience!\nYou receive 7 silver from Trooper Mozo.\nRumor has it that there is a reagents merchant in the Guild Lobby (DoN expansion) who sells Bone Chips.\nIven's Special Tip:\nEven with a very low Legion of Cabilis faction (kos) and without the Sneak skill it's possible to turn in Bone Chips. First you have to kill all the surrounding guards including the roaming crusaders as none of them can be root parked or snared.\nAfter Trooper Mozo has returned to his spawn point (guard position) you have to stand behind him and left-click two times very fast on him while having a stack of Bone Chips on the cursor. Activate an instant invisibility spell or potion immediately after this. If you do this quickly enough, the trade window will appear without anyone attacking you. Put in four (4) stacks of 1,000 Bone Chips and give them to Trooper Mozo.\nRinse and repeat until your faction standing is \"dubious\". But be careful, as many races cannot befriend crusaders like Quarg, who is on the Scaled Mystics faction. If he attacks you, all other guards will join him, regardless of your faction standing with them.\nSubmitted by: Muse ; Revamped by iventheassassinRewards:\n- Faction, Money\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "2600",
      title = "Dar Khura Journeyman (Shaman #4)",
      exp = "03",
      exp_name = "The Shadows of Luclin",
      min_lvl = 25,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "Jaima your Apprentice Cloak", count = 1 },
        { name = "to Jaima", count = 1 },
        { name = "him this note and he will guide you further", count = 1 },
        { name = "him the note", count = 1 },
        { name = "you a Supply Voucher", count = 1 },
        { name = "you the staff that you will need for your weapon", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 63822, name = "slot Brown Leather Bag", type = "item" },
        { id = 22561, name = "Cloak of the Dar Khura Journeyman", type = "item" },
        { id = 22562, name = "Sonic Wolf Bane Spear", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
        { name = "Guardians of Shar Vahl", change = 5 },
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 25\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis quest is offered by Jaima Seyel who is located in the Shaman's Guild in Shar Vahl. Give Jaima your Apprentice Cloak [item=22057].\nJaima Seyel smiles and says 'Very good. I am glad to have you here. I hope your studies have proven to be worthwhile thus far. Our sect is challenging, but we are vital to the survival of our people. Our research and ability to commune with the spirit world has allowed our people to overcome the challenges of the wilderness here. Here, take this bag. It is time for you to face your first real challenge.'\nYou say 'What challenge?'\nJaima Sayel says 'You will need to walk into the darkness of the Hollowshade Moor to face this enemy. Unlike the wolves that we have always been able to commune with, the wolves of the moor are oblivious to our attempts at communication. We have studied them for some time and our determination is that they are too corrupt for us to deal with. Their aggressive behavior and sheer numbers have forced us to research ways to kill them as quickly as possible. Fill that bag with the paws from one of those wolves. Once that task is complete, please return to me with the evidence of your encounter.'\nJaima gives you a 4-slot Brown Leather Bag [item=63822] to fill with 4 x Sonic Wolf Paws [item=11749],  the stackable, droppable kind that drop from all kinds of Sonic Wolves in Hollowshade Moor. Combine 4 paws in the bag to create a Bag of Wolf Paws, which you then give to Jaima.\nJaima Seyel says 'I see that you've met those beasts and made it back in one piece. I'm not sure if you noticed their ability to move and communicate as a pack, but it is both amazing and horrific to witness in action. They have proven to be enough of a problem to warrant special research. We have been able to build a weapon type that produces severe wounds on the wolves.'\nJaima Seyel says 'The constant threat of attack by the wolves has made it the responsibility of each citizen to carry one of those weapons. This strainer will be necessary in the construction of such a weapon. Take this note and seek out Amal Iuziq. He is a researcher that resides in the Library of Spiritual and Natural Studies. Give him this note and he will guide you further.'\nIn return you will be given a Note to Amat [item=22563] and your Ceremonial Metal Strainer.\nFind Amat Iuziq in the library right outside the Palace. Give him the note, and he will give you a Supply Voucher.\nAmat Iuziq says 'So friend, I see Jaima is preparing you to deal with the sonic wolves. Have you heard the term 'sonic wolf' used yet? We call them that because of the face they do not use eyes like an ordinary wolf. They have overcome the night by using a sensory system similar to that of a bat. I sure hope we do not turn into such monstrosities over time... Blasted darkness! Well, back to your situation. You have your strainer, I'm sure. Now, you'll need to purchase the Sonic Wilf Bane books from my frien Qua in the other library and read them. Once you've read them, please take this voucher to Arrin Murij at the general mercantile. He will give you the staff that you will need for your weapon. Good luck, friend.'\nYou have received a Supply Voucher [item=56451].\nArms Historian Qua is in the building across where you found Amat. Buy from him the three books; Wolf Bane Lore Volume I, Volume II, and Volume III. Also pick up the Weapons Assembly Kit as you'll need that.\nYou can use the Find ability to locate Arrin Murij. Hand him the supply voucher and he says:\nArrin Murij reaches behind the counter and pulls up a large spear shaft. 'Here you go, friend.' He says as he hands the staff to you. 'Be sure to take your finished spear back to Amat when you're done with it. He'll need to see your sonic wolf bane spear and the apprentice cloak you have on before he can promote you to the next rank. If he isn't able to promote you, I can't send out any more vouchers. That's an order from the General. We're training citizens as fast as we can. The war with the grunts seems to be picking up. Well, take care friend and say hello to Amat for me. He's an old war buddy of mine.'\nYou receive Dar Khura Spear Shaft [item=22549].\nCrafting these weapons requires the cooperation of all of the five Vah Shir classes:  Bard, Beastlord, Rogue, Shaman, and Warrior.  Each supplies a component that may only be crafted by Vah Shir of that class, and the components are combined to produce class-specific sonic bane weapons.\nVah Shir Shaman must contribute a Reactive Sealant Soak, which is crafted via brewing in the Ceremonial Metal Strainer (trivial around 135):\nBlackened Salt Crystals\nCrystallized Ygri Root\nDigested Night Palm\nSonic Wolf Brain\nWater Flask.\nCombine the Reactive Sealant Soak in the Weapon Assembly Kit with Sonic Wolf Bane (poison crafted by rogues), Toughened Sinew Lashings (crafted by beastlords), a Porous Dagger Blade (crafted by warriors), and a Ceramic Dagger Sleeve (crafted by bards).  This is a no-fail combine.  The result is a Sonic Wolf Bane Spear.\nGive this spear and your Cloak of the Dar Khura Apprentice to Amat Iuziq, who will give the spear back to you, along with your new Cloak of the Dar Khura Journeyman and a random low level spell.\nUpon Turnin:\nAmat Iuziq says, 'You have done well, Meowmrawr. Your progress gives me hope for the future of our people. Continue your training with the same effort and attention to detail and you should do well. I would not be surprised if you become a hero of great renown. Now, please take this new cloak and your spear and head to the moor. You will need to speak to a citizen by the name of Ahom Guzhin for your next assignment. Take care and good luck to you, Journeyman Meowmrawr.'\nYour faction standing with Guardians of Shar Vahl has been adjusted by 5.Rewards:\n- Cloak of the Dar Khura Journeyman [item=22561]\n- Sonic Wolf Bane Spear [item=22562]\n- Spell: Cancel Magic [priests/casters]\n[",
    },
