      id = "2635",
      title = "Free the Drogan Slaves",
      exp = "05",
      exp_name = "The Legacy of Ykesha",
      min_lvl = 68,
      max_lvl = 130,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Gillia Brissok",
        "I will help you get back home.",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 68\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Time Limit:** 02:00:00\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nIn the Temple of Droga, there are slaves of various races who wish to be set free. Each slave asks for three (3) items: Drogan Restorative, Goblin Rations, and the Master Shackle Key, which drop off a goblin master alchemist, a goblin food supplier, and a goblin prison warden. They appear to be on eight-hour timers.\nMake sure that you have pre-collected all required advanced quest items that the freed slaves offer, before starting this event. See quest entries: \"Revenge for ... \". The freed slaves possibly despawn after an unknown amount of time. Depending on which slave you free, the rewards are different. Freeing a slave is only spawning an NPC (in a different zone) that offers a sub-quest with an item reward. The event itself has no other function or reward to offer.\nHanding all three items to any of the slaves, starts the slave release event. This may be a somewhat tough fight for a single group, but is certainly single groupable.  It involves killing off a few waves of goblins that are somewhat tougher than any of the ones otherwise found in Droga (they hit a little bit harder, mitigate slows, and have about three times as much HP). Two named mobs spawn during the event:\n- Assistant Jailor Dravian (Hits for 434 and has about 170k HP)\n- Jailor Frixok (Hits for 565 and has at least as much HP as Dravian ; rampages)\nWhen Jailor Frixok has been killed, the slave escapes and flees to his home where it offers another quest. A different slave will spawn to take the freed slave's place.\nNote that the ring event seems to be bugged at the moment, so that the prisoner may be freed even if you don't defeat these named NPCs.\nKnown slaves:\n- Gillia Brissok (High Elf female)\n- Vaxxim T`Quoren (Dark Elf male)\n- Pagik Tsissun (Iksar male)\n- Asmodin Jru`dac (Sarnak)\n- Digmaster Duggert (Burynai)\nAfter a server reset, Gillia is the slave that spawns. Once Gillia has been freed, Vaxxim spawns in her place. The sequence is Gillia > Vaxxim > Pagik > Asmodin > Digmaster\nYou say, 'Hail, Gillia Brissok'\nGillia Brissok says 'Hail friend! Well at least I hope so. I was captured and imprisoned by the goblins while wandering the Frontier Mountains. I need to get back home. Will you help me get back home?'\nYou say, 'I will help you get back home.'\nGillia Brissok says 'For me to get home to Firiona Vie I will need to get these items to be freed from the goblin's clutches. I will need the master shackle key to free myself from these bonds. Also I will need some goblin rations and a drogan restorative so I have the strength to make the journey. Bring these back and I should be able to escape. Be warned though the goblins are sure to try to prevent my escape.'\nSubmitted by: Velsor Secarne ; Revamped by iventheassassinRewards:\n- Freed slaves offer quests\n[",
    },
