      walkthrough = "**Level:** 55\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nNioti [npc=14381] may be found at +95, +75, +100 in the Abysmal Sea.\nYou say, 'Hail, Nioti'\nNioti says 'Yes, what is it? I am a bit occupied right now with quite the [predicament]. I swear things keep getting worse and worse around here.'\nYou say, 'What predicament?'\nNioti says 'Well simply put, we are overwhelmed with repairs. While we made it safely to the shores of the new continent, we suffered some damage to the ship. To make matters worse, we are running out of supplies to complete the needed repairs and I don't have time to return to the mainland to find more. I sure could use some [assistance]. I knew we should have never come here.'\nYou say, 'What assistance?'\nNioti says 'Well I cannot really believe someone would want to help me, but if you really could help, that would be great. I would need you to find four Branches of Sylvan Oak and return them to me. If you do this for me, I will find some way to reward you for your efforts.'\nYou can forage the Branches of Sylvan Oak [item=11774] in the Eastern Wastes [zone=110] or the Wakening Land [zone=119], or simply go to The Bazaar and buy them for a few platinum.  Give four unstacked branches to Nioti.\nNioti says 'I don't think you would return. I appreciate your assistance. I hate to do this, but before I can convince my foreman to give you a reward, I am going to need to ask you to help me again. According to another adventurer that passed through here the other day, there is a golem graveyard of sorts in a temple somewhere on this continent. If you could find this place and gather one clay golem part that would help us greatly with repairs. Why do we need these golem parts you ask? I have no idea. Grumby [npc=14329], our foreman said we needed them for some sort of repairs. Oh yeah, take this badge. It identifies you as part of the ship's maintenance crew. Just hand the badge to me when you hand in the golem parts.'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a Worker's Badge [item=26106] (identifies as Worker's Badge Number One).  The Clay Golem Parts [item=26407] are a ground spawn in Barindu [zone=240] at +600, -585, in a room with Ikaav Ixvet Pox [npc=14231] who sees through Shroud of Stealth.  Hand in the parts and first Worker's Badge to Nioti:\nNioti says,'Thanks. I hope that wasn't too much trouble. Seems we need more help. Grumby just informed me that some parts on the bridge have already been damaged by rust. That doesnt sound good at all. We will need your help to get some sort of anti rust agent. What? Hey, dont get mad at me. I am sorry I keep asking for help, but I am just following Grumby's orders. There is a gnomish tinker in Ak'anon named Gilipus that might have something to help us. Go there and hand him this note along with your badge so he knows you are working for Grumby. I promise to reward you for your time when you are done helping us. Take your badge back and give it to me again when you hand in the anti-rusting agent.'\nYou receive a Note to Gilipus [item=38001] and another Worker's Badge [item=26408] (identifies as Worker's Badge Number Two).\nHead to Ak'Anon [zone=54] and find Gilipus [npc=18553] at +1385, -867 in the room next to the Ak'Anon Bank.\nYou say, 'Hail, Gilipus'\nGilipus says 'I had a wrench around here somewhere...'\nGive him the Note to Gilipus and the Worker's Badge.\nGilipus says 'Yes, what is it? Just a moment, I cannot read without my glasses.'\nGilipus rummages through his numerous pockets looking for his reading glasses. 'Oh this is most embarrassing. Seems I have lost my reading glasses. Oh wait, I know where they are. They are on this bench here.' Just as Gilipus reaches for his glasses, a small mechanical rat snatches them and hurriedly scuttles away. 'Oh drat. This isn't good at all. That defective cleaner just took my reading glasses! Think you could go get them? What defective cleaner you ask? I don't know for certain. I couldn't make out the serial number. If you can find my glasses, I will read this note you brought me.'\nYou get the Worker's Badge [item=38002] back, but this time it identifies as Worker's Badge Number Three.  Kill a defective cleaner [npc=14692] in Ak'Anon until one drops Gilipus's Reading Glasses [item=25509].  Give the Glasses and Badge back to Gilipus.\nGilipus says 'Thank you. That is much better.' Gilipus begins to read the note. 'You need something to remove rust? Yes, I do believe I have just the thing for you. Just bring me some rubbing alcohol and I can make what you need. Now where are my tools?'\nYou get the Worker's Badge [item=38004] back, but now it identifies as Worker's Badge Number Four.\nRubbing Alcohol [item=6793] may be purchased in Thurgadin [zone=102] from Adia Coldbeard [npc=5846] and Karey [npc=5942], or in West Cabilis [zone=97] from a mortician [npc=4691]. Give the Badge and the Rubbing Alcohol to Gilipus.\nGilipus says 'Hello what can I do for you? Oh yes, you needed something to remove rust. This rubbing alcohol should help you. Good thing you thought to bring it.' Gilipus begins to mix some different chemicals together in a small vial. 'Here you go. This should work. I think. By the way, have you seen a small notebook? It was green with a picture of a lovely cog on it. . .'\nYou receive a Vial of Anti-Rusting Agent [item=38007] and your Worker's Badge [item=38005], which now identifies as Worker's Badge Number Five.  Head back to Nioti and give her both pieces.\nNioti says 'What took so long? Grumby has been breathing down my neck all day asking for this stuff. I am glad you were able to acquire it. It seems like everything around here is rusting away in this salty air. Your reward? Yes, yes. I will reward you. However it seems we need more help. Grumby has informed me that we need some ore. Think you could go and get some for us? Bring back three blocks of ore and your Worker's Badge.'\nYou get the Worker's Badge [item=38006] back again (Worker's Badge Number Six now).  Blocks of Ore [item=14396] may be crafted by combining 3 x Large Brick of Ore [item=14412] with 1 x Water Flask [item=7773] in a forge, trivial 27.  Turn in the Blocks of Ore with the Badge.\nNioti says 'Not the best quality but this ore should help a lot. Now don't get mad at me, but before we can reward you, Grumby has told me that you will need to go get him some food. He said he wants some Filleted Mammoth. Oh and he also wanted a Jumjum Cake. Bring me those food items along with your worker's badge.'\nYou get the badge again, Worker's Badge [item=38003] Number Seven.\nFilleted Mammoth [item=15053] may be baked by combining Mammoth Meat [item=4234] with a Filleting Knife [item=12547] in an oven or spit, trivial 143.\nJumjum Cake [item=15166] may be baked by combining a Cake Round [item=11865], Clump of Dough [item=11840], Frosting [item=14384], Winter Chocolate [item=15158], and any of three varieties of Jumjum Stalk [item=38009] in an oven or spit, trivial 166.\nTurn in the Filleted Mammoth and the Jumjum Cake with the Badge.\nNioti says 'Looks like your work here is done. Grumby said I can reward you. Here you go. Thanks again and sorry for all the trouble.'\nReward(s):\nWorker's Earring of Efficiency [item=26452]Rewards:\n- Worker's Earring of Efficiency [item=26452]\n[",
    },
