      },
      walkthrough = "**Time:** Instant\n**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThe original versions of tradeskill grandmaster trophies did not summon bags.  If you have one of these, Jolum in The Bazaar explains how you can upgrade it to the newer version.  (All newly created trophies summon bags.)\nYou say, 'Hail, Jolum'\nJolum says 'Hail!  Nice to see ya, friend.  I've got a fine selection of spankin' good spells, perhaps you'd be interested? Or maybe you'd like to learn how to [upgrade] your Grandmaster Trade items?  Still yet, maybe you would like to know how to create a [Grandmaster's Medicine Bag]?'\nYou say, 'How can I upgrade?'\nJolum says 'What Grandmaster Trade item would you like to know how to upgrade?  I can tell you how to upgrade your [Grandmaster Baker's Spoon], [Grandmaster Brewer's Corker], [Grandmaster Fletcher's Knife], [Grandmaster Jeweler's Eyeglass], [Grandmaster Potter's Sculpter], [Grandmaster Smith's Hammer], [Grandmaster Tailor's Needle], or your [Grandmaster Tinker's Spanner].  While you can't have more than one of the new items, they will summon a [bag] for you.  Very useful for carrying heavy items about and such.'\nYou say, 'What Grandmaster Baker's Spoon?'\nJolum says 'To upgrade your Grandmaster Baker's Spoon, simply combine your old spoon in an oven with a mixing spoon and you should get a new Grandmaster Baker's Spoon in return.'\nNote:  The old Grandmaster Baker's Spoon appears to have been written over by SOE with another item, so this portion may no longer work.  Please confirm that it still works with a Dairy Spoon and provide the new dialogue, if any.\nYou say, 'What Grandmaster Brewer's Corker?'\nJolum says 'For a new and improved Grandmaster Brewer's Corker combine your old Brewer's Corker with a corking device and, voila! You have a new Grandmaster Brewer's Corker.'\nYou say, 'What Grandmaster Fletcher's Knife?'\nJolum says 'Ahh, a fletcher are you? Well in your fletching kit combine your Grandmaster Fletcher's Knife with a Fishbone Dart tool and you will have made yourself a new Grandmaster Fletcher's Knife.'\nYou say, 'What Grandmaster Jeweler's Eyeglass?'\nJolum says 'Jewelcraft is more your speed then, is it?  In a jewelers kit, combine a glass shard, a silver bar, with your old Grandmaster Jeweler's Eyeglass and your old Eyeglass will be a new Eyeglass.'\nYou say, 'What Grandmaster Potter's Sculpter?'\nJolum chuckles. 'So you like to work with clay do you?  Well in a kiln combine, with your Grandmaster Potter's Sculpter, a set of Sculpting Tools and you'll have a new and better Sculpter for your leisure.'\nYou say, 'What Grandmaster Smith's Hammer?'\nJolum eyes you for a moment. 'Yes, you have a blacksmith's arms.  If you'd like to upgrade your Grandmaster Smith's hammer, simply bang on it in a forge with a mundane Smithy Hammer.'\nYou say, 'What Grandmaster Tailor's Needle?'\nJolum says 'Oh, so you are a tailor?  Perhaps I'll see you about this hole in my robe.  In the meantime, to change your Grandmaster Tailor's Needle combine it with an Embroidering Needle in your sewing kit.'\nYou say, 'What Grandmaster Tinker's Spanner?'\nJolum says 'You tinker?  I happen to dabble with that a little bit myself.  Well that is neither here nor there.  If you'd like a new Grandmaster Tinker's Spanner, combine your old spanner with some metal bits and a sharpening stone.'Submitted by: FlevenRewards:\n- Grandmaster Baker's Spoon [item=15981]\n- Grandmaster Brewer's Corker [item=12207]\n- Grandmaster Fletcher's Knife [item=12931]\n- Grandmaster Jeweler's Eyeglass [item=12043]\n- Grandmaster Potter's Sculpter [item=12812]\n- Grandmaster Smith's Hammer [item=12034]\n- Grandmaster Tailor's Needle [item=12147]\n- Grandmaster Tinker's Spanner [item=12165]\n[",
