      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 8\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx [npc=8441] is located on the second floor of the Temple of Terror.\nYou say, 'Hail, Prime Patriarch Vuzx'\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says, 'Greetings.  I only train those who follow the path of the Patriarchs of Cabilis and have yet to develop their [powers] over the beasts of the wild, or maybe you are trained and are here to [help aid in our cause]?'\nYou say, 'I will help aid his cause.'\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says, 'Good. Well we shall see how well you match up with our needs with this first mission. Go out beyond the safety of our city walls and bring back proof of your inner strength and training. This proof will be in the form of a sarnak raider brain [item=3095], a froglok bounder javelin [item=610], an Iksar bandit mask [item=2934], and a mandible [item=2990] from a rogue shaman.'\nYou'll need to head out into the surrounding area of Cabilis to collect these items :\n- a sarnak crypt raider [npc=6675] can be found in the Lake of Ill Omen [zone=73], near the explorer tower ;\n- a froglok bounder [npc=4018] can easily be found on an island in the Swamp of No Hope [zone=74] at about -1000, 2500 ;\n- an iksar bandit [npc=3985] can be found in the pit in the Field of Bone [zone=82] ;\n- a rogue shaman [npc=4448] can also be found in the Field of Bone [zone=82] in the evening northeast of Kurn's Tower [zone=87].\nHand these four items in for your claw.\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'I said do not return without a sarnak raider brain, a goblin hunter javelin, an iksar bandit mask, and a mandible from a rogue shaman.'\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'I said do not return without a sarnak raider brain, a goblin hunter javelin, an iksar bandit mask, and a mandible from a rogue shaman.'\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'I said do not return without a sarnak raider brain, a goblin hunter javelin, an iksar bandit mask, and a mandible from a rogue shaman.'\nPrime Patriarch Vuzx says 'You have done well on your way to becoming a great patriarch. Now I must tend to other pressing issues. Take your reward and wear it proudly.'\nYour faction standing with Scaled Mystics got better.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis got better.\nYou gain experience!!Submitted by: SilraakRewards:\n- Claw of the Cub [item=28608]\n[",
