      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 60\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\n\"a shady merchant\" may be found at -460, +1900, -160 in the Crypt of Nadox.\nYou say, 'Hail, a shady merchant'\na shady merchant says 'You there!  You look like you could use a bit of [work].  If you're interested I have something that you might find very. . . lucrative.'\nYou say, 'What work?'\na shady merchant says 'My employers have been enjoying quite a bit of success lately with their operations and wish to continue them uninterrupted.  However, these operations have been put in jeopardy lately. Those stinking [pirates] are thinking of shipping off again to resume their raiding of Faydwer and Antonica.'\nYou say, 'What pirates?'\na shady merchant says 'It's no less than the Hate's Fury that is heading out again.  You can't even imagine what a ship like that can do to the operations of my employers.  We have come up with a solution, or at least a way to prolong our profits though, if you're willing to [help].'\nYou say, 'I will help.'\na shady merchant says 'Excellent, the plan is a simple one, in concept at least.  The ship needs a navigator in order to be successful in its raids.  If we can eliminate the navigator of the Hate's Fury she will not be able to leave until they can conscript a new one.  There's been a small [complication] though.'\nYou say, 'What complication?'\na shady merchant says 'The captain and his officers are a fairly vicious group, they are pirates after all.  Because of this there is a high turn over rate on the crew.  The last navigator for the ship met a rather grisly end.  They recently obtained a new navigator, but we have not been able to discover who that is so far.  This is where you come in, if you're still [interested].'\nYou say, 'I am interested.'\na shady merchant says 'We need you to venture onto the ship, find out who the navigator is, where he is located, and slay him if possible. Now get going and don't come back until he's dead!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Hate's Fury Setting Sail'.\nThe direction to someone related to your current Task has been marked on your compass.\nThe arrow takes you to \"a shady smuggler\" at -1325, +1415, -135.\nYou say, 'Hail, a shady smuggler'\na shady smuggler says 'Hmph, so you're going to stop the Hate's Fury from sailing? Well at least it will be entertaining to watch them wash your blood from the decks. Let me know when you're ready to [board the ship].'\nYou say, 'I am ready to board the ship.'\na shady smuggler says 'Off we go, I'll be waiting for you when you're done. . . If you're still alive that is.'\nYou get teleported into an instanced version of Hate's Fury called Hate's Fury:  Setting Sail.\nYour Location is -103.10, -15.03, 67.75.\nYou say, 'Hail, a shady smuggler'\na shady smuggler says 'Well you're still alive, so you've already exceeded my expectations. Let me know when you're ready to [leave].'\nThe first three stages of the task involve looting three different notes that drop randomly from all the \"trash\" mobs in the zone.  Just clear trash until all three drop. (NOTE: Although rare, it is possible for all 3 pages to not drop in a single instance due to the RNG nature of the loot)\nYou have looted A Ship's Log Page.\nYour task 'Hate's Fury Setting Sail' has been updated.\nThe next stage involves looting A Scrap of Paper\nYour task 'Hate's Fury Setting Sail' has been updated.\nThe third stage involves looting A Crumpled Note\nAfter the third piece is looted, Grimzek (yellow con according to your group's top level) spawns randomly between a few set locations, your quest journal will tell you where he can be found, along with 2 adds which may be split \"an apprentice navigator\" and \"a brokenskull mystic.\"\nLoot Rewards come from Grimzek (1 per instance), and depend on task level\nLevel 55 Version\nSalt Encrusted Platinum Ring\nRagged Sailcloth Cloak\nGilded Buccaneer's Pauldrons\nLevel 60 Version\nBejeweled Pirate's Earring\nElaborate Golden Medallion\nStudded Swashbuckler's Belt\nLevel 65 Version\nBuccaneer's Shield of Pillaging\nHelmsman's Mask of Vision\nMeticulously Crafted Sextant\nLevel 68+ Version\nTactician's Cloak of Plunder\nSparkling Ruby of Seamanship\nSilken Mantle of SkullduggeryRewards:\n- Bejeweled Pirate's Earring [item=59765]\n- Buccaneer's Shield of Pillaging [item=36714]\n- Elaborate Golden Medallion [item=57463]\n- Gilded Buccaneer's Pauldrons [item=58564]\n- Helmsman's Mask of Vision [item=37095]\n- Meticulously Crafted Sextant [item=38700]\n- Ragged Sailcloth Cloak [item=57066]\n- Salt Encrusted Platinum Ring [item=115876]\n- Silken Mantle of Skullduggery [item=36951]\n- Sparkling Ruby of Seamanship [item=36959]\n- Studded Swashbuckler's Belt [item=51059]\n- Tactician's Cloak of Plunder [item=36709]\n[",
