    {
      id = "3157",
      title = "Below the Field of Bone",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 15,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = -571.0, x = 987.0, z = 0.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Barrenzin",
        "What business?",
        "What group?",
        "Hail, Karunku Trogue",
        "Hail, a captured caravan guard",
        "business",
        "organization",
        "Interested",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "no faction hits when killed", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 38523, name = "Note About Your Fifth Trial", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 15\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nBarrenzin [npc=18623] may be found at -571,+987 in the evil section of the Plane of Knowledge.\nYou say, 'Hail, Barrenzin'\nBarrenzin says 'Greetings, ______,' Barrenzin smiles as he hands you a glass of wine.  'Thank you for coming on such short notice.  Please make yourself comfortable and then we can discuss [business].'\nYou say, 'What business?'\nBarrenzin says 'A Iksar that gets right to point,' Barrenzin smiles again. 'Such a refreshing change of pace from the pandering rabble I normally deal with.  Allow me to be blunt then.  I recently lost several, let's say, 'associates' of mine and I'm a little understaffed at the moment.  I've been following your adventuring career since Gloomingdeep and I think you could go far in my [organization].  What say you?  [Interested] in making a name for yourself?  Or perhaps you have a [group] assembled that's looking for a little coin?'\nYou say, 'What group?'\nBarrenzin says 'Yes these particular matters require the attention of a small group. . .say at least three dedicated souls.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Below the Field of Bone'.\nThe Field of Bone:  Hail Karunku Trogue in the Field of Bone\nKurn's Tower:  (Optional) Kill the Burynai Necromancers\nKurn's Tower:  Kill the Burynai Rock Seer\nKurn's Tower:  Recover the Seer's Etched Stone\nPlane of Knowledge:  Deliver the Stone Totem to Barrenzin\nFind Karunku Trogue in the Field of Bone at -900, +1175.\nYou say, 'Hail, Karunku Trogue'\nKarunku Trogue says 'About time!  I was wondering when Barrenzin would send reinforcements.  My swamp skin wuz getting' all sun-burn-ned waitin' out 'ere.  C'mon, get ready to follow me into da Kurn and stay close.  Word among de iksar is dat da Rock Seer can listen through stone itself.'\nYour task 'Below the Field of Bone' has been updated.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Kurn's Tower.\nYou say, 'Hail, Karunku Trogue'\nKarunku Trogue says 'Alright, _______, you da boss.  Lead out!'\nKarunku Trogue will now follow you around the tower.\nScattered around are NPCs called \"a captured caravan guard.\"  There is one lying on the first floor, an iksar female, who tells you to slay the necromancers.  The rest are dark elves down in the caverns.  I found three who joined me as pets and two who refused and instead cast random buffs on Karunku and myself.  Although all three scowled at my iksar shadowknight, none attacked.\nYou say, 'Hail, a captured caravan guard'\nThe iksar writhes in pain.  'Gaaa!  The burynai broke my kneecaps for attempting to escape!  Kill them!...  Errrgh!...  But, first slay the burynai necromancers upstairs.  They control the undead creations that wander this accursed tower.  With their deaths, the skeletons they created will fall.  The other caravan guards are in the mines below!...  Aaaggghhh!...  They will help you!  Avenge me!'\nPet guards say the following:\nYou say, 'Hail, a captured caravan guard'\nThe caravan guard smiles as you approach.  'Ha ha! Never thought I'd be so glad to see someone sent by Barrenzin himself.  Let's gut these burynai one at a time!'\nBuffer guards say the following:\nYou say, 'Hail, a captured caravan guard'\nA captured caravan guard says 'I'm done working for Barrenzin!  If you want to fight these badger creatures, go ahead, but I'm sneaking out in the confusion.  Here this spell might just save your fool neck!'\nThey cast a random buff on you or Karunku.\nOptional step:  kill the Burynai Necromancers.  These are casters on the upper floors who are not on Burynai Legion faction.  They /con indifferent, do not roam, drop no loot, and give no faction hits when killed.  Although they are necromancers they have no pets.  This part of the task did not even show up in my window until I had completed it so the exact number of kills necessary is unknown.  When this step is completed you see the following emote:\nA great clatter sounds throughout the tower as the Burynai skeletal constructs fall to the floor.  The Burynai Rock Seer yells, 'The intruders have destroyed our skeletal army!  All soldiers, fall back to the lowest level!'\nYour task 'Below the Field of Bone' has been updated.\nFind The Rock Seer under the tower.\nYour Location is 155.95, -171.81, -101.90\nKill The Rock Seer.\nYou have slain The Rock Seer!\n--You have looted a Etched Stone Totem.--\nYour task 'Below the Field of Bone' has been updated.\nTake this back to Barrenzin.\nYour task 'Below the Field of Bone' has been updated.\nDepending on your race, you will immediately receive one of the following tasks:\nYou have been assigned the task 'Journey to Cabilis'.\n--OR--\nYou have been assigned the task 'Journey to Halas'.\n--OR--\nYou have been assigned the task 'Journey to Oggok'.\nBarrenzin smiles as you hand him the stone totem.  'Well done, my friend!  Well done!  Looks like you'll be my first contact from here on out.  Keep playing your cards right and soon we'll be running the black market here side by side.  Rest up and let me know when you're [interested] in more work.'\nYou receive a Note About Your Fifth Trial.\nNeed information about other race-specific tasks assigned.Rewards:\n- Note About Your Fifth Trial [item=38523]\n[",
    },
