    {
      id = "3254",
      title = "Nights of the Dead: Trick or Treat for the Old Man",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 10,
      max_lvl = 90,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Old Man Draykey",
        "I have come to participate.",
        "What instructions?",
        "Trick or treat.",
        "come to participate",
        "instructions",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "you something like Coal", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 45441, name = "Bristlebane's Ticket of Admission", type = "item" },
        { id = 45453, name = "Caramel-Coated Candy Apple", type = "item" },
        { id = 45454, name = "Delicious Pumpkin Bread", type = "item" },
        { id = 45482, name = "Sweetened Gummy Bears", type = "item" },
        { id = 45481, name = "Tasty Sugar Pop", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 10\n**Maximum Level:** 90\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis quest was introduced in October 2005 and is available every year around Halloween.\nIt's one of five tasks required to receive a Bone Mask of Horror [quest=5371] (illusion click item).\nOld Man Draykey is found in the northwest corner of Kithicor Forest at about 1915, 4535.\nYou say, 'Hail, Old Man Draykey'.\nOld Man Draykey says 'Greetings, _____! Have you [come to participate] in the festivities?''\nYou say, 'I have come to participate.'\nOld Man Draykey says 'Excellent, excellent! For those of you that enjoy trick-or-treating I have set up an event beyond anything you have done before. I will have convinced ten...well beings...not all of them are really people, to help with this. It's a very tricky endeavor, with highly complex [instructions]. Prepare yourself and then I will reveal the secrets to you.'\nYou say, 'What instructions?'\nOld Man Draykey says 'First of all you need to know how to properly speak with these people. Once you find them, you simply need to say 'Trick or treat', and see what they have to say in return. I have compiled a list of my helpers around Norrath and have written them down in my book. As I have said, there are ten people each with a piece of candy you'll need to collect. Once you've collected all ten return to me with the full bag.'\nYou receive Draykey's Codex, a book of hints as to where to find the mobs, and a Trick-or-Treat Bag (10-slot GIANT container).\nThe Codex reads:\nSearch out those that have treats for you. Here is a small list of clues as to where they can be found.\n1. Hiding in the bushes of the dead house.\n2. The pinnacle of enlightenment.\n3. He's not Slate, but he's close.\n4. Wanders in a pit in the land of his kind.\n5. A short man in an icy land, food can be found in his hands.\n6. Lurking in the forest near a feline retreat.\n7. He found out the hard way that drinking and swordplay do not mix.\n8. Hidden away in the caves of his lair.\n9. Toiling in the fields of the gnoll's family.\n10. He's fallen down the stairs, but it's been kept under wraps.\nThe goal of the quest is to /target and say \"Trick or treat\" to 10 NPCs.\nNOTE: Sometimes the NPC will \"trick\" you and give you something like Coal, Sand, or Pocket Lint. If you receive a \"trick\" instead of the \"treat,\" you need to zone out and back in again to say \"trick or treat\" again (and keep doing so until you get a treat).\nCrabby the Rotten\nCrabby is found in Unrest in either of the hedge mazes.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nCrabby the Rotten says 'Gimme gimme gimme. . .You people make me sick! Here's your nasty little treat, now leave me be.'\nReceive a Candy Jack-o-Lantern.\nGrand Librarian Maelin\nMaelin is found in the Plane of Knowledge at the top of the library.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nGrand Librarian Maelin says 'Ah, here you go. Fresh from the Sugar Assembalage 2000.'\nYou receive a Jawbreaker.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nSergeant Ragus\nRagus wanders along and the path in the Commonlands.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nSergeant Ragus says 'Hah! Here's the tastiest treat of them all! Enjoy!'\nYou receive a Rock Candy.\nImmug Lashtail\nThis is a named iksar skeleton wandering the pit of the Field of Bone.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nImmug Lashtail says 'Why is it that you people keep pestering me for these? Here's your treat, now tell everyone else they can find me off under the ocean or some nonsense.'\nYou receive Gummie Kobolds.\nNilham the Chef\nIn Iceclad Ocean, Nilham sits inside igloo in the gnome village.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nNilham the Chef says 'Can ya believe the Cap'n thought these were real when I first started handing them out? Hah! At least he did until they melted in his pocket!'\nYou receive a Chocolate Coin.\nFuzz\nFuzz stands on the beach/west wall of Toxxulia Forest -- on the same side as the entrance to Kerra Isle.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nFuzz Selppa says 'Careful with these, or they'll get stuck in your teeth!'\nYou receive Carmel Apples.\nNate\nNate stands in back of the graveyard of Castle Mistmoore.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nNate says 'Well, it's not ale but you'll just have to deal with that. . .By the by did you happen to bring any ale with you?'\nYou receive Fairy Fizzles.\nPoil Lolp\nPoil Lolp can be found in any cave, standing still in Netherbian Lair.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nPoil Lolp says 'Brave of you to have come back into the dark cave. Braver still if you try this treat. . .'\nYou receive a Lollipop (note the anagram!).\nScary Miller\nScary Miller wanders the field of the Miller family farm in West Karana.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nScary Miller says 'Here's something from one of our more unusual crops, see what you think.'\nYou receive Candy Corn.\nWraps McGee\nWraps is in a locked room on the bottom floor of Befallen. Kill \"a shadowknight\" to get the key.\nYou say, 'Trick or treat.'\nWraps McGee says 'Here I'll just wrap this up for you. . . Get it? Hahaha!'\nYou receive a Tasty Candy.\nCombine all ten treats in the bag to get a Full Trick-or-Treat Bag and take it to Old Man Draykey.\nOld Man Draykey says 'Ah ha! You've found them all! Excellent work, here's a bit of candy for you and something else as well. Enjoy!'\nReward:\n1x \"Bristlebane's Ticket of Admission\"\n5x snack food\nOld Man Draykey is one of four NPCs that Zigan Ribshard in the Plane of Knowledge hints about (he is the goblin near the Field of Bone portal). For each of their tasks, you are given a ticket of admission. You hand these tickets to the \"puppet\" NPC in Kithicor to receive a monster mission.Submitted by: Vlaru of Povar, revised write-up by AegishopiRewards:\n- Bristlebane's Ticket of Admission [item=45441]\n- Caramel-Coated Candy Apple [item=45453]\n- Delicious Pumpkin Bread [item=45454]\n- Spell: Illusion: Frost Bone [item=61079]\n- Sweetened Gummy Bears [item=45482]\n- Tasty Sugar Pop [item=45481]\n[",
    },
