      walkthrough = "**Level:** 15\n**Maximum Level:** 90\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nThese shared tasks are available during the holiday season as part of Frostfell events that run from December into the first week of January.\nM.C. Tinkerton and his Clockwork Party Machine made their debut in 2005. They are located next to the Great Divide portal in the Plane of Knowledge.\nYou say, 'Hail, M.C. Tinkerton'\nM.C. Tinkerton says 'Hello, _____!  You've caught me in a bit of a [bind].'\nYou say, 'What bind?'\nM.C. Tinkerton says 'I'm trying to get my clockwork party machine up and running but the dang thing just wont move!  Its primary party motivator was stolen by the [Dark Mistletoe giants]!'\nYou say, 'Who are the Dark Mistletoe Giants?'\nM.C. Tinkerton says 'The Dark Mistletoe giants are a grumpy old clan that lives in the Great Divide.  Their leader, Old Frostbeard, complained my party machine was keeping him up at nights!  Bah!  The old geezer goes to bed at five thirty in the afternoon!  We'd be well within our rights to [steal it back]!'\nYou say, 'Will you steal it back?'\nM.C. Tinkerton says 'Wait a minute, _____!  Steal it back?  That's a great idea!  Why didn't I think of that?  Here's what you need to do!  Once you return with that motivator, we're going to party like it's 3199!'\nFrom here, you can choose one of three tasks:\nFrostbeard's Lesser Minions (for groups under Level 30)\nFrostbeard's Greater Minions (for groups Level 30-50)\nFrostbeard's Elite Minions (for groups Level 50+)\nAfter completing one of those tasks, you can request another:\nOld Frostbeard (for groups 60+)\nFrostbeard's Lesser Minions\nKill 10 Dark Mistletoe Clan Scouts 0/10 (Great Divide)\nKill Scout Master Hemlock 0/1 (Great Divide)\nThe above mobs are found around the giant mountaintop in the center of the Great Divide. They are levels 19-21.\nReturn to M.C. Tinkerton 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nRewards (for everyone in the task):\nExperience\nBauble of the New Year\nBauble of the New Year\nMAGIC ITEM LORE ITEM NO TRADE PLACEABLE\nSlot: RANGE\nCharges: Unlimited\nAC: 4\nThis item is placeable in yards and houses.\nSTR: +3 STA: +6 CHA: +3 WIS: +5 INT: +5 HP: +10 MANA: +10 ENDUR: +10\nSV FIRE: +2 SV COLD: +2 SV MAGIC: +2\nRecommended level of 15.\nEffect: Angry Bee (Any Slot, Casting Time: 3.0)\nRecast Delay: 10 seconds, Recast Type: 1\nWT: 0.5 Size: SMALL\nClass: ALL\nRace: ALL\nSlot 1, Type 7 (General: Group)\nFrostbeard's Greater Minions\nKill 10 Dark Mistletoe Clan Guards 0/10 (Great Divide)\nKill Champion Stinging Nettle 0/1 (Great Divide)\nThe above mobs are found around the giant mountaintop in the center of the Great Divide. They are levels 39-44.\nReturn to M.C. Tinkerton 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nRewards (for everyone in the task):\nExperience\nJadestone of the New Year\nJadestone of the New Year\nMAGIC ITEM LORE ITEM NO TRADE PLACEABLE\nSlot: RANGE\nCharges: Unlimited\nAC: 7\nThis item is placeable in yards and houses.\nSTR: +5 STA: +8 CHA: +5 WIS: +7 INT: +7 HP: +25 MANA: +25 ENDUR: +25\nSV FIRE: +4 SV COLD: +4 SV MAGIC: +4\nRecommended level of 35.\nEffect: Angry Bee (Any Slot, Casting Time: 3.0)\nRecast Delay: 10 seconds, Recast Type: 1\nWT: 0.5 Size: SMALL\nClass: ALL\nRace: ALL\nSlot 1, Type 7 (General: Group)\nFrostbeard's Elite Minions\nThe Dark Mistletoe Clan lives in the Great Divide. Careful, these giants are well versed in the use of potions and other forms of nastiness. They once put some holly thorns in someone's eggnog and didn't even think twice about it! They're pretty crazy like that!\nVenture to the Great Divide and take out 10 Dark Mistletoe Elders. Then give Elder Gnarled Pine a sound thrashing! The gods know he deserves it! When you've cleared those goblins out of the way, you'll be ready to get my motivator back from Old Frostbeard.\nKill 10 Dark Mistletoe Clan Elders 0/10 (Great Divide)\nKill Elder Gnarled Pine 0/1 (Great Divide)\nThe above mobs are found around the giant mountaintop in the center of the Great Divide. They are levels 60-64.\nReturn to M.C. Tinkerton 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nYou say, 'Hail, M.C. Tinkerton'\nM.C. Tinkerton gives you his thanks for clearing out the Dark Mistletoe Clan elders.\nRewards (for everyone in the task):\nExperience\nGemstone of the New Year\nGemstone of the New Year\nMAGIC ITEM LORE ITEM NO TRADE PLACEABLE\nSlot: RANGE\nCharges: Unlimited\nAC: 10\nThis item is placeable in yards and houses.\nSTR: +7 STA: +10 CHA: +7 WIS: +9 INT: +9 HP: +50 MANA: +50 ENDUR: +50\nSV FIRE: +6 SV COLD: +6 SV MAGIC: +6\nHP Regen +1\nRecommended level of 55.\nEffect: Angry Bee (Any Slot, Casting Time: 3.0)\nRecast Delay: 10 seconds, Recast Type: 1\nWT: 0.5 Size: SMALL\nClass: ALL\nRace: ALL\nSlot 1, Type 7 (General: Group)\nOld Frostbeard\nIt's time to get my machine's party motivator back. Look for Old Frostbeard. He stands on a high mountain amidst his summoned storms. He's big and nasty and cold. You can't miss him. Get a group and steal back my motivator.\nScatter five of Old Frostbeard's summoned winds 0/5 (Great Divide)\nThe above mobs are found around the giant mountaintop in the center of the Great Divide. Old Frostbeard is found on the east side of the mountaintop. He hits for a max ~725.\nThe mobs in this task summon. The dervishes cast \"Blizzard of the North Wind\". Old Frostbeard also casts that spell as well as \"Gale of the West Wind\".\nBlizzard of the North Wind: Unknown(32) 100', Cold (-200)\n1: Decrease HP when cast by 1375\n2: Decrease Attack Speed by 50%\nGale of the West Wind: Single Target, Cold (-200)\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 500 per tick\n2: Decrease AC by 300\nRecover the party motivator and return it to M.C. Tinkerton 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nThis drops from Old Frostbeard. On handing it in to M.C. Tinkerton:\nM.C. Tinkerton gives you his thanks for returning the primary party motivator.\nM.C. Tinkerton says 'Well done, my friend.  Let me just slide that party motivator back into place.'\nM.C. Tinkerton says 'Hmm. . .'\nM.C. Tinkerton says 'Should be working. . .'\nClockwork Party Machine says 'Initial-i-zing par-ty start-er sequence one-one-niner.'\nClockwork Party Machine says 'Pri-mary firework cannons: online.'\nClockwork Party Machine says 'Gy-ro-scopic dance mod-u-lator: online.'\nClockwork Party Machine says 'Par-ty favor dis-per-sal hopper: online.'\nClockwork Party Machine says 'Initial-i-zation complete.  Beginning par-ty start-er sequence one-one-niner'\nM.C. Tinkerton says 'Whew!  It worked!  Thanks again, my friend, and have a happy new year.'\nRewards (for everyone in the task):\nExperience\nEmerald of the New Year\nIn addition, several chests spawn around the Party Machine and have various items in them (some champagne, fireworks, and invisibility potions).\nEmerald of the New Year\nMAGIC ITEM LORE ITEM NO TRADE PLACEABLE\nSlot: RANGE\nCharges: Unlimited\nAC: 20\nThis item is placeable in yards and houses.\nSTR: +9 STA: +12 CHA: +9 WIS: +11 INT: +11 HP: +115 MANA: +115 ENDUR: +115\nSV FIRE: +8 SV COLD: +8 SV MAGIC: +8\nAvoidance: +5 HP Regen +2 Mana Regeneration: +2\nRecommended level of 65.\nEffect: Angry Bee (Any Slot, Casting Time: 3.0)\nRecast Delay: 10 seconds, Recast Type: 1\nWT: 0.5 Size: SMALL\nClass: ALL\nRace: ALL\nSlot 1, Type 7 (General: Group)Submitted by: Vlaru of PovarRewards:\n- Bauble of the New Year [item=55634]\n- Champagne [item=50393]\n- Emerald of the New Year [item=46085]\n- Firework: Dancing Lights [item=61737]\n- Firework: Phantom Fire [item=61623]\n- Gemstone of the New Year [item=65838]\n- Jadestone of the New Year [item=62457]\n- Mist of the Ant [item=47822]\n- Potion of Invisibility [item=25297]\n[",
