      walkthrough = "**Level:** 65\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis flags you to start the quest for the epic 1.5 if you don't have the Water Sprinkler of Nem Ankh (epic 1.0).  Find Tavon Vastsea in Nedaria's Landing near the magus.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tavon Vastsea'\nTavon Vastsea says 'Greetings ______. I am afraid that I need someone that I can [trust] with this task, these are dark times, and it is hard to tell friend from foe.'\nYou say, 'Trust?'\nTavon Vastsea says 'Hmmm, well I think I have a task I can entrust you with. Speak to my brother, tell him that I sent you to him. Earn his trust, and you shall have mine.'\nHead to Timorous Deep and find Omat Vastsea at -11565, -2225.\nYou say, 'Hail, Omat Vastsea'\nOmat Vastsea bows deeply. 'I have been expecting you, ______. The waters have foretold your arrival. I am High Priest Omat Vastsea of the Triumvirate missionaries. Please feel free to enjoy the quiet solitude of this inn.'\nYou say, 'Tavon sent me.'\nOmat stares at you. 'I received word from my brother that you would be coming. I have just the task for you. I am sure you heard of the [Plasmatic Priests]'\nYou say, 'Plasmatic Priests?'\nOmat Vastsea says 'The Plasmatic Priests were worshippers of Fennin Ro. Their numbers were all but destroyed by adventurers, and with the silence of the Pantheon they no longer draw power from the Tyrant of Fire. However they are still a danger, please find the last remnants of their order and bring me proof of their [destruction].'\nYou say, 'Destruction?'\nOmat Vastsea says 'They are in hiding, the few alcoves that I managed to find were shrouded and hidden. Take this signet and find the keeper for each alcove. Show it to him and he will drop the veil. Strike fast and exterminate the camp before he is able to cloak the camp again. Return the talisman to me with proof of the deaths of the three remaining high priests. Once you have done this, I will send you to my brother with my blessings.'\nYou receive a Talisman of the Plasmatic Priests (identifies as \"The world shall burn\").\nHead to the Lavastorm Mountains and find Laura Rako on the biggest magma lake, at +1670, +115. Give her the Talisman of the Plasmatic Priests. She gives the item back to you and respawns as High Priestess Shima, along with five Plasmatic Priests and Priestesses, then attacks.\nHigh Priestess Shima says, 'Traitor! You will burn before our might!'\nThe High Priestess hits for a max ~775 (has ~40,000 hps) while her adds hit for under 100 (each have ~25,000 hps). Loot the Head of High Priestess Shima (identifies as \"High Priestess Shima's Head\") from her corpse.\nHead to The Scarlet Desert and find Jimmic Adle in a small hut, at -1710, +1470. Give him the Talisman.  He respawns as High Priest Valon and 4 Plasmatic Priests and Priestesses, then attacks. The mobs here are of the same difficulty as the previous encounter. Loot the Head of High Priest Valon (identifies as \"High Priest Valon's Head\") from his corpse.\nHead to The Great Divide and find Gavon Morant in a hut, at -6115, -490. Give him the Talisman. He respawns as High Priest Maltan and 4 Plasmatic Priests and Priestesses, then attacks. Loot the Head of High Priest Maltan  (identifies as \"High Priest Maltan's Head\") from his corpse.\nGive the three heads and talisman to Omat Vastsea.\nOmat Vastsea says 'Excellent. I think this was the last of the organized Plasmatic Priests. You have done well, I will send you to my brother with my blessing. Thank you for your assistance.'\nCongratulations, you've finished the pre-quest.Rewards:\n[",
