      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** Yes\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Group\n**Min. # of Players:** 3\n**Max. # of Players:** 6\n\nThis is the second monster mission in a series of three which lead up to the 24-person raid monster mission, The Fall of an Empire.\nTulok may be found at +4015, +3465 in the Emerald Jungle, in some ruins on the plateau in the northwest corner of the zone.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tulok'\nTulok says 'Sssso. . .interessssted in [more] of my ssstoriesss?  Or would you prefer to hear about [me] again?'\nYou say, 'More.'\nTulok says 'Yessss. . .Venril managed to become lord over all of Kunark.  But even a lord assss powerful assss he can not prevail againssst the one true lord of darkness. . .death.  And sssoo Venril ssssought a way to cheat death.  He formed a pact with Innoruuk and sssacrificed many to feed that god's unending appetite.  Then with hisss knowledge of lichdom, Venril sssought to be [reborn].'\nYou say, 'Reborn?'\nTulok says 'Venril'ssss high priest, Drogoth, wassss about to perform the unholy ritual when Venril'ssss sssson, Rile, learned of it from his trusted priest, [Avengain].'\nYou say, 'Avengain?'\nTulok says 'Avengain informed Rile who quickly put together a group of ikssssar loyal to him and transsssported them deep into the mountain temple where the ritual was about to take placccce. They were barely [prepared for this task] when they arrived.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'To Raise the King'.\nIn this monster mission you play iksars in an instanced version of the Crypt of Dalnir (what level(s)?).  You must choose between a monk, shadowknight, and shaman.  One player must choose Rile.\nYou say, 'I am prepared for this task.'\nYou are teleported into an instanced version of the Crypt of Dalnir.  Avengain will be standing nearby.\nSpeak with Avengain - Crypt of Dalnir\nYou say, 'Hail, Avengain'\nAvengain says 'Yesss. . . my Lord. My sssuspicions were correct. Former high priest Drogoth isss trying to bring your father back. You must stop him at all costs. I can. . .aid thee my lord. . .by transporting you close to him. . .as the power he wields over thisss temple forbades me. . .from coming closer. Are you [prepared]?'\nYour task 'To Raise the King' has been updated.\nYou say, 'I am prepared.'\nYou are teleported farther into Dalnir, facing the entrance to the temple itself (/loc?).\nConfront the High Priest Drogoth - Crypt of Dalnir\nDrogoth and 2 x Drogoth High Guard will be visible at the top of the temple stairs.  When you approach him, he despawns and immediately 4 x Risen Iksar Soldier will spawn and immediately attack the party.  Upon defeating them you receive a new task update.\nFollow him into the Chamber of Tears - Crypt of Dalnir\nEnter the temple and you are immediately confronted by two more Risen Iksar Soldiers.  Kill them and proceed down the ramp to the next room, where 2 x Risen Iksar Mage await.  Kill them, then jump down to the second floor via the coffin in the middle of the room.  Finally, you will find Drogoth and his two guards again.  Approach him and he will flee again, spawning a hostile Risen Golem from the nearby altar.  Kill it to receive your next update.\nKill both of Drogoth's Guards - Crypt of Dalnir\nDrop down to the third level.  There is a ramp down with a checkerboard pattern on the floor at the base.  The pattern is a false floor.\nUpon landing, you will see one of Drogoth's guards off to the west.  Kill him and proceed past him down the hall.  A skeleton with no name will attack the party in the next room.  Kill it and use the room as a staging area for the next few minutes.\nPull the second guard back to the room.  He will bring adds (names?  levels?), which you should kill first.  Killing the second guard starts a 10-minute timer, with this message as the indicator:\nAs the din from fighting the second guard wanes down, you can begin to hear the sound of deep, intense chanting going on.  It seems the ritual has started and Drogoth and his disciples are so incredibly focused on completing it, that they are ignoring you!\nYour task 'To Raise the King' has been updated.\nStop Drogoth from completing the ceremony! - Crypt of Dalnir\nOnce the second guard is dead, immediately begin chain-pulling the sixteen mobs on the benches in the cathedral (names?  levels?  fight info?).  You can pull them two at a time, as their aggro range is limited to their own bench.  You will see various messages as you kill them:\nVenril's soul has begun to coalesce. . .\nFour minutes later you will see another message.\nBefore your very eyes, Venril's soul begins to form, taking shape. . .\nOnce you see this, you have roughly four minutes to engage Drogoth before he completes the ritual.  You must kill all 16 disciples before Drogoth becomes targetable.  The timer stops as soon as you engage Drogoth.  Kill Drogoth.\nLoot 1 Venril Sathirâ€™s Amulet of Souls\nDeliver 1 Venril Sathirâ€™s Amulet of Souls to Avengain\nLoot 1 The Unholy Book of Zebuxoruk\nDeliver 1 The Unholy book of Zebuxoruk to Avengain\nLoot the two items on his corpse, at which point the group will be teleported back to Avengain automatically.\nUpon delivering the items, a chest (called what?) will spawn with additional loot, including 6 x Shard of Wisdom (need confirmation of exact name) and one additional item.  The common drop is a Gem of Sathir, and the rare drop is a Shadowscale Belt.\nGem of Sathir transmutes to:  ???? (level 1-10), ???? (level 11-20), Lesser Gem of Sathir (level 21-30), Mediocre Gem of Sathir (level 31-40), Gem of Sathir (level 41-50), Greater Gem of Sathir (level 51-60), Flawless Gem of Sathir (level 61-70).\nShadowscale Belt which transmutes to:  ???? (level 1-10), ???? (level 11-20), Torn Shadowscale Belt (level 21-30), Patched Shadowscale Belt (level 31-40), ???? (level 41-50), Adorned Shadowscale Belt (level 51-60), Ornate Shadowscale Belt (level 61-70).\nYour task 'To Raise the King' has been updated.\nTalk to Avengain to leave.\nYou say, 'Leave.'\nYou are teleported back to Tulok.  This next part isn't necessary unless you like the lore.\nNeed task stage/description.\nYou say, 'Hail, Tulok'\nTulok says 'Ssssoooo....the ritual wassss sssstopped before.....the dark lord could be raissssed.....but that was not the end you sssseee.  No...for the Cult of the [Arisen] had planssss and Avengain....their priessst would work tirelessly towardssss them.  For you sssseeee....the cult wanted to be the one to raisssse Venril....for then would he be forever bound to them.'\nYour task 'To Raise the King' has been updated.\nYou say, 'Arisen?'\nTulok says 'Thus after Rile perisssshed....the cult took his body back to sssSebilis where they attempted to infuse Venril'ssss ssssoul into it.  But Avengain....lacking the power that Drogoth commanded....failed to bring the dark lord back...until a lowly band of sssarnak came across the body and sssomehow managed to sssuccessssfully turn Venril into a lich.  But that and the whereaboutsss of the Unholy book is a ssstory for another day.....'\nYou are now able to attempt the next monster mission in the series, \"Zebuxoruk's Pact.\"\nNeed exact in-game task stages and descriptions; dialogues; quest items; exact in-game name, /loc, fight info, level ranges for mobs; faction hits if any; any missing information.Submitted by: revised write-up by Corstin Tronedor, Sword of Fate, PrexusRewards:\n- Adorned Shadowscale Belt [item=72297]\n- Dreadscale Boots [item=61988]\n- Dreadscale Bracer [item=61824]\n- Dreadscale Gauntlets [item=62556]\n- Dreadscale Greaves [item=62315]\n- Dreadscale Helm [item=62554]\n- Dreadscale Mask [item=61770]\n- Dreadscale Vambraces [item=62555]\n- Flawless Gem of Sathir [item=51248]\n- Gem of Sathir [item=51247]\n- Gem of Sathir [item=115245]\n- Greater Gem of Sathir [item=51249]\n- Lesser Gem of Sathir [item=115235]\n- Mediocre Gem of Sathir [item=66969]\n- Ornate Shadowscale Belt [item=50836]\n- Patched Shadowscale Belt [item=115240]\n- Shadowscale Belt [item=50835]\n- Torn Shadowscale Belt [item=115236]\n[",
