    {
      id = "3984",
      title = "Strangeness in the Thicket",
      exp = "03",
      exp_name = "The Shadows of Luclin",
      min_lvl = 23,
      max_lvl = 23,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = 985.0, x = 2950.0, z = 0.0 },
      triggers = {
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "away your cover", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 23\n**Maximum Level:** 23\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nYou may be able to request this task outside the listed level (23).\nWho starts this task? (It is a task master in Shar Vahl; we know that much.)\nThis was a \"medium\" task available to a 23rd level Ranger.\nVery quickly, you need to speak with Brenyon Seng, to let them know that you're the Red Beetle.  Your contact will know what that means.\nSpeak with Brenyon Seng in Hollowshade Moors\nBrenyon is at location 985, 2950.\nYour contact was impressed that you kept your wits about you and didn't give away your cover.  Now, as to why you're here.  Your code name is Red Beetle and you've been assigned to explore the lava tunnel in the north. This is a very dangerous place where reports suggest there is a rebellion forming.  You must go there and determine whether or not this is true.\nExplore the lava tunnel in the north of Shadeweaver's Thicket\nIt looks like the insurgents are forming quickly, Red Beetle.  It's up to you to take the raven to the raven's nest and kill 10 gor taku bruisers. Only after that will you be able to retire from this life of subterfuge. Good luck.\nKill 10 gor taku bruisers in Shadeweaver's Thicket\nYou were almost discovered, and that's a quick way to foil the operation --  or worse yet -- get yourself killed.  However, you were able to secure the area and get rid of the rebels.  Find and speak with Zauvudd Gigoth, codenamed Black Bixie, to update your progress.  After that, your services will no longer be needed.\nSpeak with Zauvudd Gigoth in the Plane of Knowledge\nYou've impressed quite a few people with your cunning.  Some thought that\nyou, the Red Beetle, would fail, but others felt you had exactly what it\ntook to get the job done.  They were right.  You may be contact in the\nfuture, Red Beetle, so keep a watchful eye to the sky for the Black Bixie.\nHere's a little something for your trouble.\nYou receive 10 platium, 5 gold, 8 silver, and 7 copper.\nYou gain experience!!\nExperience gained was about 25% of a level at 23.Rewards:\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "3985",
      title = "Toasty Little Critters",
      exp = "03",
      exp_name = "The Shadows of Luclin",
      min_lvl = 22,
      max_lvl = 22,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "them back a little piece of mind", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 22\n**Maximum Level:** 22\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nYou may be able to request this task outside the listed level (22). It is not available at level 23.\nThis was a \"medium\" task available to a 22nd level Ranger.\nIt's no small wonder that the locals are skittish.   There have been reports of some monsters lurking about that are a threat to not only the people, but the livestock and supplies as well.  You're going to need to help give them back a little piece of mind.  To do that, you're going to kill 10 Firefall Saureks.  Remember, they're threatening the supplies, so be sure to loot 4 Damaged Hopper Hide, while you're out there.  The locals are counting on you.\nKill 10 Firefall Saureks in Shadeweaver's Thicket\nLoot 4 Damaged Hopper hides in Shadeweaver's Thicket\nYour help in getting rid of those mongrels is more appreciated than you know.  There's just one thing left for you to do though, and that's to deliver 4 Damaged Hopper Hide to Fellmoor Powell.  I'm sure getting some additional supplies will be a relief.\nDeliver 4 Damaged Hopper hide to Fellmoor Powell in Shadeweaver's Thicket\nYou really did a phenomenal job helping those locals out.  They were too scared to even go out at night.  It's a wonder they were able to hang in there that long.  Your help has proven to them that there's nothing that they can't handle, but they know that if they ever have problems like this again, to call on you.  They've been able to pool some of their meager earnings as thanks for your help.  Well done!\nYou receive 5 platinum, 2 gold, 9 silver, and 4 copper.\nYou gain experience!!\nExperience gained was about 10% of a level at 22.Rewards:\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "3990",
      title = "Ceremonial Functions",
      exp = "05",
      exp_name = "The Legacy of Ykesha",
      min_lvl = 65,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = 1387.06, x = 75.11, z = 3.13 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Assistant Vagli",
        "What task?",
        "task",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 65\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis task was available at 70th level. It may be available at other levels.\nAssistant Vagli can be found in the pirate village in Gulf of Gunthak. at location 1387.06, 75.11, 3.13.\nEntry for map file:\nP -75.1076, -1387.0557, 0.0020, 240, 240, 0, 3, Assistant_Vagli\nYou say, 'Hail, Assistant Vagli'\nAssistant Vagli says 'Greetings, friend. If you have come to study under the great Alvarik you have come to the right place! I help by carrying his research tomes for him. If there is one you would like to buy, feel free to browse through what we have. If you're looking for something to do, I may have a [task] available for you to get started on. Alvarik has much he needs done and I can't do it all myself!'\nYou say, 'What task?'\nAt this point you are offered three tasks, one of them being Ceremonial Functions.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Ceremonial Functions'.\nExplore the large assembly hall with uneven flooring.\nYou're going off to uncover what these lands have to offer. It won't necessarily be easy, and there will be those that want to stop you from uncovering anything at all, but you've got to be resolute in your actions. To start, you need to explore the large assembly hall with uneven flooring. Once you've done that, a courier will be sent with more information on the next step!\nThis is the large room above the trap door on the East side of Crypt of Nadox.\nYour Location is -91.00, -655.76, 37.13\nEntry for map file:\nP 655.7581, 91.0032, 34.0020, 240, 240, 0, 3, Assembly_hall\nKill 10 luggald guardians\nLoot 4 Luggald Trident\nOh no! You've been waylaid by monsters! Get rid of them so you can get back on track! Quickly, kill 10 luggald guardians, and be sure to loot 4 Luggald Trident, so there's no evidence of their deaths, just in case others come looking for them.\nLuggald Guardians can be found in the NorthWest section of Crypt of Nadox. Be sure to hold on to the Luggald Tridents you loot; you'll need the later.\nExplore the chamber with the ceremonial skull in the far east.\nThat was an exciting distraction, but you need to focus and redouble your efforts. You need to get back out there and explore the chamber with the ceremonial skull in the far east,. There's a whole world out there just waiting to have its secrets uncovered and you're perfect for the job.\nThis is a room on the East side of Torgiran Mines.\nYour Location is 1160.81, -1068.35, -78.37\nEntry for map file:\nP 1068.3469, -1160.8079, -81.4979, 240, 240, 0, 3, Ceremonial_Skull\nExplore the bridge separating the mines and the overlord's complex.\nYou've got to admit that uncovering these secrets is exciting. But you're not done yet. You've got one more spot to explore before you can call it a day. Go explore the bridge separating the mines and the overlord's complex, then you can think about heading home.\nThis is the bridge in Torgiran Mines just South of the zone from Crypt of Nadox.\nYour Location is 701.82, -395.25, -16.41\nEntry for map file:\nP 395.2510, -701.8226, -19.5362, 240, 240, 0, 3, Bridge_to_Overlord's_Complex\nKill 10 Broken Skull bloodguards\nDrat! Your attempt to hide the evidence wasn't enough and now their friends are after you. You've got to stand tall and kill 10 Broken Skull bloodguards, before they kill you!\nBroken Skull bloodguards can be found on either side of the aforementioned bridge.\nDeliver 4 Luggald Trident to Delithuea\nYou did well. you should take the evidence you collected and deliver 4 Luggald Trident to Delithuea, so they have a record of what went on today.\nDelithuea can be found in the pirate village in Gulf of Gunthak.\nYour Location is 1622.51, -160.10, 3.13\nP 160.1029, -1622.5093, 0.0020, 240, 240, 0, 3, Delithuea\nUpon handing the 4 Luggald Trident to her:\nExploration isn't all fun and games, as you discovered today. You need to always keep a sharp eye and an even sharper mind on everything around you so you aren't so easily surprised. In any case, so you can take care of any battle wounds or resupply, here's a small stipend for today's work.\nYou receive 4 copper.\nYou receive 3 silver.\nYou receive 7 gold.\nYou receive 205 platinum.\nYou gain experience!! (32% AA exp at 70th level with 90% going to AAs)\nMob info relative to a 70th level druid with 1462 AC:\nLuggald Guardians are dark blue, snareable, rootable do not summon, hit ~120-150 and take magic & fire DoTs nicely. Enrage from 9% to about 5%.\nBroken Skull bloodguards are light blue, snareable, rootable do not summon, hit ~80-100 and take magic & fire DoTs nicely.Rewards:\n[",
    },
