    {
      id = "407",
      title = "Brain Bite (Firiona Vie)",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 45,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = 270.0, x = -3800.0, z = 0.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Despondo",
        "Whats wrong?",
        "I will rescue their souls.",
        "Where are the three bottles of entrapment?",
        "What is Brain Bite?",
        "rescue their souls",
        "three bottles of entrapment",
        "Brain Bite",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "you the wizard spell [Brain Bite]'", count = 1 },
        { name = "you the bottles", count = 1 },
        { name = "him a Peridot", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 8326, name = "Scroll of Brain Bite", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 45\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Despondo'\nDespondo looks a bit troubled and says, 'Welcome, welcome adventurer, I am the wizard tutor Despondo although few need tutorage around here.  It would seem that this is no place for a student of any sorts.  The lands of Kunark are quite deadly.'\nYou say, 'Whats wrong?'\nDespondo says, 'I was bound to this post by General Veredeth.  I came to find the lost souls of my friends, but am needed here.  I must find a fellow wizard to [rescue their souls]'\nYou say, 'I will rescue their souls.'\nDespondo says, 'You will need the [three bottles of entrapment]. If you can find their remains in Kunark they you will give the bottles to the body and their soul shall enter.  Return all three bottles and I shall give you the wizard spell [Brain Bite]'\nYou say, 'Where are the three bottles of entrapment?'\nDespondo says, 'I will need three gems to prepare the bottles.  I am afraid I left my currency within the Freeport Vault.  You will have to get the gems I need: a peridot, an onyx and a star rose quartz. Then I will give you the bottles.'\nYou say, 'What is Brain Bite?'\nDespondo says, 'Brain Bite is a concussion spell created by my former friends whose souls are now lost to Kunark.  The blow to the inner brain of an enraged foe may just cause the loss of memory and lower their rage.  If you want a copy you have to [rescue their souls].'\nGive him a Peridot, an Onyx and a Star Rose Quartz. In exchange, you will receive three bottles of entrapment. They each look like a royal jelly jar and must be identified to figure out which is which.\nThey identify as Hampton, Ryla, and Mardon.\nHampton, a human skeleton, is located along the zone wall of Trakanon's Teeth location +270, -3800. Head towards the bottom right of the map, towards SEB. Once you pass through the main archway to the East area of the zone, head NE. He'll be standing by himself in the North most part. He won't agro. Hand him the correct bottle to receive a bottle of swirling smoke, which identifies as Hampton's Soul.\nRyla, a human skeleton, is located in a jail cell in Karnor's Castle. Go straight into the zone, over both bridges and then hang a left. There is a stair case in there. Take the stairs up to the roof and then go left to the edge of the wall. You may need to kill a few undead here. Hang a right and follow to the end which goes around a corner. The jail cells will be on your right. The mobs inside WILL agro if you look. The human skeleton spawns inside the 2nd on the right. Give the correct bottle to the skeleton to receive a bottle of swirling smoke, which identifies as Ryla's Soul.\nMardon, a human skeleton, is located in the City of Mist reaver tower at location +136 -641. Give the correct bottle to the skeleton to receive a bottle of swirling smoke, which identifies as Mardon's Soul.\nReturn to Despondo and hand him the three bottles to receive the spell Brain Bite.\nDespondo embraces the bottles as if they were babes. 'Rejoice, my friends!! Your souls are safe. _____, you are a good wizard.  You deserve to know the secret of concussion.'\nYour faction standing with Inhabitants of Firiona Vie got better.\nYour faction standing with Emerald Warriors got better.\nYour faction standing with Storm Guard got better.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis got worse.\nYour faction standing with Pirates of Gunthak got worse.Rewards:\n- Scroll of Brain Bite [item=8326]\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "408",
      title = "Burynai Bundt Cake",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Glinya Sweetpie",
        "treekill?",
        "burynai bundt cake",
        "Hail, Scout Treekill",
        "helm",
        "chewing",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "you this bard's helm for a burynai bundt cake!'", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAsk Glinya Sweetpie about Treekill. and she turns angry and says \"Treekill!! I do not want to see nor hear of him. He is always trying to impress me!! I finally told him that I would walk with him if he could bake a Burynai Bunt Cake.\"  Ask her 'what is a burynai bunt cake' and she says \"Burynai Bunt Cake? There is no such thing.\"  Ask Treekill about the cake and he is, quite obviously very anxious to get his hands on one to win the ladies hand.  He promises to reward you with a helm he got from a bard if you bring him a Burynai Bunt Cake.\nIt has been confirmed that this is not a quest at this time, but is simply a storyline.  Thus, there is no reward available.\nYou say, 'Hail, Glinya Sweetpie'\nGlinya Sweetpie is covered with flour. She reaches out to shake your hand. 'Pleased to meet you. Ooops! Teehee! I have gotten flour on your hand. Please forgive me. I have been quite busy baking bread for the soldiers - even that braggart, Treekill. Look around. I even have a few items shipped from the Faydwer.'\nYou say, 'treekill?'\nGlinya Sweetpie turns angry. 'Treekill! I do not want to see or hear of him. He is always trying to impress me! I finally told him I would walk with him if he could bake a burynai bundt cake.'\nYou say, 'burynai bundt cake'\nGlinya Sweetpie says, 'Burynai bundt cake? There is no such thing.'\nYou say, 'Hail, Scout Treekill'\nScout Treekill has a helm tied to his belt. He is chewing something. He spits some shells out and they land on your chest. 'Sorry about that. Hehe.'\nYou say, 'helm'\nScout Treekill grabs the helm and juggles it in front of your face. 'Bet you wish you had one. I busted some bard's lute for playing Teir'Dal songs. I told him I would move on to his face unless he had something of value. This is all he had. Said he found it in a place some call Sebilis. I took it even though it is something only a bard would wear. That's just how I am, a kindly soul. Hehehe...'\nYou say, 'burynai bundt cake'\nScout Treekill gets excited. ' What?! Do you know how to bake a burynai bundt cake. Glinya said she would marry me if I baked one! She won't let me use her oven so I had to search for one. I finally located one in some goblin mine, but I can't find the recipe or bake it. Please! I would give you this bard's helm for a burynai bundt cake!'\nYou say, 'chewing'\nScout Treekill says, 'Can't you tell?! It's on your chest. Heh! What a dim one! They're flarefire seeds. Only good thing about this land. Trackers find 'em in the Field of Bone near some lizard city.'Rewards:\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "409",
      title = "Cabilis Pale Ale (Firiona Vie)",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 1,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Lenka Stoutheart",
        "I want to see something interesting.",
        "What is Cabby Pale Ale?",
        "What is lizardtown?",
        "want to see something interesting",
        "Cabby Pale Ale",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Lenka Stoutheart'\nLenka Stoutheart sips on her ale, 'Look what we have here, Bronto! A would be hero!\nBronto Thudfoot puts his head over your head as if measuring you. 'Heh!! Going to have to grow up before the General lets him out to play in Kunark!'\nLenka Stoutheart says 'We're just kidding with you, kid. Although they are making heroes kind of small these days. Hey you [want to see something interesting]?'\nYou say,'I want to see something interesting.'\nLenka Stoutheart takes a jagged scimitar out of a wrap and lets you hold it. You feel as though it is linked to the spirit world. Lenka grabs it back. 'No, no! You cant keep it. But I can tell you there are plenty more weopons and armor like this. Just have to do a little dragon slaying.'\nBronto Thudfoot says 'No way, Lenka! This place is too dangerous for this kid. Why don't you just stay here and drink it up with us? the Samson couldn't even brew bog juice right, but every once in a while a bashed-up explorer comes in carrying [Cabby Pale Ale].'\nYou say, 'What is Cabby Pale Ale?'\nBronto Thudfoot takes a bottle from his pack and shows you. 'This is Cabby Pale Ale. CPA for short or, as they say in lizardtown, Cabilis Pale Ale. I got it off a drunken dwarf. He said he bought it off a dark elf. Where he really got it, I am not sure.'\nLenka Stoutheart says 'I hear they sell the stuff in only two places. Lizardtown and Neriak. Hmmm. Now, why is that?\nYou say, 'What is lizardtown?'\nBronto Thudfoot says 'Just like it sounds. A town full of those lizardmen called Iksar. I thought they were extinct along with raptors, the Combine Empire, and cheap booze.'\nYou say, 'What is lizardtown?'\nLenka Stoutheart says 'The trackers of Firiona Vie have come back with reports that the Iksar are back in force and have a city somewhere in the heart of Kunark. There goes the neighborhood...again.'\nYou can buy this Ale from vendors in the Field of Bones, Cabilis and Neriak, but giving it to them does not get anything.\nNeed /loc of quest mobs, list of faction hits, list of rewards.Rewards:\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "410",
      title = "Cleric Spells (Good Version)",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 50,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = -3551.0, x = 3056.0, z = -76.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Frist Furtun",
        "I am in search of new magiks.",
        "I have duplicate scrolls.",
        "have",
        "duplicate scrolls",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 50\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nFrist Furtun may be found at -3551, +3056, -76 in the southwest section of the city (on progression servers) ou at +255, -3300 in the outpost (on regular servers).\nYou say, 'Hail, Frist Furtun'\nFrist Furtun says 'Hail to thee, adventurer! I have been sent to this new land by the Clerics of Tunare in search of the new arcane magiks said to exist beyond this outpost. I myself once searched the nearby Outlands, but to go any further would lead to my certain death. Lately, the dangers have proven to be too much for adventurers and ones like myself. Have you also ventured to this land in search of these [new magiks?]'\nYou say, 'I am in search of new magiks.'\nFrist Furtun says 'Ahh, wonderful!  The more souls who search for these scrolls, the sooner I'll be able to return home and share this knowledge.  The magiks are in the form of scrolls held by the strongest creatures of the Outlands. You will probably have the best luck searching in the darkest depths of the dungeons beyond this outpost. You might want to talk to the residents of this outpost for locations of these dreadful places. If you should happen to [have] any [duplicate scrolls], please come speak to me. I might be interested in working out a trade for a scroll you do not yet have.'\nYou say, 'I have duplicate scrolls.'\nFrist Furtun says 'Great! The scrolls I am interested in are those of Death Pact, Upheaval, Yaulp IV, and Reckoning. If you bring me any one of these scrolls, I'll let you reach into my bag and pull out one of the four very rare scrolls that have come into my possession.'\nThere are no faction hits involved. On handing in one of those scrolls:\nFrist Furtun says 'Here is the scroll that I promised. We have both gained much knowledge today. I hope to do business with you again soon. Farewell!'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou will receive one of four spells: Sunskin, Word of Vigor, Unswerving Hammer of Faith, or Heroic Bond. There are no faction hits involved.Rewards:\n- Spell: Heroic Bond [item=8690]\n- Spell: Sunskin [item=8692]\n- Spell: Unswerving Hammer [item=9747]\n- Spell: Word of Vigor [item=8688]\n[",
