      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 50\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAnniversary events tend to run from mid-March to mid-April (sometimes to mid-May) each year. They are not available during the \"off season\".\nFor an overview and list of EverQuest Anniversary events, see this quest entry [quest=6782].\nZoning into Kael Drakkel with the correction faction level (amiable. What number?), you recieve the following yellow test emote.\nKivak Icekeeper says 'Welcome to our city small one. If you are interested I might have a task you could assist me with. Come find me near Pollos and his bank should you wish to help.'\nKivak Icekeeper may be found at -125, +1525 (outside the bank where Pollos Stormkeeper resides). You must have at least amiable faction with Kromzek giants before being able to do this quest.\nMap FIle Location of Kivak:\nP -1525, 130, -200, 0, 0, 0, 2, Kivak_Icekeeper_(7th_anniversary)\nYou say, 'Hail, Kivak Icekeeper'\nKivak Icekeeper says 'Ah short one, you have found me! You seem to be the helpful sort, are you [interested] in undertaking a task for me?'\nYou say, 'I am interested'\nKivak Icekeeper says 'I have this wager going with Pollos there about whether I can get all of these items collected or not. If you could gather these [items] up for me I'd be much obliged and would even toss in something special to make it worth your while.'\nYou say, 'What items?'\nKivak Icekeeper says 'This here is a list of clues for what I need. Pollos didn't think I'd be able to figure out what they meant, but now it's for you to figure out. Here's a bag for you as well. Once you fill that bag up with the items those clues refer to, return it to me and we'll see what old Pollos thinks of that!'\nYou receive a Kromzek Collection Bag and A Kromzek Clue Book, which reads:\n1. Feeling Lucky?\n2. A storied part of the snow.\n3. Split and shattered. Measure the remains.\n4. A weapon of the cruelly marked.\n5. Primitive experiments in art receive a cold reception.\n6. A verminous tribute to the bones.\n7. A small keepsake.\n8. Wild flights of safety.\n9. A taste of the hollow trunk.\n10. An extension to your phobia.\nYou are looking for:\n1. A Collector's Snow Bunny Foot, bunnies, Eastern Wastes\n2. A Collector's Cougar Tail, cougars, Iceclad Ocean\n3. A Collector's Shardwurm Scale, shardwurms, Great Divide\n4. A Collector's Wyvern Claw, a wyvern, Cobalt Scar\n5. A Collector's Ice Sculpture, an Icepaw kobold (kobold village), Velketor's Labyrinth\n6. A Collector's Chetari Ceremonial Staff, chetari, Dragon Necropolis\n7. A Collector's Velium Trinket, coldain dwarfs, Icewell Keep\n8. A Collector's Preserved Drake Wing, drakes, Western Wastes\n9. A Collector's Bulthar Tongue, bulthars, Siren's Grotto\n10. A Collector's Terror Tentacle, terrors, Crystal Caverns\nCombine these 10 items in the bag to craft a Sealed Kromzek Collection Bag.  Hand this in to Kivak Icekeeper.\nThe Kromzek Clue Book should not be placed in the bag upon combine, and can be discarded when done with the quest if so desired.\nUpon Hand In:\nKivak Icekeeper says 'Hah! Won't Pollos be surprised to see this! Lets just keep this between us though. I can't wait to see the look on his face. Take this staff as payment for your help. May it light your path for years to come.'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive Kromzekian Walking Stick of Allegiance\nYou receive a Kromzekian Walking Stick of Allegiance.Submitted by: bbotRewards:\n- Kromzekian Walking Stick of Allegiance [item=61436]\n[",
    },
