      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 60\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nFind James the Watchmaker in the Plane of Knowledge next to the Halas stone.\nHe offers a task for each one of the hotzones introduced in the April 18, 2007 patch (listed here for reference).\nYou say, 'Hail, James the Watchmaker'\nJames the Watchmaker says, 'Hello there _____! Do you happen to have the [time]?'\nYou say, 'The time?'\nJames the Watchmaker says, 'Yes, the time of day. You see I usually keep a number of watches with me at all times so I always know what time it is but I recently [lost], well, all of them.'\nYou say, 'How were they lost?'\nJames the Watchmaker says, 'I lost them when I was travelling last week. I wanted to visit some of the places in Norrath that were special to me but I seemed to run into trouble everywhere I visited! And wouldn't you know it but everytime I stopped for a bit I managed to lose one of my [watches]!'\nYou say, 'Watches?'\nJames the Watchmaker says, 'That's what I said, watches! Are you hard of hearing? I don't suppose you would like to [look] for my watches? I hate not knowing what time it is! I'm sure I could find something in my backpack to interest you if you found one of my watches!'\nYou say, 'I will look for them'\nThis brings up a quest selector with several quests: One for each hotzone ranging from 20 to 65. Each has a very original name of: \"Help me repair my watch! (Level X)\", where X is between 20 and 65, in multiples of 5.\nThe task for 60th level:\nDeliver 1 Gold Etched Gear #1 to James the Watchmaker. 0/1 Plane of Knowledge\nDeliver 1 Gold Etched Reinforced Rod to James the Watchmaker. 0/1 Plane of Knowledge\nDeliver 1 Gold Etched Gear #2 to James the Watchmaker. 0/1 Plane of Knowledge\nDeliver 1 Gold Etched Gear #3 to James the Watchmaker. 0/1 Plane of Knowledge\nThese gears are dropped randomly in Dragon Necropolis. They may be looted prior to retrieving the task.\nTurn them in and choose from different head-slot items:\n\"Helmet w/Extended Range IV (except for Melee) +2 regen for all, +2 mana regen for Caster/Priests, +5 Attack for Hybrid/Melee\"\n(What are the names of the gears dropped, and what are the different rewards?)Rewards:\n- Expert Crafted Helm of the Arcane [item=67683]\n- Expert Crafted Helm of the Attackers [item=67685]\n- Expert Crafted Helm of the Healers [item=67684]\n- Expert Crafted Helm of the Keen [item=67686]\n[",
