        { id = 9148, name = "Vision of Sebilite", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Time:** 6 hours\n**Level:** 25\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAfter the takeover of the city of Firiona Vie by the forces of Lanys T`Vyl, Luminare Pasinia may be found outside the city on a hill at /loc -249, -2351, 342.\nIn 2016 on TLP (Ragefire with Kunark enabled) she is located at -3955.45, 2626.09, -77.97 (in the building with caster GMs and spell vendors).\nYou say, 'Hail, Luminare Pasinia'\nLuminare Pasinia waves her hands as if to cast a spell. 'GREETINGS!! I am the Luminare of Firiona by decree of his royal highness, King Thex,I am here to research spells and artifacts. I have much to do. I welcome any enchanter who offers to [assist the great Luminare].'\nYou say, 'I will assist the great Luminare.'\nLuminare Pasinia says 'And great I am, indeeed!! Alas, not great enough to be everywhere at once. I would gladly reward you if you would [collect components] for me.'\nYou say, 'I will collect components for you.'\nLuminare Pasinia says 'Then go into the wilds beyond the outpost and upon your return, you shall give to me the powder of Nok, heart of ice. Ton warrior totem, and a sabertooth tiger mane. This shall earn you knowledge of an enchanter spell I recently scribed.'\n1) Powder of Nok - Nok Shaman Powder (identifies as \"Powder of Nok\") comes from a \"froglok nok shaman\" in the north area of this zone.  It looks like black pixie dust.\n2) Heart of Ice - This is dropped by various icebone skeletons in the Lake of Ill Omen, the Swamp of No Hope, or Kurn's Tower.\n3) Ton Warrior Totem - This is dropped by various frogloks found in the froglok city in the Swamp of No Hope, and identifies as \"Key of Dai -I.\".  They spawn apparently in several places but aren't very common.\n4) Sabertooth Mane - These drop off the sabertooth Tigers found in Lake of Ill Omen, the Overthere, and Trakanon's Teeth.\nBring these items back to Luminare:\nLuminare Pasinia says 'Do you not remember that I asked for powder of Nok, a Ton warrior totem, a heart of ice and a sabertooth tiger mane?  Incomplete deeds shall fetch no enchanter reward.'\nLuminare Pasinia says 'Do you not remember that I asked for powder of Nok, a Ton warrior totem, a heart of ice and a sabertooth tiger mane?  Incomplete deeds shall fetch no enchanter reward.'\nLuminare Pasinia says 'Do you not remember that I asked for powder of Nok, a Ton warrior totem, a heart of ice and a sabertooth tiger mane?  Incomplete deeds shall fetch no enchanter reward.'\nLuminare Pasinia places the items into a sack and removes a scroll from her robe.  This is yours.  A spell I discovered and translated for one with less intelligence than the great Luminare of Firiona Vie.  You may kiss my feet now.'\nYour faction standing with Inhabitants of Firiona Vie got better.\nYour faction standing with Emerald Warriors got better.\nYour faction standing with Storm Guard got better.\nYour faction standing with Legion of Cabilis got worse.\nYour faction standing with Pirates Of Gunthak got worse.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive a scroll called Vision of Sebilite, which scribes as the spell \"Illusion Iksar.\"Submitted by: Solrias Spellweaver, revised by Vaedian C`NarxRewards:\n- Spell: Illusion: Iksar [item=60560]\n- Vision of Sebilite [item=9148]\n[",
