      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "What about the skull?",
        "ribcage",
        "foot",
        "hand",
        "skull",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "your body to the soul of the slain commander", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 76893, name = "Chronobine", type = "item" },
        { id = 77490, name = "Iksar Tail Bones", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 80\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is a sub-task to be completed in conjunction with its grand task, \"The Grand Illusion\" [quest=4713]. It begins with Phara Dar in the Field of Scale.\nUpon receiving task \"The Grand Illusion\":\nPhara Dar says 'We shall see ______. We shall see. In order to make a convincing illusion, I will need a [ribcage], a [foot], a [hand], and finally a [skull]. Once I have all 4 pieces of this skeletal puzzle, not even Ganak himself will be able to see through your disguise.'\nYou say, 'What about the skull?'\nPhara Dar says 'I suspect this will be your most difficult task, _______. The skull I require must come from one who holds great power within the Iksar forces. I doubt you can confront Ganak or Kurn directly, but I am sure you can find one of command within their ranks. One word of caution though, ______. This skull must not have any of the former owner's life essence remaining within, as the illusion could overpower you and give your body to the soul of the slain commander.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Skull of the Ancient'.\nFind a suitable skull for Phara Dar's illusion 0/1 (All)\nGo to the Field of Bone (yes, the Field of BONE) and find Commander Koth (undead) in the Kaesora ruins. Kill him and loot the Petrified Skull of Commander Koth.\nDeliver the skull of Commander Koth to Phara Dar 0/1 (Field of Scale)\nHand the skull to Phara Dar for win.\nPhara Dar receives the skull with a puzzled look upon her face.\nPhara Dar says 'Strange that you bring me this skull, _____. Our scouts report Commander Koth is alive and well within Kaesora's walls. How you came to acquire such an item I do not fully comprehend, but your task is done, and you have delivered what I asked of you.'\nReward:\nExperience\nFaction (Tynoc: +105)\nChronobines (varies)\nIksar Tail BonesSubmitted by: OlivanRewards:\n- Chronobine [item=76893]\n- Iksar Tail Bones [item=77490]\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "4827",
      title = "Bristlebane's Party Favor - Bristlebane's Favor",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 75,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Fizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image",
        "A party?",
        "I",
        "party",
        "challenge",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "you warts if you pester them", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 83320, name = "Bristlebane's Party Generator", type = "item" },
        { id = 83318, name = "Celebratory Fireworks Caster", type = "item" },
        { id = 37919, name = "Distillate of Alacrity X", type = "item" },
        { id = 73177, name = "Distillate of Celestial Healing XIII", type = "item" },
        { id = 73179, name = "Distillate of Clarity XIII", type = "item" },
        { id = 73176, name = "Distillate of Divine Healing XIII", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 75\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAnniversary events tend to run from mid-March to mid-April (sometimes to mid-May) each year. They are not available during the \"off season\".\nFor an overview and list of EverQuest Anniversary events, see this quest entry [quest=6782].\nThis is an anniversary quest available only during anniversary season (a few weeks during March and April). It was introduced in 2009 as part of EverQuest's 10th anniversary.\nThis is one of 16 deity quests. For an overview of how rewards work and how these quests are linked with one another, see this writeup [quest=4843].\nBelow here are the details for this particular quest.\nFizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image wanders the Plane of Knowledge near the Soulbinder.\nYou say, 'Hail, Fizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image'\nFizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image says 'Hello there! You might know me. Then again, you might not. No matter to me, really. I just wanted to invite you to a [party]!'\nYou say, 'A party?'\nFizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image says 'It seems to me that lately you folks here on Norrath have gotten a bit too stressed out. You've been slaying dragons for a decade, it's time to relax! So I've set up some firework shows for you. Of course with any good party plans, you really should expect to go to several places to get the most out of it. So do you want to enjoy a good show? Are you up to the challenge? A party [challenge]!'\nYou say, 'I'll take the challenge'\nFizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image says 'Well then, good luck! Most of all have fun!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Bristlebane's Party Favor - Bristlebane's Favor'.\nBristlebane wants you to visit the firework shows all over Norrath. They happen only at one place at a time, so you have to keep moving!\nBristlebane told you that he's having a party and has challenged you to participate. All over Norrath, and likely a few other places, there are firework shows to enjoy. All he has asked is that you find those fireworks and enjoy them. But the fireworks show only happens in one place at a time, so you'll have to keep moving. Bristlebane assured you that nothing bad would happen to you...\nCLUE: Where there's fireworks, there's smoke. Where there's hot water, there's this.\nLOCATION: Steamfont -- SE portion of zone (40, -1264, -22) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: For small folks, they sure play a big game of chess!\nLOCATION: Butcherblock -- around PoK book (-1607, -327, 2) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Where the Windstalker used to stalk.\nLOCATION: Qeynos Hills -- south of Hadden (2380, 1015, 30) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Big feet, big sandy footprints.\nLOCATION: Southern Desert of Ro -- around spectre isle (3792,-1631,15) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: If a bear was bare here, it couldn't bear it.\nLOCATION: Everfrost -- path south of PoK book, also wanders through most of the mountain paths (2573, 431,-56)\n(CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Stone boat shuttles? Who are they kidding?\nLOCATION: Erudin -- on the docks (0,0,22) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Fear? Rot? Well, these are a few of my favorite things.\nLOCATION: The Feerrott -- wide circle around the druid ring and PoK book (212, -2040, 15) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Kurn's View isn't so nice here as it once was.\nLOCATION: Field of Bone -- walks the path from Cabilis entrance down to the pit (-2080,2684,13) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: The markets here are wonderful, though who really needs that much catnip?\nLOCATION: Shar Vahl -- bridge near Shadeweaver zone (-845,100,-186) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Only an elf would think that their dark is greater than someone else's.\nLOCATION: Greater Faydark -- underneath Kelethin, near PoD lift, NW of druid ring (75, 183, 1) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: I can't believe that those leatherfoot, er leatherfeets, are still alive.\nLOCATION: Nektolus Forest -- wizard portal area (28, -724, 9) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Trolls be wary, this is their home and they will give you warts if you pester them.\nLOCATION: Rathe Mountains -- old hill giant area (356, 2343, 3) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Are you one with the wall?\nLOCATION: Misty Thicket -- on top of the wall (-76, 588, 37) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Minitab? Is that even a word?\nLOCATION: Natimbi -- pathing IN the river, east to west (and sometimes south into the ocean), you can get update levitating above him (934, -190, 144) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: You take the low pass....\nLOCATION: Highpass Hold -- in front of Highpass Keep (-90, -170, -21) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: I'd prefer a crescent roll myself.\nLOCATION: Crescent Reach -- back part of zone, on ground below dragons (-540, -165, -42) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Home to many of the world's largest things: largest Gnome launcher, largest clockwork and largest crash site!\nLOCATION: Dragonscale Hills -- on road near the farm, around (3516, -920, 77); also has been sited on the beach by the docks and in the water there (CONFIRMED)\nnote: The party machine not only walks around in DSH, he also warps from spot to spot. Just pick one of the known sighting locations and hang out there until you see him.\nCLUE: High places are always covered with the veil of morning light.\nLOCATION: Dawnshroud Peaks -- doing a wide ring outside Sanctus Seru between the baker's camp and Netherbian (550, 1380, 111) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Where claws met Norrath.\nLOCATION: Cobalt Scar -- walking along the beach (-716, -468, 61) (CONFIRMED)\nCLUE: Edge of the sea with the same name.\nLOCATION: Barren Coast -- along the coastline near the docks (-200, -310, 5) (CONFIRMED)\nUpon completion:\nYour task 'Bristlebane's Party Favor - Bristlebane's Favor' has been updated.\nBristlebane told you that he's having a party and has challenged you to participate. All over Norrath, and likely a few other places, there are firework shows to enjoy. All he has asked is that you find those fireworks and enjoy them. But the fireworks show only happens in one place at a time, so you'll have to keep moving. Bristlebane assured you that nothing bad would happen to you...\nYou hear a laugh in your mind. Bristlebane has noticed your attendance at his party.\nFizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image shouts 'Thanks for attending my party! You've been a wonderful guest. May our next ten years together be as grand as our first!'\nFizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image says 'See ya!'\nIF YOU HAIL BRISTLEBANE'S IMAGE AFTERWARDS:\nYou say, 'Hail, Fizzlethorpe Bristlebane`s Image'\nBristlebane says, 'I hope you enjoyed the show! I bet you thought I was going to trick you and do something funny to you when you got to each of my shows. So when you got to the fireworks you were probably worried that something bad was going to happen! Well, some tricks are more subtle than a pie in the face.'\nReward(s):\nFireworks Focus of Bristlebane\nPotion of Adventure II\nPlayer flags\nBristlebane's Party Generator\nCelebratory Fireworks Caster\n3150p, 0g, 0s, 0c\nExperience\nThis option offers the following:\nOption 1: Distillate of Alacrity X\nOption 2: Distillate of Celestial Healing XIII\nOption 3: Distillate of Clarity XIII\nOption 4: Distillate of Divine Healing XIII\nOption 5: Distillate of Health XIII\nOption 6: Replenishment XIII\nOption 7: Distillate of Spirituality XIIISubmitted by: CylienaRewards:\n- Bristlebane's Party Generator [item=83320]\n- Celebratory Fireworks Caster [item=83318]\n- Distillate of Alacrity X [item=37919]\n- Distillate of Celestial Healing XIII [item=73177]\n- Distillate of Clarity XIII [item=73179]\n- Distillate of Divine Healing XIII [item=73176]\n- Distillate of Health XIII [item=73178]\n- Distillate of Replenishment XIII [item=73187]\n- Distillate of Spirituality XIII [item=73184]\n- Fireworks Focus of Bristlebane [item=83319]\n- Potion of Adventure II [item=83316]\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "4829",
      title = "Bonfires of Vanity - Solusek Ro's Favor",
