      loc = { y = 879.0, x = 3094.0, z = 0.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Avatar of Karana",
        "The key?",
        "What plan?",
        "I accept!",
        "Hail, Tober Grandim",
        "key",
        "plan",
        "accept",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "you the artifact that will conjure my power", count = 1 },
        { name = "you this as a token of my appreciation", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 15\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAnniversary events tend to run from mid-March to mid-April (sometimes to mid-May) each year. They are not available during the \"off season\".\nFor an overview and list of EverQuest Anniversary events, see this quest entry [quest=6782].\nThis is an anniversary quest available only during anniversary season (a few weeks during March and April). It was introduced in 2009 as part of EverQuest's 10th anniversary.\nThis is one of 16 deity quests. For an overview of how rewards work and how these quests are linked with one another, see this writeup [quest=4843].\nBelow here are the details for this particular quest.\nThis task begins with Avatar of Karana in South Karana (-3692.78, -1810.55 towards middle of zone - east of Splitpaw; northwest of hermit).\nYou say, 'Hail, Avatar of Karana'\nAvatar of Karana says 'Behold, mortal, I am Karana, Bringer of Storms. I find it appropriate to re-enter the mortal realm and gather new worshippers to my creed. To prosper among the other gods, I must extend my influence across the worlds, across the planes. You might hold the [key] to my success, and thus become the recipient of my favor.'\nYou say, 'The key?'\nAvatar of Karana says 'I have set much work before my followers. For my power to grow, I require greater and greater amounts of worship from the mortal flock. For that to happen, they must be inspired by displays of my power. Thus, it is not an easy thing for me to display my powers in places where I have no worshippers, in places where it never rains. I have a [plan] to overcome that dilemma.'\nYou say, 'What plan?'\nAvatar of Karana says 'I have given items and boons to my prominent followers among the mortals. If you will [accept] your fate as my loyal worshipper, I will tell you who you must follow.'\nYou say, 'I accept!'\nAvatar of Karana says 'Very well, I am pleased with your piety. I shall look to be equally pleased by your service to me. Seek out Tober Grandim, in Blightfire Moors. He will give you the artifact that will conjure my power.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Tears of a God - Karana's Favor'.\nKarana needs you to give the people of certain parts of Norrath and the Planes reason to fear him, and start worshipping him, by making it rain in these places.\nHail Tober Grandim in Blightfire Moors\nSpeak with Tober Grandim in Blightfire Moors (by the Old Tower in the NW corner of the zone, /loc +879, +3094, is KOS to certain people but you can hail from a distance or while invis).\nYou say, 'Hail, Tober Grandim'\nYour task 'Tears of a God - Karana's Favor' has been updated.\nTober Grandim says 'Ah, so Great Karana sends another willing acolyte! Perfect! I have a simple task for you, friend - as Karana has no doubt told you, he needs us to extend his power into places which never feel his power. That means it's up to us to make it rain in places that never receive a single raindrop, ever. The list of places this includes is quite a long one - but if you can make it rain in Everfrost Peaks, the Abysmal Sea, the Gulf of Gunthak, Corathus Creep, the Scarlet Desert, and the Plane of Knowledge, you will make our master very happy indeed.'\nReceive True Karanite Rod of Rainfall (used to make it rain).\nThe following steps must be done in order:\nMake it rain in Everfrost Peaks 0/1\nMake it rain in Abysmal Sea 0/1\nMake it rain in Gulf of Gunthak 0/1\nMake it rain in Corathus Creep 0/1\nMake it rain in Scarlet Desert 0/1\nMake it rain in Plane of Knowledge 0/1\nHail Tober Grandim 0/1\nYou say, 'Hail, Tober Grandim'\nYour task 'Tears of a God - Karana's Favor' has been updated.\nTober Grandim says 'Perfect, the rain has come to the driest of places! Karana be praised!'\nHail Avatar of Karana 0/1\nYou say, 'Hail, Avatar of Karana'\nYour task 'Tears of a God - Karana's Favor' has been updated.\nYou have successfully earned the favor of the Stormbringer God, Karana!\nAvatar of Karana says 'Your deeds have renewed my power in this world, already I can feel the mana from new worshippers adding into my spirit. I thank you, mortal, and give you this as a token of my appreciation.'\nReward:\nCelebratory Firework Caster (if this is your first diety task)\nFireworks Focus of Karana",
    },
