      walkthrough = "**Level:** 75\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAnniversary events tend to run from mid-March to mid-April (sometimes to mid-May) each year. They are not available during the \"off season\".\nFor an overview and list of EverQuest Anniversary events, see this quest entry [quest=6782].\nThis is an anniversary quest available only during anniversary season (a few weeks during March and April). It was introduced in 2009 as part of EverQuest's 10th anniversary.\nThis is one of 16 deity quests. For an overview of how rewards work and how these quests are linked with one another, see this writeup [quest=4843].\nBelow here are the details for this particular quest.\nThis task begins with the Primate of Prexus in Erud's Crossing (loc -1842, +712 - next to the dock when you zone in).\nYou say, 'Hail, Primate of Prexus'\nPrimate of Prexus says 'Hello Monkey! May the Ocean be calm and your catch nourishing. Is the ocean not [grand]?'\nYou say, 'Grand?'\nPrimate of Prexus says 'Yes. The way it caresses the skin and warms the blood. It is a [Blessing] to have the Ocean.'\nYou say, 'A blessing...'\nPrimate of Prexus says 'Prexus has spread his blessing over the Oceans. He gives travelers safe passage over its water, and makes sure the bounty of the ocean continues. He even blesses [Fishing] of the Oceans.'\nYou say, 'Fishing?'\nPrimate of Prexus says 'Yes. He blesses fishing. Fishing is just like hunting, part of the cycle of life. As long as you respect that the life of the oceans must continue, he does not begrudge any being the bounty of the oceans. Prexus has recently given an extra blessing to some of the fish of the Oceans. If you wish you can go fish some of these as an [offering] to Prexus.'\nYou say, 'I'll make an offering'\nPrimate of Prexus says 'May Prexus further bless your travels while you complete this offering.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Fishing for Blessings - Prexus' Favor'.\nFish for 1 Blessed Barren Flounder - Erud's Crossing\nFish for 1 Blessed Gunthak Mackerel - Ocean of Tears\nFish for 1 Blessed Timorous Tuna - Timorous Deep\nFish for 1 Blessed Iceclad Cutlassfish - Iceclad Ocean\nFish for 1 Blessed Kunark Mullet - The Field of Bone\nFish for 1 15 lb. Blessed Saltwater Tuna - Abysmal Sea\nFish for 1 Blessed Grunion - Barren Coast\nFish for 1 Blessed Ovate Jellyfish - Gulf of Gunthak\nDeliver 1 Blessed Barren Flounder to Primate of Prexus - Erud's Crossing\nDeliver 1 Blessed Gunthak Mackerel to Primate of Prexus - Erud's Crossing\nDeliver 1 Blessed Timorous Tuna to Primate of Prexus - Erud's Crossing\nDeliver 1 Blessed Iceclad Cutlassfish to Primate of Prexus - Erud's Crossing\nDeliver 1 Blessed Kunark Mullet to Primate of Prexus - Erud's Crossing\nDeliver 1 15 lb. Blessed Saltwater Tuna to Primate of Prexus - Erud's Crossing\nDeliver 1 Blessed Grunion to Primate of Prexus - Erud's Crossing\nDeliver 1 Blessed Ovate Jellyfish to Primate of Prexus - Erud's Crossing\nYour task 'Fishing for Blessings - Prexus' Favor' has been updated.\nYou caught a Blessed Barren Flounder!\nReward:\nCelebratory Firework Caster (if this is your first deity task)\nFireworks Focus of Prexus",
