      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 75\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAnniversary events tend to run from mid-March to mid-April (sometimes to mid-May) each year. They are not available during the \"off season\".\nFor an overview and list of EverQuest Anniversary events, see this quest entry [quest=6782].\nThis is an anniversary quest available only during anniversary season (a few weeks during March and April). It was introduced in 2009 as part of EverQuest's 10th anniversary.\nThis is one of 16 deity quests. For an overview of how rewards work and how these quests are linked with one another, see this writeup [quest=4843].\nBelow here are the details for this particular quest.\nAvatar of Tunare is found in the Greater Faydark, a little ways west of Felwithe's Plane of Knowledge book.\nYou say, 'Hail, Avatar of Tunare'\nAvatar of Tunare says 'Greetings, mortal. It has been far too long since I've set foot in Greater Faydark and beheld the cities of my beloved children. I still remember when many of them first set foot outside the city walls here, entranced and undoubtedly terrified by the [world] around them. Gradually, however, many of them have come to love this land as I do, and for this reason alone, I will continue to protect and nourish this land.'\nYou say, 'The world?'\nAvatar of Tunare says 'While the world has grown considerably, there are still areas that could use a helping hand. If you are [willing] to assist, I wish to offer you some seeds that I have empowered to help with the growth of this world. All I ask is you help me plant them, as they will handle the rest on their own.'\nYou say, 'I'm willing'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Gift of Life - Tunare's Favor'.\nAvatar of Tunare says 'Thank you. Lady Kimulei, one of my scouts, has already returned with suitable locations for planting those seeds. Please refer to her journal entries as a guide, and I wish you a safe journey.'\nPlant treants in ten different locations for Tunare!\nThe steps can be completed in any order by clicking on the \"Bag of Mysterious Seeds\" given to you.\n- 1. It sure is cold here, I wonder how the Sleeper is resting - Eastern Wastes\n(behind Sleeper's Tomb, /loc -7619, -60)\n- 2. The place to be if you're a Kolbok - Stonebrunt Mountains\n(near a kobold camp, /loc -3626, 1904) (or /loc -3243, 1239, 130)\n- 3. Brigands steal almost everything. Will they steal a treant? - Shadeweaver's Thicket\n(near a brigand camp, /loc -1060,-1100)\n- 4. Those Dragoons are scary. However, I think I found a safe corner to hide in.- The Overthere\n(SW corner, -3314.15, 3615.26, 255.27)\n- 5. Oh! There is a druid ring here. I wonder where to plant the treant.- Steamfont Mountains\n(in valley by druid ring, /loc -1076, 1481, -59)\n- 6. I sure wish I had a pretty robe to match my flowing black hair.- Lavastorm Mountains\n(near Najena)\n- 7. What crazy explorer would visit a lake with the name \"ill omen\" in it? - Lake of Ill Omen\n(near explorer tower, /loc 1900, -130)\n- 8. Even a lazy wizard who sits all the time can find time to visit here! - Nektulos Forest\n+455, -760, +37 Just north of the ruined wiz spires.\n- 9. Kithicor looks amazing during the day, especially when I stand by the lake. - Kithicor Forest\n(north side of lake, /loc 31, -310)\n- 10. I always thought druids were a bit unkempt. Some could even use a bath. - Mountains of Rathe\n(east side of druid rings/hill, /loc 5410, 760)\nAs you place the seeds:\nAs you drop a mysterious seed onto the ground, you watch in bewilderment as the seed instantly transforms into a full grown treant! You've always wondered where those treants came from.\nYour task 'The Gift of Life - Tunare's Favor' has been updated.\n- 11. Return to the Avatar of Tunare for a reward! - Greater Faydark\nYou say, 'Hail, Avatar of Tunare'\nYour task 'The Gift of Life - Tunare's Favor' has been updated.\nWith the task at hand complete, you begin to reflect on the growth that you yourself have gone through. At one point, you were like one of the seeds you planted, full of potential for the future. Now you are like the treant, fully grown and helping to grow and sustain this world.\nReward:\nCelebratory Fireworks Caster (only if this is the first deity task you have completed)\nFireworks Focus of Tunare\nPotion of Adventure II",
    },
