      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 10\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAnniversary events tend to run from mid-March to mid-April (sometimes to mid-May) each year. They are not available during the \"off season\".\nFor an overview and list of EverQuest Anniversary events, see this quest entry [quest=6782].\nThis is an anniversary quest available only during anniversary season (a few weeks during March and April). It was introduced in 2009 as part of EverQuest's 10th anniversary.\nThis is one of 16 deity quests. For an overview of how rewards work and how these quests are linked with one another, see this writeup [quest=4843].\nHelera Garet is located in North Qeynos near the PoK book at /waypoint 000 .\nYou say, 'Hail, Helera Garet'\nHelera Garet says 'Greetings _____. I am Helera Garet, a humble priestess of Rodcet Nife. Unlike some of the more fanatical members of my order over in the Temple of Life, who shun evil beings outright, I [view] things differently.'\nYou say, 'View?'\nHelera Garet says 'The way I look at it, Norrath is a dangerous world, and whether you're a high elf or an orc, you cannot deny the power of Rodcet Nife. For without his wonderful gift of healing, many expeditions would have no doubt been cut short. It is because this force is so vital that Rodcet Nife could not visit in person, and must continue his unending vigil to heal the [wounded].'\nYou say, 'Wounded?'\nHelera Garet says 'As I mentioned before, Norrath is a dangerous place, and as such, many creatures have become injured while fighting for survival. If you have a moment, I would like to ask a [favor] of you. It is a minor task, but it will show your appreciation for what Rodcet Nife and the wonderful healers of Norrath do on a daily basis.'\nYou say, 'Favor?'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Healing Touch - Rodcet Nife's Favor'.\nHelera Garet says 'Thank you for undertaking this task. I shall entrust you with this item, which has the power to heal injured creatures. Please help them and return to me when you're done.'\nUpon healing these NPCs, they turn into stronger versions of themselves, still non-aggressive. Use the Minor Trinket of Rodcet Nife given to you, to complete the following steps:\n- Heal an injured rat - Qeynos Hills\nFound it roaming the hills around the middle of the zone.\nTurns into a mighty rat.\n- Heal an injured skunk - Butcherblock Mountains\nFound in the eastern region near the Greater Faydark.\nTurns into a stinky skunk.\n- Heal an injured drixie - Lesser Faydark\nLooks like a fae drake. Found it at /waypoint -817, -872 .\nTurns into a carefree drixie.\n- Heal an injured drake - Crescent Reach\nIt is a red drake in the newbie area below the alligator pond.\nTurns into a majestic drake.\n- Heal an injured kodiak - Commonlands\nFound it roaming hills in the middle of the zone.\nTurns into a ferocious kodiak.\n- Heal an injured coyote - North Ro\nFound it around the inn closest to Freeport (Inn 1).\nTurns into a feral coyote.\n- Heal an injured rockhopper - Marus Seru\nFound it in the northwestern corner of the zone.\nTurns into a stout rockhopper.\n- Heal an injured snake - Nedaria's Landing\nFound it on a hill a bit away from the Magus.\nTurns into a slithering snake.\n- Heal an injured alligator - Innothule Swamp\nFound it just south of the PoK book around /waypoint -580, -240 .\nTurns into a wild alligator.\n- Heal an injured scorpion - Field of Bone\nFound it just outside the ruins leading to Kaesora, at /waypoint -2060, +362 .\nTurns into an envenomed scorpion.\nUpon completion:\nHelera Garet thanks you for your assistance, and as she hands you your reward, a sudden surge of vitality empowers you. No doubt Rodcet Nife smiles upon your actions today.\n- Celebratory Fireworks Caster (Only if this is the first deity task you have completed)\n- Fireworks Focus of Rodcet Nife\n- Potion of Adventure II\n- The choice between seven different distillates (Scaled to the PC level)\n- Player Flags (Being able to attune your fireworks to Rodcet Nife)\n- Platinum (Varies by level: 1,800 pp at level 82)\n- Experience\nSubmitted by: saroiny ; Revamped by iventheassassinRewards:\n- Celebratory Fireworks Caster [item=83318]\n- Fireworks Focus of Rodcet Nife [item=83345]\n- Potion of Adventure II [item=83316]\n[",
