      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 45\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is the seventh Warrior's Pike quest.\n(How does this quest start? We have two completely different reports.)\n1. Find Klok Scaleroot near the Tower of Death in West Cabilis. Hail her and listen to her story about mercenaries outside of Cabilis disrupting the trade. She will ask you to convince War Baron Eator to do something about it.\n2. At the end of the sixth Warrior's Pike quest, Vygan mentions going to the War Baron about the welfare of Cabilis.\nEither way, go ask the War Baron about the welfare in Cabilis.\nYou say, 'Hail, Klok Scaleroot'\nKlok Scaleroot says 'What's that? Oh, I'm sorry I've been preoccupied with the recent [attacks] as of late.'\nYou say, 'What attacks?'\nKlok Scaleroot says 'You don't know? I thought everyone was aware now. It seems as though, there have been [mercenaries] doing horrible things to the city.'\nYou say, 'What mercenaries?'\nKlok Scaleroot says 'They wear the bands of Xyzith's troop. Unfortunately, War Baron Eator doesn't believe that the situation has gotten this bad. If only someone was able to find a way to [help] show him how bad the issue is.'\nYou say, 'I will help.'\nKlok Scaleroot says 'Will you now? That is good. Bring me the bands and we will take it from there.'\nIf not where, at least we know what we are looking for.\nYou have to kill five Iksar Mercenaries in Field of Bone. They are wandering around near the Warsliks Woods zone line. They run very slowly and will stop chasing you quickly - most likely that was done so noobie Iksar aren't getting slaughtered by them.  Each Mercenary can drop one of three different lore bracers. Collect all three and bring them to Klok Scaleroot.\nKlok Scaleroot says 'What's this? I see you have the proof that I have been looking for. Take this note and speak to Drill Master Kyg. She is a stubborn one but true to keeping the Legion safe.'\nYou gain party experience!!\nYou receive 'Klok Scaleroot's Note'\nUpon turning in the note to Drill Master Kyg,\nDrill Master Kyg says, 'What's this you have? Hmmm...I knew there were issues brewing by not of this magnitude. The War Baron has seemed preoccupied with [other issues]. These issues may be one in the same.'\nYou say, 'What other issues?'\nDrill Master Kyg says, 'It seems as though a [Warlord] recently brought back news of Xyzith's fate. The War Baron could not understand how Xyzith could turn on his fellow brother so. The War Baron now seeks to find one that can solve this mystery.'\nYou say, 'Who was the Warlord?'\nDrill Master Kyg says, 'The Warlord's name? I believe it was...wait a minute! Why does this concern you? All you need know is that the Warlord is very brave and serves this Legion proudly unlike you! If you wish to prove yourself you'll speak to War Baron Eator regarding his findings and give him this to show your worth.'\nDrill Master Kyg gives you a note named Kyg's Approval for the War Baron. Deliver it and he will ask you to find out where Warlord Xyzith went, maybe that way you can find out why he changed in such a way. The War Baron also tells you that Xyzith went out to find a legendary metal that would bring new glory to Cabilis as it could be forged into a powerful weapon.\nFind War Baron Eator in East Cabilis. Turn in Kyg's Approval to him.\nWar Baron Eator says 'Ah, I see you have gained the approval of another. I suppose you are the one I should [share our findings] with then.'\nYou gain party experience!!\nYou say, 'Share our findings, this will help.'\nWar Baron Eator says 'It seems we have no clue as to why Xyzith turned against us. We need you to find where he traveled and get down to the bottom of this mystery. Go speak to Geot. He was the closest to Xyzith. He may remember where Xyzith searched for the legendary metal.'\nYou say, 'What did I miss? What legendary metal?'\nAnd then say to him, Kyg's Approval\nGo and find Warlord Geot in Lake of Ill Omen. He was Xyzith's best friend. Ask him \"Who was Xyzith?\" and also ask him \"Where did Xyzith search for the legendary metal?\" Unfortunately Geot has no idea where Xyzith went.\nYour next stop are the Mines of Nurga. That's where Xyzith hoped to find the metal but unfortunatley he didn't make it out alive. Kill A Rebellious Goblin, A Victorious Goblin, A Challenging Goblin and A Fearless Goblin. They spawn pretty close to the entrance of Nurga (Frontier Mountain side) and each possess one of Xyzith's belongings: his bracer, shield, badge and broken mancatcher.\nFor your Nurga map file:\nP 844.1221, 2065.6187, -223.9042, 240, 0, 0, 2, challenging_goblin\nP 483.8747, 1555.4758, -191.9354, 240, 0, 0, 2, rebellious_goblin\nP 968.6270, 1954.7889, -223.9042, 240, 0, 0, 2, fearless_goblin\nP 1174.5126, 1367.9830, -175.9354, 240, 0, 0, 2, victorious_goblin\nUpon handing the bracer to Warlord Geot:\nWarlord Geot says 'This was the bracer of [Xyzith]. . .I can only fear the worst now. Take this satchel with you. It was a gift from Xyzith when I first became a Warlord. Please find the rest of his remains and bring me the filled satchel again.'\nHe will return the item you showed him and also gives you a satchel called \"Geot's Pack\". Put the four items you collected in Nurga and combine them to produce Xyzith's Belongings.\nGive the Belongings to Warlord Geot:\nWarlord Geot says 'I see you have found all of his belongings. If only we could find a way to [communicate] with him again to find out what information he found during his journey.'\nYou say, 'How can we communicate with him again?'\nWarlord Geot says 'That is a good question deserving of an answer. Go seek out members of brood with necromantic origin and see if any of them know how to [speak to the dead].'\nHead to West Cabilis and talk to Master Rixiz in the Tower of Death, saying \"Can you speak to the dead?\":\nYou say, 'Hail, Master Rixiz'\nMaster Rixiz says 'You are on the grounds of the Brood of Kotiz. If you do not belong, you must leave at once. There shall be no [third rank skullcap] for you.'\nYou say, 'Can you speak to the dead?'\nMaster Rixiz says 'How dare you ask of such a thing! I am a Master of the Necromantic Arts. If you wish to have me conjure this spirit you must first seek out a traitor to our cause. His name is Ixzec. He can be found roaming with a group of renegades in a jungle not far from here. Return with his head and some items from the soul you want summoned and I will aid you in your request.'\nIxzec (called \"an Iksar traitor\") can be found in the Emerald Jungle. He hangs around at a Forsaken camp at the base of the cliff near the NW corner of the zone. Be careful, he has three friends hanging around there with him. Kill the traitor and loot his head. Bring it to Master Rixiz along with Xyzith's Belongings.\nMaster Rixiz says 'Ah, this brings me great joy. Now I shall have full control over this fool in his death. As for your request, here is what you asked for. . .'\nAs you hand Master Rixiz Xyzith's belongings, you can see black smoke begin to arise from the cracks in the floor. In a bright flash of light, the spirit of Xyzith appears in front of you and attacks!\nYou gain party experience!!\nWarlord Xyzith regards you indifferently -- he appears to be quite formidable.\nYou have slain Warlord Xyzith!\n--You have looted a Xyzith's Destroyed Belongings.--\nTurn in Xyzith's Destroyed Belongings to Master Rixiz:\nMaster Rixiz says 'You should return back to your brethren and give them the news of what has happened here young one. To make sure War Baron Eator recognizes the truth I shall give you my seal.'\nReceive a Seal of Rixiz, which you need to take to War Baron Eator:\nWar Baron Eator says 'What is this?! This cannot be true. What has happened to Xyzith to make him so against those he served so proudly? I must get to the bottom of this. I shall however reward you for courage against him. Take this and replace that which you have defeated!'\nYou receive \"Warlord Crown Plans\".\nAsk Weaponsmith Grugl \"How do I forge Warlord Mancatcher?\" and follow his instructions. Smithing combines were trivial at 86.\nWe need all dialogues, faction hits, quest items, quest mobs, additional zones, etc.\n- Warlord Mancatcher [item=29726]\n[",
