      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 52\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAfter getting Warlord Mancatcher (Warrior Pike #7):\n(Starting quest dialogues needed)\nHead to Temple of Droga and kill Stone Seer Kaigek (has a PH at -885, -514).\nKaigek drops a Broken Medal. When identified it reads: \"Bring us great honor on your mission -Geot\"\nHead to Warlord Geot in Lake of Ill Omen and give him the Medal.\nYou say, 'Hail, Warlord Geot'\nWarlord Geot says 'Where did you find this?! No matter. This was a present I gave Xyzith when he first left on his final mission. Hmm, it seems as though there is a stone hidden inside of it.'\nWarlord Geot says 'Warlord Xyzith may have fallen inside of those mines but that still does not explain his recent actions. Maybe the stone will shed light on this situation. I knew a shaman that practiced the art of alchemy. Maybe she can recall what kind of stone this is. Take this stone and search for her.'\nYou gain experience!!\nHe'll find a Black Stone in it and asks you to find someone who knows much about stones.\nHead to Timorous Deep and approach the Chessboard where you will find a female Iksar shaman called Izatri (approx. loc. is neg. 6000, 3000). Give her the Black Stone.\nYou say, 'Hail, Izatri'\nIzatri says 'Hello there yourself! If you don't mind I am quite busy here studying the rocks of this region.'\nIzatri says 'Where did you find this? Never mind that, it doesn't matter. I hope you didn't have it for long. This stone has the power to drain the soul of the owner. In its pure form it can remove curses from creatures, but the one you have has been used already. In its [dark form] it does far worse.'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou say, 'What is it's dark form?'\nIzatri says 'Well it slowly poisons the owner's mind eventually killing them. But it doesn't end at that, there's [more].'\nYou say, 'Tell me more'\nIzatri says 'Yes. . .I'm afraid it also traps the soul of the owner in the stone. I cannot perform the ritual any longer but I believe there is another that may be able to. I'm sorry I don't remember where to find him but you can ask around for him if you can't find him. His name is Liyx. Take your stone and find him. You will need it to summon the spirit to finally put him to rest properly.'\nShe returns the item (a different item of the same name) and asks you to find Hierophant Liyx.\nYou can find him in Field of Bone due west of the Plane of Knowledge book, approximate location -3000, 2700.\nYou say, 'Hail, Hierophant Liyx'\nHierophant Liyx says 'Hello. You have caught me before I started another mission. What can I do for you? Do you need my [aid]?'\nYou say, 'I need your aid'\nHierophant Liyx says 'If that is the case you must know what I specialize in. Bring me the stone, a mirrored gem, and two celestial essences. I will do the rest by helping you set your friend free.'\nBring him the Black Stone, two Celestial Essences and a Mirrored Gem. The Mirorred Gem drops off \"a reflective soul\" in Emerald Jungle (can be found in one of the northern ruins).\nUpon turning in those items:\nHierophant Liyx says 'He is here now. Send him off to the next plane.'\nYou gain experience!!\nHierophant Liyx summons Warlord Xyzith (skeleton version). He hits for a max ~150. Kill him, loot his spirit, and bring it to War Baron Eator.\nWarlord Xyzith regards you indifferently -- looks kind of dangerous.\nHierophant Liyx says, 'Now he is free. Take his essence which is now pure, and return to your Head Master. He will know what to do from here. As for me, I have other errands to tend to.' As Hierophant Liyx finishes his words, he steps into the shadows and departs again.\nYou have slain Warlord Xyzith!\nUpon turning in to War Baron Eator:\nWar Baron Eator says 'I see you have figured out the issue and ended it as well. The Legion. . .no. . .I owe you much thanks. It is regretful that Xyzith did not come back to us safely but we will all be in good hands with you here. Take these plans for the Pride of the Legion, and protect those as Warlord Xyzith did. Speak to Weaponsmith Gurgl to learn how to make your weapon of great power.'\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive Pride of Legion Plans.\nHead to Weaponsmith Grugl to find out how to make the weapon, asking \"How do I forge Pride of the Legion?\"\nYou say, 'Hail, Weaponsmith Grugl'\nWeaponsmith Grugl sets down a blood-spattered mace. 'Come to assist in the testing of the bashing equipment? Nah. Not you. You are too small. You must be here to practice your forging.'\nYou say, 'How do I forge the Pride of the Legion?'\nWeaponsmith Grugl says 'You must be special indeed to have gained the Baron's prize possession, the Pride of the Legion. To forge Pride of the Legion, a blacksmith of great skill would need a titanium rod, a forge hammer, and an unfinished mancatcher. The unfinished mancatcher is forged with a geozite tool, a blue diamond, Pride of the Legion Plans, and a Warlord's Mancatcher.'\nCombine the Plans, Warlord Mancatcher, Geozite Tool and Blue Diamond to receive an Unfinished Mancatcher.\nCombine the Unfinished Mancatcher with a Titanium Rod and Forging Hammer to receive the Pride of the Legion.\nCombines were trivial at smithing 85.\n- Pride of the Legion [item=29722]\n[",
