      walkthrough = "**Level:** 45\n**Maximum Level:** 130\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis task starts with Poison Masters in various cities and has a seven-day lockout timer. This is the first \"Small Favor\" task for rogues (the second being \"A Small Favor - Eldrith Tenk\").\nYou say, 'Hail, Poison Master Skuk'\nPoison Master Skuk looks you up and down as if assessing your worth. 'Hello there, _____. It's good that you have come to me today. I was just saying to myself, Self, I said, who is worthy of this [opportunity] that I could offer? And now, here you are!'\nYou say, 'What opportunity?'\nPoison Master Skuk nods. 'Yes, a most fantastic opportunity. I happen to have in my possession certain compounds. These compounds, when combined together, form [toxins] of various types. You might apply one of these toxics to a blade and if your hand happened to slip and the blade pierced the side of your enemy, why that enemy might begin to suffer in terrible agony. And that would be a terrible shame, wouldn't it?'\nYou say, 'What toxins?'\nPoison Master Skuk laughs. 'You're interested? Of course you are! But I'm a businessman first and foremost. You would need to perform a [service] for me first. Consider it a small token of your appreciation for the gift that I will bestow upon you.'\nYou say, 'What service?'\nPoison Master Skuk smiles grimly, the glint in his eye hinting at what a dangerous person you are dealing with. 'Here is your task, young one. Do not disappoint me. Never forget the tools of your craft - you must be invisible to detection or you will surely die. And you're no good to me dead!'\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Small Favor - Endoc Cron'.\nThe poison master has asked you to perform a simple task and promised ample rewards for your service. Travel to East Freeport and resolve a small misunderstanding between the poison master and one Endoc Cron.\nIt would be in your best interests to be hidden from view while undertaking this task as the Poison Master's informants report the Freeport Militia are on high alert.\nYou receive a Distraction Device.\nEnter East Freeport near Armor by Ikhtar via West Freeport near Grolagh's Forge and head north 0/1 (West Freeport)\nFollow the \"East Freeport\" signs after zoning into West Freeport from the Plane of Knowledge and heading through the main city gate.\nSneak along the path precisely to avoid detection 0/1 (East Freeport)\nSneak along the path precisely to avoid detection 0/1 (East Freeport)\nSneak along the path precisely to avoid detection 0/1 (East Freeport)\nSneak along the path precisely to avoid detection 0/1 (East Freeport)\nSneak along the path precisely to avoid detection 0/1 (East Freeport)\nPlant the bomb and hide 0/1 (East Freeport)\nUse the distraction device (click it inside the wagon at your last update spot).\nRun to Velith and Bardo while the guards are distracted and 'deal' with Endoc Cron 0/1 (East Freeport)\nDuring the sneak stages, mystical paths will form. Endoc is guarded by two Militia Enforcers who will run out to the noise of the bomb. This will allow you to kill Endoc.\nIf you're too late (the timer is less then 5 minutes for them to run back but no idea on the exact time), they are back guarding Endoc. The enforcers hit for 96,000, so you're not likely to succeed unless they're distracted.\n- 20 Consigned bite of the Shissar VII\n- 20 Consigned Plain Sealed Poison Vial\n- 20 Emulsifier\n- 20 Suspension Fluid\n- 20 Grade AA Mamba Venom\n[",
    },
