      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 7\n**Maximum Level:** 7\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is a long task given by Sentinel Phylos, a taskmaster in Erudin. It's known to be available at Level 7.\n(Dialogues?)\nYou have been assigned the task 'Trouble in the Highlands'.\nYou're going off to uncover what these lands have to offer. It won't necessarily be easy, and there will be those that want to stop you from uncovering anything at all, but you're going to be resolute in your actions. To start you need to explore the second cell holding a prisoner in the southeast. Once you've done that, a courier will be sent with more information about the next step.\nExplore the second cell holding a prisoner in the southeast 0/1 (The Warrens)\nHead to the Warrens via Paineel. From the zone-in, take a right and follow that corridor down until you see a door on your left. Enter the door and take the corridor to the right. Follow the stairs down. The prison door is on your left a few steps down.\nInvis helps here, as mobs run fast at low health and create nice trains.\nThis step updates at about 330, -1075, -94.\nOh no! You've been waylaid by monsters! Get rid of them so you can get back on track! Quickly kill 10 rabid kobolds, and be sure you loot 4 Bronze Yari, so there's no evidence of their deaths, just in case others come looking for them.\nKill 10 rabid kobolds 0/10 (The Warrens)\nLoot 4 Bronze Yari 0/4 (The Warrens)\nThe prison cell has no roamers. It may be best to pull to there, but beware that assist aggro here is large.\n(Anything else to this task?)\n2 platinum, 1 gold, 6 silver, 6 copper.\nExperienceRewards:\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "5095",
      title = "Bugs in the Dirt",
      exp = "03",
      exp_name = "The Shadows of Luclin",
      min_lvl = 11,
      max_lvl = 11,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = -455.0, x = -210.0, z = -190.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Khala Dun Erelk",
        "What task do you have for me?",
        "Hail, Talsanna Deephaven",
        "task",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 11\n**Maximum Level:** 11\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is a medium sized task available from Khala Dun Erelk in Shar Vahl at location -455, -210, -190. It is known to be available at Level 11.\nYou say, 'Hail, Khala Dun Erelk'\nKhala Dun Erelk says 'We are not the [task] masters, but simply the task providers. Those who have the desire to help Shar Vahl are placed into situations that best suit them. We prefer to think of it as a job for the soul and a journey through life.'\nYou say, 'What task do you have for me?'\nOne of the task choices given is \"Bugs in the Dirt\", a medium duration task with no timer.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Bugs in the Dirt'.\nEnemies are always closer then you think, aren't they? That's exactly what you're going to learn on your journey today. They're much closer then you think so there's no time to waste. Just speak with Talsanna Deephaven, for information on exactly what you need to do get to the bottom of this dilemma.\nSpeak with Talsanna Deephaven 0/1 (Shadeweaver's Thicket)\nUpon entering Shadeweaver's Thicket, the direction to this NPC will be marked on your compass. (She is at -1705, -3005, -200.)\nYou say, 'Hail, Talsanna Deephaven'\nTalsanna Deephaven says 'Thanks for contacting me, ________. Your information on this matter has been most useful.'\nBy now you're beginning to understand the complexities of the situation aren't you? You're learning how problematic it can be to have to fight off your cohorts when they go bad. Sadly, you're going to have to take the road less travelled and kill 10 muck diggers,. Sometimes it's not the easiest way, but it's got to be done.\nKill 10 muck diggers 0/10 (Paludal Caverns)\n(Glowing muck diggers count as well.)\nThen there are times when those you slaughter weren't friends at all. It's a shame you had to be deceived like that, but those mongrels were causing too many problems. Now you are ready to face the threat of someone even closer than before. You need to kill 10 mud burrowers,. Wipe them out. In addition, they're holding very sensitive items that need to be recovered. While you're out cleaning up the mess, make sure you loot 4 Mud Burrower Carapace,.\nKill 10 mud burrowers 0/10 (Paludal Caverns)\nLoot 4 Mud Burrower Carapace 0/4 (Paludal Caverns)\nOnce again you have proven that you can take the hard assignments and come out without a scratch. It's quite an accomplishment and it means you're almost done. Just deliver 4 Mud Burrower Carapace to Tesmina Boerak to finish everything off.\nDeliver 4 Mud Burrower Carapace to Tessmina Boerak 0/4 (Shadeweaver's Thicket)\nUpon entering Shadeweaver's Thicket, the direction to this NPC will be marked on your compass. (She is at -2820, -2730, -205.)\nYou really didn't know those who you were forced to slay, did you? No matter, they needed to go anyway, and you just happened to be the object of their demise. You did a clean, thorough job and you should be proud of the work you did. Here's a bit of a reward for the nightmares you're bound to have from this. Try to sleep soundly.\n1 platinum, 3 gold, 6 copper\nExperience (11% at Level 13)Rewards:\n[",
