      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis task begins with Skal Nethus [npc=35460] in the Plane of Knowledge. He's an Erudite found at location -320, 1200, -111 (close to Franklin Teek [npc=30481]).\nYou say, 'Hail, Skal Nethus'\nSkal Nethus says 'Come closer! You smell...odd. Yes, have you been crawling around in dungeons? I smell the bacterial spores on your armor. You should be careful: [dungeon rot] will make you unpleasant in ways worse than odor. '\nYou say, 'Dungeon rot?'\nSkal Nethus says 'Adventurers pass through here all the time, wreaking of the stuff. It seems to be spreading through dungeons everywhere. Just last week I was accosted by a putrid, infected halfling. He accused me of wanting to steal his powers. His skin was boiling red, and a cloud of spores billowed about his body. He lifted me above his head and tossed me into a fountain. His [anger] was five times his body size, and I was afraid for my life.'\nYou say, 'Anger?'\nSkal Nethus says 'Creatures infected with Dungeon Rot have augmented [strength] and rage. How else would a halfling overpower someone as large and fit as I? I am not positive, but I think the Rot spreads more easily to creatures with anger running through their veins. That is why I resisted the halfling's infection: I am a naturally calm, composed individual.'\nYou say, 'Strength?'\nSkal Nethus says 'Ah, you know me too well. Yes, my interest in the Rot is not wholly selfless. I would like to find a way to cure adventurers of this blight, but I am sure it would be possible to manipulate the compounds of the disease in order to safely [augment] one's strength. Doubtless, it would be safer than my previous experiments with those [Voidsouls].'\nYou say, 'How can you safely augment it?'\nSkal Nethus says 'Bring me samples of Dungeon Rot from dungeons and caves around Norrath. If I can synthesize the various strains of the disease, a power increase is almost certain...and we can cure any adventurers that are unlucky enough to become infected. Will you [collect] some samples?'\nYou say, 'I'll collect some'\nSkal Nethus says 'Thank you! Look for the stronger creatures in these dungeons. I am sure they are more susceptible to the disease because of their propensity for aggression. But be careful that the Rot does not spread from them to other nearby angry creatures.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'The Dungeon Rot Infected'.\nSearch for creatures infected by Dungeon Rot in Upper Guk, Solusek's Eye, the Crystal caverns, Kaesora, Lower Guk, the Howling Stones, the Crypt of Nadox, Ssraeshza Temple, the Bastion of Thunder, the Fortress of Zek, the Vergalid Mines, Zhisza, Toskirakk, and Kaesora Library.\n1. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Upper Guk to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n2. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Solusek to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n3. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Crystal to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n4. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Kaesora to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n5. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Lower Guk to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n6. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Stones to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n7. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Nadox to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n8. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Ssraeshza to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n9. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Thunder to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n10. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Zek to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n11. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Vergalid to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n12. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Zhisza to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n13. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Toskirakk to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n14. Deliver 1 Dungeon Rot Spores of Kaesora Library to Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\n15. Speak with Skal Nethus 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nYou say, 'Hail, Skal Nethus'\nSkal Nethus says 'My, this Dungeon Rot is potent! I am surprised you have not come to me with your face like magma and your arms waving in a frenzy. With my extensive knowledge and capabilities, I will extract the strength-giving compounds from the spores...ah, here we go. This substance I have synthesized will grant you power without ill effects. Here, take some of it as compensation for your efforts. Now I must consider whether I can concoct a cure for the blight...'\nThe above 13 items come from the 13 hot zones added with the December, 8, 2010, patch.\nThese drops may come from specific mobs or mob types. While fighting them, they'll transform into a Dungeon Rot infected mob and drop the item.\nThis is a list of confirmed mobs. Please let us know if you have any to add here.\n1. Upper Guk - yun ghoul wizard; a froglok ton knight; a froglok ton warrior.\n2. Solusek's Eye - gnome miners (note: they give negative Ak`Anon faction); east side of the zone.\n3. Crystal Caverns - a stalag terror (bottom of zone, left tunnel); a crystal crawler (near stalags).\n4. Kaesora - a skeletal guardian\n5. Lower Guk - an urd ghoul wizard; a kor ghoul wizard\n6. Howling Stones - mortiferous golem (straight east of zone-in; stairs leading up to the door are fake, can levitate over from another platform).\n7. Nadox - ?\n8. Ssraeshza Temple - an Imperial Golem - south/eastern 3rd floor section. Bone Spiked Golem and An Enchanted Golem.\n9. Bastion of Thunder - a Vann Stav (from the stormrider area, use the southwest port-up to the towers).\n10. Tactics - Hendin Shadow Master (found in the halls that lead up to Rallos Zek? above the pit, north).\n11. Vergalid - a spawn of Vergalid and a Vergalid Elite both turn into Dungeon Rot mobs; these are past the keyed area just before you get to Vergalid at the bottom of the pit.\n12. Zhisza - a Shissar deathmaker inside the pyramid in the north. Possibly other Shissar types inside the pyramid.\n13. Toskirakk - Rallosian ogres (certain types?)\n14. Kaesora Library - a corrupt defiler; a corrupt warlock\n786 platinum, 5 gold\nExperience (how much?)\nPurified Dungeon Rot [item=96135]\nMAGIC ITEM LORE ITEM NO TRADE AUGMENTATION\nAugmentation type: 7 8\nSlot: HEAD FACE EAR NECK SHOULDERS ARMS BACK WRIST HANDS FINGER CHEST LEGS FEET WAIST\nSTR: 0+1 HP: +110 MANA: +25 ENDUR: +25\nSV DISEASE: +10 SV MAGIC: +10\nRequired level of 80.\nWT: 0.0 Size: TINY\nClass: ALL\nRace: ALLRewards:\n- Purified Dungeon Rot [item=96135]\n[",
    },
