      walkthrough = "**Level:** 80\n**Maximum Level:** 90\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nNOTE: THIS TASK IS NO LONGER AVAILABLE IN GAME.\nFor an overview of Veil of Alaris pre-launch events, see this quest entry [quest=5343].\nThis is a pre-launch task leading up to the Veil of Alaris expansion, expected to be available only for a certain period of time ahead of VOA's launch.\nIt begins with a gnome named Chief Wood Engineer Gilanspring in the Steamfont Mountains. He's found in the far southeastern part of the Steamfont Mountains.\nYou say, 'Hail, Chief Wood Engineer Gilanspring'\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'Hrmf.  I'm a busy gnome.  We've got a massive [project] under way here, and I really don't have time to spare.'\nYou say, 'What project?'\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'You don't know about it? Well I don't have time to go into details.  You should talk to Olim, he likes to chat.  Then again, if you have that much spare time, maybe you could use it productively by [helping] out around here.'\nYou say, 'Helping, how?'\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'We can always use hands doing the non-skilled stuff.  I think you'll be useful doing some of those [tasks].'\nYou say, 'Tasks?'\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'Nothing too difficult for you, I hope.'\nA task window pops up with two tasks to choose from.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Gondola Hull - Hull Planking'.\nTo move the project along, the engineers need to build scaffolding to allow the workers to reach it. And this time they need good planks to build with. Fontpines aren't strong enough to make scaffolding. Go talk to someone from the Wayfarers Brotherhood and see if they can spare some good planking.\nSpeak with a Wayfarers Brotherhood supplier 0/1 (Nedaria's Landing)\nAn NPC called \"a Wayfarers Brotherhood supplier\" spawns around the south part of the dock area of Nedaria's Landing (approximate area of 250, 1450).\nYou say, 'Hail, a Wayfarers Brotherhood supplier'\na Wayfarers Brotherhood supplier says 'Hello there. You say that you are looking for some sturdy, wide planks? We can provide those. I'd like to help out, but I can't just give away Brotherhood resources. If you can provide me with just a few items we need for extended shipboard excursions, I can certainly provide you a few planks.'\nKill some sunflowers and gather the odd fruit called Scarlet Lemon 0/5 (Scarlet Desert)\nMobs called \"a sunflower\" are found mostly in the dried riverbed area. This step will update as you kill them (no actual items involved).\nDeliver 5 Tomato to a Wayfarers Brotherhood supplier 0/5 (Nedaria's Landing)\nA Tomato can be purchased from Klen Ironstove in the Plane of Knowledge (CTRL+F, findable; location -70, 240).\nDeliver 3 Flask of Orange Juice to a Wayfarers Brotherhood supplier 0/3 (Nedaria's Landing)\nFlask of Orange Juice is produced with brewing (Trivial 35): 1x Water Flask + 2x Emerald Orange (makes 5x \"Flask of Orange Juice\").\nNOTE: Emerald Oranges are foraged in the Emerald Jungle.\nUpon doing the hand-ins, you receive 2x \"Wide Jaggedpine Plank\".\nCreate 2 Jaggedpine Hull Planks 0/2 (ALL)\nTurn the planks into 2x \"Jaggedpine Hull Plank\" (one at a time) with the Recursive Clockwork Wood Reducer you received at the beginning of the task.\nDeliver the Jaggedpine Hull Planks to any wood engineer 0/2 (Steamfont Mountains)\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'Thank you for your help.'\nReturn the Recursive Clockwork Wood Reducer to any wood engineer 0/1 (Steamfont Mountains)\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'Ah, good. This will be useful later, I'm sure.'\nReward:\n1 Work VoucherRewards:\n- Work Voucher [item=97840]\n[",
