      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 75\n**Maximum Level:** 90\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nNOTE: THIS TASK IS NO LONGER AVAILABLE IN GAME.\nFor an overview of Veil of Alaris pre-launch events, see this quest entry [quest=5343].\nThis is a pre-launch task leading up to the Veil of Alaris expansion, expected to be available only for a certain period of time ahead of VOA's launch.\nIt begins with a gnome named Chief Wood Engineer Gilanspring in the Steamfont Mountains. He's found in the far southeastern part of the Steamfont Mountains.\nYou say, 'Hail, Chief Wood Engineer Gilanspring'\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'Hrmf.  I'm a busy gnome.  We've got a massive [project] under way here, and I really don't have time to spare.'\nYou say, 'What project?'\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'You don't know about it? Well I don't have time to go into details.  You should talk to Olim, he likes to chat.  Then again, if you have that much spare time, maybe you could use it productively by [helping] out around here.'\nYou say, 'Helping, how?'\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'We can always use hands doing the non-skilled stuff.  I think you'll be useful doing some of those [tasks].'\nYou say, 'What tasks?'\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring says 'Nothing too difficult for you, I hope.'\nA task window pops up with a single task to choose.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Guidance Systems - Wheel'.\nThe ship needs a steering device. The engineers understand that this usually takes the form of a wheel. The engineers would like you to gather some examples of the type so they can decide what sort they wish to use. There are several types they would like to see, and they have asked you to bring them two of them. The pirates of Dulak Harbor must have some interesting types of ship's wheels. The drowned pirates of the Buried Sea certainly had ship's wheels. Perhaps you can find one. The engineers have heard that the trolls in the Crypt of Nadox have ancient ship's wheels that might prove exciting. The engineers are also interested in ideas that might be out of the box... or wheel. Perhaps a catapult wheel would work? Find one in Sunderock Springs. Certainly a cart wheel looks like a ship's wheel. See if you can find someone to give one to you. It doesn't have to be new, we just want an example. Try one of the merchant gnomes in Dragonscale Hills.\nFind an example of the ship's wheels used in Dulak 0/1 (Dulak's Harbor)\nPirate mobs are found throughout the Dulak's Harbor zone.\nFind an example of the ship's wheels used by drowned pirates 0/1 (The Buried Sea)\nDrowned pirates are found most commonly in the waters off the coast of Deadbone Reef (the northeastern-most island in the Buried Sea).\nFind an example of the ship's wheels used by the pirates of Broken Skull 0/1 (Crypt of Nadox)\nBroken Skull mobs are found throughout the Crypt of Nadox. Any particular mob update here, or any Broken Skull troll?\nFind a catapult wheel to use as an example 0/1 (Sunderock Springs)\nAttack the catapults in Sunderock until this updates.\nFind a cart wheel to use as an example 0/1 (Dragonscale Hills)\nFind Tizzle is the Dragonscale Hills. He's found in the Gnome vendor along the northern boundary of the zone (west of the entrance from Steamfont).\nDeliver 3 Othmir Algae Ales to Tizzle 0/3 (Dragonscale Hills)\nThese are made with Brewing (Trivial: 31): See this recipe link for details.\nNote: All components can be bought from Blumblum Swigwater, the Othmir vendor in Cobalt Scar at around location 200, -1400 (northeast part of the beach).\nSpeak with Tizzle 0/1 (Dragonscale Hills)\nShow the Chief Wood Engineer what you have discovered 0/1 (Steamfont Mountains)\nChief Wood Engineer Gilanspring thanked you for the wheel samples you brought him.\nReward:\n1 Work VoucherRewards:\n- Work Voucher [item=97840]\n[",
