      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 85\n**Maximum Level:** 90\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nNOTE: THIS TASK IS NO LONGER AVAILABLE IN GAME.\nFor an overview of Veil of Alaris pre-launch events, see this quest entry [quest=5343].\nThis is a pre-launch task leading up to the Veil of Alaris expansion, expected to be available only for a certain period of time ahead of VOA's launch.\nIt begins with a gnome named Chief Engineer Dougal in the Steamfont Mountains. He's found in the far southeastern part of the Steamfont Mountains (location -1275, -1060, 0 -- overlooking the pit).\nYou say, 'Hail, Chief Engineer Dougal'\nChief Engineer Dougal says 'Hello.  Pretty busy here, you know.  Big [project] and all that.  What can I do for you?'\nYou say, 'What's this project?'\nChief Engineer Dougal says 'I'm sure you've heard.  We're building an immense rigid airship.  It will be a masterpiece when we're done.  It will be a dream come true for most of us.  Despite the [danger] that prompted this project, we're all very excited about it.  This is the sort of amazing project that comes along once in a lifetime, if that.  All of Ak'Anon is working to make this project happen.  Are you [interested] in helping?'\nYou say, 'I'm interested'\nChief Engineer Dougal says 'That's nice to hear.  I might have a [task] for you, but you should check with my chief engineers, they certainly could use some help.'\nYou say, 'What task?'\nChief Engineer Dougal says 'Hrmm...'\nA task window pops up with two tasks to choose from.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Ballast and Ornamentation - Copper Railing'.\nOne of the final touches of the ship will be the railings. Chief Dougal wants the railing to be a functional and attractive item. To that end, he has asked you to seek out a skilled smith who can work with an artist to come up with a great mold for the railing. Gan is insisting that you bring him one Darksteel weapon as his payment for doing the work. This isn't surprising from a mercenary.\nSpeak with Gan Ironsworthy 0/1 (Butcherblock Mountains)\nGan is found in the Wayfarer's camp just outside Greater Faydark.\nFind a dark steel weapon and deliver it to Gan 0/1 (Butcherblock Mountains)\nDark steel weapons drop from \"a dark assassin\" in the Umbral Plains.\nLoot some Twilight Ore from earth elementals in the Twilight Sea 0/1 (Twilight Sea)\nThis should be a random kill update.\nTell Gan that you have his Twilight Ore 0/1 (Butcherblock Mountains)\nSpeak with Mercia 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nSpeak with Chief Engineer Dougal 0/1 (Steamfont Mountains)\nGive the ruler to Mercia 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nGive the Exceptional Clay Casting Material to Mercia 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nCollect 1 Refined Underfoot Copper (ALL)\nThis is forged (300 smithing trivial; a NO TRADE item). See this recipe page for information about putting it together.\nCreate 1 Shiny Brass Railing Segment using tradeskills 0/1 (ALL)\n(What does this combine involve?)\nDeliver 1 Shiny Brass Railing Segment to Chief Engineer Dougal 0/1 (Steamfont Mountains)\n(Missing and closing dialogues needed.)\nReward:\n1 Work VoucherRewards:\n- Work Voucher [item=97840]\n[",
