      id = "5692",
      title = "Anniversary Solo Task: Spider's Bite",
      exp = "01",
      exp_name = "The Ruins of Kunark",
      min_lvl = 90,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = 1490.0, x = -5150.0, z = 0.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Sam Napth",
        "Hail, a mercenary",
        "Hail, Webmaster Katil",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 103703, name = "Severed Spider Legs", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 90\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Time Limit:** 06:00:00\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nAnniversary events tend to run from mid-March to mid-April (sometimes to mid-May) each year. They are not available during the \"off season\".\nFor an overview and list of EverQuest Anniversary events, see this quest entry [quest=6782].\nThis is a solo task introduced with EverQuest's 13th anniversary. It's expected to only be available during anniversary season (mid-March through mid-April).\nIt begins with Sam Napth, a Halfling in the Plane of Knowledge at about -215, -90, -155 (next to the Soulbinder).\nYou say, 'Hail, Sam Napth'\nSam Napth says 'I've been expecting you.  I have great need of adventurers to help me deal with an important issue.  There are a lot of tasks that need doing, I'd be grateful if you could help me out.  You see, I've been trying to prove to some important people that such things are foolishness.  So I've arranged some tests to prove it.'\nA task window pops up offering several anniversary tasks.\nYou have been assigned the task 'Spider's Bite'.\nSam Napth has asked you to kill spiders to prove that killing spiders is bad luck. You've killed plenty of spiders before, and while you've had your ups and downs, you haven't noticed any correlation. The oddest part is that he wants you to go to the Dreadlands and kill a specific set of spiders. The mercenary he sent previously has not returned or reported back in any fashion.\nJourney to the Dreadlands and find the dark elf mercenary 0/1 (Dreadlands)\nThe dark elf mercenary is located at 1490, -5150 by Webmaster Katil -- this is in the northeastern part of the zone. This step updates as you approach the location.\nYou say, 'Hail, a mercenary'\na mercenary is dead, and does not respond.\nDestroy the discovered spiders 0/3 (Dreadlands)\nThree mobs called \"a spider\" spawn and attack. They hit for a max ~3,600. They are stunnable.\nSpeak to Webmaster Katil 0/1 (Dreadlands)\nYou say, 'Hail, Webmaster Katil'\nWebmaster Katil says 'So, another one has shown up? Sent by Napth, are you? I will tell you nothing. I killed the one who came before you. I told her nothing. I do not know what you or Napth want, and I am beyond caring. I'll just kill you instead.'\nDefeat Webmaster Katil 0/1 (Dreadlands)\nKatil hits for a max ~10,000. At (random?) health spots, he may respawn at 100%. Just keep at it until he dies.\nWebmaster Katil casts a spell before being struck down. The corpse left behind is an illusory decoy. Katil still lives.\nYou have slain Webmaster Katil!\nTake water from the giants and drink it 0/1 (Dreadlands)\nTask Window Says: You feel parched and a little sick. You need a drink. The large structure of the giants should hold what you seek. It can be found in the frozen wastes nearby.\nThe water from the giants is located at -470, 1940 (inside the giant fortress in the snowy area southwest of Karnor's Castle).\nFind a cure for the poison and use it 0/1 (Dreadlands)\nTask Window Says: You are poisoned, and feel gravely ill. The large structure of the giants should hold what you seek. It can be found in the frozen wastes nearby.\nIn the northwest building inside the giant fort, find a ground spawn and drink it.\nConfront Webmaster Katil 0/1 (Dreadlands)\nTask Window Says: Webmaster Katil, a drachnid, stands in your way again.\nKatil spawns outside the giant fortress. Hail him.\nYou say, 'Hail, Webmaster Katil'\nWebmaster Katil says 'So you managed to cure your poisoning. No matter. You won't manage this time. Napth will have to come himself eventually, and I will finish him then, too.'\nKill the spider 0/1 (Dreadlands)\n\"a spider\" spawns a short distance away. Kill it.\nKill another spider 0/1 (Dreadlands)\nKill the next one. Note that these keep spawning, so you'll want to back away from the location.\nEscape and return to Sam in the Plane of Knowledge 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nTask Window Says: The spiders cannot be stopped. Flee, and return to Sam Napth in the Plane of Knowledge.\nYou say, 'Hail, Sam Napth'\nThe events certainly played out in a very unfortunate manner, as you've reported to Sam. However, you tend to think that there is something beyond simple bad luck at work in regards to what occurred.\nExperience (about 1 AA at Level 95) + one of:\n---- Option #1: 135 platinum\n---- Option #2: Severed Spider LegsRewards:\n- Severed Spider Legs [item=103703]\n[",
    },
