      items_required = {
        { name = "Renth the Box of Remains", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 2603, name = "Purse", type = "item" },
        { id = 595, name = "Rusty Dagger", type = "item" },
        { id = 10157, name = "Wrist Pouch", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
        { name = "Wolves of the North", change = 20 },
        { name = "Shamen of Justice", change = 4 },
        { name = "Merchants of Halas", change = 5 },
        { name = "Steel Warriors", change = 1 },
      },
      walkthrough = "**Time:** 4 hours\n**Level:** 10\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\n- Renth McLanis may be found in McDaniels Smokes & Spirits at +370, -280, or via the Find function (he is a Warrior Guildmaster).\nYou say, 'Hail, Renth McLanis'\nRenth McLanis says 'Hail, ______! Have ye come to train? I train all warriors. All Wolves o' the North must be strong warriors and swift as well. Are ye a young wolf, then? If so, maybe ye can [assist Renth] with his wee problem, eh?'\nYou say, 'I will assist you.'\nRenth McLanis says 'I was ordered by Kylan O'Danos to personally escort a young warrior sent to fetch the remains of his cousin, Ivan McMannus. I forgot and spent me greater time testing out the fine spirits. Now I must find the courier and the remains. Will ye [search for the courier]?'\nYou say, 'I will search for the courier.'\nRenth McLanis says 'Thank ye, _____! Go to Everfrost Peaks and seek out Arnis McLish. Ask him where Megan, the courier, is. Once ye find Megan, would you ask her where Ivan's remains are? Please go, at once!'\n- Arnis McLish may be found in Everfrost Peaks near the entrance ramp to Black Burrow at -1595, -175.  He will run eastward to the tree at -1090, -960, attacking monsters along the way.\nYou say, 'Hail, Arnis McLish'\nArnis McLish says 'My word!! I cannot believe how cold it is out here. I must keep running around just to keep warm.'\nYou say, 'Where is Megan?'\nArnis McLish says 'I heard she got lost on the plains. You should ask her dog, Snowflake, where she is. I hear he is somewhere around the pass to Halas.'\n- Snowflake may be found at +2020, -1160, near Bryndin McMill and Lish McMarrin.\nYou say, 'Hail, Snowflake'\nSnowflake says 'Grrrrrr!!'\nYou say, 'Where is Megan?'\nSnowflake says 'Ruff.. Ruff.. Woof..'\n- Snowflake will slowly walk away to the east, stopping at the pillars of the tower at (+2045, +3835).  Regardless of whether Megan is there or not, he will slowly walk back to the tree by Bryndin McMill.  You can make him return to Megan's tower during the return trip by asking asking him again \"Where is Megan?\"\nMegan OReilly stands outside the tower to the right of the pillars at (+2060, -3870) and will frequently walk to the bank of the frozen river at (+2025, -4240). Wandering orcs will sometimes attack her so you might have to wait for her.\nYou say, 'Hail, Megan OReilly'\nMegan OReilly says 'Brrrr.. It.. Is sooo.. c-cold!! I never.. sh-should've j-joined.. the.. the W-wolves of the N-north!!'\nYou say, 'Where are Ivan's remains?'\nMegan OReilly says 'You were sent to retrieve the remains?  I am sorry, I lost them.  It was not my fault!  There was no escort as I was told.  I got lost returning to Halas and ended up on a frozen river.  The ice broke and the remains were scattered into the freezing water.  Will you [dive for the remains]?'\nYou say, 'I will dive for the remains.'\nMegan OReilly says 'Thank the Tribunal!!  I would have, but I cannot swim.  Take this chest.  Fill it with the four pieces which fell below the surface.  I know not what else lies within.  When you fill the box and combine the items, return it to Renth.  Good luck, ______.'\n- You receive a 4-slot Empty Box, which identifies as \"Box For Ivan's Remains.\"\nSoutheast of Megan's tower, there is a hole in the frozen river at +1375, -4585; grab an Enduring Breath from someone and go diving.  Under the ice are various goblins (\"goblin diver\" and \"ice goblin diver\") who are KoS.  Three of the pieces of the remains are ground spawns found on the river bottom and look like bags.\nBarbarian Femur:  1405, -4570, -190\nBarbarian Jaw:  1465, -4500, -230\nBarbarian Skull:  (just north of the jawbone) 1577,-4489,-242\nThe final item, Barbarian Rib, is dropped by a \"goblin diver\" found between the spawn spots for the jaw and the skull.  Kill it for the final item, a Barbarian Rib.\n- Combine the four items in the box to craft a Box of Remains (identifies as \"Box of Ivan's Remains\").  Head back to Halas and give Renth the Box of Remains.\nRenth LcLanis says 'Good work!! Kylan will never know o' me negligence. I owe ye one, young warrior. Let's call it even with this. Twas found by one of our foraging parties. It is still useful. And... I believe ye can assist with a more [dangerous matter] as well.'\nYour faction standing with Wolves of the North has been adjusted by 20.\nYour faction standing with Shamen of Justice has been adjusted by 4.\nYour faction standing with Merchants of Halas has been adjusted by 5.\nYour faction standing with Steel Warriors has been adjusted by 1.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive 1 copper from Renth McLanis.\n- You receive a random minor item.  The more \"dangerous matter\" is the quest for the Langseax.\nNeed additional rewards, if any.Submitted by: Sleet, Kyll & VulfgangeRewards:\n- Purse [item=2603]\n- Rusty Dagger [item=595]\n- Wrist Pouch [item=10157]\n[",
