      walkthrough = "**Level:** 100\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis task begins with Lady Carolline of Thex in Northern Felwithe. She is located at 0, -170 (on the balcony overlooking the entrance: you can use the Find Feature, CTRL+F, to get to her).\nInitiating the Task\nYou say, 'Hail, Lady Carolline of Thex'\nLady Carolline of Thex smiles, trying to hide an obvious air of sadness, 'Greetings adventurer, such a lovely day isn't it?' The pained look on her face clearly gives away that something is [wrong].\nYou say, 'What's wrong?'\nLady Carolline of Thex says 'Wrong? Oh, nothing really. My beloved is off again on some [excursion] and has yet to return. I'm quite sure he will be fine though. How I miss our adventures together, the time we would spend exploring the hidden beauty of Norrath. We were especially fond of [Antonica].'\nYou say, 'Why were you fond of Antonica?'\nLady Carolline of Thex says 'A lovely land, despite the efforts of humans to ruin it...' The Koada`Dal's smile becomes more sincere. 'Lake Rathetear, oh the [stories] I could share of moonlit nights sitting on the docks. The noble aviaks keeping ardent guard over the sacred flame, the sunken towers and legend of the Megalodon...' She sighs and looks up to the sky.'\nYou say, 'What stories could you share?'\nLady Carolline of Thex blinks and looks back to you, her demeanor changing. 'Tell you what stranger, you come up with an [interesting tale] to distract me from my boredom, and I'll see if I can find something to [reward] you for your effort.'\nYou say, 'What reward would that be?'\nLady Carolline of Thex says 'Hmm, already pondering your riches before the effort of imagination? I suppose not many adventurers care to put any effort into their journeys these days.' The young high elf sighs. 'Anyway, what you will be rewarded with is something befitting a _____ such as yourself.'\nYou say, 'I have an interesting tale to tell'\nLady Carolline of Thex says, 'Something grand, truly epic and interesting! Just let me know when you've thought of a suitable story.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'An Epic Request'.\nBe sure to carry your epic artifact with you!\nExplore Locations\nNOTE: There are 16 \"explore\" locations. Each location represents one class and, for that one class, will trigger an event. The other 15 classes only need to explore the location.\nExplore the Stage of Baladric's Symphony 0/1 (Dreadlands)\nTask Window Says: Baldric Slezaf's tale is the pursuance of impossible beauty -- a symphony to rival the works of Ayonae Ro.\n/loc 780, 9690, 1070 (valley with the portals -- in a pyramid near Baldric Slezaf). For non-Bards, this is a simple location update. For Bards, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Valley of McArik's Reflection 0/1 (Lake of Ill Omen)\nTask Window Says: Keras McArik stands stoic in a valley east of what was once Veksar.\n/loc -225, -3535, 235 (near Keras McArik, due east of the center of the lake, near the zone boundary). For non-Berserkers, this is a simple location update. For Berserkers, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Depths Behind the Scaled Mystics 0/1 (East Cabilis)\nTask Window Says: Beneath the Scaled Mystics' Temple lies a rather complex series of tunnels.\n/loc 940, -450, -22 (in the halls under the Shadow Knight, Beastlord, and Shaman guild). For non-Enchanters, this is a simple location update. For Enchanters, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Outer Remnants of Torsis' Dark Mantle 0/1 (Emerald Jungle)\nTask Window Says: Standing just outside the ruins of Torsis you can feel the intense spiritual void that caused the city's downfall.\n/loc 295, -2000, -322 (at the entrance to City of Mist). For non-Shamans, this is a simple location update. For Shamans, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Oasis in a Deserted Sea 0/1 (Timorous Deep)\nTask Window Says: In a sea of desolate islands stands one secluded, sacred paradise.\n/loc -11550, -1710, 13 (in the walled isle where the Cleric 2.0 final battle is held and the triggered Faydedar is located). For non-Clerics, this is a simple location update. For Clerics, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Bloody, Forgotten Trail of Hate's First Knight 0/1 (North Ro)\nTask Window Says: When Lhranc returned to Freeport to exact vengeance upon his brother, Glohnor, he took a particular trail into the city.\n/loc 9625, 520, 25 (entrance to the Freeport Sewers in the very far northwest corner of the zone). For non-Shadow Knights, this is a simple location update. For Shadow Knights, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Orbital Children of Ro 0/1 (West Freeport)\nTask Window Says: There are not many locations on Norrath where you can see Drinal, Luclin, Anbeal, Trorsmang, Cordon, and Ro all at once.\n/loc -185, -940, 20 (a study hall in arcane tower, near entrance to Arcstone). For non-Wizards, this is a simple location update. For Wizards, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Plains of the Legendary Pegasus 0/1 (South Karana)\nTask Window Says: Many people are amazed at the constructive feats of the Aviaks. How such noble but simple creatures were able to create such a majestic tower is still a mystery.\n/loc -6745, 1065, 6 (Aviak's treehouse, just north of zone-in from Lake Rathetear). For non-Magicians, this is a simple location update. For Magicians, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Cusp of the Unkempt Border 0/1 (Jaggedpine Forest)\nTask Window Says: The Hatchling River is perhaps the most recognizable boundary between the relative safety of the Jaggedpine and the forbidden jungle.\n/loc +1000, -2120, -6 (near the broken zone line, east zone wall). For non-Druids, this is a simple location update. For Druids, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Crossroads of Taelosia and Antonica 0/1 (Nedaria's Landing)\nTask Window Says: A small family of bears has taken residence in the caves where Nideno Eliagy hides.\n/loc 1400, -450 (mouth of the bear caves in the northeast). For non-Rangers, this is a simple location update. For Rangers, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Forgotten Road of the Legendary Lich 0/1 (Everfrost Peaks)\nTask Window Says: Many have searched to expose secrets of Miragul's Highway only to discover more questions than answers...\n/loc 4730, -4150, -94 (underwater tunnels in the north-central part of the zone -- center room at the hidden portal, north wall). For non-Necromancers, this is a simple location update. For Necromancers, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore Fizzlethrope's Gallery 0/1 (Plane of Mischief)\nTask Window Says: 'Seek the walls adorned with Fizzlethorpe's visage within a single chest sits atop a pedestal.'\n/loc 20, -390, 125 (first room in the castle). For non-Rogues, this is a simple location update. For Rogues, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Sanctum of the Tortured God 0/1 (Acrylia Caverns)\nTask Window Says: Legend has it that Khati Sha, first Vah Shir Beastlord, became the subject of a failed Ssraeshzaen experiment to bestow godhood among a mortal being.\nThis updates at the zone-in. For non-Beastlords, this is a simple location update. For Beastlords, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Site of the Ancient Games 0/1 (Butcherblock Mountains)\nTask Window Says: Not far from Greater Faydark, tucked away in the hills, is an ancient stone board. Its origins remain a mystery...\n/loc 700, -2350, 11 (at the chessboard north of the Greater Faydark zone). For non-Warriors, this is a simple location update. For Warriors, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Master's Worldly Keep 0/1 (Castle Mistmoore)\nTask Window Says: Faydwer is not home to many beings called 'The Master'. So it should be no surprise that a trip to the castle of Mayong Mistmoore is in order.\nThis updates at the zone-in. For non-Paladins, this is a simple location update. For Paladins, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nExplore the Ascended Home of Wun and Po 0/1 (Plane of Sky)\nTask Window Says: Having ascended past their worldly existence, Wu and Po serve in the training grounds under the watchful eye of the Wyrm Queen.\nThis updates at the zone-in. For non-Monks, this is a simple location update. For Monks, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\nRecount your tale to Lady Carolline 0/1 (Northern Felwithe)\nHail her for the final update.\nThe Event: Summary\n(Summary needed, including task steps, mechanics, what types of spells to use on which mobs, etc.)\nNote: The event will require usage of your epic weapon, so have it on you at all times.\nThe Event: In Detail\nWith this task, you will have to zone via the boats rather than using the translocator in Butcherblock.\nTranslocator Gethia says 'Hello there, _____. You look like you are on an important adventure. I have some wonderful news from the Academy of Arcane Sciences! The Maiden's Voyage has once again resumed sailing between Timorous Deep and Firiona Vie. To board the great ship simply take one of the local shuttles.'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Timorous Deep.\nThis journey must be travelled alone. For now you must leave your allies behind. (This includes your mercenary.)\nThe gentle ebb and flow of the deep serves as a quiet backdrop to your meditations. Across the small sea of ruins is the holy site of the Triumvirate of Water. You close your eyes and contemplate the adventures that brought you here when the words of a nearly forgotten note cross your mind...\nGreetings Overking Bathezid. The time has come for you to return the boon owed to me from so long ago...'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Balance of the Triumvirate'.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Burning Woods.\nThis is the first of several monster missions in which you inhabit the body of Zordakalicus. You begin in Sarnak form.\nGeneral Bathezid says 'Zordakalicus the Flame Serpent, you honor us with your presence. Your courier has briefed me on the situation as well as Jaled Dar's orders.'\nYou say, 'Hail, General Bathezid'\nIkros Fer says 'Indeed, an army of one hundred strong has set out from their little outpost in the Karnor and will be here within the hour.'\nGeneral Bathezid says 'They don't expect to win the ensuing battle. It is no surprise that they are desperate for reinforcements.'\nGeneral Serokust says 'If they intend to test the mettle of the Di`Zok then I say we let them. The lizards are no threat to our noble blood.'\nGeneral Bathezid says 'Individually no, but you forget our numbers, general.'\nIkros Fer says 'Our leader has spared two of his finest warriors and their squires to hold the keep against the lizards.'\nGeneral Serokust says 'Yet another debt to be repaid at the whim of his majesty the Dar?'\nIkros Fer says 'You will show some respect and gratitude to the Flame Serpent, general.'\nGeneral Serokust scowls at the drake and then looks toward you, 'Very well... sir.'\nGeneral Bathezid says 'Forgive us, many of my compatriots still hold the old grudges. Our blood burns the same as yours, tainted or not by that lizard's hand.'\nThe voice of a distant Sarnak calls out, 'Shadows on the horizon! Their forces draw near!'\nGeneral Bathezid shouts, 'Soldiers of Chardok, today we make our stand against our tormentors. We hold our ground with the aid of the Ring of Scale. Defend the gates with your lives so that this keep remain ours until the end of our lineage!'\nGeneral Bathezid tells you, 'Meet me upon the battlefield and stand with me against their commander. The sight of an elder dragon will surely unsettle their ranks.'\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\na Hand of the Empire shouts 'Soldiers of Chardok, by Royal Decree of your lord, Emperor Ganak Sathir, son of your father Atrebe Sathir, you are ordered to surrender this keep and lay down your weapons. Those of you that do not resist will be enlisted to battle against the Ring of Scale. Those that survive will be given a station of honor as the empire's finest creation. Those who resist will become feed for the sokokar.'\nGeneral Bathezid turns to address his army, 'The lizards have made us their offer. Shall we serve as shields against the Ring of Scale or do we drive these lizards back to the Karnor!?'\na Sarnak flunkie shouts 'WE FIGHT!'\nThe Hand of the Empire laughs, 'How is it you so easily throw away the lives we gave you, serpentspawn?'\nGeneral Bathezid looks toward you and nods. He turns back toward the Iksar commander, 'Unexpected allies.'\nGeneral Bathezid draws his blade as you take the cue to shed your disguise.\nBattle is joined as you take Dragon form. You have three spells to cast; Fear, Fire, and Heal, but not a great deal of mana. After the battle has been won...\nVekelrek calls out, 'Zordakalicus, our mission is almost complete. Return to us now.'\nGeneral Bathezid shouts 'We are eternally indebted to you both. Our victory would have been a massacre without your intervention. Though it will take some years for us to recoup our losses, our keep is secure.'\nVekelrek Sapara shouts 'Your debt is to the Ring of Scale, a debt that must be repaid before 'some years', general.'\nGeneral Bathezid is taken aback by the Vekelrek's words, 'Our forces are decimated. It would be the end of our empire to join another battle!'\nVekelrek Sapara turns toward Zordakalicus, 'Our orders were clear. Destroy the battalion from Karnor's and reclaim the lizard's creation for our ranks. It is only a matter of time before the halfbreeds crawl back to their parents.'\nZordakalicus rears back and roars, 'Their blood is our blood, you would send them to die!?'\nVekelrek Sapara shouts 'You would defy the Dar?'\nZordakalicus nods silently.\nVekelrek Sapara shouts 'Traitor! You will fall in the name of the Ring of Scale!'\nNow begins a second battle between Zordakalicus and the dragon Vakelrek Sapara.\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\nVekelrek Sapara died.\nGeneral Bathezid says, 'Flame Serpent, the death of Vekelrek will soon reach the ears of the Ring. Where will you go?'\nZordakalicus says, 'I will abscond to the north lands and seek the tutelage of a god that does not turn brothers against one another.'\nGeneral Bathezid says, 'My kingdom remains in your debt.'\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Timorous Deep.\nYou find yourself on an island in northern Timorous Deep. You are leashed to the island (as you will be to others).\n_____ has fallen to the ground.\nYou do not feel well.\nYou hear the sound of waves crashing against a shore...\nYou struggle fiercely but eventually manage to open your eyes.\nYour head is wracked with pain that throbs to the pace of your heartbeat.\nYou muster the strength to stand up and survey your surroundings. You see no remnants or wreckage of your vessel.\nYou feel unusually weak. Your Water Sprinkler seems to be weighing you down more than normal.\nYour thoughts turn away from distant memories and fever dreams to the problems at hand, how to get off of this island.\nYou sense faint remnants of life from the nearby ruins.\nA spirit of the ruins materializes before you.\nYou say, 'How do I get off the island'\nYou think you hear voices calling out from the ruins - undead spirits that yearn to be sensed.\nYou begin casting Sense the Dead.\nYou sense undead in this direction.\nYou say, 'Hail, an echo of life'\nan echo of life says 'The fearless Jarsath must be returned to the feet of the father.'\nThe spirit vanishes but another appears elsewhere on the island.\nYou begin casting Sense the Dead.\nYou sense undead in this direction.\nYou say, 'Hail, an echo of life'\nan echo of life says 'Approach them both in guise they cannot see.'\nThe spirit vanishes but another appears elsewhere on the island.\nYou begin casting Sense the Dead.\nYou sense undead in this direction.\nYou say, 'Hail, an echo of life'\necho of life says 'Speak to them, sight unseen, the name of their tribe and your freedom shall follow.'\nA mystical path appears before you.\nYou begin casting Group Perfected Invisibility to Undead.\nYou say, 'Jarsath'\nFearless Guardian says 'Escape for us is impossible, as this is our home it is our prison. For you however, freedom awaits. Carry your burden to your strange gods of the sea to find what encumbers you so...'\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\nYou awaken on the beach.\nYour illness appears to be getting worse.\nBandit Scout, Timothy jumps back, startled by your presence. He turns to his commander and shouts, 'G..G..Ghost!'\nFirst Mate Dockins runs forward weapons drawn. He halts to look you over and turns to the scout, 'You idiot, this ain't no ghost.'\nBandit Scout, Timothy says 'Then how'd they appear out of thin air?'\nFirst Mate Dockins says 'Must be one of them magic caster types.' The bandit turns to you, 'So stranger, what brings you to the outpost of the great Gunthak Pirates? Usually we have to go out looking for saps to rob, most people are smart enough to steer clear of us!'\nBandit Scout, Timothy laughs.\nFirst Mate Dockins says 'You know the drill stranger, your [gold] or your [life].'\nYou say, 'What gold?'\nFirst Mate Dockins beams with joy that slowly fades into disappointment as he looks you over. 'Bah, from the rags you're wearing I doubt you got anything worth stealing!'\nBandit Scout, Timothy says 'Wait boss, maybe they can help us with our [situation].'\nFirst Mate Dockins glares at the scout.\nYou say, 'What situation?'\nBandit Scout, Timothy says 'Yeah, our captain's been struck with some terrible illness. No doubt these cursed ruins have infected 'em!'\nFirst Mate Dockins nods, 'Yar, maybe some of your magic tricks could be of some use. Here's the deal stranger, you cure our captain and we'll get you off this rock. I don't rightly care where you're heading but away from here is no doubt closer to where that be. [Deal]?'\nYou say, 'Deal'\nFirst Mate Dockins says 'Right then, our captain's over here.'\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\nFirst Mate Dockins looks toward you and speaks, 'He's in there stranger. Save him and you've got your freedom.'\nYou begin casting Reverent Light Rk. III.\nCaptain Gerrins looks a bit healthier.\nYou begin casting Reverent Light Rk. III\nCaptain Gerrins groans, his skin looks yellowed with disease.\nYou begin casting Reverent Light Rk. III.\nCaptain Gerrins seems to be regaining some of his strength but coughs up some vile green phlegm.\nYou begin casting Reverent Light Rk. III.\nCaptain Gerrins opens his eyes and begins shouting wildly, 'GHOSTS! DO YOU NOT SEE THEM!? CURSE OUR FOOLISHNESS IN TAKING THESE RUINS!'\nThe captain appears to be cursed with some terrible vision of ghosts. You may want to prepare yourself for battle before you continue curing him.\nYou begin casting Fraught Renewal Rk. II.\nA brilliant beam of light shines out of the captain's mouth and takes the form of a cursed spirit!\nCaptain Gerrins says 'Yar, blasted spirits think they got the better of meh!?'\nVengeful Jarsath Spirit says 'Join ussss!'\nYour Water Sprinkler of Nem Ankh feels exceedingly heavy.\nYou crush Vengeful Jarsath Spirit for 406 points of damage.\nVengeful Jarsath Spirit died.\nCaptain Gerrins says 'What's the story with the healer?'\nFirst Mate Dockins says 'They washed up on our shore and traded magic for passage.'\nCaptain Gerrins says 'Very well, a deal's a deal. Our raft's on the southern shore. Let's move out!'\nFirst Mate Dockins says 'So soon captain, are you sure you're well enough?'\nCaptain Gerrins shrugs, 'You think a little ghost is gonna slow me down?'\nCaptain Gerrins says 'It's a short ride to our outpost. From there we'll commandeer a bigger vessel for the rest of our voyage. We'll drop you off on whatever island you fancy, healer.'\nFirst Mate Dockins says 'Short trip or not we best be careful, the water's been unusually fierce. The gods seem irate.'\nBandit Scout, Timothy says 'Aye, something feels amiss...'\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\nAn uneasy tiredness falls over you. You lay down to rest as the raft takes off.\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Nagafen's Lair.\nThis is another monster mission. You inhabit Zordak Ragefire as his pilgrimage takes him to the Northlands.\nZordak says, 'I have heard him through the voice of fire. His instructions were clear, we must seek allies in these troubling times. Lord Nagafen's parting from the brood was not unlike my own, we will surely find an ally in him. What dragon would hold council with giants if both were not loyal to the Tyrant?'\nLaura Shima says, 'I don't think we're alone in our pilgrimage here.'\nGavon Malant, 'Many fresh footprints lead into the lair.'\nZordak says, 'Never a shortage of fools trudging to offer themselves as meals to Lord Nagafen.'\nJimmic Valon, 'I'm not so sure, people are more allied than they used to be. Teir`Dal and Feir`Dal coming together to take out the ancient lords and ladies. I don't like the looks of this...'\nLaura Shima nods, 'Either way, we best watch our step.'\nZordak thinks for a moment then speaks, 'It is odd that the noble fire giant guards are not at their station. Let's go, keep your guard up.'\nAs you enter the hall you see the flayed body of a fire giant noble face down in the lava.\nGavon Malant says, 'Good god, the guards are slain! What kind of force could have done this?'\nZordak says, 'The flames of Fennin shall shield us from whatever darkness has crept into the Lord's chambers.'\nThe ancient portcullis screeches as it rises revealing the remnants of recent destruction.\nLaura Shima retches, 'Slain... Nothing but bodies...'\nZordak says nothing, contemplating why Fennin would allow such horrific atrocities to befall his loyalists.\nAs you step across the bridge you look up to see that the giants were able to take out a few of the invaders.\nJimmic Valon says, 'We're close, the sweet smell of burning flesh is ripe.'\nGavon Malant says, 'What if Lord Nagafen has fallen? What then, Zordak?'\nZordak says, 'Mortals claiming the life of a dragon?'\nGavon Malant says, 'Stranger things have happened.'\nZordak says, 'We'll find our answer within his lair. Should the unthinkable have happened we will claim this site in the name of the Plasmatic Priesthood and go from there.'\nThe roar of the crowd booms as you enter the lair of Lord Nagafen, yet you do not see the proud lord standing tall. You quickly survey the room to see a heap of flesh that was once the great dragon.\nLaura Shima cries, 'Impossible, Nagafen has fallen!'\nZordak shouts, 'What is the meaning of this!?'\nA scarred and decorated figure steps forward from the crowd and speaks, 'The lord's hoard is ours. Rightfully claimed from his burning corpse. What is it you seek, stranger?'\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\nZordak says, 'Previously one thing, now two things...'\nZordak says, 'The first was council with a humble servant of fire, an opportunity your party has taken away from me.'\nZordak says, 'So now, this sacred site to mourn and serve as refuge for my order.'\nThe Raid Commander looks to Zordak and says inquisitively, 'And the second thing?'\nZordak Ragefire shouts, 'Revenge!'\nAs Zordakalicus, you fight the raid force that just defeated Lord Nagafen.\nZordak laughs, 'As well it should, but the Tyrant will protect us until this world is nothing but ash.'\nJimmic Valon nods, 'What are we to do now?'\nZordak says, 'Go out and make contact with our other allies. I will remain here in the shrine of the Tyrant and deal with any interlopers, no doubt there will be many.'\nThe priests each nod in agreement, 'As you wish, sir...'\nYour task 'Balance of the Triumvirate' has been updated.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Timorous Deep.\nYou do not feel well.\nYou feel very sick.\nBandit Scout Timothy says, 'I think the healer's dead, should we roll 'em over the side?'\nFirst Mate Dockins roars, 'Show a lil respect. If not for them Captain Gerrins would be dead!'\nCaptain Gerrins says, 'Aye, we'll put 'em down on the \n\n...[Walkthrough truncated for in-game performance]...",
