power begins to glow. A voice whispers from the orb, 'The Elements are out of balance, you must help them!' In the distance you hear a pained call. Something is amiss atop the Aviak village. Perhaps you should go [identify] the problem.\nWhen you get there there will be 4 elementals. 3 on the various Aviak perches around the top, and one in the fire pot in the middle of the large building at the top of the treehouse. C asting the spell \"Identify\" on each one will give you a hint as to what they need to 'balance' them.\nBlind Air Elemental â€\" Summoned Heatstone\nThe swirling air elemental glows, its sight returning. The element of air has returned to balance.\nWounded Earth Elemental â€\" Summoned Bandages\nThe damaged earth elemental regains its strength. The element of earth has returned to balance.\nThirsty Water Elemental â€\" Summoned Globe of Water\nThe coalesced flowing water elemental swirls with strong inner-currents. The element of water has returned to balance.\nHungry Fire Elemental â€\" Summoned Black Bread\nThe ravenous flame elemental burns brightly with its newly obtained fuel. The element of fire has returned to balance.\nIf you fail to give them the right items before a certain amount of time they aggro. They are dark blue at 100 but only hit ~400 dmg. Kill them and it progresses the task as though you had balanced them with the proper hand ins.\nThe Aviaks begin squawking, they appear to be growing restless. You should return to ground level and find out why...\nYou see what appears to be the leader of the Aviak tribe motion toward you. He squawks angrily. Perhaps if you had a [minion] that could [speak] on your behalf to this creature Once you get to the bottom an Angry Aviak will spawn and start running back and forth pulling you to it. Load up ANY level version of Monster summoning. Keep summoning a pet until the pet spawns as an Aviak. Any pet you already had, or any monster summon pets that are not Aviaks, will be killed each time the Aviak pulls you. If you donâ€™t get one up soon enough the Angry Aviak will attack. Just Kill it to continue to the next phase. Once you kill the Angry Aviak or get the Aviak pet, the Aviak despawns and you get the following message: Although you are at a loss as to why the creature attacked you, you sense something ominous in your future... The voice of the orb begins to speak but is muffled by the sound of howling wind. You should prepare yourself to face the wrath of the elements! You have two and a half minutes before the Wind Harbinger arrives. Once the time is up you get the following message: In the distance the furious flapping of wings is heard. The once boisterous Aviaks now stand silently, as if trying to avoid the incoming beast's wrath. Filthy two-legged parasite! Your corpse should prove fine sustenance for my plains. Squallmane the Harbinger of Wind spawns and attacks you. Little pegasus mobs spawn throughout the fight. They all, named pegasus included, only hit 300-500ish and con dark blue to 105. At about 50% Squallmane runs away at faster than bard speed to the top of the hill between the Aviak Village and Splitpaw with the following message: The orb's voice overpowers the sound of howling wind, 'He is retreating, chase after hâ€¦' He will start tossing you back and forth between Splitpaw and the Aviak Birdhouse. He will do this several times. He will stop after a set number of tosses. During the tossing you will land closer to the Hill he is on each time. When he stops, he will summon you to him at the top of the hill with the following message: A whirlwind begins to form around Squallmane. From the torrential gusts comes a familiar being from your pastâ€¦ The Shadow of Quillmane spawns and a couple more baby pegasus adds. After a couple seconds a voice will tell you to equip your epic. ANY epic (1.0, 1.5, 2.0) will work, but you MUST have one of either of these three epics on your person. Equip it and a skeleton of Magi`Kot will spawn, the pegasus mobs will depop, with the following dialog: Spirit of Trilith Magi`Kot says, 'Beasts, your wrath is misplaced in this Magician! He brings balance to the world despite your loss. Look to yourself, your chaos, your unbridled desire to overpower the other elements, these things should you distain...' Spirit of Trilith Magi`Kot focuses a spell of elemental balance and disperses the harbinger and its mate back into the forces of wind... A great booming voice shakes the bowels of the earth, cracks the sky and nearly throws you off of your feet, '... I... THOUGHT... MORE... OF... YOU... THAN... THIS!.. MAGI`KOT... YOUR... FATE... HAS... BEEN... DECIDED...' Your task 'An Epic Request' has been updated. The Arch Elementalist's ethereal form fades into nothingness. The gems on your weapon radiate with his presence. Magi`Kot's spirit has returned to the Orb of Mastery. The balance of the elements has been restored. - Explore the Cusp of the Unkempt Border 0/1 (Jaggedpine Forest) Task Window Says: The Hatchling River is perhaps the most recognizable boundary between the relative safety of the Jaggedpine and the forbidden jungle. /loc 1000, -2120, -6 (near the broken zone line, east zone wall). For non-Druids, this is a simple location update. For Druids, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup). - Explore the Crossroads of Taelosia and Antonica 0/1 (Nedaria's Landing) Task Window Says: A small family of bears has taken residence in the caves where Nideno Eliagy hides. /loc 1400, -450 (mouth of the bear caves in the northeast). For non-Rangers, this is a simple location update. For Rangers, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup). - Explore the Forgotten Road of the Legendary Lich 0/1 (Everfrost Peaks) Task Window Says: Many have searched to expose secrets of Miragul's Highway only to discover more questions than answers... /loc 4730, -4150, -94 (underwater tunnels in the north-central part of the zone -- center room at the hidden portal, north wall). For non-Necromancers, this is a simple location update. For Necromancers, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup). - Explore Fizzlethrope's Gallery 0/1 (Plane of Mischief) Task Window Says: 'Seek the walls adorned with Fizzlethorpe's visage within a single chest sits atop a pedestal.' /loc 20, -390, 125 (first room in the castle). For non-Rogues, this is a simple location update. For Rogues, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup). - Explore the Sanctum of the Tortured God 0/1 (Acrylia Caverns) Task Window Says: Legend has it that Khati Sha, first Vah Shir Beastlord, became the subject of a failed Ssraeshzaen experiment to bestow godhood among a mortal being. This updates at the zone-in. For non-Beastlords, this is a simple location update. For Beastlords, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup). - Explore the Site of the Ancient Games 0/1 (Butcherblock Mountains) Task Window Says: Not far from Greater Faydark, tucked away in the hills, is an ancient stone board. Its origins remain a mystery... /loc 700, -2350, 11 (at the chessboard north of the Greater Faydark zone). For non-Warriors, this is a simple location update. For Warriors, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup). - Explore the Master's Worldly Keep 0/1 (Castle Mistmoore) Task Window Says: Faydwer is not home to many beings called 'The Master'. So it should be no surprise that a trip to the castle of Mayong Mistmoore is in order. This updates at the zone-in. For non-Paladins, this is a simple location update. For Paladins, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup). - Explore the Ascended Home of Wun and Po 0/1 (Plane of Sky) Task Window Says: Having ascended past their worldly existence, Wu and Po serve in the training grounds under the watchful eye of the Wyrm Queen. This updates at the zone-in. For non-Monks, this is a simple location update. For Monks, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup). - Recount your tale to Lady Carolline 0/1 (Northern Felwithe) Hail her for the final update. The Event (Event details needed: Names of mobs and any items involved; emotes; mechanics; instanced zones, if any.) Note: The event will usually require usage of your epic weapon, so have it on you at all times. Rewards are 1 AA, plus: Option #1: Epic 1.0 Ornament Option #2: Epic 1.5 Ornament Option #3: Epic 2.0 Ornament This task is repeatable with a 20-hour lockout.Rewards: - [Focus of Primal Elements Ornamentation [item=110315]\n- Orb of Mastery Ornamentation [item=110366]\n- Staff of Elemental Essence Ornamentation [item=110367]\n[",
