\nThis updates at the zone-in. For non-Beastlords, this is a simple location update. For Beastlords, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\n- 14. Explore the Site of the Ancient Games 0/1 (Butcherblock Mountains)\nTask Window Says: Not far from Greater Faydark, tucked away in the hills, is an ancient stone board. Its origins remain a mystery...\n/loc 700, -2350, 11 (at the chessboard north of the Greater Faydark zone). For non-Warriors, this is a simple location update. For Warriors, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\n- 15. Explore the Master's Worldly Keep 0/1 (Castle Mistmoore)\nTask Window Says: Faydwer is not home to many beings called 'The Master'. So it should be no surprise that a trip to the castle of Mayong Mistmoore is in order.\nThis updates at the zone-in. For non-Paladins, this is a simple location update. For Paladins, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\n- 16. Explore the Ascended Home of Wun and Po 0/1 (Plane of Sky)\nTask Window Says: Having ascended past their worldly existence, Wu and Po serve in the training grounds under the watchful eye of the Wyrm Queen.\nThis updates at the zone-in. For non-Monks, this is a simple location update. For Monks, this initiates an event (for class event details, see the next section in this writeup).\n- 17. Recount your tale to Lady Carolline 0/1 (Northern Felwithe)\nHail her for the final update.\nThe Event\nAn Epic Request / An Epic Retelling - Shadow Knight event\n* Get your epic weaponry out of the bank.\n* Make sure you are solo -- no group and no mercenary.\n* Start the task \"An Epic Request\" in Felwithe.\nThroughout the Shadow Knight event, you will be given a number of choices. You can choose the good path like a Paladin, or you can choose the path of evil; the path of the Shadow Knight; the path of Lhranc. During at least one run-through of An Epic Request, follow the path that is the paragon of darkness to earn An Epic Retelling achievement.\n* Travel to North Ro and head to the task update spot in the northwest corner of the zone at 9600, -500.\nAs a Shadow Knight, you will receive \"Brittle Stone\" on your cursor.\n* Click the Brittle Stone to be assigned the 1-person task 'Innoruuk's Curse' (The Shadowknight's Journey) and it also points you southeast.\nIf you ever find yourself needing to re-enter an instance zone while the task is active, click the Brittle Stone again from North Ro.\nIf you don't receive a Brittle Stone, check to see if you already have one in inventory from a previous task run.\nIf you click the Brittle Stone while you are in a group, it gives you the error \"This is a journey that must begone [sic] alone. Cast off the bonds of your allies!\". Simply disband your group and click the stone again.\nYou begin casting Look Into the Eyeball.\nYour eyes feel stronger.\nAs you concentrate your gaze on the stone it takes the form of an eye that blinks quickly and then instantly repetrifies. You feel yourself drawn in this direction!\nAs you near the small wooden huts you notice something interesting. A merchant beating the life out of a fallen-battered man...\nYou have been assigned the task 'Innoruuk's Curse'.\nThe direction to someone related to your current Task has been marked on your compass.\n'Innoruuk's Curse' task step 1: Locate the Disturbance 0/1 North Desert of Ro\n-- The brittle eye-shaped stone calls out to you, beckoning you to seek the nearby conflict.\nThere is a line on your compass indicating where to go.\n* Run southeast to 8190, -1645 in North Ro to find an irate merchant beating a starving beggar.\n* Hail an irate merchant.\nAn irate merchant says, 'The merchant roars, 'Miserable fink! This is the third time this week I've caught this freeloading lump of refuse stealin' from my store!''\n'Innoruuk's Curse' task step 2: Settle the Dispute 0/1 North Desert of Ro\n-- You are posed with a simple question of morality. Decide the fate of each man.\nThe wounded human lies broken and beaten as the merchant continues to attack him. In his hand rests a bag of stolen goods...\nYou get a pop-up window called \"A Question of Morality\".\nA simple question of morality:\nDo you take pity on the weak and staving criminal or side with the merchant in defending his livelihood? [Help Merchant] [Save Thief]\nEvil choice: [Help Merchant]\nAn irate merchant says, 'Ah, a fine and fair citizen. Let's spare the militia the hassle of ridding the fields of another pest!'\nA starving beggar groans...\n* Kill a starving beggar.\nThe two figures fade from sight and are replaced by two opposing human females. They face each other but each speaks as if only to herself...\nThe Apotheosis of Hope says, 'There is hope for this one, her judgment is impartial. She knows better than to let her emotions cloud her decisions.'\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity says, 'Your optimism will be your undoing. This one is clearly the paragon of our cause.'\nThe Apotheosis of Hope says, 'We shall see...'\nGood choice: [Help Thief]\nAn irate merchant roars, 'Miserable scoundrels, the lot of you! I'll have your heads for this!'\nA starving beggar coughs, 'Thank you, stranger.'\n* Kill an irate merchant.\nThe two figures fade from sight and are replaced by two opposing human females. They face each other but each speaks as if only to herself...\nThe Apotheosis of Hope says, 'Such compassion... This is the one I choose! That is, unless you intend to take back your word. I would hardly put it past you.'\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity laughs, 'Predictable until the end. This one shall do, I sense the familiar fire burning within them.\nThe Apotheosis of Hope says, 'We shall see...'\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity says, 'Fair Knight, I sense in you the will of the Father. I shall spare you the back-story, as I sense your accomplishments already. Tell me, are you [willing] to look back through the eyes of history to settle a little bet of ours?'\n* Target The Apotheosis of Enmity and say, 'willing'\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity says, 'Very well, we shall see you soon...'\n'Innoruuk's Curse' task step 3: Witness Lhranc's escape from Freeport 0/1 The Northern Desert of Ro\n-- Strange visions have overtaken your consciousness. You find yourself many years in the past viewing life through the eye of Lhranc. Witness his wounded escape from Freeport.\nYou have entered The Northern Desert of Ro.\nYou are transported to old, original North Ro (map: nro) facing south, and shrouded as a level 35 warrior. You are affected by the aura Severe Wounds: \"You appear to be missing an eye...\"\nYou cough violently; your vision is blurred and sporadic. The expansive desert before you is dark with radically unseasonable weather.\nEscape... This word is at the forefront of your consciousness.\nIt begins to rain.\nIn the distance you hear the yelling of the militia. You must head south!\n* Move south toward the huts.\nYour wounds are becoming more severe! You won't make it much further without aid...\nYour body is wracked with intense pain.\nAs you reach the huts, you will start losing health, then fall unconscious.\nYou fall to the ground in blind agony.\nStranger?\n...\nYou did this to me! You don't... You can't love her as I do!\nBrother, we are in love... My heart does not love her to spite you. Do you find no comfort in knowing she is happy?\nHappy? She is blinded by your deceit... No... She will be mine!\nYou are out of food and drink.\n...\nYou alive?\nYou are completely healed.\nYour eyes open, your vision is blurred but you can make out the silhouette of a Barbarian against the cloudy sky.\nGuthren Sandfisher says, 'Didn't think you were gonna' make it there, stranger. Not too many folks come crawlin' out'uh Freeport missin' an eye like tha'...'\nYour hands are wound tightly with bloodstained bandages. You muster the strength to raise a hand to your face. The soft cloth of an eye patch clings tightly to your skin, bound by a film of dried blood.\nThe Barbarian walks over and offers you a flask of water. He looks down, ' 'ere, you'll need this. The desert ain't kind tah those without drink...'\nYou receive 2x Pod of Water on your cursor.\nYou are healed to full.\nGuthren Sandfisher says, 'Yeh should be gettin' along after yeh've rested up, I kin't imagine the guards are far behind yeh... I won't lie if they come askin' about yeh, but I offer yeh this head-start now...'\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity shakes her head, 'He would so easily hand you over... Seems like you would be better off without guards on your trail.'\nThe Apotheosis of Hope says, 'You would harm the stranger that saved your life and offered you respite from your abusers simply for not wanting to lie?\nGuthren Sandfisher says, 'Yer sword is over there stranger. Travel on in good health.'\nYou are no longer stunned.\n* Stand up and look a bit to the south to find a sword lying on the ground. Pick up and equip Damaged Fine Steel Greatsword - 2HS.\nYou get a pop-up window called \"A Question of Survival\".\nA question of survival:\nDo you silence the fisherman now or risk being followed further by the militia? [OK]\nGuthren Sandfisher stands along the shore fishing with his back to you.\n* Evil choice: Kill Guthren Sandfisher.\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity grins, 'Well?'\nThe Apotheosis of Hope shakes her head...\nThe mysterious figures vanish.\nYou have gained the ability \"Lifetap\" at a cost of 0 ability points.\nYour blade quickly fells the fisherman. He falls dead, a look of confusion frozen on his face.\nYou have slain Guthren Sandfisher!\nYour Monster AA Window automatically opens. Make a hotkey for Lifetap from the Class tab. You will need it.\n* Good choice: Leave Guthren Sandfisher to his fishing.\nThe Apotheosis of Hope says, 'Well?'\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity says, 'It means nothing! A trail of blood is as bad as a trail of words...'\nThe mysterious figures vanish.\n'Innoruuk's Curse' task step 4: Witness Lhranc's escape to the Oasis 0/1 The Northern Desert of Ro\n-- After receiving aid from the fisherman Lhranc made his way further south through the desert.\n* Start traveling south along the shoreline toward Oasis.\nThrough the haze you spot the faint glow of torches. It would appear the guards are patrolling the coast, you will have to take the south-west road to the Oasis...\nA gust of wind whips over the hills and kicks sand into your face... 'Why do you run, coward?'\nYou think you hear whispered voices cursing... Watch your step!\nThe tired sobbing of a woman fills your ears... 'You don't deserve her, you never will...'\n* Turn slightly southwest away from the shoreline to avoid the guards. Continue toward the southern zoneline to Oasis while avoiding guards and guard encampments in the desert. If you do get guard aggro, running away seems to leash them. If they kill you, you'll respawn back at the fisherman's hut.\nThe southwestern road into the Oasis looks clear...\nAs you reach the zone to Oasis, you are beset by either one guard or three.\nA voice breaks through the din of the storms,'Hah! You didn't expect to escape that easily, did you?'\nEvil:\nThe guards laugh, 'The Barbarian led us right to you!'\nWayguard Ginfur shouts, 'You shall not pass into the Oasis!'\nWayguard Sanwell shouts, 'You shall not pass into the Oasis!'\nWayguard Thrinn shouts, 'You shall not pass into the Oasis!'\n* You will need to kill all three guards before you can continue - don't forget to use your Lifetap ability.\nGood:\nWayguard Thrinn shouts, 'You shall not pass into the Oasis!'\n* Kill the guard.\nLhranc roamed the unforgiving deserts of Ro for weeks. His torment continued even as the militia's interest in his capture waned. As time passed he became indistinguishable from any of the nameless madmen roaming the Oasis. His thoughts were fraught with maddening voices. His brother's, his unrequited love's, unyielding multitudes of tormentors left him without solace... His disdain for humanity matured until he had been deemed ready...\nDon't actually zone to Oasis. Instead, the script sends you to Plane of Hate B.\n'Innoruuk's Curse' task step 5: Make your way to the seat of Innoruuk's power 0/1 The Plane of Hate\n-- The morality play grows more severe. Your consciousness has returned to your body but you find yourself in the Plane of Hate. Make your way to the seat of Innoruuk's power to witness a pivotal moment in history.\nYou have entered The Plane of Hate.\nYou are now your own character instead of a monster shroud.\nA slow tune begins echoing down the Maestro's halls...\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity sighs before speaking, sounding as if she is in the throes of carnal pleasure, 'The plane is alive with the will of the Father. It was on this day he gave his greatest gift to humankind.'\nThe Apotheosis of Hope says, 'However, Innoruuk's ritual did not proceed without interruption. A battalion was sent forth by the Lightbringer to end Lhranc's life before he became an unmanageable threat...'\nYour mind clouds with images of suffering as The Father's voice shakes the foundations of the plane. The words are unclear but the intent is unmistakable. The denizens of Hate are to keep intruders at bay until the ritual is complete.\nYou hear what sounds to be the grinding of planks to the south. The din fades and the sound of music in the hall grows louder.\nYou get a pop-up window called \"A Fond Memory\".\nAs you near the Maestro's chamber you come upon a curious duel. A minion of Marr stands in furious combat against one of the Father's pets. The ashenbone drake rears back, its decrepit hide invoking \"fond\" memories of your past. The Knight of Marr looks to be losing the fight... What do you do? [Kill Drake] [Kill Paladin]\nYou say, 'Hail, Valorian Rholek'\nValorian Rholek turns toward you quickly with a look of fear and disbelief, 'I can only hope you're here to help defeat this vile foe...'\nYou say, 'Hail, a decrepit ashenbone drake'\nA decrepit ashenbone drake flaps its skeletal wings angrily as it strikes at the paladin!\nEvil choice: Kill both the paladin AND the drake. To receive the item Decayed Decrepit Hide, choose to kill the Drake first, followed by the Paladin. If you're not going for the Hide, then the order doesn't matter.\nIf you choose \"Kill Drake\":\nThe Apotheosis of Hope smiles, 'Nobility in camaraderie!'\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity says, 'Perhaps just blind hatred for the beast...'\n* Kill a decrepit ashenbone drake.\nValorian Rholek turns to you and salutes, 'You have my eternal gratitude fair knight. I would not have been able to vanquish that foul beast without your help. I shall sing your praises to my brothers of Marr when I return to my battalion.'\nIf you choose \"Kill Paladin\":\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity grins, 'Yes, rid Father's domain of these pests!'\nThe Apotheosis of Hope shakes her head, 'Blinded by loyalty, such a shame.'\n* Kill Valorian Rholek.\nThe voice of Innoruuk overwhelms your thoughts, 'One less miserable pest tainting my plane. Perhaps you shall earn the right to suffer here eternally after I've killed you... This one shall return to my temple now.'\nIf you killed both the drake and the paladin:\nThe Apotheosis of Hope shakes her head is dismay...\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity breathes deeply and speaks with a voice tinged with euphoric pleasure, 'Such ruthless hatred, more!'\nIf you killed the drake and the paladin in the correct order:\nThe Maestro raises a hand to conduct his choir, their voices cry out in unison with the howl of the bleak organ. You can't help but feel the piece is being performed in your honor...\nInnoruuk's voice booms through the open doorway, 'Fools, debauched and worthless souls! You will soon know the power of an elder god!'\nYou get a pop-up window called \"Course of Action\".\nThe denizens of Innoruuk's realm are unusually indifferent to your presence. It would seem their focus is on battling the invading minions of the Lightbringer. The unmistakable presence of Marr's soldiers radiates from the north. To the south, Innoruuk's temple emites a comforting aura of corruption. You may choose to beat back the forces of Mithaniel Marr or simply travel to Innoruuk's temple to bear witness to the ascension of Lhranc. [OK]\n* Exit the Maestro building where you will find denizens of Hate battling paladins. You can ignore them, they don't count for anything.\n* Evil choice: Before heading south, go north toward the normal zone-in spot to find Squire Baerson on the platform, and kill him.\nFor Decayed Drecrepit Hide, you may have to pause while killing Squire and make sure he turns twisted before finishing him off.\nThe area around you shakes as Baerson's form shifts into that of a twisted knight!\nSquire Baerson's twisted form falls and disappears from sight, his soul returning to the Temple of Marr.\nThe Apotheosis of Enmity's disembodied voice shrieks euphorically, 'Truly, you've earned the right to serve Father!'\nThe Apotheosis of Hope is quick to retort, 'What you see as service to hatred is just as likely devotion to order...'\nYou have slain Squire Baerson!\n* Head south toward Innoruuk's den.\nYou will meet Ashenbone Skullbreaker, who throws you backwards.\nThe pile of bones begins\n\n...[Walkthrough truncated for in-game performance]...",
