      title = "Anniversary Solo Task: A Fool's Errand",
      exp = "02",
      exp_name = "The Scars of Velious",
      min_lvl = 60,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Task",
      repeatable = false,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = -297.0, x = 785.0, z = -91.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Emissary of Bristlebane",
        "A riotous antic sounds good",
        "A classic?",
        "Give me more",
        "riotous",
        "classic",
        "more",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "me more'", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 110515, name = "Fool's Pie", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 60\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** No\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Task\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis is a seasonal group task that was introduced in April 2013 as part of April Fool's Day. It's expected as being available only around April for a relatively short period of time.\nIt begins with Emissary of Bristlebane, located outside the main bank of the Plane of Knowledge.\nYou may need to be Level 60 in order to request the task. You may also need to have the Rain of Fear expansion in order to get it.\nYou say, 'Hail, Emissary of Bristlebane'\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'Greetings, wanderer! It's an exciting time for followers of Bristlebane all over Norrath. It's also a hectic time of year for Bristlebane, so he asked me, his humble servant, to take point on a new prank he devised. Would you care to take part in this most [riotous] antic?'\nYou say, 'A riotous antic sounds good'\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'Great! However, you don't seem to have the right... disposition to tackle this most sacred task. You are troubled by the many worries of this world and that is no way to pay homage to Bristlebane, my friend! You must first get into the pranking spirit and leave your worries behind, at least momentarily. We shall start you off with a simple prank. A [classic]!'\nYou say, 'A classic?'\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'Take this recipe and this ludicrous Pie Mix. Fetch the remaining ingredients and bake some pies. Don't waste them after you've made them. Throw them at the unsuspecting inhabitants of the Plane of Knowledge. That'll show them! Just let me know if you need [more] Pie Mix.'\nYou receive 1x \"Fool's Pie Recipe\" and 10x \"Prankster's Pie Mix\".\nYou have been assigned the task 'A Fool's Errand'.\nBristlebane is planning a grand prank on Norrath. His Emissary requested your help.\nEmissary of Bristlebane has given you a note with the pie recipe and some pie mix. You need to obtain the remaining ingredients to make the pies. All the ingredients can be acquired from the local baking merchants. Some items are sold in the shops. Some items are sold by merchants outside.\n- 1. You'll need at least 10 bottles of milk 0/10 (Plane of Knowledge)\n- 2. You'll need at least 10 cups of flour 0/10 (Plane of Knowledge)\n- 3. You'll need at least 10 packets of frosting 0/10 (Plane of Knowledge)\n- 4. You'll need at least 10 packets of garnish 0/10 (Plane of Knowledge)\n- 5. You'll need at least 10 cups of sugar 0/10 (Plane of Knowledge)\nAll of the above items, except the sugar, can be bought from the vendor Culkin Ironstove (outside the vendor building that's southeast of the main bank, southern side). All of the items can be bought from Chef Denrun, loc -297, 785, -91\nThe sugar (\"Cup of Sugar\") can be bought from Klen Ironstove (inside the same building).\n- 6. Bake 10 pies. Ovens can be found in the local bakery 0/10 (Plane of Knowledge)\nInside an oven, combine (10 times): 1x Cup of Sugar + 1x Bottle of Milk + 1x Garnish + 1x Frosting + 1x Cup of Flour + 1x Prankster's Pie Mix.\nNote: While the combine is technically no-fail, you can still \"fail\" it as part of the task:\nThe pie explodes and goes up in flames!\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'Did I mention that the Pie Mix is highly unstable? I forgot to, didn't I? Haha! Come see me if you need [more].'\nYou say, 'Give me more'\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'Here is more Pie Mix for you, good luck!'\n- 7. Throw the pies! 0/10 (Plane of Knowledge)\nTask Window Says: Throw the pies at your fellow adventurers or at the inhabitants of the Plane of Knowledge.\nAs it says...mercs count as well.\n- 8. Tell the Emissary that you're in the mood for pranks 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nYou say, 'Hail, Emissary of Bristlebane'\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'That is marvelous. So here is the gig: we're going to make fools out of all Norrathians. We're going to place gems on every tree, as if they were fruit, and enjoy the chaos as these simpletons stand there, in wonder of this miraculous event. Perhaps they'll even stampede to get their hands on them. Oh, the hilarity! Here's where you come in: we need gems. Go to the Dragonscale Hills at once and gather the purple gems scattered there.'\n- 9. Go to (insert zone) and gather 10 (insert color) gems 0/10 Valley of King Xorbb\nThese are pre lootable ground spawns through different zones based upon your level, so you will loot 10 ground spawns of a particular colored gem.\nThere are 5 colored gem's for all of the level ranges (these levels are based off people's reports and may not be totally accurate). Blue, Green, Purple, Red, Yellow\nAt level 60 you are sent to City of Mist to collect 10 Rough Red Gem's. (where in City of Mist? Need locations)\nAt level 65 you are sent to Dragon Necropolis to collect 10 Rough Blue Gem's in multiple locations around the zone. (Need locations)\nAt level 83 the task sends you to Harbinger's Spire to collect 10 Rough Yellow Gem's. (where in Harbinger's Spire? Need locations)\nAt level 90 to 100 the task sends you to Dragonscale Hills to collect 10 Rough Purple Gem's. They can be found in the citadel and throughout the grasslands.\nAt level 100+ the task sends you Valley of King Xorbb to collect 10 Rough Green Gem's. They can be found around the vicinity of the Shard's Landing portal, and by the halfling NPCs nearby.\n- 10. Tell the Emissary you have the 10 gems 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nYou say, 'Hail, Emissary of Bristlebane'\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'Excellent work. However, these gems have been lying in the dirt for a while and are simply not presentable. Please take them to Audri Deepfacet to have them polished for me.'\n- 11. Give the gems to Audri Deepfacet 0/10 (Plane of Knowledge)\nAudri Deepfacet says 'Welcome! You brought me gems? Ah, yes, these sure could use a nice polish. Here: professionally shined, just for you!'\nYou receive a \"Bag of Polished Gems\".\n- 12. Give the Bag of Polished Gems to the Emissary 0/1 (Plane of Knowledge)\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'Most excellent work, my friend! But we need a few more days to pull this prank off. We need to... umm... discuss the logistics. Yes, logistics. Bristlebane is very pleased with your work, so you will be rewarded. Have faith.'\nEmissary of Bristlebane says 'I'll tell you what: come back in about two weeks for your reward, it'll be a real surprise!'\nYou've helped Bristlebane prepare for the grandest prank of all time.\nSide Notes:\nThe \"two weeks\" time frame he mentions may shrink as days pass.\nThere is a bag on the ground just behind the Emissary. Each time the task is completed, the bag physically grows in size as the collected gems are added to it. Once the bag reaches its maximum size, this emote goes off:\nEmissary of Bristlebane says ''Oh my! The bag is much too full. Minions, take the surplus gems to a safe place.''\n...And the bag reverts to its default (tiny) size once again.\nFool's Pie\n107 platinum, 8 goldRewards:\n- Fool's Pie [item=110515]\n[",
    },
