      walkthrough = "**Level:** 1\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Guide\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nCertain \"Noble Exchange\" vendors will give hints as to there current whereabouts of the \"Rare Items\" merchant Marcia Attamilgad. Those in the Bazaar and the Plane of Knowledge don't seem to help, but if you speak with those in Wayfarer camps, they'll be more forthcoming with information:\nYou say, 'Hail, Karoline'\nKaroline says 'Hello, _____.  Here to do some [trading], or were you looking for my friend [Marcia]? You never know [where] she'll turn up.'\nYou say, 'Trading?'\nKaroline says 'I'm happy to exchange [Nobles] for your platinum or gold pieces if you wish.'\nYou say, 'Nobles?'\nKaroline says 'Well, that's what we call them, anyway.  Surely you must be a noble to have that much money!'\nYou say, 'Who is Marcia?'\nKaroline says 'Marcia Attamilgad, of course.  She's a somewhat shady swashbuckler who seems to be able to get her hands on a new item every time she shows up.  She charges a lot, and she never has very much stock on hand, but she claims she's the only person on Norrath who can find what she sells.  She [travels] around a lot.  Always on the move, that one.'\nYou say, 'She travels? Where?'\nKaroline says 'Marcia was here not too long ago. She was saying she might go to _____ or maybe _____.'\nCheck the zones suggested. Wherever she is, Marcia Attamilgad will always be on the Find feature (CTRL+F). If you don't see her on Find, then she's not in the zone.\nMarcia Attamilgad is an adventure merchant and only deals with the Noble [item=118277] currency. Since her inventory is small and fleeting, you'll often find her empty. If you catch her at the right time, though, you may find some exceptionally rare items available for very, very high prices.\nItems She Won't Buy\nDetails>\nEarthshaker\nDocleaf's Shattered Shard\nLepracon's Pot of Gold\nGuise of the Ancient Gods\nZatozia's Pail of Rainbow Sherbet\nZatozia's Pail of Chocolate Ice Cream\nBladecatcher of the Marshall\nBone Fragmented Necklace\nCold Visor of the Warlord\nDark Hoop of the Necromancer\nShortbow of the Fighter\nSteel Ring of the Foot Soldier\nSteel Rod of the Knight\nYou say, 'Hail, Marcia Attamilgad'\nMarcia Attamilgad says 'Hi, my name is... Well, as far as YOU know, my name is Marcia Attamilgad.  I [travel] a lot, and sometimes I find a [few] [rare items] that you might be interested in. If I don't have what you want today, find me [tomorrow].'\nYou say, 'What rare items?'\nMarcia Attamilgad says 'Well, you know how it is.  Travel around enough, meet enough people, you start finding out who has things, and how much they are.  I've got leads on quite a [few] items that I guarantee no one else will have.  If you can pay the [price], you're welcome to have one.'\nYou say, 'Just a few?'\nMarcia Attamilgad says 'I never have many of these things.  I don't carry my whole inventory around at once like some people do.  If something's especially rare, I usually can just get my hands on one at a time.  Once I've made a sale like that, though, I don't have to worry about finding something else to sell until I [move] on.'\nYou say, 'What about the price?'\nMarcia Attamilgad says 'I'll be frank with you.  This stuff costs a lot to get.  If you want it you'll have to make it worth my while, and my time is worth a lot.'\nYou say, 'Why move on?'\nMarcia Attamilgad says 'I always said I was going to travel, and now that I'm grown that's my plan.  Never see the sun rise from the same place twice in a row.'\nYou say, 'Where will you be tomorrow?'\nMarcia Attamilgad says 'Tomorrow?  I don't know where I'll be yet.  I'll be there when I wake up, and I'll have something else to sell from my stash.'Rewards:\n- Axe of the Warmaster [item=8054]\n- Barbed Scale Whip [item=172]\n- Blade of the Black Dragon Eye [item=343]\n- BladeStorm, Katana of Steel Sleet [item=450]\n- Bone Collar of the Possessed [item=8921]\n- Box of Abu-Kar [item=2369]\n- Brokenskull Club [item=583]\n- Circlet of Shadows [item=1441]\n- Earring of Death [item=8807]\n- Earring of Fond Memories [item=8123]\n- Earring of Living Slime [item=10393]\n- Everriculum [item=7175]\n- Fabled Rod of Mourning [item=35082]\n- Feather Lined Box [item=55112]\n- Firestorm Cape [item=38292]\n- Gem Encrusted Choker [item=19057]\n- Gem Encrusted Ring [item=1649]\n- Locket of Escape [item=1163]\n- Manastone [item=3650]\n- Mask of Tinkering [item=4811]\n- Mindstealer [item=18501]\n- Mosscovered Twig [item=4]\n- Ornate Velium Pendant [Unlimited]\n- Polyphenomenal Axe [item=3578]\n- Radiant Gem Encrusted Ring [item=26885]\n- Red Dragon Tooth [item=3658]\n- Ring of the Dead [Bind Affinity]\n- Ringed Mace of the Ykesha [item=130]\n- Robe of the Enslaved Soul [item=8056]\n- Rod of Annihilation [item=154]\n- Rod of Mourning [item=571]\n- Runed Fighters Staff [item=545]\n- Salindrite Dagger [item=4812]\n- Sceptre of Destruction [item=6090]\n- Shield of the Clawed Guardian [item=20263]\n- Smolder [item=6091]\n- Soulshearer, Blade of the Savage [item=33805]\n- Staff of Forbidden Rites [item=560]\n- Staff of the Elder Claws [item=6504]\n- Staff of the Morning Dew [item=5621]\n- Sword of the Undead Kings [item=62127]\n- Thex Dagger [item=621]\n- Totem of the Wizened Spirits [item=4024]\n- Warding Star [item=145]\n- Warmaster's Mask of Battle [item=8058]\n- White Dragon Tooth [item=55721]\n- Writ of Dragonkind [item=5620]\n[",
