        { id = 4236, name = "Cougarskin Mask", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 33\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nErgrez will make you a mask from the skins of your kills, but you need to bring him some food as well as the skins.  Bring him a High Quality Cougar Skin and 2 Mammoth Meats.\nEmote:\nErgrez Shortpaw works at skinning and cleaning the raw furs around him.\nYou say, 'skinning'\nErgrez Shortpaw says, 'Yes. I take skin of animal that hunters catch and make into things. Very important, very big job for clan.'\nYou say, 'important'\nErgrez Shortpaw says, 'Is important because I make all the clothes, armor, bags, hut covers, and more. Life much harder for clan if I not here to clean and cure skins. Not many who have knowledge anymore.'\nYou say, 'armor'\nErgrez Shortpaw says, 'Many armors. All of animal hides from the islands. If you wanting armor then I can make for you. All I ask is you do me favor.'\nYou say, 'what favor?'\nErgrez Shortpaw says, 'Snowfangs in need of much help lately. Once we mighty but now weak. You help us get stronger. If you want armor of wolves or cougar then I need you bring twice as many materials. For each thing you wanting I need thing. Just tell me what furs you have and I tell you what I need.'\nYou say, 'high quality cougarskin'\nErgrez Shortpaw growls loudly. 'I not like making things of cat fur. Smells bad, hurts nose. You want me to work with that you bring food, lots of food. You bring me mammoth meats.'\nYou offered 1 High Quality Cougarskin to Ergrez Shortpaw.\nYou offered 1 Mammoth Meat to Ergrez Shortpaw.\nYou offered 1 Mammoth Meat to Ergrez Shortpaw.\nErgrez Shortpaw works with the fur for awhile by skinning it and sewing it.\nYou complete the trade with Ergrez Shortpaw.\nReceive: Cougarskin MaskSubmitted by: Balkor BloodbathRewards:\n- Cougarskin Mask [item=4236]\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "969",
      title = "Velium Retrieval",
      exp = "02",
      exp_name = "The Scars of Velious",
      min_lvl = 45,
      max_lvl = 45,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = { y = 830.0, x = -435.0, z = 43.0 },
      triggers = {
        "Hail, Sentry Kale",
        "What sentinel?",
        "What problem?",
        "I will deliver the supplies.",
        "sentinel",
      },
      items_required = {
        { name = "him 50 pp", count = 1 },
      },
      rewards = {
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 45\n**Maximum Level:** 45\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis quest begins with Sentry Kale at location 830, -435, 43, in Skyshrine.\nYou say, 'Hail, Sentry Kale'\nSentry Kale says 'Another Halfling, in the great shrine? Perhaps the times have gotten worse than we had expected -- I wonder if I will need to reactivate my [sentinel] for further use in my stead.'\nYou say, 'What sentinel?'\nSentry Kale says 'It was not too long ago that I was merely a chunk of walking velium in the eyes of most who traveled through the shrine. However that golem was in fact one of my sentinels used to keep my identity secluded, and took on the tasks that I gave it. However, there has been a problem recently with our supplies, and I have had to take it offline until further notice.'\nYou say, 'What problem?'\nSentry Kale says 'As you may have noticed, there are a great deal of golems and gargoyles within the shrine that consist of velium. These are our guards and they serve us well, however with extended use of these creatures comes extensive repair needed. It is because of this necessity to keep our sentries and lookouts working well that we require a great deal of velium ore stocked and ready for use. Unfortunately, our supplies have been running thin and we are in need of a new shipment of ore.'\nYou say, 'I will deliver the supplies.'\nSentry Kale says 'I may have been wrong in my initial thoughts about your race, Halfling. You may just prove to be worth my time. Take this note now and find Ungdin. Please hurry and remember to keep this information to yourself.'\nSentry Kale will hand you a Velium Delivery Note, which you are to take to a Coldain dwarf named Ungdin in Thurgadin.\nHe is located at 150, -23, -6.25. (Go into the mines and take the center tunnel. Continue in that tunnel until you come to the next fork of three tunnels. Take the one on your right. He is at the end of that tunnel. There's a table and bench in the room with him.)\nUngdin says 'Hmmm, not sure why you're giving me all this.  50 pieces  of platinum  Whew, wow, I may be coming down with  and the note  something.'\nGive him 50 pp.\nUngdin's eyes dart about the room before retrieving a large box from under the table. He takes the platinum and the note, then hands you the box without a word.\nYou will have \"A shipment of Velium Ore\" in your inventory. Take that back to Sentry Kale in Skyshrine and he will say the following:\nSentry Kale says 'You've returned, and with the shipment of ore intact! It was wise to send you out on that mission, ______, and I'm glad you did not fail. If you're looking for more assignments to do, I may have something that is just right for you. If you're interested in it, just let me know and we'll talk.'\nYour faction standing with Claws of Veeshan got better.\nYour faction standing with Yelinak got better.\nYour faction standing with Kromzek got worse.\nYou gain experience!!\nYou receive 7 copper from Sentry Kale.\nYou receive 6 silver from Sentry Kale.\nYou receive 10 gold from Sentry Kale.\nYou receive 4 platinum from Sentry Kale.",
    },
