      rewards = {
        { id = 4269, name = "Apprentice Skullcap - 1st Rank", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Time:** 1 hour\n**Level:** 4\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nThis quest begins with Master Xydoz in West Cabilis (findable with CTRL+F).\nYou say, 'Hail, Master Xydoz'\nMaster Xydoz says 'What is it you seek within the tower? Could it be that you are a new apprentice? If so, you are required to don the [apprentice skullcap].'\nYou say, 'What apprentice skullcap?'\nMaster Xydoz says 'All new members of the Brood of Kotiz are required to don the [apprentice skullcap]. To earn one, a new apprentice is required to fetch four brains for further experiments. Not just any four brain, mind you, but the brains of [sarnak] hatchlings.'\nYou say, 'What are sarnak?'\nMaster Xydoz says 'Sarnak?!! Do not speak loudly, that name. If you seek information on the sarnak, read the tome of this tower. The tower librarian should be found within.'\nCollect 4x \"Sarnak Hatchling Brain\" from sarnak hatchlings in the Lake of Ill Omen. These spawn in the area just south of the Cabilis entrance.\nNote that the Sarnaks and Goblins are KOS to each other, so you'll have some competition on your hands.\nUpon handing in the four brains:\nMaster Xydoz says 'Good work, my young apprentice. Wear it as a sign of our circle. Do not lose it. Someday you shall wear a necromancer skullcap, but next shall come the [second rank skullcap].' Submitted by: MuseRewards:\n- Apprentice Skullcap - 1st Rank [item=4269]\n[",
    },
    {
      id = "970",
      title = "Demise of Blizzent",
      exp = "02",
      exp_name = "The Scars of Velious",
      min_lvl = 50,
      max_lvl = 125,
      quest_type = "Quest",
      repeatable = true,
      group_size = "Solo",
      npc = "player",
      loc = nil,
      triggers = {
        "hail Vorken Iceshard",
        "what allegiances?",
        "I will wage war on the Dragons an Coldain",
        "I will do great deeds",
        "what motives?",
        "how can I please you as well?",
      },
      items_required = {
      },
      rewards = {
        { id = 3970, name = "Dragonhide Belt", type = "item" },
      },
      factions = {
      },
      walkthrough = "**Level:** 50\n**Maximum Level:** 125\n**Monster Mission:** No\n**Repeatable:** Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** No\n**Quest Type:** Quest\n**Group Size:** Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** 1\n**Max. # of Players:** 1\n\nYou say, 'hail Vorken Iceshard'\nVorken Iceshard says 'I am Vorken Iceshard, one of the lords of Iceshard manor.  In this day and age you can never tell where one's allegiances are.  Leave my servants in peace or you may leave in pieces.\nYou say, 'what allegiances?'\nVorken Iceshard says 'Loyalties, of course, little one.  Each day I see more mercenaries come to Kael, seeking their fortunes .  King Tormax will use your kind to wage war on the dragons and upon the Coldain.  But I question the motives of your kind.\nYou say, 'I will wage war on the Dragons an Coldain'\nVorken Iceshard says 'So your cause is to destroy the dragons as King Tormax says?  If you wish to be noticed by King Tormax, you must do great deeds.\nYou say, 'I will do great deeds'\nVorken Iceshard says 'If you expected to come to Kael Drakkel and immediately have an audience with the king, you are a bigger fool than most.  Go out and slay the weaker members of dragonkind.  That might gain his favor.  If you do hunt the wurms and drakes, you may be able to please me as well.\nYou say, 'what motives?'\nVorken Iceshard says 'My motives are simple.  I will acquire as much power and prestige as possible before I die.  Such is life for me, a constant search for power and wealth.  But my great power and wealth have not brought me happiness.   Enough of my motives, what drives you?  A constant search for more power, a search for security and happiness?  Or do you truly believe in the rhetoric of King Tormax which advocates that we eradicate the dragons?\nYou say, 'how can I please you as well?'\nVorken Iceshard says 'In my youth, I was bitten by a very intelligent wurm named Bllizent.  My brother and I were foolish enough to try to slay the great beast.  He tasted my flesh and the flesh of my brother that day and I fear he liked it too much.  I have nightmares of this beast's return to taste me again.  I would rest easier at night if I knew Bllizent was dead and gone.   He will be quite an elderly wurm if he is still alive today.\nBlizzent can be found in the Great Divide.  He drops a Fang that can be returned for the reward.Submitted by: Kabal UDLRewards:\n- Dragonhide Belt [item=3970]\n[",
    },
